{'copyright': 'Copyright (c) 2020 The New York Times Company. All Rights Reserved.', 'response': {'docs': [{'abstract': 'An executive of Mondelez International, which ran a spot featuring nontraditional families, said, “Being fearless is the only answer right now.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/business/media/advertising-week-marketers-are-urged-to-become-fearless.html', 'snippet': 'An executive of Mondelez International, which ran a spot featuring nontraditional families, said, “Being fearless is the only answer right now.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT is rare on Madison Avenue to hear, at least publicly, suggestions that executives are scaredy-cats who are afraid to take risks. But those attending Advertising Week in New York are being advised — sometimes gently, sometimes forcefully — that to produce campaigns that will more effectively resonate with contemporary consumers, they must risk failing and risk alienating their target audiences. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marketers Are Urged to Become Fearless', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marketers Are Urged to Become Fearless', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Stuart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T00:05:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d4798c7-f04c-5bc4-836b-f348c7d5f18f', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4798c7-f04c-5bc4-836b-f348c7d5f18f'}, {'abstract': 'Why is it so hard to get pain relief in the developing world?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/opinion/dying-without-morphine.html', 'snippet': 'Why is it so hard to get pain relief in the developing world?', 'lead_paragraph': 'HUNTINGTON, N.Y. — IMAGINE watching a loved one moaning in pain, curled into a fetal ball, pleading for relief. Then imagine that his or her pain could be relieved by an inexpensive drug, but the drug was unavailable. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dying Without Morphine', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dying Without Morphine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Morphine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Access to Pain Relief Initiative', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T00:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald Piana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/de98c505-30ce-5cd8-afe5-c407bf3da021', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de98c505-30ce-5cd8-afe5-c407bf3da021'}, {'abstract': 'Comments by the deputy prime minister marked a hardening of tone from the British government, which normally adopts diplomatic language with China when speaking about its former colony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/world/europe/in-a-shift-british-sharpen-their-tone-on-hong-kong-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Comments by the deputy prime minister marked a hardening of tone from the British government, which normally adopts diplomatic language with China when speaking about its former colony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BIRMINGHAM, England — Britain on Tuesday sharply criticized the handling of pro-democracy demonstrations in its former colony, Hong Kong, with the deputy prime minister summoning the Chinese ambassador in protest and warning that the territory’s prosperity was at risk if freedoms were suppressed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Shift, British Sharpen Their Tone on Hong Kong Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Shift, British Sharpen Their Tone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clegg, Nick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T00:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/478ace3f-065f-530d-aba5-29123e8efb83', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/478ace3f-065f-530d-aba5-29123e8efb83'}, {'abstract': 'The strategy of “containment” this go-round is not what it was during the Cold War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/opinion/thomas-l-friedman-order-vs-disorder-part-4-.html', 'snippet': 'The strategy of “containment” this go-round is not what it was during the Cold War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been arguing for a while now that the Israeli-Palestinian conflict is to the wider East-West clash of civilizations what Off Broadway is to Broadway. It’s where you can see many trends at a smaller scale first. That is why I study it closely. Whether it is airline-hijacking, suicide-bombing or trying to do nation-building with the other — Israelis called it “Lebanon invasion” and “Oslo”; we called it “Iraq” and “Afghanistan” — what happens there often moves to the larger stage. So, as I have asked before: What’s playing Off Broadway now?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Order vs. Disorder, Part 4', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Order vs. Disorder, Part 4', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T00:19:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4332f6ab-74c2-559d-9829-46de9ff07f63', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4332f6ab-74c2-559d-9829-46de9ff07f63'}, {'abstract': 'The contract security guard also managed to take pictures during the encounter, an official said, violating Secret Service rules while the president was in Atlanta.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/us/armed-man-boarded-elevator-with-obama-official-reports.html', 'snippet': 'The contract security guard also managed to take pictures during the encounter, an official said, violating Secret Service rules while the president was in Atlanta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — An armed private security guard rode in an elevator with President Obama when he visited the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention in Atlanta on Sept. 16, violating Secret Service protocols that only agents and officers for the agency should carry a gun around the president, according to law enforcement officials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Armed Outside Guard Was Allowed on Elevator With President, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Armed Outside Guard Was Allowed on Elevator With Obama, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierson, Julia A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T00:19:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt and Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middle