ation cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/us/money-allocated-for-immigration-lawyers-.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Health and Human Services announced that it would provide $9 million over two years for lawyers to represent unaccompanied minors in their deportation cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Health and Human Services announced Tuesday that it would provide $9 million over two years for lawyers to represent unaccompanied minors in their deportation cases in immigration courts. The program, which will assist about 2,600 youths, is the first time the department has directly funded lawyers for those minors. In the 2014 fiscal year ending Tuesday, the department took custody of about 58,100 unaccompanied children caught at the border, officials said, more than double the number in 2013 but far fewer than estimates of 90,000 during a surge in South Texas in June. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Money Allocated for Immigration Lawyers', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Money Allocated for Immigration Lawyers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T03:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3be81de3-a9c1-5ef8-863c-77d21954cdff', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3be81de3-a9c1-5ef8-863c-77d21954cdff'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats face tough challenges in a state that is drifting right. Their popular governor must leave office because of term limits, and outside interests loom larger in a race that may determine control of the Senate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/us/politics/loss-of-a-democratic-power-leaves-arkansas-in-doubt-.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats face tough challenges in a state that is drifting right. Their popular governor must leave office because of term limits, and outside interests loom larger in a race that may determine control of the Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LITTLE ROCK, Ark. — Gov. Mike Beebe got his start in Arkansas politics the way most candidates here do, at the Gillett Coon Supper, an annual feast on an animal that is plentiful in the state’s marshes, and not all that flavorful. Any savvy politician knows to grab the boniest chunk of raccoon on the table since it will make for the best photo and have the least amount of meat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/us/01ARKANSAS-hp/01ARKANSAS-hp-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/01/us/01ARKANSAS-hp/01ARKANSAS-hp-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/us/01ARKANSAS-hp/01ARKANSAS-hp-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': 