60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3768171d-a058-5237-99dc-e01ceedc0b69'}, {'abstract': 'The Chinese authorities have detained nearly two dozen people in an effort to contain the spread of pro-democracy sentiment, a report said Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/world/asia/hong-kong-protest.html', 'snippet': 'The Chinese authorities have detained nearly two dozen people in an effort to contain the spread of pro-democracy sentiment, a report said Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Nearly two dozen people have been detained across mainland China for expressing support for the growing protests in Hong Kong, in an effort by the Chinese authorities to contain the spread of pro-democracy sentiment, human rights groups reported on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detentions of Hong Kong Protest Sympathizers Reported in Mainland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinese Human Rights Defenders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T11:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlena