l Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c50b0042-1b6f-5630-83e0-4f1cd194c11f', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c50b0042-1b6f-5630-83e0-4f1cd194c11f'}, {'abstract': 'PayPal’s numbers suggest the traditional payments system is far from done. | Winners in PayPal’s spinoff. | Darden’s sticky situation. | Two accused of insider trading on Herbalife shares.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/morning-agenda-valuing-paypals-potential/', 'snippet': 'PayPal’s numbers suggest the traditional payments system is far from done. | Winners in PayPal’s spinoff. | Darden’s sticky situation. | Two accused of insider trading on Herbalife shares.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When eBay announced on Tuesday that it would spin off PayPal as a separate public company, the news sent ripples through the payments industry. Here would be a way for investors to bet on a revolution, one that would upend the traditional payments system now seen by many as cumbersome and expensive. A closer look at PayPal’s numbers, however, suggest that the old order is far from done, DealBook’s Peter Eavis writes. Sure, PayPal processed $180 billion in payments last year, but technology investors may be yearning for more progress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Valuing PayPal’s Potential', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T12:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58670de1-df7c-5628-bdb9-bd84f7a95935', 'word_count': 1992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58670de1-df7c-5628-bdb9-bd84f7a95935'}, {'abstract': 'A new group of online lenders present another choice to consumers who want to consolidate loans or credit card debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/business/online-lending-sites-offer-alternative-to-traditional-borrowing.html', 'snippet': 'A new group of online lenders present another choice to consumers who want to consolidate loans or credit card debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Traditionally, consumers who wanted to consolidate loans or credit card debt, or borrow for a vacation or a wedding, had two basic choices: Visit a local bank for a personal loan, or use another credit card.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Lending Sites Offer Alternative to Traditional Borrowing', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prosper Marketplace Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lending Club', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T12:09:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf378614-c85b-5994-ad65-fbe302f4392f', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf378614-c85b-5994-ad65-fbe302f4392f'}, {'abstract': 'James R. Clapper Jr., the director of national intelligence, sent a message to employees on Tuesday defending the nation’s spy agencies against criticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/01/spy-chief-tries-to-squash-talk-of-a-rift-with-obama-on-isis/', 'snippet': 'James R. Clapper Jr., the director of national intelligence, sent a message to employees on Tuesday defending the nation’s spy agencies against criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s chief spy is trying to squelch any talk of a breach with the White House amid finger-pointing over who was to blame for failing to anticipate the rise of the extremist group the Islamic State, which has rampaged through Syria and Iraq and has now drawn the United States back into a Middle East conflict.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spy Chief Tries to Squash Talk of a Rift With Obama Over ISIS', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapper, James R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T12:24:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc861e5a-27d0-538b-9f44-0166f569