rn our attention to pursuits of the colder months. Like — wait for it — sitting by a warming fire, sipping a hot milk punch and solving some crossword puzzles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/crosswords/091414foliage/091414foliage-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/crosswords/091414foliage/091414foliage-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/crosswords/091414foliage/091414foliage-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/crosswords/091414foliage/091414foliage-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/crosswords/091414foliage/091414foliage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/12/crosswords/091414foliage/091414foliage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/crosswords/091414foliage/091414foliage-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Goodbye Summer; Hello Fall', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autumn (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T13:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/febbd4be-0351-5285-a02b-9b942d13e57b', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/febbd4be-0351-5285-a02b-9b942d13e57b'}, {'abstract': 'The paper, saying it needed to reduce costs to safeguard profitability, said it would cut about 100 news jobs and a smaller number in other operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/business/media/new-york-times-plans-cutbacks-in-newsroom-staff.html', 'snippet': 'The paper, saying it needed to reduce costs to safeguard profitability, said it would cut about 100 news jobs and a smaller number in other operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times plans to eliminate about 100 newsroom jobs, as well as a smaller number of positions from its editorial and business operations, offering buyouts and resorting to layoffs if enough people do not leave voluntarily, the newspaper announced on Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Times Plans to Eliminate 100 Jobs in the Newsroom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Times Plans to Eliminate 100 Jobs in the Newsroom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulzberger, Arthur Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Mark John (1957- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T13:09:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08500624-ab02-5fd9-8fa4-9f115d6c865b', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08500624-ab02-5fd9-8fa4-9f115d6c865b'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Great Britain calls up 250,000 for military service in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/1939-more-britons-called-to-service/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Great Britain calls up 250,000 for military service in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Thirty days after its declaration of war on Germany, Great Britain tonight [Oct. 1] called up for military service all men between the ages of twenty and twenty-two, bringing into the armed forces 250,000 men resident in Great Britain. This swift answer to the Russo- German move for peace was announced at 8 o’clock tonight, little more than an hour before Winston Churchill, First Lord of the Admiralty, told a worldwide radio audience that Britain and France, and not Hitler, would set the time and the terms for the end of the war.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Oct. 2, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: More Britons Called to Service', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{