ites move to Harlem, the neighborhood’s black heritage is being lost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Ephesus Seventh-day Adventist Church in Harlem restored the tip of its steeple eight years ago, leaders of the predominantly African-American congregation saw it as a “beacon of hope and love for the community.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/nyregion/02BLOCKS-1/02BLOCKS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/01/nyregion/02BLOCKS-1/02BLOCKS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/nyregion/02BLOCKS-1/02BLOCKS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/nyregion/02BLOCKS-1/02BLOCKS3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/nyregion/02BLOCKS-1/02BLOCKS-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/01/nyregion/02BLOCKS-1/02BLOCKS-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/nyregion/02BLOCKS-1/02BLOCKS-1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After 90 Years, a Harlem Church Vows to Endure Amid Relentless Change', 'kicker': 'Building Blocks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 90 Years, a Harlem Church Vows to Endure Amid Relentless Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ephesus Seventh-day Adventist Church (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T14:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d63f582f-defd-57f9-8edb-152d34503eb7', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d63f582f-defd-57f9-8edb-152d34503eb7'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the four main fashion weeks around the world in New York, London, Milan and Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/arts/international/the-figures-behind-the-catwalk.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the four main fashion weeks around the world in New York, London, Milan and Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the perspective of the buyers, models and magazine editors whose business is high style, fashion week is actually more than a month. The women’s ready-to-wear shows occur twice yearly — first in February/March, then in September/October. They begin in New York before migrating overseas to London, Milan and then finally Paris. Each event has developed its own reputation, however true: New York is populist, London edgy, Milan commercial, Paris artistic.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/arts/international/02iht-btnumbers02/02iht-btnumbers02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 115, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/arts/international/02iht-btnumbers02/02iht-btnumbers02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 115}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/arts/international/02iht-btnumbers02/02iht-btnumbers02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 196, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/arts/international/02iht-btnumbers02/02iht-btnumbers02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/arts/international/02iht-btnumbers02/02iht-btnumbers02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/02/arts/international/02iht-btnumbers02/02iht-btnumbers02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/arts/international/02iht-btnumbers02/02iht-btnumbers02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Figures Behind the Catwalk', 'kicker': 'By the Numbers', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fashion Weeks, by the Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hidalgo, Anne (1959- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federation Francaise de la Couture', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T14:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'International Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c725a4c-eb5e-5c48-9002-b7089fab2b59', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c725a4c-eb5e-5c48-9002-b7089fab2b59'}, {'abstract': 'Downtown Flushing is known for its restaurants, bakeries and Asian specialty stores, along with its easy transportation into Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/realestate/downtown-flushing-where-asian-cultures-thrive.html', 'snippet': 'Downtown Flushing is known for its restaurants, bakeries and Asian specialty stores, along with its easy transportation into Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who live and work in downtown Flushing sometimes call it “the Chinese Manhattan.” Both downtown Flushing, in north-central Queens, and Manhattan are centers of commerce, transportation and finance, and both have shiny new buildings with expensive and sought-after condominiums.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Downtown Flushing: Where Asian Cultures Thrive', 'kicker': 'Living In', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Asian Cultures Thrive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T15:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vera Haller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vera', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/789e25f4-a937-531c-8ccd-3adf59f57542', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/789e25f4-a937-531c-8ccd-3adf59f57542'}, {'abstract': 'The longtime art collector Liz Swig is putting 30 years of experience and a coterie of famous friends to use for her latest venture, which connects big-name artists with high-end retailers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/liz-swig-millionaire-matchmaker/', 'snippet': 'The longtime art collector Liz Swig is putting 30 years of experience and a coterie of famous friends to use for her latest venture, which connects big-name artists with high-end retailers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve ever wanted to sip coffee out of a Julian Schnabel ceramic or scrape the last morsels of cake from a bona fide piece of Jeff Koons pop art, Liz Swig has you covered. In the past year, the long-time collector has parlayed her position on the board of Creative Time, a New York-based nonprofit arts organization, to start LizWorks, which brokers collaborations between blue-chip artists (Marina Abramovic, Vik Muniz) and fashion brands (Hugo Boss, Vera Wang). The results of those collaborations, like the $450 Kara Walker-designed Bernardaud pitcher that Jenna Lyons and Courtney Love reviewed in T’s Fall Women’s Fashion issue, are meant to allow even casual gallery-goers to grab a piece of the art action usually reserved for the one percent. “It’s about being able to reach out to people who really want to be in this world,” Swig says. “And now they are.” Well, sort of. LizWorks‘s latest commission — a line of made-to-order, steampunk-meets-optometrist eyeglasses by the photographer Hiroshi Sugimoto — will likely appeal to a more rarefied customer when it launches at Selima Optique in New York this holiday season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/t-magazine/30swig-oloizia/30schnabel-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/30/t-magazine/30swig-oloizia/30schnabel-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/t-magazine/30swig-oloizia/30schnabel-oloizia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/t-magazine/30swig-oloizia/30schnabel-oloizia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 1386, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/t-magazine/30swig-oloizia/30schnabel-oloizia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/30/t-magazine/30swig-oloizia/30schnabel-oloizia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '