, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What You Get for ... $1,750,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T15:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f000e5aa-7458-5fd9-a8ea-4caa644b4f71', 'word_count': 1047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f000e5aa-7458-5fd9-a8ea-4caa644b4f71'}, {'abstract': 'Looking at the effect that paying down the federal debt had in the past on our economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/01/politics-helpline-debt-economics/', 'snippet': 'Looking at the effect that paying down the federal debt had in the past on our economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of our continuous political helpline, we’re taking questions from readers and answering them as fast as we can. A reader asked:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics Helpline: Debt Economics', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T15:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d33370cb-44b5-5872-86a9-f4a0b060ebea', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d33370cb-44b5-5872-86a9-f4a0b060ebea'}, {'abstract': 'Substitute almond or coconut milk for yogurt or buttermilk for some dairy-free, delicious smoothies.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/smoothies-hold-the-dairy/', 'snippet': 'Substitute almond or coconut milk for yogurt or buttermilk for some dairy-free, delicious smoothies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been giving some thought to dairy-free, not-too-sweet smoothies. I usually use yogurt or buttermilk in my smoothies, but this week I wanted to make some drinks using almond milk and coconut milk. I looked around for some brands that tasted good to me (and I did need to look around), and found some great almond milk made with just about only almonds and water (it has less than 2 percent added ingredients but no sweeteners). For the others, I wanted to use coconut milk, not coconut water, which I think tastes pretty bad no matter how good for you it’s supposed to be. I used light coconut milk in conjunction with almond milk in a few of this week’s smoothies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/science/01recipehealthoatmealalt/01recipehealthoatmealalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/01/science/01recipehealthoatmealalt/01recipehealthoatmealalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/science/01recipehealthoatmealalt/01recipehealthoatmealalt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/science/01recipehealthoatmealalt/01recipehealthoatmealalt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/science/01recipehealthoatmealalt/01recipehealthoatmealalt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/01/science/01recipehealthoatmealalt/01recipehealthoatmealalt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/science/01recipehealthoatmealalt/01recipehealthoatmealalt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Smoothies, Hold the Dairy', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coconuts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oatmeal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T15:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3542b47f-2eb6-517f-aadd-8cdf9622958f', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3542b47f-2eb6-517f-aadd-8cdf9622958f'}, {'abstract': 'The Berliner Ensemble returns to the Brooklyn Academy of Music, in tandem with the director Robert Wilson, to present “Shakespeare’s Sonnets,” featuring a score by Rufus Wainwright.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/theater/shakespeares-sonnets-with-a-rufus-wainwright-score.html', 'snippet': 'The Berliner Ensemble returns to the Brooklyn Academy of Music, in tandem with the director Robert Wilson, to present “Shakespeare’s Sonnets,” featuring a score by Rufus Wainwright.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Berliner Ensemble returns to the Brooklyn Academy of Music this week, in tandem with the director Robert Wilson, to present an elaborate musical pageant, “Shakespeare’s Sonnets,” featuring a score by the unclassifiable Rufus Wainwright. Twenty-five of the sonnets are set to music by Mr. Wainwright that will reflect his catholic taste, including “medieval German Minnesang, classical, pop and cabaret rock,” according to the publicity release. Expect a similarly venturesome staging from Mr. Wilson, whose production of “The Threepenny Opera” for the Berliner Ensemble was seen in Brooklyn recently. The characters gliding through this production — and I confidently predict a lot of glacial gliding, along with scads of white pancake makeup — will include Shakespeare himself, Elizabeth I and the two principal objects of affection addressed in the sonnets. Fluidity of gender will be emphasized by having the female roles played by men and the male roles played by women. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE2/05GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE2/05GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', '