t': 'Goldman Sachs imposed limits on bankers over investing in specific stocks, bonds and hedge funds. But, Jeffrey Goldfarb of Reuters Breakingviews asks, why are Wall Street deal makers allowed to own individual securities?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/goldmans-new-conflict-rules-go-only-so-far/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs imposed limits on bankers over investing in specific stocks, bonds and hedge funds. But, Jeffrey Goldfarb of Reuters Breakingviews asks, why are Wall Street deal makers allowed to own individual securities?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another day, another conflict of interest situation for Goldman Sachs. New internal rules at the securities firm impose fresh limits on bankers investing in specific stocks, bonds and hedge funds. Goldman knows too well how easy it is to cross a line when treading at its edge. The new policy raises a bigger question, though: Why are Wall Street deal makers allowed to own individual securities at all?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/business/dbpix-goldman/dbpix-goldman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/business/dbpix-goldman/dbpix-goldman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/business/dbpix-goldman/dbpix-goldman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/business/dbpix-goldman/dbpix-goldman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'