cument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91033d14-60bc-5f16-a30f-d32abe1869e0', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91033d14-60bc-5f16-a30f-d32abe1869e0'}, {'abstract': 'Hotel Sahrai, with its elegant design and Givenchy spa, cements the historic city as a destination.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/fez-morocco-hotel-sahrai-opens/', 'snippet': 'Hotel Sahrai, with its elegant design and Givenchy spa, cements the historic city as a destination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marrakech and Tangier have long shared double billing as Morocco’s most alluring cities. In contrast, Fez, the country’s intellectual and spiritual capital, has always been respectfully admired for its architecture and its authenticity. Classified as a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1981, it’s a reserved but fascinating town that has been ambivalent about courting tourism — and until recently, has never had an opulent luxury hotel akin to Marrakech’s famed La Mamounia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/t-magazine/01fez-lobrano/01fez-lobrano-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/01/t-magazine/01fez-lobrano/01fez-lobrano-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/t-magazine/01fez-lobrano/01fez-lobrano-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/t-magazine/01fez-lobrano/01fez-lobrano-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/t-magazine/01fez-lobrano/01fez-lobrano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/01/t-magazine/01fez-lobrano/01fez-lobrano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/01/t-magazine/01fez-lobrano/01fez-lobrano-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chic New Hotel Opens in Fez, Morocco', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fez (Morocco)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T21:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7695a9f0-2b91-5872-9ab4-4d71eb4eb25d', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7695a9f0-2b91-5872-9ab4-4d71eb4eb25d'}, {'abstract': 'The show begins previews March 27 and will open on April 21 at the Broadway Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/broadways-doctor-zhivago-to-begin-performances-in-march/', 'snippet': 'The show begins previews March 27 and will open on April 21 at the Broadway Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The musical “Doctor Zhivago,” based on Boris Pasternak’s 1957 novel about romance and revolution in Russia, will begin preview performances on Broadway on March 27 and open on April 21, the producers said on Wednesday. As expected, the show will run at the Broadway Theater. The musical had its world premiere at the La Jolla Playhouse in 2006, then underwent changes before running at the Lyric Theater in Sydney in 2011. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway’s ‘Doctor Zhivago’ to Begin Performances in March', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broadway’s ‘Doctor Zhivago’ To Start Previews in March', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T21:11:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5316b37-9225-53f1-81e9-ec243dc5f6e3', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5316b37-9225-53f1-81e9-ec243dc5f6e3'}, {'abstract': 'Eiko, of the performance team Eiko & Koma, is staging a solo work in the cavernous 30th Street Station in Philadelphia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/arts/eiko-without-koma-creates-in-philadelphia-and-fukushima.html', 'snippet': 'Eiko, of the performance team Eiko & Koma, is staging a solo work in the cavernous 30th Street Station in Philadelphia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It started ordinarily enough. Eiko, the Japanese choreographer and dancer, was waiting for a train at the 30th Street Station in Philadelphia when she began to notice the space around her, and then, the bodies in that space. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Half of a Dance Duo, a Venture Alone in a Crowd', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Half of a Dance Duo, a Venture Alone in a Crowd', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eiko', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania Academy of the Fine Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnston, William I', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T21:19:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2151e328-f678-5d9c-9eb0-fbcaceb05422', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2151e328-f678-5d9c-9eb0-fbcaceb05422'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Putin said a plan to isolate the Internet in Russia was only intended as a backup security system to keep Russian domains online in a national emergency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/world/europe/russia-vladimir-putin-internet.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Putin said a plan to isolate the Internet in Russia was only intended as a backup security system to keep Russian domains online in a national emergency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — President Vladimir V. Putin 