 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03af292e-f07b-52de-8624-84224294327d', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03af292e-f07b-52de-8624-84224294327d'}, {'abstract': 'Nigerians are getting used to being checked for fever at airports and nightclubs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/opinion/living-with-the-terror-of-ebola.html', 'snippet': 'Nigerians are getting used to being checked for fever at airports and nightclubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAGOS, Nigeria — A FEW weeks ago, I flew from Atlanta to Murtala Muhammed International Airport here. Everything about the flight was routine, until I saw a flight attendant, a face mask flattening her blond hair, tentatively approach an older woman sitting several rows behind me. Upon landing, the flight attendants informed us that there would be a delay in disembarking because the woman was ill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living With the Terror of Ebola', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Living With the Terror of Ebola', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okeowo, Alexis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lagos (Nigeria)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T22:39:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Okeowo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Okeowo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fe2f61b-314c-511a-82de-60f19589b23f', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fe2f61b-314c-511a-82de-60f19589b23f'}, {'abstract': 'As housing prices soar and inventories shrink, one community still has plenty of choices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/garden/leave-your-wings-at-the-door.html', 'snippet': 'As housing prices soar and inventories shrink, one community still has plenty of choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, Bank of America turned me down for a home mortgage. The listing, in Salt Lake City, was a steal at $100,000: a fully furnished, five-story eco-mansion with 14 rooms, including a library, a music room, an art balcony and a cupola/conservatory. The original builders and owners, Debbie and Mike Schramer, had constructed the house and décor out of all sustainable materials, including a recycled cedar-shake roof, pebble floors and wisteria-beam framing.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy/2014102-FAIRYHOUSES-slide-H3GZ-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leave Your Wings at the Door', 'kicker': 'Design Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leave Your Wings at the Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models and Replicas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorello, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T22:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tortorello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tortorello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d4401bf-9e3a-5de1-9970-463facc8d638', 'word_count': 2681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d4401bf-9e3a-5de1-9970-463facc8d638'}, {'abstract': 'Building an energy-efficient house on a tiny island means zero utility bills. The trick is not leaving your phone in a tree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/garden/the-12-volt-solution.html', 'snippet': 'Building an energy-efficient house on a tiny island means zero utility bills. The trick is not leaving your phone in a tree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANCOCK COUNTY, Me. — Even with binoculars, it’s hard to tell if the small wooded island about a half-mile off the coast here is inhabited. You can see bald eagles soaring overhead, and terns and harlequin ducks on the water below. You might even catch a glimpse of a moose or deer swimming out to visit, but they rarely stay long. Perhaps it’s too rustic for them.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 12-Volt Solution ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 12-Volt Solution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keenan, Sandy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soley, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T22:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandy Keenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/649be96a-4e30-5bc3-adc7-3e63f57e3083', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/649be96a-4e30-5bc3-adc7-3e63f57e3083'}, {'abstract': 'Margo Selby offers custom throws that combine her textured fabrics with plush backing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/garden/who-doesnt-love-a-velvet-snuggle.html', 'snippet': 'Margo Selby offers custom throws that combine her textured fabrics with plush backing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Margo Selby, a British textile designer, creates lavish three-dimensional patterns for upholstery, rugs, lampshades and more. She started her company in 2003, concocting intricate designs on an old-fashioned 24-shaft dobby floor loom before sending them off for computerized production. She has produced collections for Habitat and the British Museum.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR1COMBO/02CURR1COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR1COMBO/02CURR1COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 837}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR1COMBO/02CURR1COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 735, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR1COMBO/02CURR1COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1469, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR1COMBO/02CURR1COMBO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR1COMBO/02CURR1COMBO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR1COMBO/02CURR1COMBO-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Doesn’t Love a Velvet Snuggle?', 'kicker': 'Currents: Textiles', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Doesn’t Love a Velvet Snuggle?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Arlene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selby, Margo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T22:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ba8698a-af24-5742-be11-16d49b349b27', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ba8698a-af24-5742-be11-16d49b349b27'}, {'abstract': 'House Industries puts its retro graphics on a new collection of stoneware.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/garden/the-heritage-is-baked-in.html', 'snippet': 'House Industries puts its retro graphics on a new collection of stoneware.', 'lead_paragraph': 'House Industries’ new ceramics were inspired by early American stoneware. “We dug around and came across pieces that had really cool numbers on them, which were normally used to mark the volume,” said Andy Cruz, a founder of the Delaware producer of vintage-driven fonts, housewares and fashion. “We thought, ‘Wouldn’t it be cool to track down one of these kilns?’\xa0” It turned out that Eldreth Pottery, a 30-year-old family business that makes salt-glazed stoneware using 500-year-old German techniques, was a half-hour away in Pennsylvania. The resulting pieces include two crocks, a pitcher, a mug, two plates and a spoon rest that Mr. Cruz described as “super cool.” They were produced in the traditional gray salt glaze as well as a red salt glaze that looks brown. Prices range from $26 for the spoon rest to $164 for a lidded crock. Information: 800-888-4390 or houseind.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR5/02CURR8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR5/02CURR8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR5/02CURR8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR5/02CURR8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR5/02CURR5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR5/02CURR5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR5/02CURR5-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Heritage Is Baked In', 'kicker': 'Curents: Goods', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Heritage Is Baked In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Industries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-01T22:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb614725-bea9-5c27-bb98-9ae363c59690', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb614725-bea9-5c27-bb98-9ae363c59690'}, {'abstract': 'An online company simplifies the framing process, cutting costs along the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/garden/framers-who-make-it-easy-to-get-the-picture.html', 'snippet': 'An online company simplifies the framing process, cutting costs along the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simply Framed, an online custom framing service in Miami, aims to radically ease the process of preparing art for hanging. In most frame shops, “the shopper is overwhelmed every step of the way, with choosing the frame, mat, type of glazing and hanging hardware,” said Dara Deshe Segal, the company’s owner. “It can also quickly become prohibitively expensive, and cost much more than whatever you want to frame.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR4/02CURR7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/garden/02CURR4/02CURR7-articleLarge.jpg', 