'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9a4c334-0517-56ce-af10-dd9fed17dcba', 'word_count': 1341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9a4c334-0517-56ce-af10-dd9fed17dcba'}, {'abstract': 'A Senate candidate boasts of a “frostbit” ear and “helmet hair.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/opinion/politics-alaska-style.html', 'snippet': 'A Senate candidate boasts of a “frostbit” ear and “helmet hair.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SITKA, Alaska — IT was a banner summer for us fishermen in the far north, with long, sunlit days pulling coho and king salmon. Anchored up at night, hands hardly able to close around a can of beer, we nodded at the usual stories: the tourist couple who lost their pug when it tried to make friends with a brown bear; the local man who disappeared, his skiff found abandoned in the rocks of Auke Bay; the black bear that fell through a skylight onto a table of cupcakes at a kid’s birthday in Juneau. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/opinion/02jones/02jones-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/opinion/02jones/02jones-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/opinion/02jones/02jones-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/opinion/02jones/02jones-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio