quities Act. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Mr. Obama’s Pacific Monument', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Obama’s Pacific Monument', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Remote Islands Marine National Monument', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T00:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f918d5b-3003-534e-a614-452a9d03e276', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f918d5b-3003-534e-a614-452a9d03e276'}, {'abstract': 'The Greek government said Wednesday that it would seek a vote of confidence in Parliament next week in a bid to quash mounting speculation about early elections and to keep flagging economic reforms on track.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/world/europe/greece-push-for-a-confidence-vote.html', 'snippet': 'The Greek government said Wednesday that it would seek a vote of confidence in Parliament next week in a bid to quash mounting speculation about early elections and to keep flagging economic reforms on track.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Greek government said\xa0 Wednesday\xa0that it would seek a vote of confidence in Parliament next week in a bid to quash mounting speculation about early elections and to keep flagging economic reforms on track. Prime Minister Antonis Samaras\xa0is to make the request on Monday, when the 2015 draft budget is to be presented, and a vote would be later in the week. It comes in an increasingly tense political and social climate as international creditors are in Athens reviewing Greece’s progress on austerity measures. Meanwhile, the\xa0leftist Syriza party is pushing for snap elections. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: Push for a Confidence Vote', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: Push for a Confidence Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T00:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fc33d0b-1efe-55cc-b1d8-233098eb2374', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fc33d0b-1efe-55cc-b1d8-233098eb2374'}, {'abstract': 'A lawsuit filed in federal court in Minnesota seeks to undermine union rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/opinion/more-hurdles-for-home-care-unions.html', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit filed in federal court in Minnesota seeks to undermine union rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an attempt to build on a recent antiunion victory in the Supreme Court, the National Right to Work Legal Defense Foundation has filed another antiunion lawsuit in federal court in Minnesota. The suit seeks to weaken a new union of 27,000 home care workers there and, in the process, to undermine union rights more broadly. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Hurdles for Home Care Unions ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Hurdles for Home Care Unions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Right to Work Legal Defense Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T00:56:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c305f8e5-11af-5e56-82a9-eb786f6ee5f7', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c305f8e5-11af-5e56-82a9-eb786f6ee5f7'}, {'abstract': 'The wreck of a ship discovered last month after being trapped in Arctic ice in the 1840s has been identified as the H.M.S. Erebus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/world/americas/canada-shipwreck-in-arctic-identified.html', 'snippet': 'The wreck of a ship discovered last month after being trapped in Arctic ice in the 1840s has been identified as the H.M.S. Erebus.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The wreck of a ship discovered last month after being trapped in Arctic ice in the 1840s has been identified as the H.M.S. Erebus. It was the ship of the captain, Sir John Franklin, who led 129 men on it and H.M.S. Terror in a voyage to chart the Northwest Passage. Despite 32 rescue missions from England, he and his crew all died. Prime Minister Stephen Harper, who made a hunt for the ships a priority, announced the finding on Wednesday in the House of Commons. The confirmation was based on divers’ measurements, sonar images and underwater photographs by Parks Canada, the agency that has led six searches for the ships. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Shipwreck in Arctic Identified', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Shipwreck in Arctic Identified', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shipwrecks (Historic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exploration and Explorers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harper, Stephen J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T00:59:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e912dd-c93c-57f1-a088-d224b2850cfe', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e912dd-c93c-57f1-a088-d224b2850cfe'}, {'abstract': 'In response to a Twitter post about the fatal shooting of Michael Brown by a police officer, a user wrote: “I know someone sitting on the grand jury. There isn’t enough at this point to warrant an arrest.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/us/possible-leak-by-ferguson-grand-juror-is-investigated.html', 'snippet': 'In response to a Twitter post about the fatal shooting of Michael Brown by a police officer, a user wrote: “I know someone sitting on the grand jury. There isn’t enough at this point to warrant an arrest.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'FERGUSON, Mo. — The St. Louis County prosecutor is investigating a possible leak by a grand juror in the case of Darren Wilson, the Ferguson police officer who shot and killed 18-year-old Michael Brown in August, a spokesman for the prosecutor’s office said Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Possible Leak by Grand Juror Is Investigated in Ferguson Police Shooting Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Possible Leak by Ferguson Grand Juror', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Darren (1986- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T01:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original':