name': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d458a66-f0a4-5683-887e-89736f2ea327', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d458a66-f0a4-5683-887e-89736f2ea327'}, {'abstract': 'In his best-known project, Mr. Paparazzo sought to limit driving, preserve trees and arrange homes close together to increase open space and reduce infrastructure costs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/business/otto-paparazzo-innovative-developer-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'In his best-known project, Mr. Paparazzo sought to limit driving, preserve trees and arrange homes close together to increase open space and reduce infrastructure costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Otto Paparazzo, a New England developer who drew national attention in the 1960s and ’70s for popularizing a novel concept in American housing at the time — large condominium and clustered-housing projects in often sleepy small towns — died Sept. 23 in Southbury, Conn., the site of his best-known development, the “planned adult community” Heritage Village. He was 88. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/business/PAPARAZZO-2-obit/PAPARAZZO-2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/business/PAPARAZZO-2-obit/PAPARAZZO-2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/business/PAPARAZZO-2-obit/PAPARAZZO-2-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None