: 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/45f383e7-1fa6-5356-be3b-2ea87278dd24', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45f383e7-1fa6-5356-be3b-2ea87278dd24'}, {'abstract': 'Since the Ebola virus began spreading through West Africa, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention has been pushing the worst-hit countries to implement screening for air passengers. \xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/us/man-in-us-with-ebola-had-been-screened-to-fly-but-system-is-spotty.html', 'snippet': 'Since the Ebola virus began spreading through West Africa, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention has been pushing the worst-hit countries to implement screening for air passengers. \xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'As he was preparing to leave Liberia for Dallas two weeks ago, Thomas E. Duncan, the man confirmed to be the first Ebola case in the United States, was checked at the airport for signs of the disease. He was determined to have no fever and allowed to board his flight, American officials say.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man in U.S. With Ebola Had Been Screened to Fly, but System Is Spotty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man in U.S. With Ebola Had Been Screened to Fly, but System Is Spotty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Thomas Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T01:34:22+0000', 'document