 general partner, borrowed his father’s tactic from the aftermath of the 1981 World Series and apologized to fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/sports/baseball/hal-steinbrenner-apologizes-for-yanks-year.html', 'snippet': 'With the Yankees missing the playoffs for a second consecutive season, Hal Steinbrenner, the team’s managing general partner, borrowed his father’s tactic from the aftermath of the 1981 World Series and apologized to fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the Yankees missing the playoffs for a second consecutive season, Hal Steinbrenner, the team’s managing general partner, borrowed his father’s tactic from the aftermath of the 1981 World Series and apologized to fans. “I apologize,” Hal Steinbrenner said on the “Michael Kay Show” on ESPN Radio. “We did not do the job this year. We know what you expect of us, and we expect the same thing of ourselves.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hal Steinbrenner Apologizes for Yanks’ Year', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steinbrenner Apologizes for Yanks’ Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, Hal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, George M 3d', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T04:37:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8529bb5f-11ff-5810-9ed2-23be6813b9da', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8529bb5f-11ff-5810-9ed2-23be6813b9da'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (NBC) BAD JUDGE Kate Walsh stars as Rebecca Wright, a party girl, rocker chick and tough-as-nails criminal court judge with a reputation for questionable courtroom behavior. Rebecca gives no indication of changing her wild ways until an 8-year-old boy (Theodore Barnes), whose parents she imprisoned, seeks her help in this new comedy series. In “A to Z,” at 9:30, Cristin Milioti plays Zelda, a practical-minded lawyer who signs up on an Internet dating site called Wallflower, where a computer glitch sends her a total mismatch. Ben Feldman is Andrew, a closet romantic who works at the site and meets Zelda when she visits the company. She thinks it’s mere chance that they’ve encountered each other. He thinks it’s fate — and that she’s actually the beauty in a shimmering silver dress he spied at a concert a couple of years earlier and couldn’t stop thinking about. Writing in The New York Times, Alessandra Stanley called “A to Z” “a love story that braids coincidence and destiny” and likened it to the Nora Ephron movie “Sleepless in Seattle,” “though it is also infused with some of the bittersweet self-consciousness of ‘(500) Days of Summer.’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e6d68c2-3c1e-5f86-b9a6-7c5ede51324e', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e6d68c2-3c1e-5f86-b9a6-7c5ede51324e'}, {'abstract': 'Moody’s Investors Service said it was considering a downgrade in light of what it called a “softening” of both Met ticket sales and contributions from donors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/arts/music/metropolitan-operas-credit-rating-is-under-review-for-possible-downgrade.html', 'snippet': 'Moody’s Investors Service said it was considering a downgrade in light of what it called a “softening” of both Met ticket sales and contributions from donors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The gravity of the Metropolitan Opera’s financial challenges was underscored on Wednesday when Moody’s Investors Service said it was putting the opera company under review for a possible downgrade of its credit rating.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Metropolitan Opera’s Credit Rating Is Under Review for Possible Downgrade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met Opera’s Credit Rating Faces Possible Downgrade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T05:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_