and I interviewed a candidate for a senior communications role at Posse. We met at a coffee shop and he seemed perfect: charming, smart and passionate about our business. He’d been successful in similar roles, and he came to the interview prepared with suggestions relevant to our strategy. I was impressed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Women Manage Men Who Don’t Respect Women', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T11:12:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebekah Campbell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebekah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Campbell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ee945a7-8fb0-5414-9363-25da2854964d', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ee945a7-8fb0-5414-9363-25da2854964d'}, {'abstract': 'A group backed by the billionaire Koch brothers is shifting tactics in several of the most competitive Senate races and will begin more direct and aggressive attacks on Democratic candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/02/today-in-politics-7/', 'snippet': 'A group backed by the billionaire Koch brothers is shifting tactics in several of the most competitive Senate races and will begin more direct and aggressive attacks on Democratic candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exclusive: Koch Group Drops Its Guard in New Attacks', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':