or': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Naples (Fla)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T19:12:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/758594a1-4a57-530c-9124-4dbbe569df26', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/758594a1-4a57-530c-9124-4dbbe569df26'}, {'abstract': 'The stories in Hilary Mantel’s new collection are designed to frighten readers and make them laugh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/books/review/the-assassination-of-margaret-thatcher-by-hilary-mantel.html', 'snippet': 'The stories in Hilary Mantel’s new collection are designed to frighten readers and make them laugh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading through Hilary Mantel’s vastly entertaining new collection of stories, I had an experience that, given my day job (literature professor) and age (implacably advancing), hasn’t happened in a while: I ran into an English word I had never seen before. Simple looking, a mere four letters, the word in question appears in “Comma,” the book’s spare and horrifying second tale. Two little girls have clambered over a wall in order to spy on the residents of a mansion known simply as the Hathaways’ house. Mary, a budding juvenile delinquent and the older and bossier of the pair, has told her companion, the 8-year-old narrator, Kitty, that something frightful and mysterious dwells in the house: a pale lumpen creature “wrapped in a blanket,” “something you couldn’t put a name to.” It might be human (“It’s got arms”), but all Mary can say for sure is that it’s awful and shaped like a “comma.” While they hide in the bushes, breathlessly hoping for some glimpse of the creature — it’s a parched midsummer day — Kitty notices “that in the beds of this garden the roses were already scorched into heavy brown blebs on the stalk.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05castle/05castle-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05castle/05castle-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05castle/05castle-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05castle/05castle-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1944, 'width': 1952, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05castle/05castle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05castle/05castle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05castle/05castle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Within Her Sights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Within Her Sights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Assassination of Margaret Thatcher (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantel, Hilary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T19:12:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8510cf50-9773-57d8-9152-0b1dd2672bb5', 'word_count': 2358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8510cf50-9773-57d8-9152-0b1dd2672bb5'}, {'abstract': 'Derek Boogaard gave everything he had to a sport that ultimately destroyed his life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/books/review/john-branchs-boy-on-ice.html', 'snippet': 'Derek Boogaard gave everything he had to a sport that ultimately destroyed his life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As genres go, the sports biography plays by established rules. More often than not the young hero, toiling in obscurity, is suddenly recognized for his or her formidable talents. So begins the stirring journey to fame. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05almond/05almond-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1568, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/books/review/05almond/05almond-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1568}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10