missions from burning of coal and other fossil fuels for energy production.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Carbon Capture Plant Opens in Canada', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plant to Capture Carbon Opens in Western Canada', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Capture and Sequestration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saskatchewan (Canada)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T20:12:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/92446f6f-3b9a-59d3-b703-aa1c88480994', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92446f6f-3b9a-59d3-b703-aa1c88480994'}, {'abstract': 'Although Ebola is new to the United States, the goal of contact tracing is the same in any disease: Track down those who could have been exposed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/us/tracing-ebola-contacts-can-stop-virus-in-its-tracks-experts-say.html', 'snippet': 'Although Ebola is new to the United States, the goal of contact tracing is the same in any disease: Track down those who could have been exposed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ebola’s arrival in Texas has set off waves of concern across the country, but desp