': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T20:43:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c77e7bf-6168-57b2-bac8-ac0c7e0964d7', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c77e7bf-6168-57b2-bac8-ac0c7e0964d7'}, {'abstract': 'A mindless spirit of mild, polysexual eroticism prevails in these photographs of nude men and women in their 20s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/arts/design/ryan-mcginley-yearbook.html', 'snippet': 'A mindless spirit of mild, polysexual eroticism prevails in these photographs of nude men and women in their 20s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nudity in public imagery is a knotty topic. These days, it’s commonplace in mainstream movies and on cable TV. But when female celebrities’ private naked pictures are publicly exposed, it’s a scandal. On the other hand, for many young people, displaying themselves naked for cameras seems to be an anti-puritanical expression of freedom from socialized shame.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4/MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4/MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4/MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4/MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4/MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4/MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4/MCGINLEY-GALLERIES-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan McGinley: ‘Yearbook’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ryan McGinley: ‘Yearbook’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGinley, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T20:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf9a9165-310b-583c-9262-4f65da8ede7d', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf9a9165-310b-583c-9262-4f65da8ede7d'}, {'abstract': 'Revisiting the open-letter gang.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/knaves-fools-and-quantitative-easing/', 'snippet': 'Revisiting the open-letter gang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the going gets tough, the people losing the argument start whining about civility. I often find myself attacked as someone who believes that anyone with a different opinion is a fool or a knave; as I’ve tried to explain, however, that’s mainly selection bias. I don’t spend much time on areas where reasonable people can disagree, because there are so many important issues where one side really is completely unreasonable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knaves, Fools, and Quantitative Easing', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T20:51:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/548ed179-3140-542e-b73c-5890f150e49c', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/548ed179-3140-542e-b73c-5890f150e49c'}, {'abstract': 'The man was killed when several artillery shells hit the offices of the Red Cross in Donetsk, in eastern Ukraine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/world/europe/swiss-employee-of-red-cross-killed-in-ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'The man was killed when several artillery shells hit the offices of the Red Cross in Donetsk, in eastern Ukraine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONETSK, Ukraine — A Swiss employee of the International Committee of the Red Cross was killed Thursday evening when several artillery shells hit the organization’s offices in Done