nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f37c522-ebfe-5820-b219-a53cc651d11e', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f37c522-ebfe-5820-b219-a53cc651d11e'}, {'abstract': 'Revisiting the legacy of Sir Victor Sassoon, who decades ago transformed the skyline of the Chinese city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/travel/the-man-who-changed-the-face-of-shanghai-.html', 'snippet': 'Revisiting the legacy of Sir Victor Sassoon, who decades ago transformed the skyline of the Chinese city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the table before me, a martini glass of chilled gin, Cointreau and vermouth, spiked with a shot of crème de menthe, seemed to glow green from within. Raising slender arms, a chanteuse in a qipao — scarlet, tightfitting and sleeveless — stilled a babble of Mandarin, German and Japanese voices as she trilled the first tones of  "Ye Shang Hai,”  an aching anthem to the legendary night life of the China coast.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/travel/05-shanghai-top/05-shanghai-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/travel/05-shanghai-top/05-shanghai-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/travel/05-shanghai-top/05-shanghai-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/travel/05-shanghai-top/05-shanghai-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1836, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 