 offering a course about the winemaking process as one of its children’s programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wine-themed vacations aren’t usually suited for kids, but Viña Vik, a winery and spa in Millahue, Chile, is changing that with its new children’s programming.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/travel/02winery/02winery-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/02/travel/02winery/02winery-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/travel/02winery/02winery-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/travel/02winery/02winery-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/travel/02winery/02winery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/02/travel/02winery/02winery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/02/travel/02winery/02winery-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Younger Travelers, Lessons in Winemaking', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "If You're Under 21: Winemaking for the Younger Set", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T21:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01d665a6-7bbc-5c74-a962-6468d7c7291c', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01d665a6-7bbc-5c74-a962-6468d7c7291c'}, {'abstract': '“Edgewise” is an oral history commemorating the life of the influential critic, actress and art-world luminary, who collaborated with the likes of John Waters and Nan Goldin.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/cookie-mueller-photos-edgewise-downtown-icon/', 'snippet': '“Edgewise” is an oral history commemorating the life of the influential critic, actress and art-world luminary, who collaborated with the likes of John Waters and Nan Goldin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It might seem unlikely that a woman introduced to the world in the second-most shocking scene in a movie full of them — John Waters’s revolutionary classic “Pink Flamingos,” in which she shares an intimate moment with a beau and a live chicken — would go on to become one of the most influential if unheralded figures in late 20th-century American culture. But Cookie\xa0Mueller\xa0— the late actress, writer, musician and model who died of AIDS in 1989 — was both a fixture of the downtown avant-garde and one of its most perceptive critics. Now, her legacy is being celebrated in “Edgewise,” a new oral history (out from Bbooks Verlag, $25) told in the words of Mueller’s friends, lovers, family and fans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Book Celebrates the Downtown Icon Cookie Mueller', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T21:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Dorris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69e294f5-4264-5f4c-b0dd-832641a4d0b5', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69e294f5-4264-5f4c-b0dd-832641a4d0b5'}, {'abstract': 'In “Drive Hard,” a former racecar driver becomes the wheelman in a bank robbery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/movies/drive-hard-stars-john-cusack-as-a-thief.html', 'snippet': 'In “Drive Hard,” a former racecar driver becomes the wheelman in a bank robbery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DRIVE HARD', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03DRIVE/03DRIVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03DRIVE/03DRIVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03DRIVE/03DRIVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03DRIVE/03DRIVE-superJumbo.jpg'