-1ccb-561a-9094-c19389696d9b'}, {'abstract': 'Frank Gehry’s modified design for the Eisenhower Memorial in Washington won preliminary approval Thursday from the National Capital Planning Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/design-for-eisenhower-memorial-wins-preliminary-approval-from-washington-panel/', 'snippet': 'Frank Gehry’s modified design for the Eisenhower Memorial in Washington won preliminary approval Thursday from the National Capital Planning Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Gehry’s revised design for a memorial to Dwight D. Eisenhower on the Washington Mall was given preliminary approval in a 10-1 vote on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Design for Eisenhower Memorial Wins Preliminary Approval from Washington Panel', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenhower, Dwight David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gehry, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commission of Fine Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eisenhower, Dwight D, Memorial Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Capital Planning Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T21:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fe49714-ddfb-5245-9d8d-35c8cfeea434', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fe49714-ddfb-5245-9d8d-35c8cfeea434'}, {'abstract': 'This show at the David Zwirner gallery goes into great detail about PeaRoeFoam, a material Mr. Rhoades created in 2002.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/arts/design/jason-rhoades-pearoefoam.html', 'snippet': 'This show at the David Zwirner gallery goes into great detail about PeaRoeFoam, a material Mr. Rhoades created in 2002.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might think of PeaRoeFoam, an unlikely concoction of green peas, salmon eggs and white polystyrene beads, as the glue holding together the messy, anarchic oeuvre of Jason Rhoades (1965-2006). Known for sprawling installations that give simple assembly-line processes a kind of byzantine intrigue, Rhoades came up with this strange product in 2002 and marketed it in a series of exhibitions that year (one of which was at the David Zwirner gallery in SoHo). Now reinstated at Zwirner in Chelsea, in the midst of a touring international retrospective, the PeaRoeFoam project lends some clarity to the whole Rhoadesian enterprise while affirming his roles of impresario and inventor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jason Rhoades: ‘PeaRoeFoam’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jason Rhoades: ‘PeaRoeFoam’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhoades, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T21:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/97f70dcf-f12c-5047-b6fd-d84a04b07681', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97f70dcf-f12c-5047-b6fd-d84a04b07681'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic presented more works by the Danish composer Carl Nielsen on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/arts/new-york-philharmonic-plays-carl-nielsen.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic presented more works by the Danish composer Carl Nielsen on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Alan Gilbert began championing the Danish composer Carl Nielsen (1865-1931), his 150th birthday next year would have probably passed unnoticed amid the blitz of anniversaries celebrated each year by ensembles in New York. But his symphonic music (last heard regularly here under the baton of Leonard Bernstein) has been receiving welcome airings recently as part of the New York Philharmonic’s multiyear project to record and perform Nielsen’s six symphonies and three concertos. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 's