RK, N.J. — With the Jets mired in a three-game losing streak, Woody Johnson, the team’s owner, said Thursday that Coach Rex Ryan and his players had “fallen short” so far this season, but he pledged his faith in the embattled quarterback Geno Smith.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets Owner Woody Johnson Still in Geno Smith’s Corner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Jet's Owner Gives Backing", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Woody', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-02T21:44:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0957f775-8afa-5d36-a160-571bfad658d0', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0957f775-8afa-5d36-a160-571bfad658d0'}, {'abstract': '“Thomas Hart Benton’s ‘America Today’ Mural Rediscovered” offers a raucous, wide-angle look at America as it entered the Depression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/arts/thomas-hart-bentons-america-today-mural-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': '“Thomas Hart Benton’s ‘America Today’ Mural Rediscovered” offers a raucous, wide-angle look at America as it entered the Depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The prickly American Regionalist Thomas Hart Benton had his share of detractors. But even they would probably acknowledge that his early mural “America Today” is the best of its kind, a raucous, cartwheeling, wide-angle look at 1920s America that set the standard for the Works Progress Administration’s mural program and has remained a New York City treasure.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03SUBJPBENTON/SUBJPBENTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03SUBJPBENTON/SUBJPBENTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 217}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03SUBJPBENTON/SUBJPBENTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03SUBJPBENTON/SUBJPBENTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03SUBJPBENTON/SUBJPBENTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03SUBJPBENTON/SUBJPBENTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03SUBJPBENTON/SUBJPBENTON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brother, Can You Spare a Wall? ', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brother, Can You Spare