athieu Amalric’s film version of Georges Simenon’s “The Blue Room” deals with adultery, crime and the relationship of sights and sounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/movies/mathieu-amalric-takes-on-the-blue-room.html', 'snippet': 'Mathieu Amalric’s film version of Georges Simenon’s “The Blue Room” deals with adultery, crime and the relationship of sights and sounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a shot at the start of “The Blue Room,” an elegant psychological freak-out about adultery and other madness, of a vacated hotel room. The calm gray-blue walls and understated furnishings paint a tranquil scene. Yet it’s here that Julien (Mathieu Amalric) and Esther (Stéphanie Cléau) have routinely broken their marriage vows in a frenzy of tangled and sweat-slicked limbs. With its covers thrown back, the large bed that dominates the room seems less empty than ravaged. It looks like a stage after the final performance. It also looks like the scene of a crime.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03BLUEROOM/03BLUEROOM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03BLUEROOM/03BLUEROOM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03BLUEROOM/03BLUEROOM-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/arts/03BLUEROOM/03BLUEROOM-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 1435, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': N