value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T00:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/3030a266-f2b1-5a99-99fc-d23da4237f43', 'word_count': 2799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3030a266-f2b1-5a99-99fc-d23da4237f43'}, {'abstract': 'Franchisees and low-wage workers in California won’t get help this time, but change in this industry is inevitable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/opinion/gov-browns-disappointing-veto.html', 'snippet': 'Franchisees and low-wage workers in California won’t get help this time, but change in this industry is inevitable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he vetoed a bill this week that would have strengthened the legal rights of franchisees in dealings with their corporate owners, Gov. Jerry Brown of California condoned an economic status quo that squeezes small businesses and low-wage workers even as corporate profits rise. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gov. Brown’s Disappointing Veto ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gov. Brown’s Disappointing Veto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Franchises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T00:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf1a004-aa6a-5797-817f-8ec8a20fd770', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf1a004-aa6a-5797-817f-8ec8a20fd770'}, {'abstract': 'The government needs to press schools and the loan servicing companies to educate students on affordable partial payment plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/opinion/what-to-do-about-student-loan-defaults.html', 'snippet': 'The government needs to press schools and the loan servicing companies to educate students on affordable partial payment plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The good news in the federal student loan default data released by the Department of Education last Wednesday is that the default rate has ticked slightly downward — to 13.7 last year from 14.7 percent in 2012 — after rising steadily through the recession. The bad news is that 650,000 borrowers who started repayment in 2011 had already defaulted by 2013. The government needs to continue pressing both schools and the loan servicing companies to educate students on affordable partial payment plans that can keep them out of default.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Do About Student Loan Defaults ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What to Do About Student Loan Defaults', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T00:59:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8913a4b6-daff-55cb-a557-8ece73dfc8e1', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8913a4b6-daff-55cb-a557-8ece73dfc8e1'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli prime minister and President Obama meet, yet again, shortly after the announcement of another housing project in East Jerusalem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/opinion/another-israeli-housing-project-threatens-a-peace-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The Israeli prime minister and President Obama meet, yet again, shortly after the announcement of another housing project in East Jerusalem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In what has become a depressingly familiar routine, Israel has given final approval for construction of 2,610 housing units in geographically sensitive parts of East Jerusalem that will make it harder, maybe impossible, to reach a two-state solution with the Palestinians.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Netanyahu’s Strange Course', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Netanyahu’s Strange Course', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T01:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb48d4a-0149-5368-a5ac-812e8325f0f4', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb48d4a-0149-5368-a5ac-812e8325f0f4'}, {'abstract': 'Some experts say the system, relying heavily on the honesty of travelers and the diligence of airport workers, could quickly be overwhelmed by rapidly spreading disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/us/ebola-patients-journey-shows-how-global-travel-is-open-to-the-spread-of-disease.html', 'snippet': 'Some experts say the system, relying heavily on the honesty of travelers and the diligence of airport workers, could quickly be overwhelmed by rapidly spreading disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROVIA, Liberia — The arrival in the United States of a Liberian man infected with the Ebola virus shows how difficult it is to control or restrict the disease from spreading, and how porous current procedures are in a world of globalized air travel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ebola Patient’s Journey Shows How Global Travel Spreads Disease', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Journey Illustrates How Global Travel Is Open to the Spread of Disease', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onishi, Norimitsu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Thomas Eric', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T01:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onishi and Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norimitsu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fab95e0-a448-51fe-a9e7-db2d528bc62d', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fab95e0-a448-51fe-a9e7-db2d528bc62d'}, {'abstract': 'The American promise to build 18 Ebola treatment centers has been stalled by, among other things, broken equipment and numerous holes on an airport runway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/us/us-effort-in-liberia-barely-gets-on-the-ground.html', 'snippet': 'The American promise to build 18 Ebola treatment centers has been stalled by, among other things, broken equipment and numerous holes on an airport runway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROVIA, Liberia — In the furious battle against time and a rampaging Ebola epidemic, the gravel crusher joined a long list of enemies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/JP-LIBERIA/JP-LIBERIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/03/us/JP-LIBERIA/JP-LIBERIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/JP-LIBERIA/JP-LIBERIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/JP-LIBERIA/JP-LIBERIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/JP-LIBERIA/JP-LIBERIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/03/us/JP-LIBERIA/JP-LIBERIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/JP-LIBERIA/JP-LIBERIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Aid Effort in Liberia Barely Off the Ground as Ebola Rages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Setbacks on Ebola: Contamination in Dallas, Slow Aid in Liberia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T01:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e54e55b9-d286-55ad-a865-a9de040bc398', 'word_count': 1367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e54e55b9-d286-55ad-a865-a9de040bc398'}, {'abstract': 'Part of the challenge of fighting the Islamic State is the difficulty of grasping the savagery of its acts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/opinion/the-fundamental-horror-of-isis.html', 'snippet': 'Part of the challenge of fighting the Islamic State is the difficulty of grasping the savagery of its acts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mind rebels at the reports of cruelty by the Islamic State, the beheadings, crucifixions, tortures, rapes and slaughter of captives, children, women, Christians, Shiites. The evidence is there on YouTube, in gruesome images and the cries of witnesses too numerous to deny or doubt. Even in a part of the world where terror has been perversely enshrined as a legitimate weapon by Islamist zealots, the Islamic State — led by Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi — stands alone in its deliberate, systematic and public savagery.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fundamental Horror of ISIS', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fundamental Horror of ISIS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T01:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f37d38b-bd69-5793-aaa7-220c13012641', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f37d38b-bd69-5793-aaa7-220c13012641'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Neugebauer’s biggest achievement was in detecting and interpreting infrared radiation emanating from outer space to provide insights about the universe that radio waves or X-rays cannot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/us/gerry-neugebauer-pioneer-in-space-studies-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Neugebauer’s biggest achievement was in detecting and interpreting infrared radiation emanating from outer space to provide insights about the universe that radio waves or X-rays cannot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gerry Neugebauer, an astrophysicist who pioneered ways to peer into previously invisible sectors of outer space, helping to discover hundreds of thousands of planets, stars and galaxies, died on Sept. 26 in Arizona. He was 82.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/03NeugebauerObit/03NeugebauerObit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 812, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/03/us/03NeugebauerObit/03NeugebauerObit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 812}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/03NeugebauerObit/03NeugebauerObit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/03NeugebauerObit/03NeugebauerObit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1802, 'width': 1331, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/03NeugebauerObit/03NeugebauerObit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name