ot', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: Officials Say They Uncovered a Terrorist Plot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maziotis, Nikos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T01:34:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/36286a9b-94fa-52ca-a642-cd5e1a874c60', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36286a9b-94fa-52ca-a642-cd5e1a874c60'}, {'abstract': 'Penn State’s decision follows a similar move by the University of Chicago, delivering a fresh setback to China’s soft-power push on American college campuses.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/02/penn-state-severs-ties-to-confucius-institute/', 'snippet': 'Penn State’s decision follows a similar move by the University of Chicago, delivering a fresh setback to China’s soft-power push on American college campuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pennsylvania State University has terminated its partnership with the Confucius Institute, the global learning network sponsored by the Chinese government, delivering a fresh setback to China’s soft-power push on American college campuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another U.S. University Severs Ties to Confucius Institute', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 