nd assistant hitting coach, Luis Natera, will not return next season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets’ hitting coach, Lamar Johnson, and assistant hitting coach, Luis Natera, will not return next season. Johnson joined the Mets only in late May, after Dan Hudgens was fired. Under him, the Mets offense did not show drastic improvement.\xa0 The Mets averaged 3.88 runs a game for the season, tied for 21st in baseball. Mike Barwis will now oversee the Mets’ strength and conditioning program, essentially replacing Jim Malone. Barwis has been a consultant for the Mets since 2011. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Drop Hitting Coaches', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Drop Hitting Coaches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lamar (1950- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Natera, Luis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T03:38:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/672655f2-8829-5f9f-b048-06cc884a80f3', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/672655f2-8829-5f9f-b048-06cc884a80f3'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 493 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/word-of-the-day-trajectory/', 'snippet': 'This