is playing three special concerts of music mostly by American composers at the Shubert Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perched atop the podium at Yale’s Woolsey Hall, William Boughton cuts an imposing figure. Long of limb and long on contacts — he is a scion of a family that made its mark in music across the British Isles — Mr. Boughton, the music director and principal conductor of the New Haven Symphony Orchestra, seems every inch an Englishman and the master of his fate. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSCT1/05ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 233, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSCT1/05ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 233}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSCT1/05ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSCT1/05ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 796, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSCT1/05ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSCT1/05ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSCT1/05ARTSCT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'su