reated over 100 canvases. But the exhibition moves on quickly from that. More important, rather than showing Motherwell (1915-1991) as a younger member of the New York School, a term he coined, the show of approximately 25 works brings together his fusion of gestural abstraction and color field painting, while also including some of his collages and published examples of his work as an editor.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2/05ARTSLI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2/05ARTSLI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 845}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2/05ARTSLI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 728, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2/05ARTSLI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1455, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2/05ARTSLI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2/05ARTSLI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2/05ARTSLI2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'