dio/2014/10/03/books/review/05books_pod-blog.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Walter Isaacson and John Branch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Walter Isaacson and John Branch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside The New York Times Book Review: ‘The Innovators’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T15:55:30+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/f0fbb002-2865-5e8f-aa14-9923fd9abb8d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/f0fbb002-2865-5e8f-aa14-9923fd9abb8d'}, {'abstract': 'Composed by Christopher Cerrone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2014/10/05/nyregion/invisible.html', 'snippet': 'Composed by Christopher Cerrone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Composed by Christopher Cerrone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpt From “Invisible Cities”', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T15:56:43+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/07da89d9-6154-5b94-8bad-aef67466bac0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/07da89d9-6154-5b94-8bad-aef67466bac0'}, {'abstract': 'Before my son started school, I shared my parents’ hippie view of the P.T.A. as a perfect-parent filled hassle and just another part of The Establishment trying to squelch creativity out of learning.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/not-a-pta-mom/', 'snippet': 'Before my son started school, I shared my parents’ hippie view of the P.T.A. as a perfect-parent filled hassle and just another part of The Establishment trying to squelch creativity out of learning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I used to make terrible judgments about what it meant to be a “PTA mom,” which stood for “Perfect Type A.” I envisioned a carefully coifed, cupcake-baking beast of a woman whose pastel capris never bore so much as a smudge of child-effluence, all with a polished smile. These PTA moms of my imagination not only prepared five-course bento boxes full of nutritionally balanced meals, they also pulled off school functions like Martha Stewart on steroids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/motherlode-pta/motherlode-pta-jumbo.png', 'height': 525, 'width': 394, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/motherlode-pta/motherlode-pta-superJumbo.png', 'height': 525, 'width': 394, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/motherlode-pta/motherlode-pta-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/03/us/motherlode-pta/motherlode-pta-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/motherlode-pta/motherlode-pta-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not a ‘PTA Mom’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parent-Teacher Associations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T15:57:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Rosenfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a990625d-7c2e-5c8e-b327-ae28cb170699', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a990625d-7c2e-5c8e-b327-ae28cb170699'}, {'abstract': 'An orchestral performance for the lead-up to New York Comic Con will include contemporary classical works alongside music from film, television and video games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/nyregion/at-comic-con-a-fanfare-for-the-fanboys.html', 'snippet': 'An orchestral performance for the lead-up to New York Comic Con will include contemporary classical works alongside music from film, television and video games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The orchestra will be dressed in steampunk finery, and the audience is likely to include Spider-Man, Galactic Empire storm troopers and various Middle Earth types. They will take their seats in the 92nd Street Y’s Kaufmann Concert Hall on Monday night for a concert of contemporary orchestral music.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05JPCONCERT1/05jpCONCERT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/nyregion/05JPCONCERT1/05jpCONCERT1-a