f07-c8ac21726b98', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dc3f858-2ae0-59b2-9f07-c8ac21726b98'}, {'abstract': 'The latest unemployment reading points to a healthy economic expansion, and yet wage growth remains subdued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/upshot/jobs-report-highlights-the-wage-growth-puzzle.html', 'snippet': 'The latest unemployment reading points to a healthy economic expansion, and yet wage growth remains subdued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest round of labor market data released Friday add to an emerging puzzle whose resolution will be central to the future of the recovery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs Report Highlights the Wage Growth Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Recovery in Need of Recovery', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T16:09:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Wolfers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56e69d3a-4c3d-5e75-ab9c-188cffcad980', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56e69d3a-4c3d-5e75-ab9c-188cffcad980'}, {'abstract': 'After nearly two years at CNN, Jeff Zucker is trying to raise ratings, partly by emphasizing just a few stories a day, rather than delivering an all-encompassing report of the headlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/business/media/at-crossroads-cnn-seeks-to-reassert-itself.html', 'snippet': 'After nearly two years at CNN, Jeff Zucker is trying to raise ratings, partly by emphasizing just a few stories a day, rather than delivering an all-encompassing report of the headlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Zucker, the president of CNN Worldwide, seemed to be having a blast Wednesday evening at a party for a new original series. Perched on the arm of a chair, he watched intently as a magician performed tricks with coins, cards and a Rubik’s cube.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/business/media/04cnn-pic1/04cnn-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/04/business/media/04cnn-pic1/04cnn-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/business/media/04cnn-pic1/04cnn-pic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/business/media/04cnn-pic1/04cnn-pic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/business/media/04cnn-pic1/04cnn-pic1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/04/business/media/04cnn-pic1/04cnn-pic1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/business/media/04cnn-pic1/04cnn-pic1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Jeff Zucker Is Seeking to Reshape CNN', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressure to Burnish a Big Brand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zucker, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T16:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Steel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ac15fd-ae28-546e-87e3-682b95281f2c', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ac15fd-ae28-546e-87e3-682b95281f2c'}, {'abstract': 'The Bukharian kosher restaurant with a vast array of kebabs has a birthday ritual, including pulsing green strobes, that transforms the dining room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/nyregion/the-30-second-silk-road-disco-party-at-salute.html', 'snippet': 'The Bukharian kosher restaurant with a vast array of kebabs has a birthday ritual, including pulsing green strobes, that transforms the dining room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All along a stretch of 108th Street in Forest Hills, Queens, the savory perfume of grilled meat, fried dumplings and cumin-spiced rice hangs heavy in the air. This is Bukharian Broadway, a strip dotted with kosher restaurants that serve the tens of thousands of Central Asian Jews who live nearby. The dishes offered inside are a richly layered amalgam of the community’s ancient Persian roots mixed with cuisines from along the Silk Road — Tajikistan, Uzbekistan, Afghanistan, Tibet and India, among other places.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 30-Second Silk Road Disco Party at Salute', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 30-Second Silk Road Disco Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koenig, Leah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Forest Hills (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Salute (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T16:19:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Koenig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koenig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5601ab5d-ddc1-57fe-8330-f8db14104c75', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5601ab5d-ddc1-57fe-8330-f8db14104c75'}, {'abstract': 'The Brown sisters have been photographed every year since 1975. The latest image in the series is published here for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/magazine/40-portraits-in-40-years.html', 'snippet': 'The Brown sisters have been photographed every year since 1975. The latest image in the series is published here for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicholas Nixon was visiting his wife’s family when, “on a whim,” he said, he asked her and her three sisters if he could take their picture. It was summer 1975, and a black-and-white photograph of four young women — elbows casually attenuated, in summer shirts and pants, standing pale and luminous against a velvety background of trees and lawn — was the result. A year later, at the graduation of one of the sisters, while readying a shot of them, he suggested they line up in the same order. After he saw the image, he asked them if they might do it every year. “They seemed O.K. with it,” he said; thus began a project that has spanned almost his whole career. The series, which has been shown around the world over the past four decades, will be on view at the Museum of Modern Art, coinciding with the museum’s publication of the book “The Brown Sisters: Forty Years” in November.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1621, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ/05thebrownsisters_ss-slide-ZKLJ-thumbStanda