a bereaved married couple (the forever underrated Donald Sutherland and a radiant Julie Christie) visiting Italy who keep crossing an entity who may be the spirit of their dead daughter. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE4/05GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE4/05GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE4/05GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE4/05GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1456, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE4/05GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE4/05GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/arts/05GUIDE4/05GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grief in Venice', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grief in Venice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Don't Look Now (Movie)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roeg, Nicolas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IFC Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T19:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e516c92-6c4b-54cb-8b9a-6c2e2541be7a', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e516c92-6c4b-54cb-8b9a-6c2e2541be7a'}, {'abstract': 'The first Charles and Joan Gross Family Foundation prize is won by the choreographer Aszure Barton and the composers Lev Zhurbin and Curtis MacDonald.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/choreographer-and-composers-win-new-dance-prize/', 'snippet': 'The first Charles and Joan Gross Family Foundation prize is won by the choreographer Aszure Barton and the composers Lev Zhurbin and Curtis MacDonald.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer Aszure Barton and the composers Lev Zhurbin and Curtis MacDonald have won the first Charles and Joan Gross Family Foundation Prize for their collaboration “Awáa,” the foundation announced Friday. The award will be given biennially to choreographers and composers for the best new dance with original music to have its premiere during a two-year judging period. The composers and choreographers each receive $15,000.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Choreographer and Composers Win New Dance Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barton, Aszure', 'r