r and lyrist Antonis Xylouris. When the Australian drummer Jim White was a teenager, he was playing in a Melbourne noise band called the People With Chairs Up Their Noses.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/music/04xylouris-SUB/04xylouris-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 235, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/music/04xylouris-SUB/04xylouris-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 235}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/music/04xylouris-SUB/04xylouris-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/music/04xylouris-SUB/04xylouris-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 1226, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/music/04xylouris-SUB/04xylouris-SUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/music/04xylouris-SUB/04xylouris-SUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/music/04xylouris-SUB/04xylouris-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Both Born to the Form, a Couple of Continents and Major Traditions Apart ', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Both Born to the Form, a Couple of Continents and Major Traditions Apart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xylouris, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Jim (1962- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union Pool (Brooklyn, NY, Music Venue)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xylouris White (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T21:37:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa12042f-5958-5261-9319-cb26a705fbbd', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa12042f-5958-5261-9319-cb26a705fbbd'}, {'abstract': 'In the latest installment of the “What Made Me” video series by Poppy de Villeneuve, the celebrated chef remembers her childhood desire to chase down criminals and the trip that taught her to respect the countryside.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/03/april-bloomfield-chef-profile-video/', 'snippet': 'In the latest installment of the “What Made Me” video series by Poppy de Villeneuve, the celebrated chef remembers her childhood desire to chase down criminals and the trip that taught her to respect the countryside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the chef April Bloomfield — of the Spotted Pig, the Breslin, the John Dory Oyster Bar, Salvation Taco and Tosca, as well as the author of the memoir “A Girl and Her Pig” — culinary school happened to be plan B. In the latest installment of T’s “What Made Me” video series by Poppy de Villeneuve, Bloomfield remembers her childhood desire to chase down criminals and the trip that taught her to respect the countryside, an appreciation that still informs her work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'April Bloomfield on Wanting to Be a Cop and Cooking Her Way to the Top', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomfield, April', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Salvation Taco (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotted Pig (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T21:40:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Poppy de Villeneuve', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Poppy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Villeneuve', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b10ba987-cf23-51fd-b90e-056b702a4fa7', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b10ba987-cf23-51fd-b90e-056b702a4fa7'}, {'abstract': 'Leading up to her centennial homage to Edgard Varèse, the flutist Claire Chase unveiled the second installment of her annual program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/arts/music/claire-chase-performs-part-ii-of-density-2036.html', 'snippet': 'Leading up to her centennial homage to Edgard Varèse, the flutist Claire Chase unveiled the second installment of her annual program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Get your tickets now: In 2036, the flutist Claire Chase will give a 24-hour marathon performance of all the works she will, by then, have commissioned as part of “Density 2036.” This eye-poppingly ambitious centennial homage to Edgard Varèse’s pathbreaking 1936 flute solo, “Density 21.5,” will in the meantime result each year in an hourlong concert of new pieces for Ms. Chase’s instrument. It’s the gift that keeps on giving.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/chase/chase-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/chase/chase-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/chase/chase-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/chase/chase-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/chase/chase-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/chase/chase-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/04/arts/chase/chase-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Building Momentum Toward a Centennial', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building Momentum Toward a Centennial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varese, Edgard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kitchen, The (Manhattan, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chase, Claire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T21:41:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/efd3db60-f9e2-5d3e-b88a-74940f339838', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efd3db60-f9e2-5d3e-b88a-74940f339838'}, {'abstract': 'With tens of thousands attending the festival, in the eastern state of Bihar, federal officials questioned whether the local government had taken adequate safety steps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/world/asia/at-least-30-killed-in-stampede-at-religious-festival-in-india.html', 'snippet': 'With tens of thousands attending the festival, in the eastern state of Bihar, federal officials questioned whether the local government had taken adequate safety steps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — At least 30 people were killed and 25 were injured in the eastern state of Bihar on Friday evening in a stampede during a celebration of the Hindu festival of Dashahara, officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Least 30 Killed in Stampede at Religious Festival in India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Deadly Stampede Mars Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Hari', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stampedes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bihar (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-03T21:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b5f14fa-aa80-5b91-bfc5-7162a3fa694e', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b5f14fa-aa80-5b91-bfc5-7162a3fa694e'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet presented the premiere of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Pictures at an Exhibition,” a whirl of changing idioms set to Mussorgsky’s score.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/arts/dance/city-ballet-presents-pictures-at-an-exhibition.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet presented the premiere of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Pictures at an Exhibition,” a whirl of changing idioms set to Mussorgsky’s score.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The knockout central ingredient of Alexei Ratmansky’s fresh, complex, many-chambered new ballet, “Pictures at an Exhibition,” is its Mussorgsky score as played onstage. In this 1874 score, the Russian composer gave himself the challenge of asking music to depict paintings; the result is intensely theatrical. New York City Ballet performed the world premiere of Mr. Ratmansky’s “Pictures” on Thursday at the David H. Koch Theater, and Cameron Grant, company pianist, rose superbly to the challenge. The music — and his playing — propelled, underpinned and gave atmosphere to the ballet.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'