inal': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd58367e-edc3-5603-839f-f4273f6dcb84', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd58367e-edc3-5603-839f-f4273f6dcb84'}, {'abstract': 'A meeting convened by Pope Francis will begin a process on whether the Roman Catholic Church will change its approach to issues like divorce, gay civil unions or single parents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/world/europe/under-francis-catholic-leaders-prepare-to-debate-whether-church-should-change.html', 'snippet': 'A meeting convened by Pope Francis will begin a process on whether the Roman Catholic Church will change its approach to issues like divorce, gay civil unions or single parents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — From the outset of his papacy, Pope Francis has encouraged a robust and open debate over the contentious social issues that have long sundered the Roman Catholic Church. Now, with a critical meeting on the theme of family about to begin at the Vatican, he is seemingly getting what he wanted: a charged atmosphere with cardinals jousting over how and whether the church should change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Francis, Catholic Leaders Prepare to Debate Whether Church Should Change', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under Francis, Catholic Leaders Prepare to Debate Whether Church Should Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Mar