give-ukraine-a-chance-sanctions-on-russia-must-continue.html', 'snippet': 'The United States and the European Union need to support Kiev unwaveringly and maintain demands on Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany knows a bit about dealing with Russia. She has spoken with Russia’s president, Vladimir Putin, more often than any other Western leader, and, more to the point, she grew up under Moscow’s yoke in East Germany. So when she says that it’s far too early to lift the sanctions imposed on Russia, Western capitals should listen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping the Pressure on Mr. Putin', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping the Pressure on Mr. Putin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crimea (Ukraine)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poroshenko, Petro Olekseyevich', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-04T01:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c51d677-10ce-5492-988d-580a43613a47', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c51d677-10ce-5492-988d-580a43613a47'}, {'abstract': 'The M.T.A. has a lot of needs but not enough money to fill them. Finding the funds will require new thinking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/opinion/minding-the-transit-gap.html', 'snippet': 'The M.T.A. has a lot of needs but not enough money to fill them. Finding the funds will require new thinking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Prendergast, chairman of the Metropolitan Transportation Authority, last week described his vast network of subways, buses and commuter trains as the “engine” for a regional economy that accounts for 11 percent of the nation’s gross domestic product. Without the M.T.A., he wrote, “New York as we know it could not function.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Minding the Transit Gap ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Minding the Transit Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prendergast, Thomas V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-04T01:18:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce6f9060-f785-56a3-8761-0d9b40416b6f', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce6f9060-f785-56a3-8761-0d9b40416b6f'}, {'abstract': 'The City Council speaker plans to introduce two bills that would help to improve a broken and unjust system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/opinion/new-yorks-sensible-immigration-shift.html', 'snippet': 'The City Council speaker plans to introduce two bills that would help to improve a broken and unjust system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City Council is about to take a welcome step toward more sensible and constitutional immigration policies. Its speaker, Melissa Mark-Viverito, plans to introduce two bills next week to limit the city’s cooperation with federal authorities in jailing immigrants and to remove federal immigration agents from Rikers Island. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Sensible Immigration Shift', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Sensible Immigration Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mark-Viverito, Melissa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-04T01:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e19b5bf9-70f9-5c