imes.com/2014/10/05/world/asia/hong-kong-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Tens of thousands gathered outside the government headquarters after the territory’s leader said “all actions necessary” would be taken to allow government workers to return to work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Pro-democracy protesters in Hong Kong held one of the largest rallies of their campaign Saturday evening, a gesture of defiance following attacks on their encampments and a declaration by the territory’s leader that major roads they have occupied for the last week must be cleared by Monday morning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Leader’s Warning Renews Protesters’ Zeal as Crowds Swell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hong Kong Leader’s Warning Renews Protesters’ Zeal as Crowds Swell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leung Chun-ying', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-04T08:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy and Alan Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ebcc73d-a4ae-57f8-95f2-97d62e33b868', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ebcc73d-a4ae-57f8-95f2-97d62e33b868'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Hatters’ supplies fall short because of the war in Europe in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/04/1914-war-may-rise-price-of-hats-in-america/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Hatters’ supplies fall short because of the war in Europe in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hat manufacturers and importers are of the opinion that prices on derbys, soft, velour and other hats will have to be advanced soon owing to the cutting off of supplies by the European war. It is agreed that hatters’ supplies of all kinds are short and that an advance in the better grades of hats is practically inevitable. The shortage includes such supplies as hatters’ furs and dyes as well as shellac for stiffening, trimmings, bands and braids. Some of the larger manufacturers have supplies on hand for possibly six months, while importers say the general stocks in this country will not last more than three months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-old-hats/30iht-old-hats-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-old-hats/30iht-old-hats-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-old-hats/30iht-old-hats-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 547, 'width': 766, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None,