-68c4-5244-b8e9-9ad2e6f8e862'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Duvalier returned to Haiti in 2011 after a 25-year exile and continued to defend what human rights workers called one of the most oppressive governments in the Western Hemisphere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/world/americas/jean-claude-duvalier-haitis-baby-doc-dies-at-63.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Duvalier returned to Haiti in 2011 after a 25-year exile and continued to defend what human rights workers called one of the most oppressive governments in the Western Hemisphere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jean-Claude Duvalier, a former president of Haiti known as Baby Doc who ruled the country with a bloody brutality and then shocked it anew with a sudden return from a 25-year exile in 2011, died on Saturday in Port-au-Prince, Haiti. He was 63.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jean-Claude Duvalier Dies at 63; Ruled Haiti in Father’s Brutal Fashion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jean-Claude Duvalier, 63, 2nd-Generation Dictator of Haiti', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duvalier, Francois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duvalier, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-04T16:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://articl