ths were cleared for government workers to reach their offices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Pro-democracy demonstrators, defiant but their numbers diminished, eased their blockade of Hong Kong government offices and allowed civil servants to return to work\xa0Monday\xa0morning after the authorities set a deadline for the police to restore access to the buildings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/world/HONGKONG/HONGKONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/06/world/HONGKONG/HONGKONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/world/HONGKONG/HONGKONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/world/HONGKONG/HONGKONG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/world/HONGKONG/HONGKONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/06/world/HONGKONG/HONGKONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/world/HONGKONG/HONGKONG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters in Hong Kong Ease Sit-In Near Government Headquarters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters in Hong Kong Ease Sit-In Near Government Headquarters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leung Chun-ying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-05T08:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher and Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95ca92b8-5023-58d0-aa61-4eb0cce26004', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95ca92b8-5023-58d0-aa61-4eb0cce26004'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Reconnaissance flights were witnessed over Turkey in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/1914-germans-piloting-turkish-aeroplanes/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Reconnaissance flights were witnessed over Turkey in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Turkish military aeroplanes, piloted, it is believed, by German officers, continue, according to reliable reports from Constantinople, to make aerial reconnaissances over the Dardanelles and the Gallipoli peninsula. Forty-two submerged mines have been placed in the Straits by the Turks, completely preventing navigation for vessels not accompanied by official pilots. It is announced here, however, that the Khedivial steamship from Black Sea ports will arrive at The Piroeus to-day [Oct. 3], the Turkish authorities having allowed this vessel to pass the Dardanelles. All the foreign post offices in Constantinople and throughout the Ottoman Empire were closed by order yesterday.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Oct. 5, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Germans Piloting Turkish Aeroplanes', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Aircraft', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-05T09:38:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a22bb4d7-7a03-5b5b-98e5-f3666a501eae', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a22bb4d7-7a03-5b5b-98e5-f3666a501eae'}, {'abstract': 'A New York Times reporter carries a gas mask and goggles, among other items, in a backpack each day to cover the pro-democracy demonstrations in Hong Kong.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/reporting-gear-to-cover-hong-kong-protests/', 'snippet': 'A New York Times reporter carries a gas mask and goggles, among other items, in a backpack each day to cover the pro-democracy demonstrations in Hong Kong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This photograph shows most of the gear I carry in a backpack each day when I go out to cover the pro-democracy demonstrations in Hong Kong that have become one of the biggest challenges to the authority of the Chinese Communist Party in years. It is a very modest gear list compared to what reporters carry in war zones such as Syria and Iraq, where I worked for three and a half years. But it’s more than what I would haul around to do interviews in Beijing, where I live. This is the first reporting assignment on which I’ve carried a gas mask and plastic goggles. Those are to protect against tear gas and pepper spray, which have been constant potential threats from the police.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/world/asia/05sino-gear/05sino-gear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/world/asia/05sino-gear/05sino-gear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/world/asia/05sino-gear/05sino-gear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/world/asia/05sino-gear/05sino-gear-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1426, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/world/asia/05sino-gear/05sino-gear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/05/world/asia/05sino-gear/05sino-gear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75