'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3342207b-dce1-564f-8d70-3a6b6a67470d', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3342207b-dce1-564f-8d70-3a6b6a67470d'}, {'abstract': 'I was certain I would be the perfect stepmother, part Mary Poppins, part Maria from “The Sound of Music,” as I helped to intertwine our families.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/stepmother-not-evil-not-perfect-not-mom/', 'snippet': 'I was certain I would be the perfect stepmother, part Mary Poppins, part Maria from “The Sound of Music,” as I helped to intertwine our families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the fact that most of my insights on stepmothers were derived from fairy tales and Disney movies (in which they are at best oblivious and at worst murderous), I accepted the job of stepparent eagerly when I reconnected romantically with a childhood friend after my first marriage ended. We were both bringing a child to the relationship — my son M was almost 2, and his daughter E was 5. I enjoyed being a mother (most of the time) and felt I had the disposition and generosity of heart to open my life to another child.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/motherlode-cinderella/motherlode-cinderella-jumbo.png', 'height': 399, 'width': 591, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/03/us/motherlode-cinderella/motherlode-cinderella-superJumbo.png', 'height': 399, 'width': 591, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '