course, zero evidence for this proposition and lots of evidence against. For later reference, I thought I’d post a couple of charts, one that won’t surprise you and one that might.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Presidents and Jobs', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-05T13:37:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4be2922-c242-501e-b28e-e6e2689fef0b', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4be2922-c242-501e-b28e-e6e2689fef0b'}, {'abstract': 'The YouGov online surveys are being used to supplement, not replace, the Times’s traditional telephone polls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/upshot/the-methodology-of-the-midterm-battleground-tracker.html', 'snippet': 'The YouGov online surveys are being used to supplement, not replace, the Times’s traditional telephone polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Data in the third wave of the New York Times/CBS News Battleground Tracker is based on online interviews with 105,277 voters conducted Sept. 20 to Oct. 1 in all 50 states and 435 congressional districts across the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Methodology of the Midterm Battleground Tracker', 'kicker': 'Midterm Calculus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouGov', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-05T14:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a03710cd-3561-5693-8f96-be5766cf15d2', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a03710cd-3561-5693-8f96-be5766cf15d2'}, {'abstract': 'But the latest YouGov panel suggests Democrats are hanging tough in Colorado and Iowa and doing a better job of mobilizing voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/upshot/republicans-maintain-edge-in-senate-races-poll-finds.html', 'snippet': 'But the latest YouGov panel suggests Democrats are hanging tough in Colorado and Iowa and doing a better job of mobilizing voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fight for control of the Senate is stable and tight, with Republicans maintaining the inside track to a majority in the latest round of data from the New York Times/CBS News/YouGov online panel of more than 100,000 respondents.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/06up-yougov-chart-1412365454221/06up-yougov-chart-1412365454221-articleLarge.png', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/06up-yougov-chart-1412365454221/06up-yougov-chart-1412365454221-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/06up-yougov-chart-1412365454221/06up-yougov-chart-1412365454221-jumbo.png', 'height': 445, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'super