ld', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54082893-e6a8-5764-b5f5-8852e49e3e65', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54082893-e6a8-5764-b5f5-8852e49e3e65'}, {'abstract': 'If you are dying, how do you want to spend your time? The answer is not always obvious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/05/opinion/sunday/the-best-possible-day.html', 'snippet': 'If you are dying, how do you want to spend your time? The answer is not always obvious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A COUPLE of years ago, I got a call from the husband of Peg Bachelder, my daughter Hunter’s piano teacher. “Peg’s in the hospital,” Martin said. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/sunday-review/1005GAWANDE/1005GAWANDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/sunday-review/1005GAWANDE/1005GAWANDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/sunday-review/1005GAWANDE/1005GAWANDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/sunday-review/1005GAWANDE/1005GAWANDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/