a18-df0d-5054-84ff-aad461bd3fe2', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/869c7a18-df0d-5054-84ff-aad461bd3fe2'}, {'abstract': 'There will be no more live racing at the Massachusetts track, which in its heyday hosted crowds of 35,000 people, cheering on legends like Seabiscuit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/us/suffolk-downs-is-put-out-to-pasture.html', 'snippet': 'There will be no more live racing at the Massachusetts track, which in its heyday hosted crowds of 35,000 people, cheering on legends like Seabiscuit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST BOSTON, Mass. — When the track here opened in 1935, it boasted the first concrete grandstand in the country, and a throng of 35,000 gleefully cheered thoroughbred racing to Puritan Massachusetts. It drew legends — like Seabiscuit, who ran here in 1937, and the Beatles, who played here in 1966 — as well as scores of horse trainers, clerks and gamblers who, over time, came to know this place, Suffolk Downs, better than an old pair of slippers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suffolk Downs Is Put Out to Pasture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suffolk Downs Is Put Out to Pasture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Suffolk Downs (Boston, Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T02:03:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qual