d dousing Glass, too. Moments later, Manager Ned Yost wrapped Glass in a bear hug and held him close.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/sports/SUBROYALS/SUBROYALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 838, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/06/sports/SUBROYALS/SUBROYALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 838}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/sports/SUBROYALS/SUBROYALS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/sports/SUBROYALS/SUBROYALS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1466, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/sports/SUBROYALS/SUBROYALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/06/sports/SUBROYALS/SUBROYALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/sports/SUBROYALS/SUBROYALS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Royals Skip Extra Innings for a Change and Sweep the Angels Away', 'kicker': 'Royals 8, Angels 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Royals Skip Extra Innings for a Change and Sweep the Angels Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yost, Ned', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trout, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scioscia, Mike', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hosmer, Eric', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shields, James', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Royals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T04:06:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee259d61-4ecd-50dc-981c-44515bcebb15', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee259d61-4ecd-50dc-981c-44515bcebb15'}, {'abstract': 'Using $50 million from the Einhorn Family Charitable Trust, the college will require all students to take at least one course with a community component during their undergraduate careers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/nyregion/cornell-plans-to-expand-off-campus-engagement.html', 'snippet': 'Using $50 million from the Einhorn Family Charitable Trust, the college will require all students to take at least one course with a community component during their undergraduate careers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not just conducting laboratory experiments about water filtration, but building water filtration systems and installing them in towns that cannot afford to buy them. Not just studying South American musical traditions, but going to a village in Peru to hear them first hand, armed with a slew of instruments on which to train local children. Not just reading about workplace diversity, but going to India to assist with an employment program for people with disabilities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cornell Plans to Expand Off-Campus Engagement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cornell Plans to Expand Off-Campus Engagement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaminer, Ariel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Einhorn Family Charitable Trust', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T04:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16c69708-5bcc-5668-96e7-4727cb0d8067', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16c69708-5bcc-5668-96e7-4727cb0d8067'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/arts/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (13) THE ACT OF KILLING (2013) Using re-enactments created with the help of Anwar Congo and Herman Koto, gangsters involved in the brutal campaign nearly 50 years ago against Communists, ethnic Chinese and critics of the military government that overthrew President Sukarno of Indonesia, the filmmaker Joshua Oppenheimer recounts massacres that began in 1965 and claimed as many as 2.5 million lives over the next year. “The garish absurdity of some of their performances — there is a musical number in front of a waterfall and another in which dancers parade from the mouth of a giant fish — does not distract from the horror,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about this Oscar-nominated documentary, presented here by “POV.” “On the contrary, the way that Anwar and Herman use the fantasy language of genre movies as a tool of stylized, half-earnest confession is what grounds this film’s moral inquiry.” He added: “Some queasiness may linger at the thought of a Western filmmaker indulging the creative whims of mass murderers, exploiting both their guilelessness and the suffering of Indonesians who remain voiceless and invisible here. But this discomfort is an important indicator of just how complicated, how perverse, the cinematic pursuit of truth can be.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T04:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bd58655-2b9c-570a-9569-6591ecf6e91c', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bd58655-2b9c-570a-9569-6591ecf6e91c'}, {'abstract': 'Avila, Detroit’s catcher, sustained his fourth significant blow to the head of the season as the Tigers lost Game 3 of their American League division series against the Baltimore Orioles and were swept.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/sports/baseball/blow-to-head-of-tigers-alex-avila-is-his-fourth-of-the-season.html', 'snippet': 'Avila, Detroit’s catcher, sustained his fourth significant blow to the head of the season as the Tigers lost Game 3 of their American League division series against the Baltimore Orioles and were swept.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — A foul tip cracked off the mask of Detroit Tigers catcher Alex Avila in the sixth inning Sunday, his third blow to the head in a little more than a month and his fourth of the season. Avila fell to his right, away from the batter, Baltimore’s Steve Pearce. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/sports/06orioles1/06orioles1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/07/sports/06orioles1/06orioles1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/sports/06orioles1/06orioles1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/sports/06orioles1/06orioles1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1596, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/sports/06orioles1/06orioles1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/07/sports/06orioles1/06orioles1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':