 [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcd0271b-d32e-5bab-bfb2-527f17039a23', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcd0271b-d32e-5bab-bfb2-527f17039a23'}, {'abstract': 'While pro-establishment newspaper editorials call on Hong Kong to clamp down on the pro-democracy demonstrations, liberal papers, like Apple Daily, sympathize with the struggle.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/hong-kong-newspapers-pro-and-anti-beijing-weigh-in-on-protests/', 'snippet': 'While pro-establishment newspaper editorials call on Hong Kong to clamp down on the pro-democracy demonstrations, liberal papers, like Apple Daily, sympathize with the struggle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While many residents believe Hong Kong has in recent years fallen susceptible to Chinese censorship of the media, the city prides itself on freedom of the press, a right enshrined in Article 27 of the Basic Law, which serves as the city’s mini-constitution, and in the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/world/06sino-newspapers/06sino-newspapers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/06/world/06sino-newspapers/06sino-newspapers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/world/06sino-newspapers/06sino-newspapers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':