Becton, Dickinson & Company is buying CareFusion for about $12 billion. | Bitcoin’s price tumbles. | Questioning a window for insider sales.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/morning-agenda-hp-announces-a-split/', 'snippet': 'Hewlett-Packard plans to split into two companies. | Becton, Dickinson & Company is buying CareFusion for about $12 billion. | Bitcoin’s price tumbles. | Questioning a window for insider sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hewlett-Packard confirmed on Monday that it planned to break into two companies, Quentin Hardy and David Gelles write in The New York Times. The company, considered a foundational institution of Silicon Valley, said in a news release that it intended to divide itself into a company aimed at business technology, including computer servers and data storage equipment, software and services, and a company that sells personal computers and printers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: HP Announces a Split', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T12:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c43632d5-178e-5aa4-afa7-47fd8ecbbe02', 'word_count': 2001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c43632d5-178e-5aa4-afa7-47fd8ecbbe02'}, {'abstract': 'Spend-happy Americans will return to powering the economy, according to a Bureau of Labor Statistics forecast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/upshot/dont-sell-consumer-spending-short-a-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'Spend-happy Americans will return to powering the economy, according to a Bureau of Labor Statistics forecast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The encouraging September jobs report, which showed unemployment dipping below 6 percent, stole the limelight on Friday, but it is the quiet release of another government report that has presented economists with unexpected fodder for debate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/07up-consumer-1412555906227/07up-consumer-1412555906227-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/07up-consumer-1412555906227/07up-consumer-1412555906227-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/07up-consumer-1412555906227/07up-consumer-1412555906227-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/07up-consumer-1412555906227/07up-consumer-1412555906227-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1048, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/07up-consumer-1412555906227/07up-consumer-1412555906227-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/07up-consumer-1412555906227/07up-consumer-1412555906227-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/upshot/07up-consumer-1412555906227/07up-consumer-1412555906227-thumbLarge-v2.png