ield’s worth of land every hour. Photographer Jeff Riedel took aerial photographs of the state’s coastal region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louisiana is losing about a football field’s worth of land every hour. That’s just one striking way to sum up what’s at stake in an environmental lawsuit over the state’s disappearing wetlands, which Nathaniel Rich writes about for the Oct. 5 cover story. Another way is to get a photographer like Jeff Riedel to take aerial photographs of the state’s coastal region. One of those pictures appears on the cover. Riedel said he was shocked while up in the air. “You realize that this is actually happening,” he said. “It’s not any sort of hyperbole.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05cover_type/05cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05cover_type/05cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05cover_type/05cover_type-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05cover_type/05cover_type-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05cover_type/05cover_type-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/05/magazine/05cover_type/05cover_type-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheigh