bola “a top national security priority,” but did not specify how screening procedures would be changed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/us/ebola-patient-in-dallas-still-in-critical-condition-cdc-chief-says.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama called the fight against Ebola “a top national security priority,” but did not specify how screening procedures would be changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — As this city waited anxiously to learn whether Ebola has spread beyond one victim, President Obama announced on Monday that the government would increase screening for the virus at airports both in the United States and in West Africa.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ebola Screening at Airports Will Increase, Obama Says ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ebola Screening at Airports Will Increase, Obama Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sack, Kevin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Thomas Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Health Presbyterian Hospital', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T15:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Sack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organiz