90b-8a12-da1b44746e6c', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7a5047e-c0da-590b-8a12-da1b44746e6c'}, {'abstract': 'A big hurdle in the “spoofing” case against a high-frequency trading firm is that a jury must decide whether one computer fooling another is a crime, Peter J. Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/a-new-crime-with-a-catchy-name-spoofing/', 'snippet': 'A big hurdle in the “spoofing” case against a high-frequency trading firm is that a jury must decide whether one computer fooling another is a crime, Peter J. Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giving a crime a catchy moniker is a good way to get attention when prosecutors pursue a new form of misconduct. There is, for instance, a type of money laundering called “smurfing,” named for the cute blue cartoon characters, that involves runners for a drug organization making small cash deposits at various banks to avoid the currency transaction reporting rules. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/business/dbpix-trading/dbpix-trading-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/07/business/dbpix-trading/dbpix-trading-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/business/dbpix-trading/dbpix-trading-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/business/dbpix-trading/dbpix-trading-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/business/dbpix-trading/dbpix-trading-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/07/business/dbpix-trading/dbpix-trading-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/business/dbpix-trading/dbpix-trading-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Spoofing,’ a New Crime With a Catchy Name', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Conduct Authority (Great Britain)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Panther Energy Trading LLC', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T16:39:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aadb4fc-4523-52bc-9b2f-55cfe6046421', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aadb4fc-4523-52bc-9b2f-55cfe6046421'}, {'abstract': 'The campaign is designed to promote the city for living and working by building a sense of place into the ads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/business/media/a-new-effort-from-a-new-jersey-city-urges-make-it-yours.html', 'snippet': 'The campaign is designed to promote the city for living and working by building a sense of place into the ads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jersey City, once described as "an unfashionable town named after an unfashionable state,” has been having a moment lately, deemed "much transformed" from “a scruffy ne’er-do-well” into “a gentrifying bedroom community.” Now, to keep that momentum going, the city is teaming with the Jersey City Economic Development Corporation for a campaign meant to encourage more people to consider Jersey City as a place to live, visit and locate businesses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/business/06adnews-1-pic1/06adnews-1-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/06/business/06adnews-1-pic1/06adnews-1-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 460}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/business/06adnews-1-pic1/06adnews-1-pic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/business/06adnews-1-pic1/06adnews-1-pic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1571, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/business/06adnews-1-pic1/06adnews-1-pic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/06/business/06adnews-1-pic1/06adnews-1-pic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/business/06adnews-1-pic1/06adnews-1-pic1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Effort From a ‘New’ Jersey City Urges, ‘Make It Yours’', 'kicker': 'Campaign Spotlight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T16:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63ca685d-f56a-58cd-b0ec-1616c0071493', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63ca685d-f56a-58cd-b0ec-1616c0071493'}, {'abstract': 'The Tokyo police said Monday that they were investigating several university students suspected of planning to go to Syria to fight for the Islamic State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/world/asia/japanese-men-were-planning-to-fight-for-isis-police-say.html', 'snippet': 'The Tokyo police said Monday that they were investigating several university students suspected of planning to go to Syria to fight for the Islamic State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The Tokyo police said Monday that they were investigating several Japanese men suspected of planning to go to Syria to fight for the jihadist group Islamic State. The police provided few details of the men, whom they described as university students in their 20s who were not actively attending classes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japanese Men Were Planning to Fight for ISIS, Police Say', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T16:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/febae705-82ca-586d-93d9-75bd5c7c57bf', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/febae705-82ca-586d-93d9-75bd5c7c57bf'}, {'abstract': 'Guests who book a special package at the Hudson New York Hotel get tickets for popular events during the Food Network New York City Wine and Food Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/get-a-room-get-into-a-food-festival/', 'snippet': 'Guests who book a special package at the Hudson New York Hotel get tickets for popular events during the Food Network New York City Wine and Food Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the 110 events for the Food Network New York City Wine and Food Festival, taking place throughout the city from Oct. 16 to 19, are sold out, but guests who book the Premier package at the Hudson New York Hotel get tickets to four of the most popular options.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/travel/06foodweek/06foodweek-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/06/travel/06foodweek/06foodweek-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/travel/06foodweek/06foodweek-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/travel/06foodweek/06foodweek-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/travel/06foodweek/06foodweek-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/06/travel/06foodweek/06foodweek-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/06/travel/06foodweek/06foodweek-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Get a Room, Get Into a Food Festival', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'se