attering historical events.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/protesting-for-the-right-to-learn-about-protest/', 'snippet': 'Students in Jefferson County, Colo., worry that the school board is trying to de-emphasize unflattering historical events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When conservative reformers took over the school board in Jefferson County, Colo., last year they promised a more patriotic approach to what students learn about American history, with an emphasis on respecting authority and free enterprise and rejecting lessons that “encourage or condone civil disorder.” What the board ignited instead is an on-going lesson from students and teachers about the real-life power of protest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesting for the Right to Learn About Protest', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Board', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T17:05:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e680a3c-956e-5440-9f43-904aa00c0af9', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e680a3c-956e-5440-9f43-904aa00c0af9'}, {'abstract': 'Hilton Worldwide, the seller, will continue to operate the hotel under a 100-year management contract with Anbang Insurance Group of China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/nyregion/waldorf-astoria-hotel-to-be-sold-for-195-billion.html', 'snippet': 'Hilt