s', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Learning From Europe', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T20:06:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a24e60b-d74b-54e9-9ec7-ad8afed451ab', 'word_count': 19, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a24e60b-d74b-54e9-9ec7-ad8afed451ab'}, {'abstract': 'In some ways, Egypt’s new government has become even more repressive and intolerant than the regime that was overthrown in early 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/the-crackdown-on-gay-men-in-egypt/', 'snippet': 'In some ways, Egypt’s new government has become even more repressive and intolerant than the regime that was overthrown in early 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In some ways, Egypt’s new government has become even more repressive and intolerant than the regime that was overthrown in early 2011. One disturbing example is the incarceration of dozens of gay men, a crackdown that has vilified a community that had hoped the popular uprising in 2011 would bring minorities greater freedom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Crackdown on Gay Men in Egypt', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T20:10:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ernesto Londo&#241;o', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Londo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86f7b4c9-6343-5b79-8eb2-97b6a7d80818', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86f7b4c9-6343-5b79-8eb2-97b6a7d80818'}, {'abstract': 'The new Sugar Hill subsidized housing complex in Upper Manhattan goes beyond even the more ambitious developments by providing a school and a children’s museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/arts/sugar-hill-housing-will-have-a-school-and-a-museum.html', 'snippet': 'The new Sugar Hill subsidized housing complex in Upper Manhattan goes beyond even the more ambitious developments by providing a school and a children’s museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the price of real estate so dear, every new building in New York comes with big expectations, but this one more than most. The $84 million subsidized housing complex in Upper Manhattan called Sugar Hill Development has outsize ambitions. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/arts/SUGARHILL/SUGARHILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/07/arts/SUGARHILL/SUGARHILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/arts/SUGARHILL/SUGARHILL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/arts/SUGARHILL/SUGARHILL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1642, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup