reau, but a decades-old government ban on new names in wilderness areas may present an insurmountable obstacle to the effort.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Thoreau to Mountain Tops', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thoreau, Henry David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Nevada Region (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-06T20:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/14eb81b8-8897-5507-a089-c648b4f449a1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/14eb81b8-8897-5507-a089-c648b4f449a1'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch architect Winy Maas on his iconic (he accepts the word) food hall, where you can actually live.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/09/garden/building-a-better-hybrid-in-rotterdam.html', 'snippet': 'The Dutch architect Winy Maas on his iconic (he accepts the word) food hall, where you can actually live.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since cofounding the Dutch architecture firm MVRDV in 1993, Winy Maas, 55, has built one oddball hybrid after another: an expo building with a forest on an upper floor, a library shaped like a mountain of books. His habit of mixing functions may have reached its apex in the Markthal, a horseshoe-shaped building in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, that combines a food hall the size of a football field with 228 apartments around it.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/garden/09qna-1-copy/09