'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5082ea8-086c-5a66-beb4-f80325744991', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5082ea8-086c-5a66-beb4-f80325744991'}, {'abstract': 'A retired police officer who failed to win a seat in Brazil’s Senate seized the nation’s attention by slapping a voter at a polling site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/world/americas/senate-candidate-in-brazil-in-hiding-after-slapping-voter-on-election-day.html', 'snippet': 'A retired police officer who failed to win a seat in Brazil’s Senate seized the nation’s attention by slapping a voter at a polling site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A retired police colonel who failed to win a seat in Brazil’s Senate on Sunday still managed to seize the nation’s attention by slapping a voter in the face — in full view of witnesses and at least two cameras — when she objected to his attempt to cut the line at a polling place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Candidate in Brazil in Hiding After Slapping Voter on Election Day', 'kicker': 'Open Source', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T00:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/673e3d4b-e25f-5e4b-a3c9-3f7aae4f08c2', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/673e3d4b-e25f-5e4b-a3c9-3f7aae4f08c2'}, {'abstract': 'Abortion clinics forced to close last week by stringent new regulations in the state have filed an emergency appeal to the Supreme Court, arguing that the rules are an unconstitutional infringement of rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/us/texas-abortion-clinics-closing-is-appealed.html', 'snippet': 'Abortion clinics forced to close last week by stringent new regulations in the state have filed an emergency appeal to the Supreme Court, arguing that the rules are an unconstitutional infringement of rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abortion clinics forced to close last week by stringent new regulations in the state have filed an emergency appeal to the Supreme Court, arguing that the rules are an unconstitutional infringement of rights. The motion, argued by the Center for Reproductive Rights, says that the United States Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit erred Thursday when it said the state could require abortion clinics to meet the standards of hospital-like surgery centers. The rule serves no medical purpose and has left nearly one million women living more than 150 miles from the nearest abortion clinic, the appeal states, imposing an “undue burden” on women’s rights. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Abortion Clinics’ Closing Is Appealed ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Abortion Clinics’ Closing Is Appealed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N