itled “Strategy to Reduce Methane Emissions.” A big part of the strategy was built around cutting down on the methane emissions that result from oil and gas production, particularly the hydraulic fracturing method of extracting natural gas from the ground — a.k.a., fracking. In the white paper, the administration said that the Environmental Protection Agency would decide by the fall how best to go about it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Moment of Truth’ on Emissions', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Moment of Truth’ on Emissions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T00:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/40516ab7-f5c2-520c-9b9f-9feabfed6438', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40516ab7-f5c2-520c-9b9f-9feabfed6438'}, {'abstract': 'Teachers are scrambling to educate students without the classrooms they need and with no prospect of new ones being built anytime soon, as people move back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/us/las-vegas-schools-groan-from-growing-pains.html', 'snippet': 'Teachers are scrambling to educate students without the classrooms they need and with no prospect of new ones being built anytime soon, as people move back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Schools in this suddenly robust community are so packed these days that 13 of them stay open 12 months a year. Children go to classes and eat lunch in cramped, windowless trailers, bustling with restless students. Thousands more take online classes at home, and school district administrators, desperate for space, are looking to abandoned strip malls for classrooms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/us/JPVEGAS/JPVEGAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/07/us/JPVEGAS/JPVEGAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/us/JPVEGAS/JPVEGAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/us/JPVEGAS/JPVEGAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/us/JPVEGAS/JPVEGAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/07/us/JPVEGAS/JPVEGAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/us/JPVEGAS/JPVEGAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Las Vegas Schools Groan From Growing Pains', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Las Vegas Schools Groan From Growing Pains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T00:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07d857e0-b386-5318-8be2-620436f15ecd', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07d857e0-b386-5318-8be2-620436f15ecd'}, {'abstract': 'Activist investors are eager to take small stakes in big companies and call for breakups, betting that profit will follow.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/06/breaking-up-is-the-new-thing-to-do/', 'snippet': 'Activist investors are eager to take small stakes in big companies and call for breakups, betting that profit will follow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the aftermath of the financial crisis, investors bet on companies that seemed too big to fail. Even if a business wasn’t growing at breakneck speed, there was safety in large numbers; the more sales the better, it seemed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/business/Split2/Split2-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/07/business/Split2/Split2-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/busi