e most exhilarating news came not from anything the justices did, but from one thing they didn’t do. Without explanation and against expectations, the court declined to hear any of the seven petitions asking them to reject a constitutional right to same-sex marriage. By choosing not to review those cases, the justices made it possible for same-sex couples in a majority of states to marry. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Step Closer to Marriage Equality ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Step Closer to Marriage Equality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T00:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd570dea-c8bb-5cc7-936d-5c1d35bfba96', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd570dea-c8bb-5cc7-936d-5c1d35bfba96'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s episode included some comic book outrage, along with Gordon’s usual existential crises.', 'web_url': 'http