ilver-Greenberg write. With evidence mounting that a number of foreign and American banks colluded to set the price of foreign currencies, prosecutors are aiming to file charges against at least one bank by the end of the year, according to interviews with lawyers briefed on the matter. Several banks are expected to plead guilty to resolve the investigation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: More Trouble for Big Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T11:55:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d70099d2-c630-5558-95cc-6bbcce056946', 'word_count': 2474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d70099d2-c630-5558-95cc-6bbcce056946'}, {'abstract': 'The former lobbyist and British Conservative faced more skepticism in a rare second hearing, declining to name banks he had worked for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/business/international/jonathan-hill-nominee-to-oversee-eu-financial-sector-makes-fresh-appeal-to-lawmakers.html', 'snippet': 'The former lobbyist and British Conservative faced more skepticism in a rare second hearing, declining to name banks he had worked for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Jonathan Hill, the Briton nominated to oversee European Union financial markets, left some members of Parliament skeptical about his suitability for the job for a second time on Tuesday after declining to name the banks and financial services companies that he represented when he worked in public relations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtyp