e projects and acquisitions.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/more-paris-institutions-turn-to-crowd-funding/', 'snippet': 'The Louvre is the second major French museum to turn to Internet fund-raising this month to finance projects and acquisitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The Louvre kicked off its latest crowd-funding campaign on Tuesday with an appeal for a million euros to help fund the €12.5 million purchase of a jeweled piece of 18th-century furniture, known as the “Table of Peace,” which belonged to a French diplomat who negotiated the end of a Bavarian war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Paris Institutions Turn to Crowd-Funding', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Courbet, Gustave', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louvre Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orsay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T12:13:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ad70bf-33a9-5397-ad39-5dcc60e7bece', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ad70bf-33a9-5397-ad39-5dcc60e7bece'}, {'abstract': 'With four weeks until Election Day, the race for the Senate remains up for grabs, according to the Upshot Senate model, with the Republican Party listed as slight 61 percent favorites to take control of the chamber in November. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/07/the-upshot-g-o-p-remains-sligh