icle/4de39d27-945d-5630-bb5b-cc66354b7b50'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of National News Engagement Day, here are 50 ideas to help teachers bring current events into the classroom.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/50-ways-to-teach-current-events/', 'snippet': 'In honor of National News Engagement Day, here are 50 ideas to help teachers bring current events into the classroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How can we make sure that students are informed about what’s going on around the world? That they are armed with the tools to be able to distinguish between opinion and fact; between evidence-based statements and empty rhetoric; between sensationalism and solid journalism? Just like most other things in life, the best way to do all that is through practice. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/learning/50WaysCurrentEventsLN/50WaysCurrentEventsLN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/learning/50WaysCurrentEventsLN/50WaysCurrentEventsLN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/learning/50WaysCurrentEventsLN/50WaysCurrentEventsLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/08/learning/50WaysCurrentEventsLN/50WaysCurrentEventsLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/learning/50WaysCurrentEventsLN/50WaysCurrentEventsLN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'w