mes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.M.F. Asks Rich Nations for Support', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.M.F. Asks Rich Nations for Support', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagarde, Christine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchard, Olivier J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T13:33:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr. and Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e9ddbfe-f2d3-5ce5-81cb-2748552e6199', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e9ddbfe-f2d3-5ce5-81cb-2748552e6199'}, {'abstract': 'Nuclear nonproliferation is impossible without disarmament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/opinion/nuclear-security-nuclear-dangers.html', 'snippet': 'Nuclear nonproliferation is impossible without disarmament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Re “Backsliding on nuclear promises” (Editorial, Sept. 24): We agree with your approval of President Obama’s wish to see a world without nuclear weapons, and with your criticism of the decisions to spend tens of billions on upgrading America’s nuclear arsenal. Your ensuing focus upon nuclear security, however, reflects a common wrong turn in mainstream discourse about nuclear danger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nuclear Security, Nuclear Dangers', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMS CONTROL AND LIMITATION AND DISARMAMENT', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T13:34:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/293f198d-e501-57da-9139-c25eb7450d8d', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/293f198d-e501-57da-9139-c25eb7450d8d'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French troops paraded captured German flags in Paris in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/1914-german-flags-hung-in-invalides/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French troops paraded captured German flags in Paris in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Six flags taken from the Germans in the course of the fighting of the last few weeks were hung in the Hôtel des Invalides after an enthusiastic crowd had accompanied them from the Palais de l’Élysée. When first captured, the flags were sent to Bordeaux and were brought to Paris by President Poincaré on his visit to ‘‘the front.’’ The banners were not thrown triumphantly to the breeze, but were carried after the fashion of the colors of the vanquished, each folded and thrown across the shoulders of one of the six non-commissioned officers. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Oct. 8, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/blogs/07iht-old08-Invalides/07iht-old08-Invalides-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 472, 'width': 575, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/blogs/07iht-old08-Invalides/07iht-old08-Invalides-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 472, 'width': 575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/blogs/07iht-old08-Invalides/07iht-old08-Invalides-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/07/blogs/07iht-old08-Invalides/07iht-old08-Invalides-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/07/blogs/07iht-old08-Invalides/07iht-old08-Invalides-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: German Flags Hung in Invalides', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T13:40:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename'