/2014/10/07/sinead-oconnors-memoir-promises-deep-dish-dirt/', 'snippet': 'The Irish singer said, “I look forward to dishing the sexual dirt on everyone I’ve ever slept with” in the book, coming in March 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Irish singer Sinead O’Connor plans to follow other music stars like Keith Richards by writing her memoirs, her publisher announced today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/07artsbeat-sinead/07artsbeat-sinead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/07artsbeat-sinead/07artsbeat-sinead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/07artsbeat-sinead/07artsbeat-sinead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/07artsbeat-sinead/07artsbeat-sinead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 903, 'width': 1354, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/07artsbeat-sinead/07artsbeat-sinead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/07artsbeat-sinead/07artsbeat-sinead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/07artsbeat-sinead/07artsbeat-sinead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sinead O’Connor’s Memoir Promises Deep-Dish Dirt', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, Sinead", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T14:44:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8ce5c0b-d233-5b8a-bc83-6f24339b184d', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8ce5c0b-d233-5b8a-bc83-6f24339b184d'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Angry taxi drivers failed to blockade the center of Paris in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/07/1964-police-foil-plans-of-taxi-drivers/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Angry taxi drivers failed to blockade the center of Paris in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The taxi drivers of Paris, droll fellows at times, tried tonight [Oct. 7] to create a massive traffic jam in the center of the city but did not quite succeed. Hundreds of policemen invested the area around the Place de l’Opéra and shunted many taxis away from a planned rendezvous during the evening rush hour that was to call attention to demands for increased fares and improved working conditions. In fact, the traffic flow was better than most nights, according to a newspaper vendor on the scene. ‘‘Voilà,’’ snorted a taxi driver, ‘‘it only goes to show what the police can do if they get out and do their duty.’’  — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Oct. 8, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Police Foil Plans of Taxi Drivers', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T14:55:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1bf385b-1bd7-5882-bc34-009b27531d40', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1bf385b-1bd7-5882-bc34-009b27531d40'}, {'abstract': 'Rock the Vote launches a new get out the vote campaign, #turnoutforwhat, featuring Lil John and Lena Dunham.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/07/turn-out-for-what-exactly-says-rock-the-vote/', 'snippet': 'Rock the Vote launches a new get out the vote campaign, #turnoutforwhat, featuring Lil John and Lena Dunham.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lil John meets Lena Dunham at a voting booth, or “Lil Lena,” as she calls herself, after hanging up on Whoopi Goldberg. Just your average midterm election voting experience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turn Out for What? Exactly, Says Rock the Vote', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T14:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'by