raph': 'At the Page 1 meeting Monday afternoon, a Metro editor pitched the story of a 4-year-old boy who had died of enterovirus, a respiratory infection, for the front page of the paper. Barbara Strauch, editor of the Science desk, argued that it was not front-page news and that placing it there could create unnecessary panic. Ms. Strauch discussed the balance between being on top of a story and not causing undue alarm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arguing a Story Off the Front Page', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauch, Barbara', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T19:05:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e0dbbe4-f392-553f-9e74-55600696a4ad', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e0dbbe4-f392-553f-9e74-55600696a4ad'}, {'abstract': 'The government strategy to subsidize higher education is failing at its core task: giving less privileged Americans a real shot at a college degree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/business/economy/why-federal-aid-for-higher-education-is-missing-the-mark.html', 'snippet': 'The government strategy to subsidize higher education is failing at its core task: giving less privileged Americans a real shot at a college degree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1987, when he was Ronald Reagan’s education secretary, the conservative culture warrior William J. Bennett wrote a famous essay denouncing federal aid for higher education because it allowed colleges “blithely 