'Thomas Eric Duncan, a Liberian who is battling the virus, is also being treated with an experimental antiviral drug in a Dallas hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/us/ebola-patient-on-ventilator-and-getting-kidney-dialysis-officials-say.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Eric Duncan, a Liberian who is battling the virus, is also being treated with an experimental antiviral drug in a Dallas hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — The Liberian man battling the Ebola virus is on a ventilator and receiving kidney dialysis, health officials said Tuesday, but for the first time doctors had some positive news to report about his condition. Family members who were briefed by doctors said they were told Mr. Duncan’s temperature and blood pressure are back to normal and the debilitating diarrhea Ebola brings had slowed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/DALLAS/DALLAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/us/DALLAS/DALLAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/DALLAS/DALLAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/DALLAS/DALLAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/DALLAS/DALLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/08/us/DALLAS/DALLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/DALLAS/DALLAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Several Positive Signs Reported for Ebola Patient in a Dallas Hospital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Several Positive Signs Reported for Ebola Patient in a Dallas Hospital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Dave', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sack, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Thomas Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Jesse L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-07T21:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Philipps and Kevin Sack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Philipps', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18f85f00-4638-54a7-8ad8-2abf505d08a6', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18f85f00-4638-54a7-8ad8-2abf505d08a6'}, {'abstract': 'Pacific Northwest Ballet cements its reputation as a transmitter of Balanchine traditions in its production of “Jewels.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/arts/dance/suzanne-farrell-coaches-pacific-northwest-ballet-balanchine.html', 'snippet': 'Pacific Northwest Ballet cements its reputation as a transmitter of Balanchine traditions in its production of “Jewels.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — Pacific Northwest Ballet opens in Manhattan on Wednesday with a program of new ballets at the Joyce Theater. Last weekend, however, here in its hometown, the company could be seen at full stretch in George Balanchine’s three-part “Jewels.” I caught three performances at the Marion Oliver McCaw Hall from Friday to Sunday. The troupe’s Balanchine style is milder in dynamics than New York City Ballet’s, but the dancers fill the theater with light, radiant, musical dancing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/JEWELS/JEWELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/JEWELS/JEWELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 789}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/JEWELS/JEWELS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/JEWELS/JEWELS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1368, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/JEWELS/JEWELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/08/arts/JEWELS/JEWELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 't