 Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fredrik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Logevall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gordon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/05ccc0c7-f25a-5a93-8d1b-52abf2680190', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05ccc0c7-f25a-5a93-8d1b-52abf2680190'}, {'abstract': 'With technology for liquefying natural gas improving, so is the likelihood of the United States become an exporter rather than an importer of L.N.G. in the coming years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/one-key-to-exports-liquid-gas.html', 'snippet': 'With technology for liquefying natural gas improving, so is the likelihood of the United States become an exporter rather than an importer of L.N.G. in the coming years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New methods of producing natural gas are expected to turn the United States from an importer into a large exporter in less than a decade, assuming that the gas can be exported in sufficient quantities cheaply enough to compete on world markets.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08LIQUEFY/08LIQUEFY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08LIQUEFY/08LIQUEFY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08LIQUEFY/08LIQUEFY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo',