 for the recent major lapses from the Secret Service?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/opinion/thomas-friedman-the-secret-service-and-the-political-class.html', 'snippet': 'Who’s to blame for the recent major lapses from the Secret Service?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m sure there are many technical explanations for the recent breakdowns in Secret Service protection that allowed an armed intruder to run right through the front door of the White House and an armed felon to ride on an elevator with President Obama. But I’d also put some blame on the nation’s political class.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Running on Empty', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Running On Empty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T00:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdf36224-4570-58be-ae2c-524606e74f0a', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdf36224-4570-58be-ae2c-524606e74f0a'}, {'abstract': 'Democratic candidates — even those in states like Virginia that the president carried in 2008 and 2012 — do not want President Obama to campaign for them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/us/politics/in-this-election-obamas-party-benches-him.html', 'snippet': 'Democratic candidates — even those in states like Virginia that the president carried in 2008 and 2012 — do not want President Obama to campaign for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — When he soared to victory by almost 10 million votes in 2008, President Obama won in states like Virginia that Democratic candidates had not captured since 1964. He was trumpeted as a transformational leader who remade American politics by creating a new electoral map and a diverse voter coalition to shape the Democratic Party for the 21st century.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1233, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/08/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In This Election, Obama’s Party Benches Him', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In This Election, Obama’s Party Benches Him', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T00:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d6f87e2-fb93-5a3d-ad5f-e2f0effbad50', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d6f87e2-fb93-5a3d-ad5f-e2f0effbad50'}, {'abstract': 'As the production of energy grows, there’s a new need for energy companies to build up to 1.3 gigawatts of energy storage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/business/energy-for-a-rainy-day-or-a-windless-one.html', 'snippet': 'As the production of energy grows, there’s a new need for energy companies to build up to 1.3 gigawatts of energy storage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With new energy supplies and demand growing rapidly worldwide, companies in the United States, Europe and across the developing world are spending billions of dollars each year on new power plants, wind turbines and solar panels. Now the focus is increasingly on how to store the bonanza, so that electricity generated from the likes of renewables can be quickly pumped into a country’s energy network as demand skyrockets — say, when people return home from work.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08STORAGE1/08STORAGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 293, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08STORAGE1/08STORAGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 293}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08STORAGE1/08STORAGE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08STORAGE1/08STORAGE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 969, 'width': 1984, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08STORAGE1/08STORAGE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08STORAGE1/08STORAGE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/energy-environment/08STORAGE1/08STORAGE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy for a Rainy Day, or a Windless One', 'kicker': 'Energy Special Section', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Energy for a Rainy Day, or a Windless One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Storage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T00:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9c09505-ec8a-5360-a814-9fdf70517489', 'word_count': 1101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9c09505-ec8a-5360-a814-9fdf70517489'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Kay Hagan of North Carolina announced she had raised $4.9 million in the third quarter, but the more interesting number is what she spent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/07/more-interesting-than-what-kay-hagan-raised-what-she-spent/', 'snippet': 'Senator Kay Hagan of North Carolina announced she had raised $4.9 million in the third quarter, but the more interesting number is what she spent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senate candidates who have good news to report have begun to leak their most recent fund-raising figures, and the first Democrat in the mix is the North Carolina incumbent, Kay Hagan, who announced a $4.9 million haul for the three months ending in September. But as is often true in politics, the more interesting number is how much she spent: a princely $11.6 million, based on her reported cash on hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/politics/08firstdraft-hagan/08firstdraft-hagan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/us/politics/08firstdraft-hagan/08firstdraft-hagan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/politics/08firstdraft-hagan/08firstdraft-hagan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/politics/08firstdraft-hagan/08firstdraft-hagan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/politics/08firstdraft-hagan/08firstdraft-hagan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/08/us/politics/08firstdraft-hagan/08firstdraft-hagan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/politics/08firstdraft-hagan/08firstdraft-hagan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Interesting Than What Kay Hagan Raised? What She Spent.', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagan, Kay R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tillis, Thomas R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T00:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eb96cce-39bd-5006-a3b7-700660c77578', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eb96cce-39bd-5006-a3b7-700660c77578'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators need to make sure that smaller brewers have a shot and should not allow the beer giants to get even bigger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/opinion/monopolizing-beer.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators need to make sure that smaller brewers have a shot and should not allow the beer giants to get even bigger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The global beer industry is already dominated by a handful of large businesses, and, if corporate deal makers have their way, there will be even less competition. The industry’s second-biggest player, SABMiller, made a takeover offer for Heineken, the world’s third-largest brewer, which Heineken rejected last month. That news was quickly followed by reports that the beer industry’s leader, Anheuser-Busch InBev, was trying to get the financing to buy SABMiller. If that deal happens, about 30 percent of the global beer industry, which has annual sales of nearly $150 billion, would be controlled by one company. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monopolizing Beer', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Monopolizing Beer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anheuser-Busch InBev NV', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SABMiller', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heineken NV', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T00:52:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/515f6db1-032a-570d-8d31-0615557b2a9e', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/515f6db1-032a-570d-8d31-0615557b2a9e'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio took a modest step toward fairness with a plan to improve 35 of the city’s most neglected parks and playgrounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/opinion/a-brighter-future-for-the-neediest-parks.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio took a modest step toward fairness with a plan to improve 35 of the city’s most neglected parks and playgrounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Yorkers love their parks, but love isn’t money, which is why many public parks across the boroughs are battered and shabby.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Brighter Future for the Neediest Parks', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Brighter Future for the Neediest Parks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playgrounds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Mitchell J', 'rank': 