 Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/opinion/dont-gamble-away-sterling-forest.html', 'snippet': 'A proposed casino would pose a major threat to forests that provide refuge for wildlife and clean drinking water for millions in New York and New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1996, a coalition of environmentalists, state and federal politicians and private donors cobbled together a deal that saved more than 20,000 acres of woodlands 44 miles away from New York City from development. The forests, some in New Jersey but most in New York, provide refuge for wildlife and clean drinking water for millions of people in New York and New Jersey. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Gamble Away Sterling Forest', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Gamble Away Sterling Forest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuxedo (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genting Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sterling Forest State Park (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T01:05:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5298ac-936f-5464-b427-d730f06a10fb', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5298ac-936f-5464-b427-d730f06a10fb'}, {'abstract': 'Passen