: 1636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e9bc202-cfa0-52a0-be02-0061ca6215e3'}, {'abstract': 'The White House tell-all is hardly a new phenomenon. But what may be new is how much more amplified these books have become with the advent of the Internet, social media and cable television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/us/amplified-by-social-media-insider-memoirs-make-more-racket.html', 'snippet': 'The White House tell-all is hardly a new phenomenon. But what may be new is how much more amplified these books have become with the advent of the Internet, social media and cable television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Leon E. Panetta’s new memoir was out, and the president was livid. The president, it asserted, was “blind” to major problems and presided over a White House with a “lack of principles.” The president told aides the book was a “case study on how to screw the White House.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/MEMO/MEMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/us/MEMO/MEMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/MEMO/MEMO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/MEMO/MEMO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/us/MEMO/MEMO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 