-89dec0e24f48', 'word_count': 1761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/179b1e99-ca3a-5681-8aac-89dec0e24f48'}, {'abstract': 'Vivienne Harr became an Internet sensation for a lemonade stand she started to end child slavery. Now, she has a crowdfunding app that’s funded by Twitter and Google luminaries. Hers is a story of the power of networking in the social media age.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/daily-report-from-lemonade-stand-to-twitters-i-p-o-a-10-year-olds-journey-to-silicon-valley/', 'snippet': 'Vivienne Harr became an Internet sensation for a lemonade stand she started to end child slavery. Now, she has a crowdfunding app that’s funded by Twitter and Google luminaries. Hers is a story of the power of networking in the social media age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vivienne Harr first achieved fame by ringing the bell at the New York Stock Exchange last November, when Twitter went public. Standing beside her were the actor Patrick Stewart and Cheryl Fiandaca, a former spokeswoman for the Boston Police Department. Vivienne was chosen by Twitter for the honor because of her lemonade stand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: From Lemonade Stand to Twitter’s I.P.O., a 10-Year-Old’s Journey to Silicon Valley', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorsey, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harr, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harr, Vivienne', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Biz', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tan, Chade-Meng', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Make a Stand Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T12:09:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96888672-1ab8-528e-85dd-82d8b5cae655', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96888672-1ab8-528e-85dd-82d8b5cae655'}, {'abstract': 'Compared with their earnest allies at other sites, demonstrators in Mong Kok show a combativeness that could be harder for the authorities to bring to heel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/09/world/asia/in-a-gritty-hong-kong-district-protests-display-a-populist-edge.html', 'snippet': 'Compared with their earnest allies at other sites, demonstrators in Mong Kok show a combativeness that could be harder for the authorities to bring to heel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Elaborately tattooed, adorned in rock-star jewelry and flaunting a shock of flamingo-pink hair, Chan Ming-fai usually sells plastic models of movie superheroes at his shop in Mong Kok, a teeming, neon-soaked part of Hong Kong. Now he volunteers as a helper at the protest camp here.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/09protest-01/09protest-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/09/world/09protest-01/09protest-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/09protest-01/09protest-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/09protest-01/09protest-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/09protest-01/09protest-01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/09/world/09protest-01/09protest-01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/09protest-01/09protest-01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Gritty Hong Kong District, Demonstrators Show a Populist Edge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Gritty Hong Kong District, Demonstrators Show a Populist Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leung Chun-ying', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Joshua (1996- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T12:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy and Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8db608f8-3746-57a2-b335-1f4b53f7e69f', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8db608f8-3746-57a2-b335-1f4b53f7e69f'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever one makes of the rights and wrongs of Hong Kong’s protests, they have shown a society that can be flamboyantly individualist and willing to engage in passionate debate about the city’s future. Nowhere more so than Mong Kok.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/hong-kong-protests-mong-kok-style/', 'snippet': 'Whatever one makes of the rights and wrongs of Hong Kong’s protests, they have shown a society that can be flamboyantly individualist and willing to engage in passionate debate about the city’s future. Nowhere more so than Mong Kok.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mong Kok is an area where, tradition holds, Hong Kong people go to relax by slogging through one of the city’s most crowded neighborhoods, a noisy, grimy maze of narrow streets, cheap shops and restaurants, and specialist markets. Recently, it has also become a magnet for mainland Chinese shoppers. These days, though, it has also become known as the site of one of the city’s pro-democracy sit-ins, and Nathan Road, the main street, is occupied by protesters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/08sino-mongkok02/08sino-mongkok02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/09/world/08sino-mongkok02/08sino-mongkok02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/08sino-mongkok02/08sino-mongkok02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/08sino-mongkok02/08sino-mongkok02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/08sino-mongkok02/08sino-mongkok02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/09/world/08sino-mongkok02/08sino-mongkok02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/world/08sino-mongkok02/08sino-mongkok02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Protests, Mong Kok Style', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T12:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4662ce93-96e1-5ce6-8ec5-7951ab3a40bc', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4662ce93-96e1-5ce6-8ec5-7951ab3a40bc'}, {'abstract': 'Daily Clip Report is a collection of articles about the media and The Times that is emailed each day to senior executives and newsroom managers here.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/10/08/daily-clip-report-36/', 'snippet': 'Daily Clip Report is a collection of articles about the media and The Times that is emailed each day to senior executives and newsroom managers here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Clip Report', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T12:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30e454fc-2c14-55e9-b89b-6b41d4622935', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30e454fc-2c14-55e9-b89b-6b41d4622935'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Rob Portman of Ohio says his fellow Republicans, by and large, are not ready to support same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/08/g-o-p-senator-expects-his-gay-marriage-stance-to-stay-lonely/', 'snippet': 'Senator Rob Portman of Ohio says his fellow Republicans, by and large, are not ready to support same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Supreme Court tacitly allowed same-sex marriage in five more states on Monday, the country moved a little bit closer to giving marriage rights to gay couples nationwide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Senator Expects His Gay-Marriage Stance to Stay Lonely', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T12:37:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bf6292c-958c-5bb1-acc9-e722b99e039d', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bf6292c-958c-5bb1-acc9-e722b99e039d'}, {'abstract': 'Slashing investment in a time of free money.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/disinvestment-madness/', 'snippet': 'Slashing investment in a time of free money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m at an IMF seminar today, discussing infrastructure investment — or actually lack thereof. And this is a good time to think about what we’ve actually done. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disinvestment Madness', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T12:49:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5cd36bd-f3b4-5c5f-8b85-f8f8c12ee9ea', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5cd36bd-f3b4-5c5f-8b85-f8f8c12ee9ea'}, {'abstract': 'The project to build the country’s first nuclear power plant since the mid-1990s could encourage companies to build more such sites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/09/business/international/eu-approves-plan-for-new-nuclear-power-station-in-britain.html', 'snippet': 'The project to build the country’s first nuclear power plant since the mid-1990s could encourage companies to build more such sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The European authorities on Wednesday approved construction of Britain’s first nuclear power station since the mid-1990s, in a ruling that could clear the way for other European countries to plan nuclear plants as part of their energy future.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/business/UKNuclear/UKNuclear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 266, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/09/business/UKNuclear/UKNuclear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 266}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/business/UKNuclear/UKNuclear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/business/UKNuclear/UKNuclear-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 909, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/business/UKNuclear/UKNuclear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/09/business/UKNuclear/UKNuclear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/09/business/UKNuclear/UKNuclear-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'E.U. Approves Plan for New Nuclear Power Station in Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.U. Approves British Plan for Nuclear Power Plant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Electricite de France (EDF)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-08T12:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dddad973-fdcf-5f87-9995-1fac545ca4c3', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dddad973-fdcf-5f87-9995-1fac545ca4c3'}, {'abstract': 'The proprietor of a showroom beloved by big-name designers has opened a storefront in the city’s downtown.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/08/vintage-scott-corey-store-julienne-barth/', 'snippet': 'The proprietor of a showroom beloved by big-name designers has opened a storefront in the city’s downtown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than a decade, Scott Corey’s by-appointment-only showroom has been Santa Fe’s best-kept fashion secret, with big-name designers making pilgrimages to his warehouse to source denim, cowboy boots and Southwest antiques. With the jewelry designer Julienne Barth, Corey has opened Santa Fe Vintage Outpost, a new shop along the historic East Palace Avenue, just a block down from where the Manhattan Project physicist J. Robert Oppenheimer once kept an office. The adobe storefront houses Mexican peasant dresses, wool blankets and reworked indigo Mali cloth alongside Barth’s own creations and jewelry from Zuni, Navajo, Hopi and Santo Domingo tribes. “If it’s interesting and unusual,” Corey says, “it’s in here.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/t-magazine/19ten-look-santafe/19ten-look-santafe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 466, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/t-magazine/19ten-look-santafe/19ten-look-santafe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 466}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/t-magazine/19ten-look-santafe/19ten-look-santafe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/t-magazine/19ten-look-santafe/19ten-look-santafe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 797, 'width': 1027, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/t-magazine/19ten-look-santafe/19ten-look-santafe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/t-magazine/19ten-look-santafe/19ten-look-santafe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/t-magazine/19ten-look-santafe/19ten-look-santafe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vintage Americana in Santa Fe', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'pri