tte Moss. The story, which ran in T’s Culture Issue earlier this year, opened with a picture of a hardy orange tree that flanks the library there. It is one of the many artfully arranged fruit trees she planted, which include the espalier apple tree, shown in the above photo of Mellon at home in 1982. In fact, she loved fruit trees so much that she used them to anchor the Rose Garden at the White House, which she designed at the Kennedys’ request. She even wore one as a brooch: circa 1950, Duke Fulco di Verdura designed a 14-karat-gold and platinum brooch to look like the very same espalier apple tree Mellon grew at home. With diamonds for leaves and rubies as apples, the design is estimated to fetch from $2,500 to $3,500 next month at Sotheby’s, which will host auctions of all of Mellon’s most beautiful belongings (she passed away this past spring at the age of 103).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bunny Mellon’s Garden-Inspired Jewelry Designed by Verdura', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mellon, Rachel Lambert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verdura (EJ Landrigan Inc)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T14:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d8a1f8b-8036-58ec-bfae-ef45e923cfb8', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d8a1f8b-8036-58ec-bfae-ef45e923cfb8'}, {'abstract': 'Are there marriage reforms that would not carry Catholicism into self-contradiction?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/09/what-the-church-can-do/', 'snippet': 'Are there marriage reforms that would not carry Catholicism into self-contradiction?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since my comments on the issue of the moment in Roman Catholicism, communion for the divorce and remarried, have been overwhelmingly critical of the main proposals for a change in the church’s discipline, I think it’s only fair to write a post that addresses itself to what I think the church can\xa0do, without lurching into self-contradiction or betraying the New Testament, that might lift unnecessary burdens off some couples’ backs. I’ll use as my jumping-off point this post from Kyle Cupp at Patheos, which sketches a situation in which, as he puts it, “following doctrine can have harmful side effects”:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Church Can Do', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T14:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95027bde-ebc9-5f02-96bb-68709bd42223', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95027bde-ebc9-5f02-96bb-68709bd42223'}, {'abstract': 'Where the Communist Party’s heavy hand is most keenly felt, it is hard to find people who openly support the Hong Kong protesters and their demands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/world/asia/in-beijing-young-chinese-see-little-to-cheer-in-hong-kong-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Where the Communist Party’s heavy hand is most keenly felt, it is hard to find people who openly support the Hong Kong protesters and their demands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The pro-democracy demonstrations in Hong Kong would seem to have universal appeal — a David and Goliath tale starring young idealists, polite and considerate in their defiance, standing up to a mighty authoritarian government with a history of mercilessly crushing dissent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/world/10beijing/10beijing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/10/world/10beijing/10beijing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/world/10beijing/10beijing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/world/10beijing/10beijing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/world/10beijing/10beijing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbn