astructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consolidated Edison Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T14:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cac58cc8-9937-5146-a9c4-9599bb3482bf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cac58cc8-9937-5146-a9c4-9599bb3482bf'}, {'abstract': 'This episode of “Living City,” a video series about New York’s infrastructure, looks at the history of the city’s steam system, the largest in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/nyregion/miles-of-steam-pipes-snake-beneath-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'This episode of “Living City,” a video series about New York’s infrastructure, looks at the history of the city’s steam system, the largest in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First developed in the 1880s, New York City’s steam system is the largest in the world. No other urban steam system comes close.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miles of Steam Pipes Snake Beneath New York', 'kicker': 'Living City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Living City (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T14:28:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Moyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/917b23b7-a613-56ca-ac26-4e0024e4ba8a', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/917b23b7-a613-56ca-ac26-4e0024e4ba8a'}, {'abstract': 'The International Monetary Fund has a few ideas about reforming the Wall Street incentives that played a leading role in the 2008 financial crisis and still pose a threat, William D. Cohan writes in the Street Scene column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/09/i-m-f-takes-aim-at-wall-streets-pay-system/', 'snippet': 'The International Monetary Fund has a few ideas about reforming the Wall Street incentives that played a leading role in the 2008 financial crisis and still pose a threat, William D. Cohan writes in the Street Scene column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We don’t like to concede that a primary cause of the financial crisis was a Wall Street compensation system that rewarded executives, bankers and traders for taking big risks with other people’s money without holding them the least bit accountable. And because we don’t like to discuss such things in polite company, it is certainly unsurprising that six years later, not a single fundamental aspect of how Wall Street pays its top people has changed. The incentive system that handed out millions of dollars in bonuses to bankers and traders who packaged shoddy mortgages into securities and sold them as AAA-rated investments remains intact and no doubt is well on its way to planting the seeds for the next Wall Street-inspired financial crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/dealbook/dbpix-scene/dbpix-wall-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/08/business/dealbook/dbpix-scene/dbpix-wall-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/dealbook/dbpix-scene/dbpix-wall-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/dealbook/dbpix-scene/dbpix-wall-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/dealbook/dbpix-scene/dbpix-wall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/08/business/dealbook/dbpix-scene/dbpix-wall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/08/business/dealbook/dbpix-scene/dbpix-wall-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I.M.F. Takes Aim at Wall Street’s Pay System', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T14:33:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 's