re About Malaysian Plane Crash in Ukraine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dutch Official’s Disclosure in Crash Inquiry Criticized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines Flight 17', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T20:47:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73281558-2cc5-58b5-8b5d-6b2b1a1f8778', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73281558-2cc5-58b5-8b5d-6b2b1a1f8778'}, {'abstract': 'The Connecticut governor’s debate on Thursday turned nasty quickly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/09/truce-offered-and-rejected-in-connecticut-governors-debate/', 'snippet': 'The Connecticut governor’s debate on Thursday turned nasty quickly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This afternoon’s debate in the Connecticut governor’s race, already dominated by personal attacks, quickly descended into playground taunts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Truce Offered, and Rejected, in Connecticut Governor’s Debate', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foley, Thomas C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malloy, Dannel P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T20:49:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa8265c5-6abf-5d80-8a91-8d0844b9d25b', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa8265c5-6abf-5d80-8a91-8d0844b9d25b'}, {'abstract': 'Derrick Adams’s larger-than-life collages at Tilton Gallery draw on images and themes from the early days of color television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/arts/design/derrick-adams-live-and-in-color.html', 'snippet': 'Derrick Adams’s larger-than-life collages at Tilton Gallery draw on images and themes from the early days of color television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since first appearing on the scene over a decade ago, Derrick Adams has been multidisciplinary with a vengeance. Working in performance art, painting, sculpture and music, he has sardonically explored the intersections of popular culture, fashion, black experience and the art of the past. His general approach is to layer and hybridize, so it’s not surprising that about three years ago, he added collage to his repertory. His latest efforts in this medium are big, booming and seductive, but sharp-edged.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1/DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1/DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1/DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1/DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1/DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1/DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1/DERRICKADAMS-GALLERY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Derrick Adams: ‘Live and in Color’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Derrick Adams: ‘Live and in Color’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Derrick (Artist)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T20:50:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cf188e5-bae4-52a3-a97a-3a27b2bea294', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cf188e5-bae4-52a3-a97a-3a27b2bea294'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Schiele’s bright, eye-catching and cleverly constructed works have much in common with those of other painters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/arts/design/kristen-schiele-spirit-girls.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Schiele’s bright, eye-catching and cleverly constructed works have much in common with those of other painters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kristen Schiele’s works are bright, eye-catching, cleverly constructed — and share many characteristics with shows nearby. Like Lisa Beck, at 33 Orchard, and Rachel Garrard, at Klemens Gasser & Tanja Grunert, Ms. Schiele borrows visual motifs from spiritual traditions that became fodder for New Age kitsch. Lines and stars radiate from the centers of her paintings and prints; several, including an installation of rectilinear sticks on the wall, offer Navajo patterns, which are popular now.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kristen Schiele: ‘Spirit Girls’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kristen Schiele: ‘Spirit Girls’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiele, Kristen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-09T20:51:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/812646dc-99da-5586-bf55-0c0036f6ef82', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/812646dc-99da-5586-bf55-0c0036f6ef82'}, {'abstract': '“Meet the Mormons,” directed by Blair Treu, explores stereotypes about a religion with a global focus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/movies/meet-the-mormons-explores-stereotypes-about-a-religion.html', 'snippet': '“Meet the Mormons,” directed by Blair Treu, explores stereotypes about a religion with a global focus.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Meet the Mormons” begins from an oddly defensive posture, with its M.C. and narrator, Jenna Kim Jones, interviewing passers-by in Times Square about their perceptions of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Television and movie clips bolster the notion that the media fosters stereotypes of the religion. (The blockbuster musical around the corner goes curiously undiscussed.) “What are Mormons really like?” Ms. Jones asks. “You decide.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10MEETMORMANS/MEETMORMANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 303, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10MEETMORMANS/MEETMORMANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 303}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10MEETMORMANS/MEETMORMANS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10MEETMORMANS/MEETMORMANS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1033, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/ar