y a robot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/movies/autmata-stars-antonio-banderas-in-a-devastated-world.html', 'snippet': 'In “Autómata,” an investigator in a shrinking world looks into the death of a dog killed by a robot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until it dissolves into a heap of gelatinous mush, “Autómata,” a post-apocalyptic thriller with a bleeding heart, imagines a grim future 30 years hence in which the world’s population has dwindled to 21 million. Most of the planet is a radioactive desert. Clustered in deteriorating, walled cities, the surviving humans are served by primitive robots built by a sinister corporation and installed with protocols that preclude them from altering themselves or from harming any form of life. The world has gone backward technologically in a cycle known as the regression.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10AUTOMATA/AUTOMATA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10AUTOMATA/AUTOMATA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10AUTOMATA/AUTOMATA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10AUTOMATA/AUTOMATA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/10/arts/10AUTOMATA/AUTOMATA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandar