id': 'nyt://article/da8201e6-756e-56e0-ab7b-774699dc22ed', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da8201e6-756e-56e0-ab7b-774699dc22ed'}, {'abstract': 'Court documents reveal a lengthy court fight between the reporter, Mike Levine, and the Justice Department over whether he could be forced to reveal his sources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/us/fox-news-reporter-fought-subpoena-in-leak-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'Court documents reveal a lengthy court fight between the reporter, Mike Levine, and the Justice Department over whether he could be forced to reveal his sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When the Justice Department was hunting for government leakers in 2011, it said that Mike Levine, a Fox News reporter, must reveal his sources because the universe of people who knew the secret information — analysts, prosecutors, agents, press aides and more — was too vast to narrow any other way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox News Reporter Fought Subpoena in Justice Dept. Leak Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reporter Fought Subpoena in Leak Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News Sources, Confidential Status of', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, Mike (Journalist)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T00:48:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Apuzzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Apuzzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c23e5f4f-4970-584e-a9cd-9a0ba79c5ea6', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c23e5f4f-4970-584e-a9cd-9a0ba79c5ea6'}, {'abstract': 'It will take constant outside pressure to end the brutality and corruption at the Rikers Island jail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/10/opinion/new-yorks-jails-need-federal-oversight.html', 'snippet': 'It will take constant outside pressure to end the brutality and corruption at the Rikers Island jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City has failed for so long to control the corruption and brutality in its jail system that it’s fair to ask whether it will ever do so. The Justice Department is wholly justified in threatening to sue the city if Mayor Bill de Blasio does not act promptly and persuasively to improve conditions in the chamber of horrors that is the Rikers Island jail. In the meantime, federal officials should consider using civil rights statutes to prosecute cases of brutality and misconduct that local authorities have overlooked or declined to bring to court. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Jails Need Federal Oversight ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Jails Need Federal Oversight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {