 an adaptation of a Roth novel per se, “Listen Up Philip” underscores the novelist’s hold on filmmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If after years as an elder statesman of American letters, Philip Roth were ever in danger of fading from interest among younger artists, the 30-year-old filmmaker Alex Ross Perry might readily serve as his champion. With Roth’s work combining “comedy and pathos and perversion and commentary,” Mr. Perry said recently, “it really felt like all of his books were written just for me.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eternal Regard for a Self-Obsessed Id ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eternal Regard for a Self-Obsessed Id', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapold, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Alex Ross', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Philip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartzman, Jason', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pryce, Jonathan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Listen Up Philip (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T03:23:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cd79f42-2ccd-50d1-a51d-b70e79ff6ad7', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cd79f42-2