-award-with-syrian-human-rights-advocate/', 'snippet': 'Salman Rushdie will share the PEN Pinter Prize with a Syrian lawyer and human rights advocate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Salman Rushdie is sharing this year’s PEN Pinter Prize with the Syrian lawyer and human rights advocate Mazen Darwish, who was arrested in Damascus in February 2012 in connection with efforts to document abuses in that country. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rushdie Shares Award With Syrian Human Rights Advocate', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English PEN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T17:20:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79338571-e408-5d15-bde9-159b0d336dc2', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79338571-e408-5d15-bde9-159b0d336dc2'}, {'abstract': 'Murals by Robert Winthrop Chanler may be seen at Coe Hall in Oyster Bay, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/realestate/an-aristocratic-painters-astonishing-aesthetic.html', 'snippet': 'Murals by Robert Winthrop Chanler may be seen at Coe Hall in Oyster Bay, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Winthrop Chanler lived big, painted big, loved big and was just plain big, 6-foot-4, 200-plus pounds, with a giant crown of shaggy hair.\xa0Despite all that, he remains an elusive figure among New York artists of the early 20th century. He is known for his serene fauvist-style paintings and fantastical scenes of forest and marine wildlife, but many of his works are lost; some are documented only through old photographs.\xa0', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Aristocratic Painter’s Astonishing Aesthetic ', 'kicker': 'Streetscapes Robert Winthrop Chanler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Aristocratic Painter’s Astonishing Aesthetic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chanler, Robert Winthrop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T17:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4f7fb96-a7e4-5f5b-aec5-457aee38c1fb', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4f7fb96-a7e4-5f5b-aec5-457aee38c1fb'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent review of Mark Whitaker’s “Cosby” and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/books/review/letters-a-comedian-and-a-scholar.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent review of Mark Whitaker’s “Cosby” and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Comedian and a Scholar', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: A Comedian and a Scholar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T17:22:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d6a1604-9b40-523f-a061-614469b48275', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d6a1604-9b40-523f-a061-614469b48275'}, {'abstract': 'The anti-vaccination movement thrives in California, but in New York strict immunization requirements and doctors’ efforts help keep the movement from spreading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/nyregion/fear-of-vaccines-goes-viral.html', 'snippet': 'The anti-vaccination movement thrives in California, but in New York strict immunization requirements and doctors’ efforts help keep the movement from spreading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month The Hollywood Reporter published an illuminating investigation on immunization trends in Los Angeles County, which revealed that vaccination rates on the city’s wealthy west side, in neighborhoods like Beverly Hills and Santa Monica, had plummeted, as incidents of whooping cough surged. The piece had the virtue of offering New Yorkers yet another opportunity to feel smugly superior to their counterparts in L.A., because of course here on the East Coast we like our science to come from scientists, not from former Playboy models and people who feel entitled to pontificate about public health because they drink kefir. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12BIGCITY/12BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12BIGCITY/12BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12BIGCITY/12BIGCITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12BIGCITY/12BIGCITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12BIGCITY/12BIGCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12BIGCITY/12BIGCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12BIGCITY/12BIGCITY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fear of Vaccines Goes Viral', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vaccine Fear Goes Viral', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cal