ere-and-batiashvili-plays-brahms.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic presented the premiere of Christopher Rouse’s “Thunderstuck” at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few composers are lucky enough to have an advocate like the New York Philharmonic’s music director, Alan Gilbert. According to the Philharmonic’s archives, Thursday’s premiere of Christopher Rouse’s new homage to soft rock, “Thunderstuck,” at Avery Fisher Hall, was the 36th performance Mr. Gilbert has given of his composer-in-residence’s work since February 2010.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/rouse/rouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/rouse/rouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/rouse/rouse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/rouse/rouse-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/rouse/rouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/rouse/rouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/rouse/rouse-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rock Beat of His Youth, Echoing Again in August Precincts ', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Rock Beat of His Youth, Echoing Again in August Precincts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouse, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Batiashvili, Lisa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T21:48:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca84fe26-0e5c-5df8-b7fd-22a6a56d6b92', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca84fe26-0e5c-5df8-b7fd-22a6a56d6b92'}, {'abstract': 'In “Chalk and Soot” at the Lincoln Center White Light Festival, John Heginbotham choreographs to silence and Colin Jacobsen has turned to writing vocals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/11/arts/dance/chalk-and-soot-in-white-light-festival.html', 'snippet': 'In “Chalk and Soot” at the Lincoln Center White Light Festival, John Heginbotham choreographs to silence and Colin Jacobsen has turned to writing vocals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer John Heginbotham doesn’t shy from whimsy. In his two-act “Chalk and Soot,” a collaboration with the composer Colin Jacobsen as part of the Lincoln Center White Light Festival, he finds inspiration in Kandinsky’s “Sounds,” a book of woodcuts and Modernist poetry published in 1912. In the program, there are translated lines such as “You, good-for-nothing snail, you who don’t love me.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/chalk/chalk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/chalk/chalk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 305}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/chalk/chalk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/chalk/chalk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1041, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/chalk/chalk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/chalk/chalk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/chalk/chalk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blithely Stepping Out of a Comfort Zone ', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blithely Stepping Out of a Comfort Zone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 