ne, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c910a120-6065-581a-8e7b-669630399e07', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c910a120-6065-581a-8e7b-669630399e07'}, {'abstract': 'The trumpeter Nicholas Payton, appearing with Vicente Archer and Bill Stewart, is spending more time at pianos this week at Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/11/arts/music/nicholas-payton-trio-features-payton-mostly-on-piano.html', 'snippet': 'The trumpeter Nicholas Payton, appearing with Vicente Archer and Bill Stewart, is spending more time at pianos this week at Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first part of Nicholas Payton’s career, he was effectively in the business of knocking you back in your chair. These days he seems to want to make you lean forward instead. The transition wasn’t sudden, not if you’ve been attuned to his music over the last decade. Still, it can be a striking thing to absorb over the course of a set, like the one on Thursday that began his four-night run at Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/PAYTON/PAYTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/PAYTON/PAYTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/PAYTON/PAYTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/PAYTON/PAYTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1262, 'width': 2048, '