 turns one this month. Despite the rocky rollout, premiums have not skyrocketed and millions of uninsured Americans now have coverage. But as the 2015 enrollment period approaches, some employers are scaling back benefits, offering plans with higher deductibles and in some cases, forcing employees into the marketplace to find coverage. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s Money Talking', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T22:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Dallett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dallett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be07b79c-3278-5dd1-84b0-92c859d08763', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be07b79c-3278-5dd1-84b0-92c859d08763'}, {'abstract': 'In “Chita’s Back!,” her show at Birdland, the Broadway giant Chita Rivera brings her drive and power to the old songs from shows like “Bye Bye Birdie,” “West Side Story” and “All That Jazz.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/11/arts/music/chita-rivera-kicks-up-her-heels-at-birdland.html', 'snippet': 'In “Chita’s Back!,” her show at Birdland, the Broadway giant Chita Rivera brings her drive and power to the old songs from shows like “Bye Bye Birdie,” “West Side Story” and “All That Jazz.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“The one thing I won’t give up is my rhythm,” Chita Rivera declared on Thursday evening at Birdland. Watching this Broadway giant, whom I’ve seen onstage many times (and I always come away walking on air), I marveled once again as that rhythm seized her body and zigzagged through her like lightning. A signature posture is a haughty, self-assertive strut in which she throws back her head, then jerks forward in a kind of whiplash. Ms. Rivera is 81, and though the width of her stride may have diminished, her essential drive is as powerful and determined as ever.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/CHITA/CHITA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/CHITA/CHITA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/CHITA/CHITA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/CHITA/CHITA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/CHITA/CHITA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/CHITA/CHITA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/11/arts/CHITA/CHITA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Doin’ a Lot of Livin’ in Anecdote and Song', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Doin’ a Lot of Livin’ in Anecdote and Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Chita', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Birdland (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-10T22:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ca1638d-7bc4-5ab7-b2dc-ed253aab0480', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ca1638d-7bc4-5ab7-b2dc-ed253aab0480'}, {'abstract': 'Several Connecticut orchards are offering varieties not available in grocery stores.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/nyregion/3-apple-orchards-offering-heirlooms.html', 'snippet': 'Several Connecticut orchards are offering varieties not available in grocery stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buying locally grown produce takes on a special flavor in the first crisp weeks of autumn, as Connecticut’s apple orchards bring in their harvest. This is the time to look past the commonplace varieties carried by supermarkets and sample some of the more unusual types that are available only at area farms. Here are three orchards especially notable for cultivating heirloom and heritage breeds of apples.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/nyregion/12DINECT6/12DINECT6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 