': 'nyt://article/0555663d-b5a8-5445-8abd-ed332c1a478c'}, {'abstract': 'Cambios en el ámbito político estadounidense hacen de este el momento propicio para renovar la relación con Cuba y reanudar vínculos diplomáticos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/opinion/sunday/tiempo-de-acabar-el-embargo-de-cuba.html', 'snippet': 'Cambios en el ámbito político estadounidense hacen de este el momento propicio para renovar la relación con Cuba y reanudar vínculos diplomáticos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cuando mira un mapa del mundo, el Presidente Obama debe sentir angustia al contemplar el lamentable estado de las relaciones bilaterales que su administración ha intentado reparar. Sería sensato que el líder estadounidense reflexione seriamente sobre Cuba, donde un giro de política podría representar un gran triunfo para su gobierno.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiempo de acabar el embargo de Cuba', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tiempo de Acabar el Embargo de Cuba', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-11T16:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By El Comité Editorial', 'person': [{'firstname': 'El', 'middlename': 'Comité', 'lastname': 'Editorial', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b38f5ff-105e-563a-a1d9-2a577ef05354', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b38f5ff-105e-563a-a1d9-2a577ef05354'}, {'abstract': 'Providence’s love affair with its charming, bullying, felonious ex-mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/opinion/sunday/good-buddy-bad-buddy.html', 'snippet': 'Providence’s love affair with its charming, bullying, felonious ex-mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PROVIDENCE, R.I. — THE biggest story in Rhode Island this fall isn’t the potential election on Nov. 4 of the state’s first female governor, Gina M. Raimondo, a Democrat, or its first Asian-American governor, Allan Fung, a Republican. Instead it’s the improbable comeback of Buddy Cianci, the felonious former mayor of Providence, who spent two decades in City Hall and is now running for yet another term. Hailed as a savior, condemned as a sinner, the 73-year-old is a fractured city monument who could steal the epitaph from H. P. Lovecraft’s tombstone at Swan Point Cemetery: I am Providence.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sunday-review/1012PROVIDENCE/1012PROVIDENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/12/sunday-review/1012PROVIDENCE/1012PROVIDENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sunday-review/1012PROVIDENCE/1012PROVIDENCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sunday-review/1012PROVIDENCE/1012PROVIDENCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sunday-review/1012PROVIDENCE/1012PROVIDENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/12/sunday-review/1012PROVIDENCE/1012PROVIDENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sunday-review/1012PROVIDENCE/1012PROVIDENCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Buddy, Bad Buddy', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Buddy, Bad Buddy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cianci, Vincent A Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Providence (RI)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racketeering and Racketeers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-11T16:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Stanton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c01d7d-da8e-5fd0-8d7b-e9c4d375a218', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c01d7d-da8e-5fd0-8d7b-e9c4d375a218'}, {'abstract': 'After South Korean activists sent anti-Pyongyang leaflets across the border and troops from both sides exchanged fire, the state news agency said talks with Seoul could be canceled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/world/asia/north-korea-warns-south-over-leaflets.html', 'snippet': 'After South Korean activists sent anti-Pyongyang leaflets across the border and troops from both sides exchanged fire, the state news agency said talks with Seoul could be canceled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — North Korea’s state-run news agency said on Saturday that the country’s plans to resume high-level government dialogue with South Korea were in danger of being canceled after troops from both sides exchanged machine-gun fire across the heavily armed border.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Warns South Over Leaflets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Warns South Over Leaflets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyongyang (North Korea)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-11T17:19:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5944ef90-2119-5570-9997-212eee981a7b', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5944ef90-2119-5570-9997-212eee981a7b'}, {'abstract': 'The trade by the Kansas City Royals of Zack Greinke, a Cy Young Award winner, to the Milwaukee Brewers in 2010 paved the way for this season’s postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/sports/baseball/how-a-disgruntled-ace-gave-the-royals-a-full-house-.html', 'snippet': 'The trade by the Kansas City Royals of Zack Greinke, a Cy Young Award winner, to the Milwaukee Brewers in 2010 paved the way for this season’s postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — It was December 2010, and Dayton Moore had a problem. As the general manager of the woebegone Kansas City Royals, Moore was used to problems. But this one also offered an opportunity. By seizing it, Moore set the Royals on a path to this American League Championship Series.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sports/DOG-KEPNER-1/DOG-KEPNER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/12/sports/DOG-KEPNER-1/DOG-KEPNER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sports/DOG-KEPNER-1/DOG-KEPNER-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sports/DOG-KEPNER-1/DOG-KEPNER-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1504, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sports/DOG-KEPNER-1/DOG-KEPNER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/12/sports/DOG-KEPNER-1/DOG-KEPNER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/sports/DOG-KEPNER-1/DOG-KEPNER-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'wi