', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — A nurse here became the first person to contract Ebola within the United States, prompting local, state and federal officials who had settled into a choreographed response to scramble on Sunday to solve the mystery of how she became infected, despite wearing protective gear, and to monitor additional people possibly at risk.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/us/13EBOLA-3/13EBOLA-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/us/13EBOLA-3/13EBOLA-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/us/13EBOLA-3/13EBOLA-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/us/13EBOLA-3/13EBOLA-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/us/13EBOLA-3/13EBOLA-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/13/us/13EBOLA-3/13EBOLA-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/us/13EBOLA-3/13EBOLA-3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2nd Ebola Case in U.S. Stokes Fears of Health Care Workers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dallas Nurse Contracts Ebola Virus, Elevating Response and Anxiety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Health Presbyterian Hospital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-12T10:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ed81b74-088d-5223-bff4-2dc8f30e94f3', 'word_count': 1686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ed81b74-088d-5223-bff4-2dc8f30e94f3'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrations continued after Leung Chun-ying, the city’s chief executive, said the possibility of a reversal of the Chinese legislature’s policy is “almost nil.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/13/world/asia/hong-kong-protesters-appeal-to-xi-jinping-in-open-letter.html', 'snippet': 'Demonstrations continued after Leung Chun-ying, the city’s chief executive, said the possibility of a reversal of the Chinese legislature’s policy is “almost nil.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Rows of police officers took pro-democracy protesters by surprise on Monday morning and began removing barricades on major avenues here, as the student leaders appealed directly to President Xi Jinping of China to reconsider the government’s position and Hong Kong’s top official again rejected their demands.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/world/asia/A1-Honk-Kong-refer/A1-Honk-Kong-refer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/world/asia/A1-Honk-Kong-refer/A1-Honk-Kong-refer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/world/asia/A1-Honk-Kong-refer/A1-Honk-Kong-refer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/world/asia/A1-Honk-Kong-refer/A1-Honk-Kong-refer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1213, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/world/asia/A1-Honk-Kong-refer/A1-Honk-Kong-refer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/13/world/asia/A1-Honk-Kong-refer/A1-Honk-Kong-refer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/world/asia/A1-Honk-Kong-refer/A1-Honk-Kong-refer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Move on Barricades; Hong Kong Leader Rejects Protesters’ Appeal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Move on Barricades; Hong Kong Leader Rejects Protesters’ Appeal