ee men further into space than ever before in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Soviet Union today [Oct. 12] sent three men into orbit aboard the world’s first ‘‘passenger spaceship.’’ The official announcement said the flight would be ‘‘long.’’ The spacecraft — known as ‘‘Voskhod,’’ or ‘‘Sunrise’’ — is orbiting as high as 254.14 miles from earth, higher than man ever has been before. The flight was also the first which man has made ‘‘in a shirt-sleeve atmosphere.’’', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/blogs/12iht-old13/12iht-old13-articleLarge.png', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/12/blogs/12iht-old13/12iht-old13-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/blogs/12iht-old13/12iht-old13-jumbo.png', 'height': 486, 'width': 785, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/blogs/12iht-old13/12iht-old13-superJumbo.png', 'height': 486, 'width': 785, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/blogs/12iht-old13/12iht-old13-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/12/blogs/12iht-old13/12iht-old13-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/blogs/12iht-old13/12iht-old13-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'th