k Taper Forum with Lois Smith in the title role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The young man in the tie seems nice enough, gently nagging the old woman to eat something, even if she has no appetite. Is he a social worker, someone who’s come to check up on her? Wait, no: He launches into a story he thinks she’ll like, about the time the two of them went to see “My Best Friend’s Wedding,” and he proposed afterward.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/MARJORIE/MARJORIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/MARJORIE/MARJORIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/MARJORIE/MARJORIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/MARJORIE/MARJORIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1412, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/MARJORIE/MARJORIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/MARJORIE/MARJORIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/MARJORIE/MARJORIE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Memories by Rewriting the Past ', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Memories by Rewriting the Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center Theater Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Les', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wood, Frank (1960- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emery, Lisa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Marjorie Prime (Play)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-12T20:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb67cad4-1faf-5c9b-8774-3d73c3db20bc', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb67cad4-1faf-5c9b-8774-3d73c3db20bc'}, {'abstract': 'As its dispute with the publisher continues, Amazon wants to make it difficult to buy Hachette books, but it does not want to be accused of banning them.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/12/amazon-and-its-missing-books/', 'snippet': 'As its dispute with the publisher continues, Amazon wants to make it difficult to buy Hachette books, but it does not want to be accused of banning them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writer Ursula K. Le Guin recently weighed in on Amazon’s dispute with the publisher Hachette over e-book pricing. Referring to how Amazon is making Hachette books harder to buy on its site, she said, “We’re talking about