 there were an award for best-looking cast, the director Bille Woodruff’s “Addicted” would take the prize — or at least be nominated. Led by Sharon Leal and Boris Kodjoe, the actors are uniformly handsome and mostly serviceable, though the same can’t be said about the filmmaking or the writing. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/ADDICTED/ADDICTED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/ADDICTED/ADDICTED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/ADDICTED/ADDICTED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/ADDICTED/ADDICTED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/ADDICTED/ADDICTED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/ADDICTED/ADDICTED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/arts/ADDICTED/ADDICTED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wife Addicted to Lust, No Matter the Cost', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wife Addicted to Lust, No Matter the Cost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodruff, Bille', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leal, Sharon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kodjoe, Boris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ADDicted (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-12T22:06:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Herrington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herrington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/34794371-0347-55b7-98db-940f83973c6a', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34794371-0347-55b7-98db-940f83973c6a'}, {'abstract': 'Maybe he is still out there somewhere, hiding in the shadows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/13/opinion/monsters-in-the-woods.html', 'snippet': 'Maybe he is still out there somewhere, hiding in the shadows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUSHKILL, Pa. — IT was a full two hours before dawn on a morning in late summer when my wife, a woman neither given to flights of fantasy nor easily spooked, brusquely elbowed me out of a deep slumber. As I shook off the sleep, I could tell by the look in her eyes that something had rattled her. That look rattled me.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/opinion/1013OPEDdezso/1013OPEDdezso-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/opinio