ice Press Bureau, the ‘‘eye-witness,’’ writing on October 9, continues his narrative of events as follows: In spite of the perfection of their arrangements for ranging and observation, there has been much waste of ammunition by the Germans. For instance, within an area of two acres on our side of the Aisne there are over one hundred craters made by their heavy high-explosive shell.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Oct. 14, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/14iht-oldoct14-Aisne/14iht-oldoct14-A