r Watch column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/13/when-the-art-of-the-deal-becomes-a-crime/', 'snippet': 'Two cases raise the question about what role the courts should play in policing negotiations and the limits that can be applied to the tactics one side can use in making a deal, Peter J. Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the television game show “Let’s Make a Deal,” the host Monty Hall offered contestants the chance to trade a prize for what was hidden behind one of three doors. Make the wrong choice, and you could go home with little more than memories. In any negotiation, there is a danger that one party will make a bad deal with little recourse unless it can be shown that the winning side violated the law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/business/dbpix-henning2/dbpix-henning2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/business/dbpix-henning2/dbpix-henning2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/business/dbpix-henning2/dbpix-henning2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/business/dbpix-henning2/dbpix-henning2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1583, 'width': 1938, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/business/dbpix-henning2/dbpix-henning2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb