re cash to hire one. The 42-year-old ensemble, which has always prided itself on its ability to perform complex works through a collaborative interpretive process, and without anyone on its podium, has been awarded a $400,000 grant from the Andrew W. Mellon Foundation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$400,000 Grant to Help Connect Orchestra With Next Generation', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mellon Foundation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orpheus Chamber Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-13T17:53:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5fbad06-cbfc-5ae9-a744-d495b44a09b9', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5fbad06-cbfc-5ae9-a744-d495b44a09b9'}, {'abstract': 'The Philippine and American authorities are investigating whether a member of the United States military killed a 26-year-old Filipino.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/world/asia/member-of-us-military-questioned-in-death-of-filipino.html', 'snippet': 'The Philippine and American authorities are investigating whether a member of the United States military killed a 26-year-old Filipino.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OLONGAPO CITY, Philippines — The Philippine police and United States Navy officials are investigating whether a member of the United States military killed a 26-year-old Filipino cross-dresser in a hotel over the weekend, the police said Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Member of U.S. Military