ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19046bc2-1706-519f-a061-152564fbc169', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19046bc2-1706-519f-a061-152564fbc169'}, {'abstract': 'The action by Parliament was seen as an indication of how public opinion has shifted since the breakdown of peace talks and the Gaza conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/world/europe/british-parliament-palestinian-state.html', 'snippet': 'The action by Parliament was seen as an indication of how public opinion has shifted since the breakdown of peace talks and the Gaza conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Against a backdrop of growing impatience across Europe with Israeli policy, Britain’s Parliament overwhelmingly passed a nonbinding resolution Monday night to give diplomatic recognition to a Palestinian state. The vote was a symbolic but potent indication of how public opinion has shifted since the breakdown of American-sponsored peace negotiations and the conflict in Gaza this summer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/world/BRITAIN/BRITAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/world/BRITAIN/BRITAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/world/BRITAIN/BRITAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/world/BRITAIN/BRITAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'c