lue': 'Sisi, Abdel Fattah el-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-13T21:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ab1ac14-500f-58e6-972a-7c1080a3275a', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ab1ac14-500f-58e6-972a-7c1080a3275a'}, {'abstract': 'The AMC program crushed even the N.F.L. on Sunday night among the 18-49 demographic. Also, the networks reported improved ratings for the premiere week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/business/media/walking-dead-premiere-draws-17-million-viewers-a-record-for-a-cable-tv-drama.html', 'snippet': 'The AMC program crushed even the N.F.L. on Sunday night among the 18-49 demographic. Also, the networks reported improved ratings for the premiere week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ratings news from Sunday night was unusually buoyant across the board, as “The Walking Dead” on AMC shattered its own previous record as the most-watched drama in cable television history, and the four broadcast networks all posted increased numbers for premiere week, when delayed viewing over seven days was counted.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Walking Dead’ Season 5 Draws 17 Million Viewers in Premiere, a Record for a Cable TV Drama ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Walking Dead’ Premiere Tops 17 Million Viewers, Setting Record for a Cable Drama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMC (TV Network)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gotham (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Walking Dead (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-13T21:29:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4e3e94a-2dc5-5701-9a80-635f55c0a6d4', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4e3e94a-2dc5-5701-9a80-635f55c0a6d4'}, {'abstract': 'The group from Peshawar, Pakistan, performed as part of a cultural exchange program of the State Department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/arts/music/khumariyaan-performed-at-asia-society-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'The group from Peshawar, Pakistan, performed as part of a cultural exchange program of the State Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s more to Khumariyaan than the twangy, accelerating melodies and snappy rhythms that eventually got the audience at Asia Society on its feet and dancing on Sunday night. During the concert Sparlay Rawail, the four-man group’s lead guitarist, matter-of-factly described its repertory as “music of the oppressed.” Khumariyaan means “intoxicators.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/pushtoon/pushtoon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/pushtoon/pushtoon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/pushtoon/pushtoon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/pushtoon/pushtoon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1238, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/pushtoon/pushtoon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/pushtoon/pushtoon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/pushtoon/pushtoon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With a Slight Western Inflection, Culturally Charged Pashtun Folk Melodies ', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With a Slight Western Inflection, Culturally Charged Pashtun Folk Melodies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Khumariyaan (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-13T21:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8924350b-f616-5eb3-a228-6c51ecf60313', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8924350b-f616-5eb3-a228-6c51ecf60313'}, {'abstract': 'In Colm Toibin’s new novel, “Nora Webster,” the flinty heroine is a just-widowed mother of four who returns to work and finds the experience slowly transformative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/books/nora-webster-by-colm-toibin.html', 'snippet': 'In Colm Toibin’s new novel, “Nora Webster,” the flinty heroine is a just-widowed mother of four who returns to work and finds the experience slowly transformative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nora Webster, the stern heroine of Colm Toibin’s new novel, is just widowed as the book begins. She is grieving, but not in the usual ways. Annoyance with a nonstop flow of pious visitors overrides other emotions Nora might feel. When one woman arrives to commiserate — and to peer too closely at Nora’s face, “forcing her to express interest and surprise,” while perhaps seeking some tidbit that can be gossiped about — Nora finds the familiarity unbearable. It’s true of this woman, and no doubt other visitors, that Nora “knew the story of her life down to her maiden name and the plot in the graveyard where she would be buried.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 862}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 713, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1426, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Change in the Climate for an Icy Irish Matron', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Change in the Climate for an Icy Irish Matron', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toibin, Colm', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nora Webster (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-13T21:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/887153f4-2cad-5c51-a245-21788e90d523', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/887153f4-2cad-5c51-a245-21788e90d523'}, {'abstract': 'Google’s “Helpouts” platform is experimenting with a new product that lets consumers talk to doctors over video.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/13/am-i-sick-google-has-a-doctor-waiting-on-video/', 'snippet': 'Google’s “Helpouts” platform is experimenting with a new product that lets consumers talk to doctors over video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Internet can be a dangerous place to get medical advice. Stomachaches turn into cancer, stress becomes an endocrine tumor. Crack remedies and strange diets abound. Now Google is playing with a new technology that it hopes will help people find more reliable medical information. It’s called a doctor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/technology/13bits-googlehealth/13bits-googlehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 343, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/technology/13bits-googlehealth/13bits-googlehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 343}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/technology/13bits-googlehealth/13bits-googlehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/technology/13bits-googlehealth/13bits-googlehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/technology/13bits-googlehealth/13bits-googlehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/13/technology/13bits-googlehealth/13bits-googlehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/