 'snippet': 'In Sunday night’s victory over the Giants, Molina strained an oblique, a side abdominal muscle. That sort of injury typically takes many weeks to fully heal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — The air had left Busch Stadium on Sunday night, and it had little to do with the deflating double play that Yadier Molina had just bounced into. As eyes shifted back toward the batter’s box, where Molina was doubled over and where his manager and trainer were rushing to his side, hearts began to sink. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/sports/Y-MOLINA/Y-MOLINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/sports/Y-MOLINA/Y-MOLINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/sports/Y-MOLINA/Y-MOLINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/sports/Y-MOLINA/Y-MOLINA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/sports/Y-MOLINA/Y-MOLINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/14/sports/Y-MOLINA/Y-MOLINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/sports/Y-MOLINA/Y-MOLINA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 