te 1980s to preserve the legacy of victims of Stalinism. An affiliated organization, the Memorial Center for Human Rights, founded in 1991, focuses on current human rights abuses, and has been the target of repeated efforts of government officials to curtail its activities. This year the center was forcibly registered as a “foreign agent” for receiving grants from abroad in a campaign to clamp down on hundreds of nongovernmental organizations that are perceived as threatening the Kremlin’s interests. The ministry’s lawsuit against the Memorial Society was filed last month but reported only on Friday. A report on the NTV television channel accused the Memorial Center for Human Rights of supporting Islamic terrorists. The Justice Ministry press service told the official RIA Novosti news agency on Monday that the Memorial Society’s structure violated Russian laws and its own charter. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Ministry Takes Aim at a Human Rights Group', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Ministry Takes Aim at a Human Rights Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kishkovsky, Sophia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court of Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memorial', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T01:26:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Kishkovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kishkovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/209d4a7f-10b1-5f5d-9c34-018b8b10a1ff', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/209d4a7f-10b1-5f5d-9c34-018b8b10a1ff'}, {'abstract': 'The organizer behind the social media drive Let NY Play is MGM Resorts International in Las Vegas, which has made no secret of its ambition to be a big player in Internet gambling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/nyregion/an-online-gambling-push-in-new-york-from-2500-miles-away.html', 'snippet': 'The organizer behind the social media drive Let NY Play is MGM Resorts International in Las Vegas, which has made no secret of its ambition to be a big player in Internet gambling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The postings, with their populist tone, started appearing on Facebook and Twitter a few weeks ago. Their message was simple: If people in New Jersey can play poker online legally, New Yorkers should be able to as well.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/nyregion/14poker/14poker-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/nyregion/14poker/14poker-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 656}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/nyregion/14poker/14poker-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/nyregion/14poker/14poker-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio