country on Monday, an event the government called a step toward reconciliation and national unity after a long civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Sri Lanka reopened a rail link between Jaffna in the north and the rest of the country on Monday, an event the government called a step toward reconciliation and national unity after a long civil war. In 1985, Tamil rebel cadres attacked the train, known as the Queen of Jaffna, and destroyed part of the railway, severing a physical and psychological link between the Tamils in the north and the Sinhalese south. The war ended in 2009 when government troops crushed the rebels. The Colombo-Jaffna railway line was reconstructed with the help of an $800 million loan from India. But deep wounds remain from the war, and the government has been urged to address accusations of human rights violations during the war’s final phase. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sri Lanka: Railway Severed by Civil War Reopens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sri Lanka: Railway Severed by Civil War Reopens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaffna (Sri Lanka)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombo (Sri Lanka)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T02:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dharisha Bastians', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dharisha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bastians', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/66f7d88f-e475-5f24-a15b-2198ffb39b0c', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66f7d88f-e475-5f24-a15b-2198ffb39b0c'}, {'abstract': 'Both candidates reached absurd heights in the art of weasel-wording.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/13/mcconnell-and-grimes-debate-united-in-vagueness/', 'snippet': 'Both candidates reached absurd heights in the art of weasel-wording.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LEXINGTON, Ky. – Political campaigns aren’t generally associated with specificity or truth-telling and political debates are no different. But at Monday night’s debate in Lexington, both Senator Mitch McConnell and his Democratic challenger, Alison Lundergan Grimes, the Kentucky Secretary of State, reached absurd heights in the art of weasel-wording.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alison Lundergan Grimes and Mitch McConnell, United in Vagueness', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimes, Alison Lundergan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T02:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c602a280-9bd3-5c86-ba8a-352530824477', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c602a280-9bd3-5c86-ba8a-352530824477'}, {'abstract': 'Whether it was a bizarre prank or something more malicious, the police said they were searching for the man, who they say is wanted for reckless endangerment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/nyregion/he-tossed-smoke-bomb-at-diners-and-then-escaped-underground-.html', 'snippet': 'Whether it was a bizarre prank or something more malicious, the police said they were searching for the man, who they say is wanted for reckless endangerment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The yellow metal door in the sidewalk opened slowly, causing a pedestrian to pause and walk around it. The passer-by continued on, not noticing that something was afoot. A few moments later, a young man poked his head out, tossed a canister of pink smoke into the patio of a nearby Italian restaurant, and quickly ducked back underground. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/multimedia/reckless-endangerment-promo/reckless-endangerment-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/13/multimedia/reckless-endangerment-promo/reckless-endangerment-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/multimedia/reckless-endangerment-promo/reckless-endangerment-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/13/multimedia/reckless-endangerment-promo/reckless-endangerment-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum