soils, seas and other natural assets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m catching up with the “Nature is Speaking” education push by Conservation International, featuring a set of videos in which actors give voice to the oceans, rain forests and other beautiful and bounteous facets of the planet’s sheath of life. The writing is engaging and just a bit edgy and aimed at increasing young people’s awareness that a thriving environment is an underpinning of human wellbeing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/dotnorton/dotnorton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 330, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/dotnorton/dotnorton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 330, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/dotnorton/dotnorton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/dotnorton/dotnorton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/blogs/dotnorton/dotnorton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nature Talks Back, and Sounds a Lot like Edward Norton', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norton, Edward', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Randy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Julia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN PSYCHOLOGICAL ASSN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservation International', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T12:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38009375-cc04-5fe8-9da3-7b96d499d558', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38009375-cc04-5fe8-9da3-7b96d499d558'}, {'abstract': 'Could the lengthy rollout of Peter Copping’s move to Oscar de la Renta actually have been a strategic move?', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/fashion-rumor-on-peter-copping-and-oscar-de-la-renta/', 'snippet': 'Could the lengthy rollout of Peter Copping’s move to Oscar de la Renta actually have been a strategic move?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to a month of rampant rumor-mongering, the final confirmation on Monday that Peter Copping had been named creative director of Oscar de la Renta felt to many in the fashion world — let’s be honest here — like something of the ultimate anticlimax. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/fashion/14runway/14r