etry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my piece today on South Dakota’s unpredictable Senate race, I noted how the candidates there represented a departure from the cookie-cutter homogeneity that is now commonplace in races around the country. Few, however, break the mold like Larry Pressler, the former Republican senator now running for his old seat as an independent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He’ll Fight Every Day for the Poetry of South Dakota', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pressler, Larry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T12:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a0ee54a-b0d0-5666-897c-0edc912a62b0', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a0ee54a-b0d0-5666-897c-0edc912a62b0'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: After stopping and aiding a badly injured bicyclist on the West Side, a good Samaritan left him a note he found later.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/help-and-a-card-for-an-injured-cyclist/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: After stopping and aiding a badly injured bicyclist on the West Side, a good Samaritan left him a note he found later.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Help, and a Card, for an Injured Cyclist', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{