Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The midterm elections may be three weeks away, but for prognosticators in the news media, 2016 is just around the corner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton and Christie Are Stealing 2016 Headlines', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T14:28:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/227bdfef-95ea-531e-9f11-456fc3f29175', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/227bdfef-95ea-531e-9f11-456fc3f29175'}, {'abstract': 'As fashion designers blur the lines between the sexes, boys and girls forge their own identities.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/androgynous-style/', 'snippet': 'As fashion designers blur the lines between the sexes, boys and girls forge their own identities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As fashion designers blur the lines between the sexes, boys and girls forge their own identities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One: The Freedom to Dress Regardless of Gender', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emporio Armani SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prada SpA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T14:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f675758a-525d-504d-a13d-eccf8a3d393e', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f675758a-525d-504d-a13d-eccf8a3d393e'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Martin Luther King Jr. was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/1964-martin-luther-king-jr-awarded-nobel-peace-prize/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Martin Luther King Jr. was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSLO — The Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King, the 35-year-old American Negro leader, today [Oct. 14] was awarded the 1964 Nobel Peace Prize for his ‘‘consistent support’’ of the principle of nonviolence in the Negro campaign for civil rights. He said he would use the 273,000 Swedish crowns prize (about $53,000) to strengthen the civil rights campaign in the United States. Dr. King is the 12th American to receive the prize. He is the second Negro leader to win in four years. The 1960 award was given to Albert Luthuli, of South Africa. A third Negro, Dr. Ralph J. Bunche, of the United States, was the 1950 winner. Dr. King, whose fight against racial discrimination has brought him many jail terms, will receive the prize at Oslo University on Dec. 10. ‘‘I do not consider this merely an honor to me personally, but a tribute to the discipline, wise restraint and majestic courage of the millions of gallant Negro and white persons of good will who have followed a nonviolent course in seeking to establish a reign of justice and a rule of love across this nation of ours,’’ he said. Dr. King was selected from a list proposed by former Peace Prize winners, members of governments and parliaments around the world and other dignitaries.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Oct. 15, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/blogs/15iht-oldoct15-MLK/15iht-oldoct15-MLK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 369, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/blogs/15iht-oldoct15-MLK/15iht-oldoct15-MLK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 369, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/blogs/15iht-oldoct15-MLK/15iht-oldoct15-MLK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/15/blogs/15iht-oldoct15-MLK/15iht-oldoct15-MLK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/blogs/15iht-oldoct15-MLK/15iht-oldoct15-MLK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Martin Luther King Jr. Awarded Nobel Peace Prize', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T14:49:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4d22ba7-3a25-5a8e-8184-53ed0fd059dd', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4d22ba7-3a25-5a8e-8184-53ed0fd059dd'}, {'abstract': 'Ann Romney speaks about a possible third presidential run by her husband, Mitt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/14/just-to-be-clear/', 'snippet': 'Ann Romney speaks about a possible third presidential run by her husband, Mitt.', 'lead_paragraph': '— Ann Romney, on a potential third presidential run by her husband, Mitt. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just to Be Clear . . .', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T14:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70fd583d-4c7d-5031-8227-e8eeced86937', 'word_count': 30, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70fd583d-4c7d-5031-8227-e8eeced86937'}, {'abstract': 'Yanira Castro brings music, dance and the audience into play with her work “Court/Garden.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/arts/dance/court-garden-an-interactive-work-from-yanira-castro.html', 'snippet': 'Yanira Castro brings music, dance and the audience into play with her work “Court/Garden.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sanctuary at St. Mark’s Church is a flexible space, configurable in any number of ways. If you frequent Danspace Project, you’ve probably seen dance from all sides of that room. But until Thursday, at the premiere of Yanira Castro’s “Court/Garden,” I had never been herded midperformance up onto the altar, a kind of limbo where the audience waited out a set change, a “labor spectacle,” the program called it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14torsi-1/14torsi-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14torsi-1/14torsi-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14torsi-1/14torsi-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14torsi-1/14torsi-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14torsi-1/14torsi-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14torsi-1/14torsi-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14torsi-1/14torsi-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spectacle Not Meant for Just Watching ', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Spectacle Not Meant for Just Watching ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danspace Project', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Yanira', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T14:52:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2a0c332-0ec7-5275-b7ed-1988dc766ce8', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2a0c332-0ec7-5275-b7ed-1988dc766ce8'}, {'abstract': 'The choreography of RoseAnne Spradlin was only one element in a multisensory program, “g-h-o-s-t- c-r-o-w-n,” at New York Live Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/arts/dance/roseanne-spradlins-g-h-o-s-t-c-r-o-w-n-working-title-.html', 'snippet': 'The choreography of RoseAnne Spradlin was only one element in a multisensory program, “g-h-o-s-t- c-r-o-w-n,” at New York Live Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From its title forward, RoseAnne Spradlin’s “g-h-o-s-t c-r-o-w-n (working title)” is extravagantly enigmatic. In one section, two dancers turn and leap like ballet bacchantes. In another, five dancers endure grueling variations on kicking and pivoting for 18 minutes. A Chinese silent film from 1931 is screened in fast forward. Bands of light arranged like hexagrams from the I Ching slice up the performers before they strip naked as newborns. A large metal sculpture looms onstage, an onion-like orb of concentric rings; when it rotates, its whirlpool patterns could induce hypnosis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14spradlin-1/14spradlin-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14spradlin-1/14spradlin-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14spradlin-1/14spradlin-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14spradlin-1/14spradlin-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14spradlin-1/14spradlin-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14spradlin-1/14spradlin-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/14spradlin-1/14spradlin-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cr