 France once coveted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/10/14/the-songbird-french-chefs-love-to-eat-reporters-notebook/', 'snippet': 'Liz Alderman provides an inside look at her reporting on an article about the controversy surrounding the ortolan, a tiny songbird that gourmands in France once coveted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liz Alderman wrote an article in The Times on Monday about the controversy surrounding the ortolan, a tiny songbird that gourmands in France once coveted and, by tradition, consumed in a single, steaming mouthful while covering their heads with white napkins to conceal the act. Here she provides an inside look at her reporting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Songbird French Chefs Love to Eat: Reporter’s Notebook', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alderman, Liz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T16:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/517bb5c9-01e2-5d24-b22e-545293be168d', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/517bb5c9-01e2-5d24-b22e-545293be168d'}, {'abstract': 'De Sade is the subject of two shows, one of which, at Musée d’Orsay, is being promoted with a video that has attracted a lot of attention.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/marquis-de-sade-in-paris-retains-the-power-to-shock/', 'snippet': 'De Sade is the subject of two shows, one of which, at Musée d’Orsay, is being promoted with a video that has attracted a lot of attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Two hundred years after his death, the Marquis de Sade, dark philosopher of libertines and sexual freedom, is making a comeback as a muse for art exhibitions, a video game and an unlikely museum trailer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/SADE/SADE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/SADE/SADE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/SADE/SADE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/SADE/SADE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1124, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/SADE/SADE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/SADE/SADE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/arts/SADE/SADE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marquis de Sade, in Paris, Retains the Power to Shock', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'p