e}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02513f23-3413-5c07-9491-64d9976e6250', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02513f23-3413-5c07-9491-64d9976e6250'}, {'abstract': 'T’s highlights from contemporary art’s biggest event across the pond, both inside and outside the tent at Regent’s Park.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/frieze-london-2014-preview/', 'snippet': 'T’s highlights from contemporary art’s biggest event across the pond, both inside and outside the tent at Regent’s Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While New York is counterintuitively learning to associate the word Frieze with spring’s defrosting (the successful May art fair on Randall’s Island now has three years under its belt, with another on the way), each year the original Frieze Art Fair held in London lands on autumn’s doorstep. The massive tent in Regent’s Park will open to the public for the twelfth time on Wednesday. Among the 162 galleries participating within, the menagerie of projects without and an entire capital’s span of exhibitions and events happening concurrently, here is T’s look ahead to some of Frieze week’s highlights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-frieze1/14symonds-frieze1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-frieze1/14symonds-frieze1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-frieze1/14symonds-frieze1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-frieze1/14symonds-frieze1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-frieze1/14symonds-frieze1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-frieze1/14symonds-frieze1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-frieze1/14symonds-frieze1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to See (and Hear, Taste and Smell) at Frieze London', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze Art Fair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Al-Maria, Sophia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Isabel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolaas, Sissel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Selfridges', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T18:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47798109-a527-5403-b5a1-b63d4324c058', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47798109-a527-5403-b5a1-b63d4324c058'}, {'abstract': 'The chef David Waltuck has moved on from Chanterelle and is writing a new script, filled with surprises, at Élan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/dining/restaurant-review-elan-in-the-flatiron-district.html', 'snippet': 'The chef David Waltuck has moved on from Chanterelle and is writing a new script, filled with surprises, at Élan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you remember David Waltuck’s cooking at Chanterelle, eating at his new restaurant, Élan, can be a little unnerving. Chanterelle, a downtown pioneer when it opened in 1979, was an institution by the time it went out of business, just a few months short of its 30th anniversary. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shedding the Burden of Tradition ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shedding the Burden of Tradition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flatiron District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'elan (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waltuck, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T18:16:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6ad4448-9b1d-51d4-9948-bf246bb1480a', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6ad4448-9b1d-51d4-9948-bf246bb1480a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Greenglass, whose testimony against his sister and brother-in-law, Ethel and Julius Rosenberg, in a 1951 spy trial helped send them to the electric chair, later admitted to lying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/us/david-greenglass-spy-who-helped-seal-the-rosenbergs-doom-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Greenglass, whose testimony against his sister and brother-in-law, Ethel and Julius Rosenberg, in a 1951 spy trial helped send them to the electric chair, later admitted to lying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the most notorious spy case of the Cold War — the conviction and execution of Julius and Ethel Rosenberg for passing atomic secrets to the Soviet Union — and it rested largely on the testimony of Ms. Rosenberg’s brother David Greenglass, whose name to many became synonymous with betrayal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/us/15GREENGLASS-hp/15GREENGLASS-hp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1027, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/us/15GREENGLASS-hp/15GREENGLASS-hp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1027}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/us/15GREENGLASS-hp/15GREENGLASS-hp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 599, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/us/15GREENGLASS-hp/15GREENGLASS-hp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1197, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/us/15GREENGLASS-hp/15GREENGLASS-hp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/14/us/15GREENGLASS-hp/15GREENGLASS-hp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7