 of Sept. 29 for the first time in over 260 weeks, it turns out that NBC News won that week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first fallout is in from the long-running misreporting of ratings by the Nielsen Company, and ABC News has lost its best story of the year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nielsen Recount Strips ABC News of Win Over NBC News', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nielsen Recount Strips ABC News of Win Over NBC News', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wurtzel, Alan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T18:23:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b91ddcc1-5c15-505d-a411-50dea3512ba5', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b91ddcc1-5c15-505d-a411-50dea3512ba5'}, {'abstract': 'Kansas becomes a tossup, and several key campaigns are trending toward the Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/upshot/gop-at-72-percent-to-take-senate-control.html', 'snippet': 'Kansas becomes a tossup, and several key campaigns are trending toward the Republicans.', 'lead