ytimes.com/2014/10/14/liberals-and-affirmative-consent/', 'snippet': 'Some thoughts on Ezra Klein’s fear-based argument for yes-means-yes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been fascinating to follow the\xa0various interventions, pro and con, surrounding\xa0the new “affirmative consent” standard for sexual assault\xa0on California’s college campuses and the collegiate approach to adjudicating rape allegations generally. The\xa0debate has\xa0divided the left\xa0against itself; it’s divided moderate\xa0liberals\xa0from what you might call\xa0the millennial left;\xa0it’s pitted\xa0conservatives\xa0against\xa0libertarians, and\xa0against each other.\xa0In this post I’m going to talk about the most interesting liberal argument in favor of the new standard (with another post to come on the most interesting conservative argument in its favor), which has been offered up\xa0by Vox’s Ezra Klein. It’s interesting because he concedes, upfront, that the California policy’s critics have a reasonable point:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberals and Affirmative Consent', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Ezra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T18:44:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/641df576-1a0d-53d0-a7fc-2b1b85ef8b93', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/641df576-1a0d-53d0-a7fc-2b1b85ef8b93'}, {'abstract': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton continued to laugh off questions about her presidential aspirations on Tuesday, but she did shed some light on what she thinks is wrong in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/14/clintons-diagnosis-of-whats-wrong-with-politics/', 'snippet': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton continued to laugh off questions about her presidential aspirations on Tuesday, but she did shed some light on what she thinks is wrong in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton continued to laugh off questions about her presidential aspirations on Tuesday, but she did shed some light on what she thinks is wrong in Washington. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton’s Diagnosis of What’s Wrong With Politics', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwab, Klaus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Salesforce.com Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T18:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/141b96c3-392b-5753-b2af-6843e883796f', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141b96c3-392b-5753-b2af-6843e883796f'}, {'abstract': 'The coffee purveyor has teamed up with its fellow Bay Area-based company Timbuk2 to create a travel kit.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/14/blue-bottle-coffee-timbuk2-kit/', 'snippet': 'The coffee purveyor has teamed up with its fellow Bay Area-based company Timbuk2 to create a travel kit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of Blue Bottle Coffee know that picking up a cup at one of its cafes is not an in-and-out experience, but rather a test of patience — the brew seeps through a Japanese filter slower than a leaking faucet. Still, devotees of the brand insist it’s worth the wait. And the same meticulous attention to craftsmanship informed the making of Blue Bottle’s first-ever coffee travel kit— created in collaboration with Timbuk2, another Bay Area-based company — which comes out tomorrow. For example, the custom-made zarfs (coffee-cup sleeves) included in the kit were tweaked when James Freeman, Blue Bottle’s founder and C.E.O., noticed during the design process that they sat too high on the cups and might touch a drinker’s lips.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-bluebottle/14symonds-bluebottle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-bluebottle/14symonds-bluebottle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-bluebottle/14symonds-bluebottle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/14/t-magazine/14symonds-bluebottle/14symonds-bluebottle-superJum