he 10-year-old design collective known for its meticulously curated new Californian lifestyle aesthetic, celebrates its anniversary with a self-titled monograph (Abrams, $60). The paperback book, encased in a hand-drawn graphic black-and-white slipcover,\xa0chronicles more than\xa025 projects the Los Angeles—based firm has undertaken, from residential bungalows in Los Angeles to retail spaces in New York to plates with Heath Ceramics. Roman Alonso, one of the four friends who founded Commune in 2004 (alongside Steven Johanknecht and the siblings Ramin and Pamela Shamshiri), opened up to T about the new tome, what their interiors really look like when not staged for a photo shoot and the firm’s relationship to the past —\xa0and its\xa0clients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commune’s Newest Design: a Coffee Table Tome', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alonso, Roman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commune', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-14T20:45:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua David Stein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Stein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09c6c1c4-7927-56d5-8e5f-0b98851fc047', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09c6c1c4-7927-56d5-8e5f-0b98851fc047'}, {'abstract': 'The hospital will treat any confirmed cases from within the public hospital system and also be able to receive transfers from private city hospitals or airports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/nyregion/bellevue-hospital-center-to-treat-new-york-citys-ebola-patients.html', 'snippet': 'The hospital will treat any confirmed cases from within the public hospital system and also be able to receive transfers from private city hospitals or airports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York’s premier public hospital will become a center for treatment of the Ebola virus in the city, hospital and city officials said on Tuesday, amid widespread concerns that the disease may not be so easily contained by every hospital that has an isolation unit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/world/BELLEVUE/BELLEVUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/world/BELLEVUE/BELLEVUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/world/BELLEVUE/BELLEVUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/world/BELLEVUE/BELLEVUE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/world/BELLEVUE/BELLEVUE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/15/world/BELLEVUE/BELLEVUE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 's