 Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f76bc4e-477b-53a0-838c-5beb10ca9970', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f76bc4e-477b-53a0-838c-5beb10ca9970'}, {'abstract': 'A look at data from the Federal Election Commission shows that TV ads continue to be important, though Internet spending has grown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/upshot/senate-races-where-outside-groups-spend-their-money.html', 'snippet': 'A look at data from the Federal Election Commission shows that TV ads continue to be important, though Internet spending has grown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For outside groups spending money in Senate races, television is still king. Although these independent groups have increased their investments in online ads and other Internet spending, the groups still spend most of their money on TV ads to reach voters, according to data in filings to the Federal Election Commission.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/upshot/16up-spending/16up-spending-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/upshot/16up-spending/16up-spending-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/upshot/16up-spending/16up-spending-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/upshot/16up-spending/16up-spending-superJumbo.jpg', 'height'