 Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bfe02cf-f9e9-52b0-a2fe-10a5b0f37e3a', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bfe02cf-f9e9-52b0-a2fe-10a5b0f37e3a'}, {'abstract': 'The iconic American photographer teamed up with Shinola to create a line of leashes, collars, toys and beds — to the delight of his own five pooches.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/bruce-weber-dog-accessories/', 'snippet': 'The iconic American photographer teamed up with Shinola to create a line of leashes, collars, toys and beds — to the delight of his own five pooches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early stages of developing a new collection of pet accessories in collaboration with the Detroit-based company Shinola, the photographer Bruce Weber hosted several members of the Shinola design team at his home. “They came to visit me and met all my dogs. I had just gotten back from California, where I met Lassie, so we were talking about Lassie a lot,” Weber explains, with a laugh. “That was the high point of my life, man!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruce Weber’s Photogenic Dog Accessories', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Bruce (1946- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shinola (Manhattan, NY, Retail Store)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montauk (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T15:05:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/155c4e61-7a0a-5f32-a92c-5f11bf4a8012', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/155c4e61-7a0a-5f32-a92c-5f11bf4a8012'}, {'abstract': 'Mohammad Sarfaraz Hussain, a New Yorker from Pakistan, was tagged for deportation at age 18 after complying with the post-Sept. 11 “special registration” program. Now Mr. Hussain, an E.M.T., is becoming a citizen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/nyregion/citizenship-after-22-years-in-new-york-and-threats-of-deportation.html', 'snippet': 'Mohammad Sarfaraz Hussain, a New Yorker from Pakistan, was tagged for deportation at age 18 after complying with the post-Sept. 11 “special registration” program. Now Mr. Hussain, an E.M.T., is becoming a citizen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He had left his native Pakistan for the United States at age 8 to see his dying mother. By 18, he was the star of his high school basketball team in Queens, so Americanized that as he waited with thousands of men to be fingerprinted and questioned at federal immigration headquarters, he had just one worry: missing basketball practice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/nyregion/CITIZEN/CITIZEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/nyregion/CITIZEN/CITIZEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/nyregion/CITIZEN/CITIZEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/nyregion/CITIZEN/CITIZEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/nyregion/CITIZEN/CITIZEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/16/nyregion/CITIZEN/CITIZEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/nyregion/CITIZEN/CITIZEN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Deportation Threats and a Long Wait, Citizenship for a Lifesaver', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Deportation Threats and a Long Wait, Citizenship for a Lifesaver', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Nina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussain, Mohammad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T15:07:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e92fbd5f-26f9-55de-82c0-66b16af8b2ec', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e92fbd5f-26f9-55de-82c0-66b16af8b2ec'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Calls for blockading slave trade in Africa were heard in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/1889-fight-slavery-with-fire/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Calls for blockading slave trade in Africa were heard in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conference for the extinction of the African slave trade will meet at Brussels on November 18. Mr. Huntington, our enterprising compatriot, and who is one of the founders of the Congo Railway, and one of the shareholders of the East African Company, published a short time ago a letter to show that slavery should be fought with fire. Mr. Huntington wishes to establish a vast police cordon. If this be done, it will be certain that slavery will receive its deathblow. — The New York Herald, European Edition, October 16, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1889: Fight Slavery With Fire', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T15:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', '