l': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77b370b1-47e9-5b6d-a2e1-f0778b5dcd82', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77b370b1-47e9-5b6d-a2e1-f0778b5dcd82'}, {'abstract': 'The two titles, Martha Stewart Living and Martha Stewart Weddings, will be pitched to advertisers along with 14 Meredith brands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/business/media/martha-stewarts-magazines-to-outsource-business-side-to-meredith.html', 'snippet': 'The two titles, Martha Stewart Living and Martha Stewart Weddings, will be pitched to advertisers along with 14 Meredith brands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia, which has been struggling to make its award-winning magazines profitable, is outsourcing its advertising, circulation and printing operations to the Meredith Corporation, the magazine giant that owns titles like Family Circle and EatingWell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Martha Stewart’s Magazines to Outsource Business Side to Meredith', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outsourcing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Meredith Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Martha', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T20:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/133084cc-3fca-56e4-b0b8-40891691eb25', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/133084cc-3fca-56e4-b0b8-40891691eb25'}, {'abstract': 'Since 1992, more than 20 neighborhood food halls have been remodeled in the Catalan capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/travel/in-barcelona-making-the-markets-fresh-again.html', 'snippet': 'Since 1992, more than 20 neighborhood food halls have been remodeled in the Catalan capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pere Sirvent strode into the food market in the Sants neighborhood of Barcelona on a recent morning and looked around with satisfaction. Under the vaulted ceiling of the 1913 building, which reopened in late spring after a four-year, 10-million-euro renovation, the fishmongers arranged ruddy wedges of tuna on crushed ice. Produce sellers bagged glistening cherries. At a large stall offering prepared foods, customers eyed the truita de patates, a crustless quiche made with potatoes.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BARCELONA1-sf/19BARCELONA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BARCELONA1-sf/19BARCELONA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BARCELONA1-sf/19BARCELONA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BARCELONA1-sf/19BARCELONA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BARCELONA1-sf/19BARCELONA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BARCELONA1-sf/19BARCELONA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BARCELONA1-sf/19BARCELONA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Barcelona, Making the Markets Fresh Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Market, to Market', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Margolies, Jane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Spain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T20:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Margolies', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Margolies', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17c65fec-7459-5def-935f-6e48348a500c', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17c65fec-7459-5def-935f-6e48348a500c'}, {'abstract': 'Avant-garde cooking is served at gentle prices at the latest venture from the prolific young chef José Avillez.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/travel/restaurant-report-mini-bar-in-lisbon-.html', 'snippet': 'Avant-garde cooking is served at gentle prices at the latest venture from the prolific young chef José Avillez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The evening began with a cocktail, of sorts: a margarita vacuum-packed inside an apple slice, topped with the sea salt and chile powder typically destined for the rim of a glass. It set the tone at Mini Bar, a casual spot that opened on a steep slope in Lisbon’s Chiado neighborhood last summer. The food is modern, playful and features the sort of trompe l’oeil presentation that, while new to the Portuguese capital, is now commonly found in cities around the world.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BITES/19Bites-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BITES/19Bites-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BITES/19Bites-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BITES/19Bites-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BITES/19Bites-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BITES/19Bites-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/travel/19BITES/19Bites-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Report: Mini Bar in Lisbon  ', 'kicker': 'Bites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Borrowing From Barcelona', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lisbon (Portugal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T20:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Cheshes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cheshes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27013c15-ab8f-577e-bf3b-f03f37c147b0', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27013c15-ab8f-577e-bf3b-f03f37c147b0'}, {'abstract': 'Thoughts on political self-interest, ideology and crisis management.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/the-politics-of-ebola/', 'snippet': 'Thoughts on political self-interest, ideology and crisis management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It looks like I’ll have reason to write more on this issue soon, but as we reckon with the rather extraordinary incompetence of the authorities, local and national, in the face of just one Ebola case from overseas, I thought I’d say something about the argument here, from Jonathan Last, speculating about an ideological element in the administration’s approach to the disease. This point in particular, about the White House’s reluctance to institute a travel ban, is a version of something I’ve heard a lot of conservatives raise and float and talk about of late:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Politics of Ebola', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T20:16:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31e0ba26-d51a-51a4-9a89-a8055512d6b2', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31e0ba26-d51a-51a4-9a89-a8055512d6b2'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s grant in humanistic photography goes to Joseph Sywenkyj, who has spent years documenting one family’s struggle in Ukraine. It is not, he said, a story of quick change or fast healing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/10/15/blogs/20141015-lens-smith.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s grant in humanistic photography goes to Joseph Sywenkyj, who has spent years documenting one family’s struggle in Ukraine. It is not, he said, a story of quick change or fast healing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year’s grant in humanistic photography goes to Joseph Sywenkyj, who has spent years documenting one family’s struggle in Ukraine. It is not, he said, a story of quick change or fast healing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/blogs/20141015-lens-smith-slide-5RYX/20141015-lens-smith-slide-5RYX-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/blogs/20141015-lens-smith-slide-5RYX/20141