'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8121f74e-d616-5eb2-84d2-05053af1c09f', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8121f74e-d616-5eb2-84d2-05053af1c09f'}, {'abstract': 'DeMarco Murray’s record-setting pace for rushing attempts may not continue, but he remains a top fantasy play at running back, particularly against the Giants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/sports/football/fantasy-football-week-7-favorable-and-unfavorable-matchups.html', 'snippet': 'DeMarco Murray’s record-setting pace for rushing attempts may not continue, but he remains a top fantasy play at running back, particularly against the Giants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The workhorse running back is dead! Long live the workhorse running back?', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: Week 7 Matchups', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Promising Day for Versatile Quarterbacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sablich, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sablich, Justin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Carson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tannehill, Ryan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellington, Andre', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, DeMarco', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T20:32:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Sablich and Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca320134-fb11-5206-834f-28fa9a8877a6', 'word_count': 1984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca320134-fb11-5206-834f-28fa9a8877a6'}, {'abstract': 'A new show at the Skirball Center features all the usual juggling, acrobatics and feats of derring-do — in a charming, bearded new context.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/15/cirque-alfonse-artisanal-circus/', 'snippet': 'A new show at the Skirball Center features all the usual juggling, acrobatics and feats of derring-do — in a charming, bearded new context.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, NYU’s Skirball Center has made itself a prime venue for a very niche form of entertainment: contemporary circus arts from Quebec, whose legendary National Circus School has spawned not only the glitzily famous Cirque du Soleil but a slew of smaller, more DIY companies, such as Cirque Eloize, which performed at Skirball last winter. Now through Sunday comes Cirque Alfonse’s “Timber,” which takes circusry to an artisanal, organic extreme. The troupe —\xa0which hails from the sylvan-paradise village of Saint-Alphonse-Rodriguez and is composed largely of burly, bearded fellas who lift themselves and one another into the air in various improbable configurations, plus three generations of family members, from a lovably cranky grandpa right down to an adorable mop-haired tyke — makes all of its sets and equipment from wood and other materials found on its own farm. The stage has an indie-woodsy look for which most Brooklyn coffee-shop owners would sacrifice their flannel and Red Wings. And the performers come by this show’s name the hard way: over the course of its hour-plus run time, no end of sharp-edged hatchets and giant crosscut saws are juggled, tossed and spun — often mere, unnerving inches away from those bushy beards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Québécois Circusry, Artisanal Edition', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque Alfonse', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Timber (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T20:33:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65ce22eb-cf86-5b02-9649-9c62f938d95d', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65ce22eb-cf86-5b02-9649-9c62f938d95d'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement of the tablets, which are expected to have significant upgrades, is coming as sales have slowed and competition has toughened.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/technology/apple-set-to-unveil-new-ipads.html', 'snippet': 'The announcement of the tablets, which are expected to have significant upgrades, is coming as sales have slowed and competition has toughened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Consumers around the world seem to have an endless appetite for new versions of Apple’s iPhone. But that hearty taste hasn’t