ck-and-white tile floor modeled on the old store’s and mixes new and classic designs with vintage items (cookbooks, a brass duck press) like those he once sold. There is also a cooking school and an edible garden, and the house behind the shop where Mr. Williams once lived has also been incorporated.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS5/1016CURRENTS5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS5/1016CURRENTS5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 323}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS5/1016CURRENTS5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS5/1016CURRENTS5-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1102, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS5/1016CURRENTS5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS5/1016CURRENTS5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS5/1016CURRENTS5-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back to the Cutting Board', 'kicker': 'Currents: Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back to the Cutting Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sonoma (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams-Sonoma Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T21:54:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e5b24f3-a5ae-5786-9713-6e968b2a21fc', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e5b24f3-a5ae-5786-9713-6e968b2a21fc'}, {'abstract': 'From Workstead, a Brooklyn studio, campaign furniture that is easily taken apart and carried.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/garden/for-that-battlefield-known-as-the-living-room-.html', 'snippet': 'From Workstead, a Brooklyn studio, campaign furniture that is easily taken apart and carried.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workstead, a Brooklyn studio that designs lighting suggestive of 20th-century factory interiors, looked to another epoch and environment for its first chair. “We were impressed by campaign furniture,” said Robert Highsmith, who founded the studio with Stefanie Brechbuehler, his wife. Easily disassembled and carried between battlefields, such pieces were popular with 19th-century British soldiers.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/g