_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/garden/secret-lives-and-personas-now-up-for-auction.html', 'snippet': 'A flea-market find of 340 photographs of the cross-dressing men of Casa Susanna is to be auctioned this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was more than a decade ago that Robert Swope came across a startling cache of photos at the 26th Street flea market: hundreds of images of men dressed cozily as women, engaging in domestic pursuits like putting on makeup, having dinner or playing Scrabble. He and his partner, Michel Hurst, longtime midcentury-furniture dealers, soon learned that these were the men of Casa Susanna, a weekend safe haven in the Catskills for early ’60s cross-dressers. Mr. Swope and Mr. Hurst collected 120 of the photos into a book, published in 2005 by Powerhouse and now in its third printing. The photos even inspired a Broadway play, “Casa Valentina,” by Harvey Fierstein, which opened last spring. Now, Mr. Hurst and Mr. Swope are selling all 340 images at auction at Wright in Chicago on Oct. 30, hoping an institution will buy them for public display. “There’s a special magic seeing the pictures in person,” Mr. Swope said. The New York preview is Oct. 16 to 30 at Wright, 980 Madison Avenue (77th Street); 212-585-0200 or wright20.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS2/1016CURRENTS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 861, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS2/1016CURRENTS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 861}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/garden/1016CURRENTS2/1016CURRENTS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0