: 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4233fda6-b6d0-56e7-9195-edd2d0beb578', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4233fda6-b6d0-56e7-9195-edd2d0beb578'}, {'abstract': 'The virus’s genome is already online. You just need the right lab.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/opinion/resurrecting-smallpox-easier-than-you-think.html', 'snippet': 'The virus’s genome is already online. You just need the right lab.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — ON Oct. 16, 1975, 3-year-old Rahima Banu of Bangladesh became the last human infected with naturally occurring smallpox (variola major). When her immune system killed the last smallpox virus in her body, it also killed the last such smallpox virus in humans. In what is arguably mankind’s greatest achievement, smallpox was eradicated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/opinion/1016OPEDbajtlik/1016OPEDbajtlik-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/opinion/1016OPEDbajtlik/1016OPEDbajtlik-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/opinion/1016OPEDbajtlik/1016OPEDbajtlik-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/opinion/1016OPEDbajtlik/1016OPEDbajtlik-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/opinion/1016OPEDbajtlik/1016OPEDbajtlik-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thu