/10/16/opinion/ending-this-fee-for-all.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators must get tougher on the hidden charges that assail consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBUS, Ohio — LAST week, AT&T agreed to pay $80 million to customers who had been overbilled for charges they had not authorized. This was an all-too-rare case of a perpetrator brought to book: In recent decades, Americans have increasingly been hit with fees they know nothing about, which have contributed to a crisis of consumer debt. We must hope we are entering a new era of regulatory activism that will shine a light on hidden fees. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ending This Fee for All', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ending This Fee for All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fergus, Devin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-15T23:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Devin Fergus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Devin', 'middlename': 