f-life.html', 'snippet': 'The director Jorge R. Gutierrez and the art director Paul J. Sullivan describe how Mexican folk art influenced the look of “The Book of Life.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Mexican folk art to Sergio Leone to Radiohead, the director Jorge R. Gutierrez reached far and wide for inspiration in making “The Book of Life,” his first 3-D animated feature. The story of a woman and the two men who pine for her in a small Mexican village is at the heart of this mythic adventure, which has tinges of spaghetti westerns and makes room for magic, bullfighting and pop music.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hand-Carved Love Triangle ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hand-Carved Love Triangle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Mekado', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gutierrez, Jorge R (1975- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Paul J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Book of Life (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T00:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfab3618-4645-5175-abf3-9e7df1b61d3c', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfab3618-4645-5175-abf3-9e7df1b61d3c'}, {'abstract': 'In a strongly worded complaint, the lawyers contend that the “new G.M.” that emerged from bankruptcy in 2009 so valued cost-cutting that it “produced an inordinate number of vehicles with serious safety defects.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/business/class-action-case-accuses-gm-of-neglect-beyond-ignition-switch.html', 'snippet': 'In a strongly worded complaint, the lawyers contend that the “new G.M.” that emerged from bankruptcy in 2009 so valued cost-cutting that it “produced an inordinate number of vehicles with serious safety defects.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers in sweeping class-action litigation against General Motors have significantly broadened their case against the embattled automaker, claiming that the company disregarded and concealed safety issues far beyond the defective ignition switch that is now linked to 27 deaths. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/business/Motors/Motors-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/business/Motors/Motors-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/business/Motors/Motors-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/business/Motors/Motors-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/business/Motors/Motors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/16/business/Motors/Motors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/business/Motors/Motors-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Class-Action Case Accuses G.M. of Neglect Beyond Ignition Switch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Class-Action Case Accuses G.M. of Neglect Beyond Ignition Switch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T00:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Stout', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stout', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9025334e-c55d-586f-bd5c-4adf9f8a3710', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9025334e-c55d-586f-bd5c-4adf9f8a3710'}, {'abstract': 'The order will allow more clinics offering safe and legal abortion to continue operating pending a final court resolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/opinion/the-supreme-court-acts-for-texas-women.html', 'snippet': 'The order will allow more clinics offering safe and legal abortion to continue operating pending a final court resolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a brief unsigned order on Tuesday, the Supreme Court acted to prevent Texas from enforcing two key parts of the state’s 2013 package of extreme new abortion restrictions. While the legal battle over the provisions continues, and is very likely to land back at the court before long, the order was a significant victory for women in Texas. The important result is that it will allow more clinics offering safe and legal abortion care to continue operating pending a final court resolution. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Supreme Court Acts for Texas Women ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Supreme Court Acts for Texas Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T01:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9424f22-c936-5fd4-b42b-631ea4b73642', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9424f22-c936-5fd4-b42b-631ea4b73642'}, {'abstract': 'Infection control experts say many American hospitals have improperly trained their staffs to deal with Ebola patients because they were following federal guidelines that were too lax.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/us/lax-us-guidelines-on-ebola-led-to-poor-hospital-training-experts-say.html', 'snippet': 'Infection control experts say many American hospitals have improperly trained their staffs to deal with Ebola patients because they were following federal guidelines that were too lax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many American hospitals have improperly trained their staffs to deal with Ebola patients because they were following federal g