et': 'An investigation in The Times exposed shocking failings by the Pentagon that allowed highly dangerous chemical weapons to be left behind in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another chapter has been added to the dismal legacy of America’s involvement in Iraq. An investigation by C.J. Chivers, published in The Times on Wednesday, found that American and American-trained Iraqi troops discovered thousands of abandoned and highly dangerous chemical weapons left over from the rule of Saddam Hussein. These weapons, found from 2004 to 2011, wounded troops from both armies. There are now fears that some could fall into the hands of fighters for the Islamic State, which now controls much of the territory where the weapons were found.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/opinion/nyto-1016chemical/nyto-1016chemical-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/opinion/nyto-1016chemical/nyto-1016chemical-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/opinion/nyto-1016chemical/nyto-1016chemical-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 509, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/opinion/nyto-1016chemical/nyto-1016chemical-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/opinion/nyto-1016chemical/nyto-1016chemical-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard'