iew', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/813d3780-3aa5-5a7b-af20-1419a53e638c', 'word_count': 1373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/813d3780-3aa5-5a7b-af20-1419a53e638c'}, {'abstract': 'Justin Simien’s “Dear White People” explores the hypocrisy, awkward good will and unwitting racism that hamper relations between white and black students at a fictional Ivy League school.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/movies/dear-white-people-about-racial-hypocrisy-at-a-college.html', 'snippet': 'Justin Simien’s “Dear White People” explores the hypocrisy, awkward good will and unwitting racism that hamper relations between white and black students at a fictional Ivy League school.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dear White People” is the name of Justin Simien’s first feature film, and I’ll say right away that it is as smart and fearless a debut as I have seen from an American filmmaker in quite some time: knowing but not snarky, self-aware but not solipsistic, open to influence and confident in its own originality. It’s a clever campus comedy that juggles a handful of hot potatoes — race, sex, privilege, power — with elegant agility and only an occasional fumble. You want to see this movie, and you will want to talk about it afterward, even if the conversation feels a little awkward. If it doesn’t, you’re doing it wrong. There is great enjoyment to be found here, and very little comfort.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE/JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE/JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE/JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE/JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1205, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE/17JPDEARWHITEPEOPLE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advanced Course in Diversity', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Advanced Course in Diversity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simien, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Tessa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dear White People (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parris, Teyonah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_nam