 an email from the mother of a student I taught a few years ago. Her son is away, so she decided to clean out her temporarily empty nest of the remnants of her son’s past life. She found his middle school backpack in a closet, and down at the bottom, amid the crumpled and squashed detritus, was a still-sealed thank you note from me, written in 2012. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/us/motherlode-organization1/motherlode-organization1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/us/motherlode-organization1/motherlode-organization1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/us/motherlode-organization1/motherlode-organization1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/us/motherlode-organization1/motherlode-organization1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/us/motherlode-organization1/motherlode-organization1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/15/us/motherlode-organization1/motherlode-organization1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/us/motherlode-organization1/motherlode-organization1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mid-Semester Organization Regroup', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Lahey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lahey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/909ba902-d6a5-588a-a41f-74975ce17fdb', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/909ba902-d6a5-588a-a41f-74975ce17fdb'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy loses its foreign minister in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/1914-italys-foreign-minister-is-dead/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy loses its foreign minister in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Marchese di San Giuliano, Italy’s veteran Minister of Foreign Affairs, whose ill-health and indecision have been dictating the Italian policy of ‘‘wait-and-see,’’ died at twenty minutes past two this afternoon [Oct. 16]. He had struggled heroically to stick to his post and disregarded his doctors’ imperative orders to take a long rest. But his condition lately became rapidly worse, and a few days ago all hope of his recovery was abandoned. King Victor Emmanuel had repeatedly inquired as to his condition through the Prefect of the Royal Palace. Signor Salandra, the Premier, will, for the present, take over the portfolio of Foreign Affairs.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Oct. 17, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/blogs/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 367, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/blogs/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/blogs/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/17/blogs/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/blogs/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano/17iht-oldoct17-SanGiuliano-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Italy’s Foreign Minister Is Dead', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecc76a9a-0d99-50d6-8bff-72812e5762dc', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc76a9a-0d99-50d6-8bff-72812e5762dc'}, {'abstract': 'A congressional committee criticized the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, as officials said Nina Pham, a nurse infected with Ebola, would be transferred to a specialized unit in Maryland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/us/ebola-dallas-texas-presbyterian-hospital-apology.html', 'snippet': 'A congressional committee criticized the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, as officials said Nina Pham, a nurse infected with Ebola, would be transferred to a specialized unit in Maryland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Facing sharp questioning at a Congressional hearing on Thursday about the troubled handling of Ebola cases in the United States, federal health officials said that a nurse with Ebola would be transferred to a specialized unit at the National Institutes of Health in Maryland, to ease the burden of the Dallas hospital where she became infected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Scrutinizes Handling of Ebola Cases in Texas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress Scrutinizes Handling of Ebola Cases in Texas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Health Presbyterian Hospital', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:17:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13cde9e9-c16a-5b55-9680-887e2f620da4', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13cde9e9-c16a-5b55-9680-887e2f620da4'}, {'abstract': 'This episode of “Living City,” a video series about New York’s infrastructure, looks at the network of 19 reservoirs that make up the New York City watershed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/nyregion/new-york-city-water-supply.html', 'snippet': 'This episode of “Living City,” a video series about New York’s infrastructure, looks at the network of 19 reservoirs that make up the New York City watershed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is considered the gold standard of urban water systems. It covers parts of eight New York counties and a sliver of Connecticut. It includes 19 reservoirs and three controlled lakes, which can be used to feed the water supply. It has the capacity to hold approximately 580 billion gallons of water. And 9.4 million people depend on it when they turn on their taps.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Marvel of Engineering Meets the Needs of a Thirsty New York', 'kicker': 'Living City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reservoirs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catskills (NYS Area)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:24:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_