//article/f0c8b46e-8f4f-51a1-b97e-b4eeeb06349b'}, {'abstract': 'NBC has decided to cancel “Mission Control” before it makes what was expected to be a mid-season debut.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/houston-we-really-have-a-problem-tv-series-canceled-before-it-airs/', 'snippet': 'NBC has decided to cancel “Mission Control” before it makes what was expected to be a mid-season debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New TV shows, even troubled ones, typically get an airing or two before networks cancel them. But NBC has decided to abort “Mission Control,” a comedy from Will Ferrell and Adam McKay’s production company, months before its expected midseason debut, according to The Hollywood Reporter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Houston, We Really Have a Problem: TV Series Canceled Before It Airs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrell, Will', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKay, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ritter, Krysten', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:39:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lorne Manly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lorne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4bec045-2706-59ac-b498-53b2c2e5ed3b', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4bec045-2706-59ac-b498-53b2c2e5ed3b'}, {'abstract': 'Until now, a video about a class of Palestinian children who hoped to compete in a music competition in East Jerusalem has never been published.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/10/16/when-a-story-becomes-a-casualty-of-war/', 'snippet': 'Until now, a video about a class of Palestinian children who hoped to compete in a music competition in East Jerusalem has never been published.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past spring, Erica Berenstein, a New York Times video journalist, and Fares Akram, a contributing writer based in Gaza, reported on a class of Palestinian children who hoped to compete in a music competition in East Jerusalem. Shortly after the story was completed, war broke out in Gaza, and the video’s tone felt inappropriate. The fighting continued and communication with the story’s subjects shifted from fact-checking to checking on the children’s safety. Until now, the video was never published. Here is the story of how it was made:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Story Becomes a Casualty of War', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Jerusalem', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:49:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Berenstein and Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80b51add-88a4-58b7-a38b-9939e84f7bb9', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80b51add-88a4-58b7-a38b-9939e84f7bb9'}, {'abstract': 'Madeleine Albright gets her own Wheaties box.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/16/move-over-michael-jordan/', 'snippet': 'Madeleine Albright gets her own Wheaties box.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First Draft is calling every grocery store in America to see if they’re being sold to the public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Move Over, Michael Jordan', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cereals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALBRIGHT, MADELEINE K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T14:56:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c5a206f-ac41-5eff-994d-92f904031ecb', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c5a206f-ac41-5eff-994d-92f904031ecb'}, {'abstract': 'Suha Arraf, who directed “Villa Touma,” identified her film as Palestinian at the Venice Film Festival. Israel, which helped finance it, objected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/movies/israel-and-suha-arraf-differ-on-nationality-of-villa-touma.html', 'snippet': 'Suha Arraf, who directed “Villa Touma,” identified her film as Palestinian at the Venice Film Festival. Israel, which helped finance it, objected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like most film festivals around the world, the Toronto International Film Festival provides audiences with standard information about the movies on its menu: screening dates and times, duration, director. Also, nationality: The 366 films at last month’s festival came from 70 countries; each of the films had a geographic designation. All, that is, except one.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19VILLA1/19VILLA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19VILLA1/19VILLA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 323}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19VILLA1/19VILLA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19VILLA1/19VILLA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1103, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19VILLA1/19VILLA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19VILLA1/19VILLA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19VILLA1/19VILLA1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hand That Feeds Bites Back ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hand That Feeds Bites Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arraf, Suha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aceea838-e9ee-5c9d-9581-c59bba4d8ef3', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aceea838-e9ee-5c9d-9581-c59bba4d8ef3'}, {'abstract': 'In the dyspeptic comedy “Listen Up Philip,” Jason Schwartzman plays a shabby, self-loathing novelist whose agonies affect everyone around him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/movies/listen-up-philip-with-jason-schwartzman.html', 'snippet': 'In the dyspeptic comedy “Listen Up Philip,” Jason Schwartzman plays a shabby, self-loathing novelist whose agonies affect everyone around him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the biliously, often hilariously funny tragicomedy “Listen Up Philip,” the alternately self-regarding and self-loathing novelist played in 50 shades of black by a peerless Jason Schwartzman stalks New York like a madman or, perhaps, a murderer. Philip Lewis Friedman doesn’t have blood on his hands (at least not yet), though he routinely goes in for the kill. If he looked shabbier, less domesticated, he could be mistaken for one of those thrown-away men who roam city streets muttering into the void of other people’s indifference. When the movie opens, he seems willfully teetering on the edge of that terrible darkness, inching ever closer to its maw with each furiously detonated word. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/arts/listen1/listen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/arts/listen1/listen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/arts/listen1/listen1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/arts/listen1/listen1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/arts/listen1/listen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/16/arts/listen1/listen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/arts/listen1/listen1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He Suffers for Art, and Forces Everyone Around Him to Do So', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Suffers for Art, and Forces Everyone Around Him to Do So', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 