Carolina has become the most southern state where same-sex marriage is clearly legal, and dozens of gay couples have wasted no time getting married. But conservatives are still waging a desperate rear-guard action to prevent it — at considerable cost to the taxpayers — and one of them happens to be the Republican candidate for senator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In North Carolina, Thom Tillis is the Last Holdout Against Gay Marriage', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tillis, Thomas R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T16:02:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b4d6dea-3152-597f-80b9-f99bb25f60e3', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b4d6dea-3152-597f-80b9-f99bb25f60e3'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Luck joins Peyton Manning and Aaron Rodgers in Tier 1 for quarterbacks this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/sports/football/fantasy-football-week-7-player-tiers.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Luck joins Peyton Manning and Aaron Rodgers in Tier 1 for quarterbacks this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this statistical model, I apply a clustering algorithm called the Gaussian mixture model to an aggregation of expert ranking data provided by Fantasypros.com. The algorithm finds natural tiers and clusters within the data. The charts that result visualize the tiers and help you decide your starting lineup each week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: Week 7 Player Tiers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T16:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Boris Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Boris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d257cb2d-8cd9-5522-b3c7-684aae1057d0', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d257cb2d-8cd9-5522-b3c7-684aae1057d0'}, {'abstract': 'Anas Haqqani, a son of the group’s founder, and Hafiz Rashid, a senior commander who coordinated suicide attacks, could become bargaining chips for the new Afghan government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/world/asia/haqqani-leaders-arrested-afghanistan-khost.html', 'snippet': 'Anas Haqqani, a son of the group’s founder, and Hafiz Rashid, a senior commander who coordinated suicide attacks, could become bargaining chips for the new Afghan government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — In a blow to a major component of the Taliban insurgency, two senior leaders of the Haqqani Network, a group responsible for numerous attacks against the Afghan government and its Western allies, were reported to be in Afghan custody on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/world/AFGHANISTAN-1/AFGHANISTAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'h