ct': 'This Japanese photographer is exhibiting pictures she took of personal artifacts from the victims of the 1945 atomic bombing of Hiroshima.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/arts/design/ishiuchi-miyako-here-and-now-atomic-bomb-artifacts-hiroshima-1945-2007.html', 'snippet': 'This Japanese photographer is exhibiting pictures she took of personal artifacts from the victims of the 1945 atomic bombing of Hiroshima.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much of Ishiuchi Miyako’s photography since the 1970s has been about her past. In three different series, she revisited the industrial port city of Yokosuka, Japan, near where she was born in 1947. In 2005, she exhibited a pictorial inventory of personal items that had been owned by her mother, who had died five years earlier. The pictures in her current solo are from a collective past, a wrenching episode in her country’s history, the American bombing of Hiroshima on Aug. 6, 1945.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5/MIYAKO1-GALLERY5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non