None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/623b5d44-61cf-54e6-a0c3-6fe89e5c16a9', 'word_count': 1505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/623b5d44-61cf-54e6-a0c3-6fe89e5c16a9'}, {'abstract': 'In “Being Mortal: Medicine and What Matters in the End,” Atul Gawande explores how to bring meaning and purpose to the last phase of life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/arts/being-mortal-by-atul-gawande.html', 'snippet': 'In “Being Mortal: Medicine and What Matters in the End,” Atul Gawande explores how to bring meaning and purpose to the last phase of life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Atul Gawande’s “Being Mortal: Medicine and What Matters in the End” introduces its author as a myopically confident medical school student whose seminar in doctor-patient interaction spent an hour on Tolstoy’s novella “The Death of Ivan Ilyich.” As a young man, he was not ready to understand the title character’s loneliness, suffering and desire to be pitied. He saw medical compassion as a given and Ivan Ilyich’s condition as something modern medicine could probably cure. He and his fellow students cared about acquiring knowledge and competence. They did not see mortality as part of the medical equation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPBOOKGAWANDE/17JPBOOKGAWANDE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPBOOKGAWANDE/17JPBOOKGAWANDE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPBOOKGAWANDE/JPBOOKGAWANDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPBOOKGAWANDE/JPBOOKGAWANDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPBOOKGAWANDE/JPBOOKGAWANDE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Prescription for Life’s Final Stretch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Prescription for Life’s Final Stretch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gawande, Atul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Being Mortal: Medicine and What Matters in the End (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T21:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ee3da6-dadb-5983-8c14-d51afe2ddc3e', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ee3da6-dadb-5983-8c14-d51afe2ddc3e'}, {'abstract': '“Foo Fighters: Sonic Highways” on HBO is tied into the band’s coming album, but is a blend of travelogue, history and music that can stand on its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/arts/television/dave-grohl-in-foo-fighters-sonic-highways-on-hbo.html', 'snippet': '“Foo Fighters: Sonic Highways” on HBO is tied into the band’s coming album, but is a blend of travelogue, history and music that can stand on its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reviewing a Foo Fighters concert in 2003, Jon Pareles wrote in The New York Times that they had the “virtues of journeymen: conviction and tenacity.” That description also applies to the fledgling filmmaking career of the band’s founder, Dave Grohl. You could add generosity and, up to a point, modesty. As a director, he’s less a frontman than a skilled and reliable session player.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPFOO/JPFOO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPFOO/JPFOO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPFOO/JPFOO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPFOO/JPFOO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPFOO/JPFOO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPFOO/JPFOO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17JPFOO/JPFOO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Musical History Tour Is Dying to Take You Away', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Musical History Tour Is Dying to Take You Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grohl, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foo Fighters', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Foo Fighters: Sonic Highways (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T21:44:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/57f1e2de-3012-5c43-b8f6-3f063bfc056c', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57f1e2de-3012-5c43-b8f6-3f063bfc056c'}, {'abstract': 'The “Masters of Hawaiian Music” tour, featuring George Kahumoku Jr., Ledward Kaapana and Uncle Richard Ho‘opi‘i, brought folklore and island memory to SubCulture on Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/arts/music/masters-of-hawaiian-music-play-at-subculture.html', 'snippet': 'The “Masters of Hawaiian Music” tour, featuring George Kahumoku Jr., Ledward Kaapana and Uncle Richard Ho‘opi‘i, brought folklore and island memory to SubCulture on Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During a handful of small, transcendent moments in “Masters of Hawaiian Music,” at SubCulture on Wednesday night, the line between craftsmanship and showmanship blurred to the point of irrelevance. The concert’s distinguished artists — George Kahumoku Jr. and Ledward Kaapana on guitars, and Uncle Richard Ho‘opi‘i on ukulele — played and sang in a traditional Hawaiian mode, bringing folklore and cultural memory into a performance that unfolded as breezy entertainment. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17SLACKKEY/17SLACKKEY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17SLACKKEY/17SLACKKEY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17SLACKKEY/17SLACKKEY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17SLACKKEY/17SLACKKEY-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1288, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17SLACKKEY/17SLACKKEY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17SLACKKEY/17SLACKKEY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/arts/17SLACKKEY/17SLACKKEY-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Virtuosic Keepers of a Cultural Flame', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virtuosic Keepers of a Cultural Flame', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Ho'opi'i, Richard", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahumoku, George Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaapana, Ledward', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T21:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d76f781-d130-51eb-bc12-c8e8088af6e7', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d76f781-d130-51eb-bc12-c8e8088af6e7'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Ballet presented the New York premiere of Jean-Pierre Frohlich’s “Varied Trio (in four),” set to the colorful music of Lou Harrison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/arts/dance/city-ballet-presents-varied-trio-in-four-.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City Ballet presented the New York premiere of Jean-Pierre Frohlich’s “Varied Trio (in four),” set to the colorful music of Lou Harrison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s good to hear the music of the American composer Lou Harrison at New York City Ballet. His sense of instrumental color, his feeling for both folk vitality and Asian delicacy, his modernist adaptations of classic forms always rinse the aural palate. On Wednesday at the David H. Koch Theater, City Ballet gave the New York premiere of a 14-minute pas de deux by Jean-Pierre Frohlich set to Harrison’s Varied Trio for piano, violin and percussion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '