ng a lovable-neurotic shtick. It’s clear he’d be better off undead.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Selfish Slob to Sex God', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer of Blood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tukel, Onur', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Summer of Blood (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T22:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4a0b675-49fd-5174-ba12-1247aceb4b10', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4a0b675-49fd-5174-ba12-1247aceb4b10'}, {'abstract': 'A meeting of geologists and other analysts explores whether Earth has entered a geological age made by humans.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/does-the-anthropocene-the-age-of-humans-deserve-a-golden-spike/', 'snippet': 'A meeting of geologists and other analysts explores whether Earth has entered a geological age made by humans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — I just participated in\xa0the first face-to-face meeting of the Anthropocene Working Group, a subset of a branch of\xa0the International Commission on Stratigraphy\xa0examining whether humanity’s growth spurt (in both numbers and resource appetites) has caused sufficient change to Earth systems to leave a discernible trace in layered rocks that will build and endure far into the future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credi