ef-14e7-51e4-becc-67c767b8bbea'}, {'abstract': 'The debate over women’s careers is ignoring the medical reality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/opinion/dont-depend-on-those-frozen-eggs.html', 'snippet': 'The debate over women’s careers is ignoring the medical reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you’re a woman worried about how to balance work and family, it’s a good time to job-hunt in Silicon Valley. This week it was revealed that Facebook and Apple will include egg freezing in their benefits packages. After receiving your job offer, you can order your hormone shots and be on your way to stashing away some good eggs so you can ascend to Sheryl Sandberg-esque greatness and still have a chance of having a biological family in your 40s and beyond. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Depend on Those Frozen Eggs', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Depend on Those Frozen Eggs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egg Donation and Freezing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Sarah Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T23:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Elizabeth Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Elizabeth', 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d6b2206-095a-5ffa-9b92-94c4d25880bb', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d6b2206-095a-5ffa-9b92-94c4d25880bb'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, as more investors fled Greek bonds, they drove the government’s long-term borrowing costs to nearly 9 percent — up from 7 percent on Wednesday and the highest level since January.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/business/international/eu-praise-for-greece-fails-to-stem-bond-sell-off.html', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, as more investors fled Greek bonds, they drove the government’s long-term borrowing costs to nearly 9 percent — up from 7 percent on Wednesday and the highest level since January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Just a few months ago, Greece appeared to be on the road to recovery. But in recent days it has helped stir up a storm in European bond markets as investors realized that Athens might not be on such a firm path after all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.U. Praise for Greece Fails to Stem Bond Sell-Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-16T23:46:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aa94544-184e-56fa-8ec6-17ef0191c5fa', 'word_count': 1200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aa94544-184e-56fa-8ec6-17ef0191c5fa'}, {'abstract': 'The social network, which allows users to post updates without using their real names, is facing criticism that it promises more privacy than it’s capable of delivering.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/16/privacy-questions-emerge-for-the-social-app-whisper/', 'snippet': 'The social network, which allows users to post updates without using their real names, is facing criticism that it promises more privacy than it’s capable of delivering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is often said that anonymity is impossible on the Internet, yet Whisper — a young social media start-up based in Southern California — has generated attention for saying it can do just that. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/technology/16bits-whisper/16bits-whisper-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 258, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/technology/16bits-whisper/16bits-whisper-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 258, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/technology/16bits-whisper/16bits-whisper-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/16/technology/16bits-whisper/16bits-whisper-t