alry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/17/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 770}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1597, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/17/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/business/Adco/Adco-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Stetson Cologne Reaches Out Through Gallantry ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Stetson Cologne Reaches Out Through Gallantry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stetson, John B, Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levere, Jane L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T00:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane L. Levere', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Levere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9022536a-01f3-5019-97d0-8809708ba60e', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9022536a-01f3-5019-97d0-8809708ba60e'}, {'abstract': 'The deputy attorney general, James M. Cole, who has served as the No. 2 person in the Justice Department for four years, said Thursday that he plans to resign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/us/justice-department-deputy-will-leave.html', 'snippet': 'The deputy attorney general, James M. Cole, who has served as the No. 2 person in the Justice Department for four years, said Thursday that he plans to resign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deputy attorney general, James M. Cole, who has served as the No. 2 person in the Justice Department for four years, said Thursday that he plans to resign. The announcement, coming on the heels of the planned resignation of Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr., means that the Justice Department will have a significantly new leadership team for the final two years of the Obama administration. Mr. Cole said he would stay on the job until a successor was named. While the White House does not plan to nominate a new attorney general until after next month’s election, Mr. Cole’s acting successor could be named sooner. This week, Mr. Holder announced that Vanita Gupta, a senior lawyer at the American Civil Liberties Union, would take over as the head of the Civil Rights Division. Ms. Gupta will serve on an interim basis, but officials said they expected the president to nominate her to the position permanently at some point. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Department Deputy Will Leave ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice Department Deputy Will Leave', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, James M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Vanita', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T00:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Apuzzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Apuzzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec35a172-2da4-56fd-9ad9-08bc633b3a2c', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec35a172-2da4-56fd-9ad9-08bc633b3a2c'}, {'abstract': 'As the Aggies head to Alabama on Saturday, questions remain about the identity of the program, which is growing in prominence and trying to maintain its momentum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/sports/ncaafootball/one-year-after-johnny-manziel-texas-am-adjusts-to-higher-expectations.html', 'snippet': 'As the Aggies head to Alabama on Saturday, questions remain about the identity of the program, which is growing in prominence and trying to maintain its momentum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLLEGE STATION, Tex. — The last time Texas A&M traveled to Tuscaloosa to play Alabama, on Nov. 10, 2012, the overlook