ytimes.com/2014/10/17/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': "9 P.M. (Starz) THE MONUMENTS MEN (2014) George Clooney, doing his best Gregory Peck imitation, stars as Frank Stokes, an art historian who leads an eccentric bunch of curators, restorers and archivists in the Monuments, Fine Arts and Archives section, an Allied effort to rescue Europe’s artistic treasures from the Nazis. The exploits of the 350 or so men and women from 13 countries who were with the unit from 1943 to 1951 have been chronicled in books including “The Monuments Men: Allied Heroes, Nazi Thieves, and the Greatest Treasure Hunt in History,” written by Robert M. Edsel, with Bret Witter, which served as the basis for this film directed by Mr. Clooney, who wrote the screenplay with his producing partner, Grant Heslov. “ 'The Monuments Men’ slices off a sliver of a great World War II story and turns it into a lightweight entertainment that doesn’t ask you to think too hard,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “That’s too bad, because if there’s anyone who you expect to smarten up a joint, it’s Mr. Clooney. The brain trust behind the original Monuments Men was staggering and included individuals who helped run some of America’s greatest cultural institutions. At the very least you expect their fictional counterparts to exchange a little shoptalk and some thoughts on art, literature and the latest restoration techniques or maybe just gossip about Picasso’s latest mistress.”", 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f967865b-bd48-5e4f-b750-10600e202bfb', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f967865b-bd48-5e4f-b750-10600e202bfb'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Friday, October 17, 2014', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/pageoneplus/corrections-october-17-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Friday, October 17, 2014', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 17, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T05:50:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1f9cdf3-e8b8-5977-9391-324029f247ab', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1f9cdf3-e8b8-5977-9391-324029f247ab'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, October 17, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, October 17, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It seemed that everything was fine. The weather was fine. The trail was not so hard. Until the storm.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T05:50:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name