 billion, in funds under management.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/old-mutual-acquires-british-wealth-manager-for-936-million/', 'snippet': 'The acquisition of Quilter Cheviot would bolster Old Mutual Wealth, the insurer’s wealth management division, and the combined unit would have about £92 billion, or about $147 billion, in funds under management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The insurer Old Mutual said Friday that it had agreed to acquire Quilter Cheviot, the private equity-backed British wealth manager, in a deal worth up to 585 million pounds, or about $936.6 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Mutual to Acquire British Wealth Manager for $936.6 Million', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bridgepoint Capital', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evercore Partners Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merrill Lynch & Co', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Old Mutual', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rothschild, N M, & Sons Ltd', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SHEARMAN & STERLING', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T10:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14ad1c27-da87-5eac-8c6a-bcc4bc15423d', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14ad1c27-da87-5eac-8c6a-bcc4bc15423d'}, {'abstract': 'Apps like Lists for Writers aim to help with creativity, but some question whether that’s really possible.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/will-an-app-change-your-writing-life/', 'snippet': 'Apps like Lists for Writers aim to help with creativity, but some question whether that’s really possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m a messy writer. I don’t mean that my handwriting is bad (although it is), or that my desk is cluttered with empty mugs and books and baggies of trail mix (although it, too, is). I mean I tend to compose right in a browser window, alongside a whole bunch of open tabs (right now I have 14\xa0— just kidding, 15, because I opened another one while composing this sentence). I’m not particularly proud of this strategy, though, and I often think about what would happen to my writing if I adopted a less chaotic system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/16/opinion/nyto-writing/nyto-writing-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/16/opinion/nyto-writing/nyto-writing-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't