to share? This is your place. Go.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Turn: A Weekend Thread, Open for Comments', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T13:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f01b5d91-18ee-50d9-b150-ddda782ab189', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f01b5d91-18ee-50d9-b150-ddda782ab189'}, {'abstract': 'Immigrant rights activists plan to sing protest songs every Monday afternoon in downtown Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/chant-down-the-walls-of-the-metropolitan-detention-center/', 'snippet': 'Immigrant rights activists plan to sing protest songs every Monday afternoon in downtown Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In protest advocacy, there are times for marches and speeches. But sometimes, you just have to sing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Chant Down the Walls’ of the Metropolitan Detention Center', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T13:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/597d4d78-f3f7-5e6a-9a5d-fdbf4cbe63b1', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/597d4d78-f3f7-5e6a-9a5d-fdbf4cbe63b1'}, {'abstract': 'How to create a marketing plan. Apple Pay arrives Monday. And does dressing like a man lead to success?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/today-in-small-business-paying-retail-employees-50000-a-year/', 'snippet': 'How to create a marketing plan. Apple Pay arrives Monday. And does dressing like a man lead to success?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Small Business: Paying Retail Employees $50,000 a Year', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T13:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b8502d5-701d-5b0f-9d6e-b615f5b64dab', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b8502d5-701d-5b0f-9d6e-b615f5b64dab'}, {'abstract': 'The sisters behind the textile company take T on a tour of the making of their Autumn/Winter collection, which hits stores today.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/block-shop-textiles-india/', 'snippet': 'The sisters behind the textile company take T on a tour of the making of their Autumn/Winter collection, which hits stores today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twice a year, Lily and Hopie Stockman, the siblings behind the textiles label Block Shop, begin designing a new collection from their home base in Los Angeles before traveling to India to oversee final production. “It’s gleefully low-tech,” remarks Lily of the entirely handmade process. The two-year-old brand, known for its colorful palette of limited-edition printed scarves and textiles, collaborates exclusively with a co-op in Bagru, a small city near Jaipur known for its natural dye processes and craftsmanship in traditional block printing. “We know every printer in our co-op, so we know who prints what scarf,” Lily says, adding that proceeds from sales go back into Bagru’s local community (earlier this year, the sisters sponsored a mobile health care clinic that treated over 200 individuals).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Printing Textiles in India With Block Shop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stockman, Hopie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stockman, Lily', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Block Shop', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T14:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Neilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7635505-c135-5875-9805-9b20d15a7ba1', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7635505-c135-5875-9805-9b20d15a7ba1'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics on “Dear White People,” “Birdman” and “Fury.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/video-reviews-of-dear-whi