 animals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/books/review/john-sandfords-deadline-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'In John Sandford’s “Deadline,” dogs are being stolen and auctioned off for resale as laboratory animals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are plenty of fictional cops and private eyes with anger issues, woman troubles and drinking problems. And then there’s Virgil Flowers, the happy-go-lucky hero of John Sandford’s roughneck crime novels set in rural Minnesota. A tall, lean guy who lives in cowboy boots and T-shirts from vintage-band concerts, Virgil wears his blond hair “country-long like Waylon Jennings.” He leaves the big-time crime-busting to his boss in Minneapolis, Lucas Davenport (“not a bad guy, though a trifle intense”), so he can grab the fun assignments for himself.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/books/review/1019-bks-CRIME/1019-bks-CRIME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/books/review/1019-bks-CRIME/1019-bks-CRIME-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 718}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/books/review/1019-bks-CRIME/1019-bks-CRIME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 857, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/books/review/1019-bks-CRIME/1019-bks-CRIME-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1713, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/books/review/1019-bks-CRIME/1019-bks-CRIME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75,