65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/520550d1-9c9e-5c56-ae68-6bc8eeef7095'}, {'abstract': 'The police, who had gained control of the street in the Mong Kok district only hours before, retreated to avoid a confrontation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/18/world/asia/hong-kong-protesters-retake-street-defying-government.html', 'snippet': 'The police, who had gained control of the street in the Mong Kok district only hours before, retreated to avoid a confrontation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Protesters demanding democracy in Hong Kong delivered a stinging rebuff to the government late on Friday by reclaiming parts of a street that police had forcibly cleared earlier in the day. Hundreds of demonstrators cheered ecstatically when, after hours of mounting tensions, the outnumbered police were ordered to retreat rather than risk an escalating confrontation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/world/18hongkong10/18hongkong10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/18/world/18hongkong10/18hongkong10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/world/18hongkong10/18hongkong10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/world/18hongkong10/18hongkong10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/world/18hongkong10/18hongkong10-thumbStandard.jpg', 