h pasta or pastry?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I tell my old farmer friend, who grew up poor, regularly eating potatoes and not much else, that I’m crazy for them. My favorite vegetable! “Fine, please pass the steak,” he says.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/dining/22KITCHEN4/1022KITCHEN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/22/dining/22KITCHEN4/1022KITCHEN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/dining/22KITCHEN4/1022KITCHEN4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/dining/22KITCHEN4/1022KITCHEN4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/dining/22KITCHEN4/1022KITCHEN4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/22/dining/22KITCHEN4/1022KITCHEN4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/dining/22KITCHEN4/1022KITCHEN4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Savory Potato Tart Recipe With a Relaxed Attitude on Starch', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Relaxed Attitude on Starch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanis, Daivd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potatoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T18:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21bb0b9b-e917-582b-85a4-bdc9fe9051e4', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21bb0b9b-e917-582b-85a4-bdc9fe9051e4'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Steyer’s opinions should not be amplified just because he’s rich.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/good-luck-distinguishing-between-good-oligarchs-and-bad-oligarchs/', 'snippet': 'Tom Steyer’s opinions should not be amplified just because he’s rich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Kat Taylor, who is married to the billionaire Tom Steyer, there is “the private empire,” and there is the Earth. As she explained in an eye-opening article by Jim Rutenberg in this Sunday’s New York Times magazine, the private empire is the dark world of the Kochs and other right-wing oligarchs, who are spending large fortunes on this year’s midterms to elect candidates to serve their personal and business interests.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Luck Distinguishing Between Good Oligarchs and Bad Oligarchs', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steyer, Thomas F', 'rank': 2