o Grandl (also known as the street-style shutterbug The Urban Spotter) took to the tent in pursuit of the fair’s human element: the gallerists, writers, artists, collectors and enthusiasts gathered to see what’s new. His findings? Plenty of Issey Miyake, Acne Studios and Alexander Wang fans; pops of color to offset the perennial art-world all-black-everything; permanently present smartphones and at least one tiny trendsetter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Frieze London, Art Admirers of All Shapes and Sizes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze Art Fair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Acne Studios', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T18:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Bruno Grandl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'Bruno', 'lastname': 'Grandl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d950d08-30f2-5e35-9903-b26ed6eaf727', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d950d08-30f2-5e35-9903-b26ed6eaf727'}, {'abstract': 'New mobile dating apps are increasingly targeting narrow communities. Is this exacerbating existing problems with self-segregation on the Internet?', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/is-online-dating-revealing-our-biases-or-reinforcing-them/', 'snippet': 'New mobile dating apps are increasingly targeting narrow communities. Is this exacerbating existing problems with self-segregation on the Internet?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent\xa0weeks, two new mobile dating apps have been added to what’s becoming an increasingly crowded market. One, called Meld, is marketed to black professionals seeking meaningful long-term relationships; the other, Luxy, invites wealthy individuals to find someone with whom to share their high-end lifestyles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/opinion/nyto-kiss/nyto-kiss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/opinion/nyto-kiss/nyto-kiss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/opinion/nyto-kiss/nyto-kiss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/opinion/nyto-kiss/nyto-kiss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 2020, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/opinion/nyto-kiss/nyto-kiss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/20/opinion/nyto-kiss/nyto-kiss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/opinion/nyto-kiss/nyto-kiss-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Online Dating Revealing Our Biases, or Reinforcing Them?', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': N