is island in the Venice Lagoon, glassmaking has been revered by doges and tourists alike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the sort of thing that would never happen to George Clooney: As I stepped off the packed vaporetto onto the island of Murano, I slipped on the rain-slicked dock and my trolley bag went click-clacking across the dock’s wooden planks. When neither the suitcase nor I fell into the Venice Lagoon, my audience — a boat full of amused Italian passengers — went back to their cellphones and newspapers and the vaporetto chugged off toward Venice.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murano, Italy, Still Sparkling After 700 Years  ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Sparkling After 700 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Murano (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mirrors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods and Services', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T20:04:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ferren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8e92865-40af-5a53-9c97-23dd20f49183', 'word_count': 1821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8e92865-40af-5a53-9c97-23dd20f49183'}, {'abstract': 'News about the measures being taken to prevent travelers from spreading Ebola.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/travel/the-latest-on-ebola-and-travel.html', 'snippet': 'News about the measures being taken to prevent travelers from spreading Ebola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The international response to the West African Ebola outbreak has affected travel by air, rail and cruise ship. And the news that a nurse who contracted Ebola while treating its first casualty in the United States flew commercially and another employee who was not infected was aboard a cruise ship has stoked fears that it could spread here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest on Ebola and Travel', 'kicker': 'Update', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T20:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a47c167-daf2-5900-8719-278b66e58d1f', 'word_count': 1848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a47c167-daf2-5900-8719-278b66e58d1f'}, {'abstract': 'The politics of Ebola have been swirling, and Senator Kay Hagan, in a tough re-election race in North Carolina, has reversed herself and called for a ban on flights from the West African countries battling the epidemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/17/hagans-180-on-ebola-travel-ban/', 'snippet': 'The politics of Ebola have been swirling, and Senator Kay Hagan, in a tough re-election race in North Carolina, has reversed herself and called for a ban on flights from the West African countries battling the epidemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:26 p.m. | The politics of Ebola have been swirling for awhile, and Senator Kay Hagan, the Democratic incumbent facing a tough re-election race in North Carolina, just made a change in direction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hagan’s Shift on Ebola Travel Ban', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagan, Kay R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T20:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ac77f91-0750-5180-bff8-c8d575367277', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ac77f91-0750-5180-bff8-c8d575367277'}, {'abstract': 'Of course not. But studies suggest we have a natural urge to think so.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/opinion/sunday/does-everything-happen-for-a-reason.html', 'snippet': 'Of course not. But studies suggest we have a natural urge to think so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON April 15, 2013, James Costello was cheering on a friend near the finish line at the Boston Marathon when the bombs exploded, severely burning his arms and legs and sending shrapnel into his flesh. During the months of surgery and rehabilitation that followed, Mr. Costello developed a relationship with one of his nurses, Krista D’Agostino, and they s