me': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Theft', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Julie Hirschfeld', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T21:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/847b3068-834b-5af3-9eb1-8f9aef4f15d5', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/847b3068-834b-5af3-9eb1-8f9aef4f15d5'}, {'abstract': 'The first formal exhibition of Bill Lynch’s warm paintings on plywood ends next week at White Columns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/18/arts/design/bill-lynchs-paintings-get-a-show-at-white-columns.html', 'snippet': 'The first formal exhibition of Bill Lynch’s warm paintings on plywood ends next week at White Columns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Genius lands where genius will, and I’m pretty sure some alighted on Bill Lynch. His ineffably elegant, tender-tough paintings on salvaged plywood, seen at White Columns in his first formal solo exhibition in New York, are a delight, one of the season’s sleepers. With their calligraphic brushwork, shifting cultural quotations and eccentric (and knotty) painting surfaces, these personal variants of landscape and still life painting also form a largely inadvertent coda to the painting of the 1980s. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/arts/billylynch/billylynch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/18/arts/billylynch/billylynch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 801}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/arts/billylynch/billylynch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/arts/billylynch/billylynch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1535, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/arts/billylynch/billylynch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/18/arts/billylynch/billylynch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/arts/billylynch/billylynch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Natural Painter’s Singular View of the Natural World', 'kicker': 'Last Chance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Natural Painter’s Singular View of the Natural World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Bill (1960-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White Columns (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-17T21:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a83faa0f-9973-5933-aa56-7f91a356fc55', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a83faa0f-9973-5933-aa56-7f91a356fc55'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Ratliff and Jon Caramanica discuss Scott Walker and Sunn O)))’s “Soused.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/17/popcast-the-myth-of-scott-walker/', 'snippet': 'Ben Ratliff and Jon Caramanica discuss Scott Walker and Sunn O)))’s “Soused.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 71-year-old singer Scott Walker, collaborating with the drone-metal band Sunn O))), has made a new record called “Soused,” out next Tuesday from 4AD. It’s strong, strange and achieved, with Mr. Walker’s baritone pushed high over deep, loud, long-tones of electric guitar and bass. Other sounds — a bell, a bullwhip, a half-valved trumpet moan — enter the music strategically, as references to his lyrics of violence and discomfort, or as characters in a kind of abstract audio play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/arts/12SCOTTWALKER1/12SCOTTWALKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/12/arts/12SCOTTWALKER1/12SCOTTWALKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 707}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/12/arts/12SCOTTWALKER1/12SCOTTWALKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 870, 'subTyp