 'height': 261, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/magazine/19analyticsbox/19analyticsbox-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 261}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/magazine/19analyticsbox/19analyticsbox-jumbo.png', 'height': 446, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/magazine/19analyticsbox/19analyticsbox-superJumbo.png', 'height': 530, 'width': 1217, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/magazine/19analyticsbox/19analyticsbox-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/magazine/19analyticsbox/19analyticsbox-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/magazine/19analyticsbox/19analyticsbox-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Analytics: Run, Mitt, Run?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovich, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T11:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c36961-05ca-5887-a586-99bb63ae5a80', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c36961-05ca-5887-a586-99bb63ae5a80'}, {'abstract': 'Of derp, homework, and ad hominem.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/18/the-civility-whine/', 'snippet': 'Of derp, homework, and ad hominem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At this point in the great inflation-deflation debate, a lot of what the inflationistas have to say takes the form of whining about the rudeness of their critics — of course, me in particular. I would say that this is a de facto confession that they’ve run out of substantive defenses for their position — although I guess I would say that, wouldn’t I?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Civility Whine', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T13:08:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9affdb0f-ca4e-5ecc-9adc-2ddcd4f2b217', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9affdb0f-ca4e-5ecc-9adc-2ddcd4f2b217'}, {'abstract': 'Wessel explains.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/18/why-to-worry-about-deflation/', 'snippet': 'Wessel explains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Wessel has a very nice explainer in the WSJ — although I wonder how the editor allowed his citation of a particular expert under point #2 to slip through. One thing he doesn’t do, however, is make it clear that zero is not a magic red line here — as even the IMF has made a point of emphasizing, too-low inflation has all the adverse effects of outright deflation, just to a lesser degree. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why To Worry About Deflation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T13:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b55fde0-fc2e-5f50-bd28-b7229bc3c295', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b55fde0-fc2e-5f50-bd28-b7229bc3c295'}, {'abstract': 'The ballet teacher Irina Kolpakova is currently preparing the cast of “Raymonda Variations,” for American Ballet’s Theater’s fall season, which opens Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/arts/dance/irina-kolpakova-trains-dancers-at-american-ballet-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The ballet teacher Irina Kolpakova is currently preparing the cast of “Raymonda Variations,” for American Ballet’s Theater’s fall season, which opens Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Strrrrrrrrretch!” Irina Kolpakova called out. “Up, up, up, up! More, more, more!”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19IRINA1/19IRINA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19IRINA1/19IRINA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19IRINA1/19IRINA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19IRINA1/19IRINA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1233, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19IRINA1/19IRINA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19IRINA1/19IRINA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19IRINA1/19IRINA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Teacher Who Bridges the Eras ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Teacher Who Bridges the Eras', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulcas, Roslyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kolpakova, Irina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T14:13:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b09bb08-5e50-557a-9950-794df1a13b1e', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b09bb08-5e50-557a-9950-794df1a13b1e'}, {'abstract': 'More than a year after the breakup of his band, My Chemical Romance, Gerard Way talks about his comeback solo album, “Hesitant Alien.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/arts/music/gerard-way-talks-about-his-comeback-album-hesitant-alien.html', 'snippet': 'More than a year after the breakup of his band, My Chemical Romance, Gerard Way talks about his comeback solo album, “Hesitant Alien.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Chemical Romance, co-founded by the singer-songwriter Gerard Way, was an apt rock band for the hectic 2000s. Unlike the Strokes or Interpol, it was uncool and a bit manic, five comics-obsessed outsiders from the New Jersey suburbs. In 2004, the group’s second studio album, the histrionic but hooky “Three Cheers for Sweet Revenge,” set it apart from the pop-punk Warped Tour bands they had toured alongside when they began their career. Next up was an ambitious rock opera, “The Black Parade,” with Mr. Way casting himself as the Patient, a dying, defiant, messianic narrator. It reached No. 2 on the Billboard 200 and was certified platinum. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19WAY/19WAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19WAY/19WAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19WAY/19WAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19WAY/19WAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19WAY/19WAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19WAY/19WAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19WAY/19WAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fell to Earth, but He’s Back on His Feet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fell to Earth, but He&#8217;s Back on His Feet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'My Chemical Romance (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Way, Gerard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T14:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/187e78df-a8af-5e9a-a292-9d51331c3950', 'word_count': 1376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/187e78df-a8af-5e9a-a292-9d51331c3950'}, {'abstract': 'Kindness, Vök, the Bots, Natalie Mering, and Abigail Washburn and Béla Fleck release new music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/arts/music/kindness-vk-and-the-bots-release-new-albums.html', 'snippet': 'Kindness, Vök, the Bots, Natalie Mering, and Abigail Washburn and Béla Fleck release new music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kindness', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/arts/19PLAYLIST1/19PLAYLIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleL