stract': 'George Spitz, the often overlooked inspiration behind the New York City Marathon’s move from Central Park to the city’s streets, will be inducted into the New York Road Runners Hall of Fame on Oct. 30.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/sports/one-mans-vision-footrace-in-new-york-city-five-boroughs.html', 'snippet': 'George Spitz, the often overlooked inspiration behind the New York City Marathon’s move from Central Park to the city’s streets, will be inducted into the New York Road Runners Hall of Fame on Oct. 30.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By even the dauntingly high standards of New York, the man who “invented” the New York City Marathon, George Spitz, is a bona fide character. Two weeks after this year’s marathon, he will celebrate his 92nd birthday by doing what he does most days: writing the history of New York City for an independent book project. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/spitz1/spitz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/spitz1/spitz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 827}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/spitz1/spitz1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 744, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/spitz1/spitz1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1487, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/spitz1/spitz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'th