 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19TENNIS/19TENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19TENNIS/19TENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19TENNIS/19TENNIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19TENNIS/19TENNIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19TENNIS/19TENNIS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19TENNIS/19TENNIS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19TENNIS/19TENNIS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As the Return of Serve Gains Importance, the Third Shot Is the Charm ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As the Return of Serve Gains Importance, the Third Shot Is the Charm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarey, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Women's Tennis Assn", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T18:25:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3cb5489-f2f8-5dfb-a4a0-373a08c3585b', 'word_count': 1155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3cb5489-f2f8-5dfb-a4a0-373a08c3585b'}, {'abstract': 'Is espresso the miniature one, or is that cappuccino?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/opinion/sunday/i-am-not-a-coffee-drinker.html', 'snippet': 'Is espresso the miniature one, or is that cappuccino?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I DON’T know what an Americano is. I don’t know what Chemex is, though I thought the point was to get chemicals out of our foods, not into. Maybe that is what the “ex” is for. I don’t know what cold drip is. (I do know what iced coffee is. Iced tea, too — Mayor Bloomberg tried to ban it and that’s what got him voted out of office, right?) I know what a latte is. I know what Starbucks is. Starbucks invented the latte, in Seattle, where the rain and natural beauty make people stay inside and create sprawling companies that eventually make people dependent and angry. I know what addiction is: I recently rewatched every episode of “The Wire.” Is espresso the miniature one, or is that cappuccino? I don’t know what Nespresso is. Did Nestlé buy espresso? Hello, Federal Trade Commission? Isn’t this against the law? I know what a barista is. They pull levers and shout and have better taste in music than I do. Some of them have mustaches and, so I have heard, draw pictures in the foam atop the coffee. Good for them — I am an ardent supporter of the arts. I know what free Wi-Fi is. That means you can check your email and tweet a picture of your muffin and do Facebook things. Catfishing and so forth. (I know what catfishing is.) I don’t know what “Fair Trade” is. I grew up with an older brother. I don’t know what pour-over is. I know what a comb-over is. I don’t know what single origin is. From what I understood in the sex ed classes of my youth, nothing originates from anything single. (Sorry, religious counselors and fathers of daughters.) Except amoebas. (That was in science class, not blush-inducing health and its desire-killing human anatomy illustrations.) I don’t know what the Cup of Excellence is. Congratulations, Germany. I don’t know what Keurig is. Could that be my Ikea couch? When I assembled it from the pictogram that came with it, I had several screws left over. Probably someday it will collapse. (Don’t go to Ikea on a Sunday unless you need to feel relieved about being single and childless.) A few weeks ago we celebrated National Coffee Day. Seems like that should come after the one when you fast, not before, no? But I am not a coffee drinker. Also not a morning person.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COFFEE/19COFFEE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 537, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COFFEE/19COFFEE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COFFEE/19COFFEE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COFFEE/19COFFEE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COFFEE/19COFFEE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Am Not a Coffee Drinker', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Am Not a Coffee Drinker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hauser, Ethan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T18:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a9b5382-1325-554c-8613-f42d55f3df0f', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a9b5382-1325-554c-8613-f42d55f3df0f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers discuss a column by Ross Douthat about helping the terminally ill end their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/opinion/sunday/assisted-dying-laws.html', 'snippet': 'Readers discuss a column by Ross Douthat about helping the terminally ill end their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers discuss a column by Ross Douthat about helping the terminally ill end their lives.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/1019LETTERS/1019LETTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/1019LETTERS/1019LETTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/1019LETTERS/1019LETTERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/1019LETTERS/1019LETTERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/1019LETTERS/1019LETTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/1019LETTERS/1019LETTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/1019LETTERS/1019LETTERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Assisted Dying Laws', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Assisted Dying Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maynard, Brittany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T18:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd377c47-c245-563b-abfa-3d8f561a05dd', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd377c47-c245-563b-abfa-3d8f561a05dd'}, {'abstract': 'Home economics fell out of popularity by the time I was in high school. Now no one knows how to sew on a button.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/opinion/sunday/jennifer-finney-boylan-knitting-backward.html', 'snippet': 'Home economics fell out of popularity by the time I was in high school. Now no one knows how to sew on a button.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BELGRADE LAKES, Me. — MY friend’s son was unconcerned that the pants didn’t fit. “It’s fine,” he said, of the half-dozen pinstripe suits he’d bought on sale. Their cuffs were unhemmed. “My mother can fix them.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-articleLarge-v6.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-articleLarge-v6.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-jumbo-v7.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-superJumbo-v6.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-thumbStandard-v7.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-thumbStandard-v7.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-thumbLarge-v6.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knitting Backward', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knitting Backward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Economics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boylan, Jennifer Finney', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knitting and Knit Goods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T18:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Finney Boylan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Finney', 'lastname': 'Boylan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/445f6e92-53f8-5888-af0e-c98420aab38c', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/445f6e92-53f8-5888-af0e-c98420aab38c'}, {'abstract': 'The closing of a nonprofit’s Cairo office is a damning critique of President Abdel Fattah el-Sisi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/opinion/sunday/from-jimmy-carter-a-rebuke-to-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The closing of a nonprofit’s Cairo office is a damning critique of President Abdel Fattah el-Sisi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over three decades, the Carter Center in Atlanta, led by former President Jimmy Carter, has established itself as a respected advocate for human rights and democracy. It has sent observers to 97 elections in 38 countries, worked to persuade governments to respect freedoms and human rights, and supported citizens who defend those principles. But it has thrown in the towel on Egypt. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Jimmy Carter, a Rebuke to Egypt ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Jimmy Carter, a Rebuke to Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carter Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdel Fattah el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T18:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0582a4b-ad7e-5756-955a-558f89f204d4', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0582a4b-ad7e-5756-955a-558f89f204d4'}, {'abstract': 'The boring requirements and tenuous rewards of life as an American citizen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/opinion/sunday/voting-in-the-rain.html', 'snippet': 'The boring requirements and tenuous rewards of life as an American citizen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — OF all the rights associated with adulthood — the ability to purchase alcohol, rent cars, have sex — the one I most looked forward to when I was a child was voting. Voting was your own business, a government-sanctioned secret. I was told that no one would ever ask me whom I voted for, and if for some reason of ignorance or terrible manners they did ask, I didn’t have to tell. The notion that I got to choose the person who ran the country (a minor misconception of how voting worked) without admitting that I was the one who had done it appealed to me greatly.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19ELECTION/19ELECTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19ELECTION/19ELECTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19ELECTION/19ELECTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19ELECTION/19ELECTION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19ELECTION/19ELECTION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19ELECTION/19ELECTION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, '