om/2014/10/19/sports/hockey/sharks-profess-unity-after-playoff-failures-.html', 'snippet': 'In recent years, the San Jose Sharks have known nothing but disappointment in the Stanley Cup playoffs, but the players say that any problems have been addressed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hockey has its own peculiar calculus of success. To win a majority of games, year after year, means little. Only a postseason championship is truly meaningful, and when even excellent teams fail to achieve that, they can be torn down to the foundation and rebuilt.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19SHARKS/19SHARKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19SHARKS/19SHARKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19SHARKS/19SHARKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19SHARKS/19SHARKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19SHARKS/19SHARKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19SHARKS/19SHARKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sports/19SHARKS/19SHARKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharks Profess Unity After Playoff Woes ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharks Profess Unity After Playoff Woes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hannan, Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose Sharks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marleau, Patrick (1979- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thornton, Joe (1979- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T18:52:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f54d60ce-0af5-51e1-9f1b-1376e01e42e6', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f54d60ce-0af5-51e1-9f1b-1376e01e42e6'}, {'abstract': 'In an era of systematic clinical research, medicine still requires the vignette.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/18/why-doctors-need-stories/', 'snippet': 'In an era of systematic clinical research, medicine still requires the vignette.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FEW weeks ago, I received an email from the Danish psychiatrist Per Bech that had an unexpected attachment: a story about a patient. I have been writing a book about antidepressants — how well they work and how we know. Dr. Bech is an innovator in clinical psychometrics, the science of measuring change in conditions like depression. Generally, he forwards material about statistics.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COUCHcover/19COUCHcover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COUCHcover/19COUCHcover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 537}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COUCHcover/19COUCHcover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 916, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COUCHcover/19COUCHcover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1831, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COUCHcover/19COUCHcover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COUCHcover/19COUCHcover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/sunday-review/19COUCHcover/19COUCHcover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Doctors Need Stories', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Doctors Need Stories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIDEPRESSANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T19:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter D. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63558354-59a8-5154-a3ed-50c6974f5bff', 'word_count': 1683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63558354-59a8-5154-a3ed-50c6974f5bff'}, {'abstract': 'A White House proposal would help protect service members from predatory loans, but a national lending standard is needed for the country as a whole.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/opinion/sunday/a-rate-cap-for-all-consumer-loans.html', 'snippet': 'A White House proposal would help protect service members from predatory loans, but a national lending standard is needed for the country as a whole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration has proposed much-needed improvements in federal rules that are supposed to protect service members from predatory loans that trap them in debt and, in certain circumstances, can end their military careers. The changes would repair glaring weaknesses in the rules used to carry out the Military Lending Act of 2007. But the administration and Congress should not stop there. Millions of civilians are also exposed to ruinously priced loans. What is needed is a national consumer lending standard — and interest rate cap — to ensure fair credit in the country as a whole. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/opinion/19editorial-pic/19editorial-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/opinion/19editorial-pic/19editorial-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/opinion/19editorial-pic/19editorial-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/opinion/19editorial-pic/19editorial-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/opinion/19editorial-pic/19editorial-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/19/opinion/19editorial-pic/19editorial-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/opinion/19editorial-pic/19editorial-pic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rate Cap for All Consumer Loans ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rate Cap for All Consumer Loans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'ran