t://article/e9ebfadd-2b07-5d50-933c-c069f9e1ad8d'}, {'abstract': 'Grand ambitions to restore the country’s run-down train services to their former glory have been impeded by Islamic State’s advances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/19/world/a-train-ride-through-time-from-iraqs-checkered-past-into-an-uncertain-future.html', 'snippet': 'Grand ambitions to restore the country’s run-down train services to their former glory have been impeded by Islamic State’s advances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Saad al-Tammimi is in his fourth decade working for Iraq’s railroads, a career that has taken him all around his country, and around the Middle East. Nowadays, though, he can go only from Baghdad to Basra, across the relatively calm Shiite-dominated south of this war-torn country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Train Ride Through Time: From Iraq’s Checkered Past Into an Uncertain Future ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Train Ride Through Time: From Iraq’s Checkered Past Into an Uncertain Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arango, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mosul (Iraq)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Basra (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-18T22:38:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'or