elbarrow and then, as if continuing with his yard work, starts to dance. It’s a flailing, stumbling dance — twisting and swerving, intercepting itself at odd junctures — but also intensely focused, each moment both a necessity and a surprise. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/PAXTON/PAXTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/PAXTON/PAXTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 624}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/PAXTON/PAXTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 985, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/PAXTON/PAXTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1970, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/PAXTON/PAXTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/PAXTON/PAXTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/PAXTON/PAXTON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Choreographer Drawn to Change', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Choreographer Drawn to Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dia: Beacon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paxton, Steve (1939- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-19T22:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d32600c6-5fef-569f-969f-9d84de72fafa', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d32600c6-5fef-569f-969f-9d84de72fafa'}, {'abstract': '“Twin Sisters” follows the lives of Chinese-born girls, one raised in California, the other in Norway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/arts/twin-sisters-from-china-stay-in-touch.html', 'snippet': '“Twin Sisters” follows the lives of Chinese-born girls, one raised in California, the other in Norway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everything about the Norwegian film “Twin Sisters” seems too good to be true. The stars are a pair of adorable 10-year-olds as energetic as they are well-adjusted. The supporting players look like the four nicest, most supportive parents you could meet. The story hinges on a set of fateful coincidences that profoundly change the lives of everyone involved. “Twin Sisters” is a documentary, though, so there’s no need to suspend disbelief. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/SISTERS/SISTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/SISTERS/SISTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty