www.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/books/the-hot-zone-author-tracks-ebolas-evolution.html', 'snippet': '“The Hot Zone,” the nonfiction thriller about Ebola that Richard Preston wrote 20 years ago, is back on best-seller lists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Ebola outbreak in West Africa began to escalate a few months ago, the writer Richard Preston was working on a children’s fantasy novel. He dropped that and called David Remnick, the editor of The New Yorker. “I said, ‘I’ve got to get back to Ebola,’\xa0” Mr. Preston said. “I’ve got to cover this.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/JPPRESTON/JPPRESTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/JPPRESTON/JPPRESTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 789}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/JPPRESTON/JPPRESTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/JPPRESTON/JPPRESTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1558, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/JPPRESTON/JPPRESTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/JPPRESTON/JPPRESTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/arts/JPPRESTON/JPPRESTON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Updating a Chronicle of Suffering: Author of ‘The Hot Zone’ Tracks Ebola’s Evolution', 'kicker': 'A Word With: Richard Preston', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Updating a Chronicle of Suffering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Hot Zone: The Terrifying True Story of the Origins of the Ebola Virus (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-19T22:13:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Alter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cfe015c-6326-5e6b-9164-e07ba4c07ffa', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cfe015c-6326-5e6b-9164-e07ba4c07ffa'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bull Mixed Pairs at the world championships in Sanya, China, was won on Friday by Kerri Sanborn of Delray Beach, Fla., and Jie Zhao, known as Jack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/crosswords/bridge/red-bull-mixed-pairs-at-world-championships.html', 'snippet': 'The Red Bull Mixed Pairs at the world championships in Sanya, China, was won on Friday by Kerri Sanborn of Delray Beach, Fla., and Jie Zhao, known as Jack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Red Bull Mixed Pairs at the world championships in Sanya, China, was won on Friday by Kerri Sanborn of Delray Beach, Fla., and Jie Zhao, known as Jack. Zhao is officially listed as from China, but he has lived in Boca Raton, Fla., for a few years.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/crosswords/bridge/20card/20card-jumbo.gif', 'height': 1003, 'width': 552, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/crosswords/bridge/20card/20card-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 1003, 'width': 552, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/crosswords/bridge/20card/20card-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/20/crosswords/bridge/20card/20card-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/crosswords/bridge/20card/20card-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bull Mixed Pairs at World Championships', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Red Bull Mixed Pairs at World Championships', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-19T22:20:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c09cc039-ca60-56d3-afd6-3f532dac0d5f', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c09cc039-ca60-56d3-afd6-3f532dac0d5f'}, {'abstract': 'The musical “Here Lies Love” is bidding farewell to New York with plans to take its show on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/theater/here-lies-love-to-close-at-the-public.html', 'snippet': 'The musical “Here Lies Love” is bidding farewell to New York with plans to take its show on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The musical “Here Lies Love” is bidding farewell to New York with plans to take its show on the road. The producers Joey Parnes and Emursive recently announced that the musical, which uses a discothèque atmosphere to explore the rise and fall of Imelda Marcos, former first lady of the Philippines, will have its last performance at the Public Theater on Jan. 3. But plans are in the works to take it to global audiences. “Here Lies Love,” written by David Byrne of Talking Heads and Fatboy Slim, had a well-received three-month engagement at the Public’s LuEsther Hall in 2013 and returned in April for an open-ended run. Despite its popularity, the musical struggled to find a location that could accommodate its needs in terms of space and scheduling. Producers declined to comment on the show’s finances. The National Theater’s production of the musical recently opened at the Dorfman Theater in London, and casting for an Australian version is to begin this month. There are also plans for a United States tour, as well as for performances in South America, South Korea, Singapore, Japan and the Philippines.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/theater/20here/20here-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width