', 'snippet': 'What do we learn when we ride a fellow mammal who can read us at a deeper level than we can read ourselves?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sasa’s name means “so-so” in Portuguese. It’s a little joke, because the gray lusitano gelding is anything but — he’s a beautiful horse who can, like many Iberian equines, claim descent from the war horses of the Renaissance. Look at Uccello’s “Battle of San Romano” and there’s Sasa’s likeness carrying a Florentine general: compact as a rubber ball, strong enough to balance on his hinds, and with a crested neck that ends in ears tilting forward like his rider’s lance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/opinion/menagerie-sasa/menagerie-sasa-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 670, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/opinion/menagerie-sasa/menagerie-sasa-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 670, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/opinion/menagerie-sasa/menagerie-sasa-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/17/opinion/menagerie-sasa/menagerie-sasa-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/17/opinion/menagerie-sasa/menagerie-sasa-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Horses, One Language', 'kicker': 'Menagerie', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dressage (Equestrian Sport)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-19T23:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanna Forrest', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forrest', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c5ca40-8736-567d-a206-e9dc0538e395', 'word_count': 1887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c5ca40-8736-567d-a206-e9dc0538e395'}, {'abstract': 'The Islanders’ good start to their season dovetails well with a campaign to attract new fans in Brooklyn, where the team will move next season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/sports/hockey/barclays-center-to-sound-horn-for-islanders-.html', 'snippet': 'The Islanders’ good start to their season dovetails well with a campaign to attract new fans in Brooklyn, where the team will move next season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Islanders opened with four straight wins for just the third time in franchise history, and that momentum to begin their last season at Nassau Veterans Memorial Coliseum — despite their first loss, at Pittsburgh\xa0on Saturday — made Brett Yormark happy.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/sports/20isles1/20isles1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/sports/20isles1/20isles1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,