ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b0b5481-30b5-5dfa-8033-97181e69be50', 'word_count': 1338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b0b5481-30b5-5dfa-8033-97181e69be50'}, {'abstract': 'The investigation may be complicated by conflicting accounts from witnesses and some of the freshman football players targeted by older members of the Sayreville War Memorial High School team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/nyregion/in-new-jersey-young-players-recall-hazing.html', 'snippet': 'The investigation may be complicated by conflicting accounts from witnesses and some of the freshman football players targeted by older members of the Sayreville War Memorial High School team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAYREVILLE, N.J. — The freshmen were easy prey in the locker room. They slinked away when the older varsity boys barreled in, blasting their music, shooting each other with Nerf guns and stripping down with the kind of confidence that freshmen could only fake. Intimidated by the older boys, most played invisible. But on the day of the second game of the season, Sept. 19, the freshmen became targets in a pastime very different from football.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/nyregion/19SAYREVILLE2/19SAYREVILLE2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/19/nyregion/19SAYREVILLE2/19SAYREVILLE2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/19/nyregion/19SAYREVILLE2/19SAYREVILLE2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2