nhappy-customer/', 'snippet': 'We needed to get to some resolution, because we can’t afford to lose this client — but we also can’t afford to pay for those inspections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the complaint I described in my last post, we needed and we got a face-to-face meeting with our demanding customer. We weren’t sure what to expect from this client who wanted to begin a 100-percent inspection of all of the parts we process for them because their inspectors had found six bad parts out of the hundreds of thousands we had finished.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meeting Face-to-Face With Our Unhappy Customer', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T11:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred Warmbier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warmbier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8831d294-818c-519d-83d2-1ed612b67013', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8831d294-818c-519d-83d2-1ed612b67013'}, {'abstract': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m. Eastern time.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/whats-going-on-in-this-picture-oct-20-2014/', 'snippet': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m. Eastern time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated: Oct. 21, 2014', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/learning/VTS10-20-14LN/VTS10-20-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/18/learning/VTS10-20-14LN/VTS10-20-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/learning/VTS10-20-14LN/VTS10-20-14LN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/learning/VTS10-20-14LN/VTS10-20-14LN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2020, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/learning/VTS10-20-14LN/VTS10-20-14LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/18/learning/VTS10-20-14LN/VTS10-20-14LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/learning/VTS10-20-14LN/VTS10-20-14LN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Going On in This Picture? | Oct. 20, 2014', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T11:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a741756-4f70-5850-b501-53044370a02f', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a741756-4f70-5850-b501-53044370a02f'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A German oil tanker was captured in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/1914-seizure-of-oil-steamer-interests-united-states/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A German oil tanker was captured in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — There is a good deal of excitement here over the seizure of the Brindillo. While no definite details are known, it is supposed she was seized because of doubts as to whether her cargo was really meant for Alexandria, and whether this was not part of an organized attempt to enable Austria to offset the loss of her Galician oil fields. It is hoped that Great Britain will be able to make good her case for the seizure. The right of Great Britain to insist that ships acquired by Americans be used strictly in neutral trade, and not to help late owners, is regarded as undoubted. The Brindillo is a German oil-tank steamer, now flying the American flag. She was captured by the cruiser Suffolk and taken into Halifax, N.S., by the armed cruiser Caronia.  — The New York Herald, European Edition, Oct. 21, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Seizure of Oil Steamer Interests United States', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'majo