'uri': 'nyt://article/1e96c6b7-998b-54cd-8cb5-975084a8fb93'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Jean-Paul Sartre planned to refuse the Nobel Prize, if awarded to him, in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/1964-jean-paul-sartre-set-to-reject-nobel-prize/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Jean-Paul Sartre planned to refuse the Nobel Prize, if awarded to him, in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reporters questioning Jean-Paul Sartre after he refused the Nobel Prize for Literature in October 1964. (From the archives of France’s National Audiovisual Institute, no audio available for this footage)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Jean-Paul Sartre Set To Reject Nobel Prize', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sartre, Jean-Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T11:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/218c5bf1-3dfc-5926-b536-ba23e4e8e70c', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/218c5bf1-3dfc-5926-b536-ba23e4e8e70c'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking answers after the 10-year Treasury note’s volatility on Wednesday. | Behind private equity’s curtain. | New player joins dollar store battle. | Bond trading gets automated.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/morning-agenda-a-bonds-white-knuckle-move/', 'snippet': 'Seeking answers after the 10-year Treasury note’s volatility on Wednesday. | Behind private equity’s curtain. | New player joins dollar store battle. | Bond trading gets automated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the global markets swooned last Wednesday, an unnerving event in the bond markets also took place. Soon after 9 a.m., the yield on one of the world’s most-traded bonds, the 10-year Treasury, went into a bizarre free fall, DealBook’s Peter Eavis writes. This Treasury note is tracked obsessively by Wall Street and is a reference for other interest rates across the wider economy. Investors see it as a haven in times of stress. After the Treasury market opened on Wednesday morning, the yield on the 10-year Treasury plunged far below 2.2 percent, where it had closed the day before. By 9:36 a.m. on Wednesday, it hit 1.9 percent. Then it snapped right back, and within 15 minutes, was again trading above 2 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: A Bond’s White-Knuckle Gyration', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T11:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2cf5b8e-2697-5354-9ad9-07d8871db159', 'word_count': 2198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2cf5b8e-2697-5354-9ad9-07d8871db159'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey, in an apparent shift, said that it would facilitate the movement of Iraqi Kurdish forces to the embattled Syrian city of Kobani to join the battle against militants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/world/middleeast/kobani-turkey-kurdish-fighters-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey, in an apparent shift, said that it would facilitate the movement of Iraqi Kurdish forces to the embattled Syrian city of Kobani to join the battle against militants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MURSITPINAR, Turkey — Turkey will allow Iraqi Kurdish forces, known as pesh merga, to cross its border with Syria to help fight militants from the group called the Islamic State who have besieged the Syrian town of Kobani for more than a month, the Turkish foreign minister announced Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/world/21Kobani/Kobani-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/21/world/21Kobani/Kobani-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/world/21Kobani/Kobani-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/world/21Kobani/Kobani-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/world/21Kobani/Kobani-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/21/world/21Kobani/Kobani-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/world/21Kobani/K