th, Donald Ervin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scientific American', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T16:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b40ac8bc-e1ca-5385-b101-dbe72dff3025', 'word_count': 1526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b40ac8bc-e1ca-5385-b101-dbe72dff3025'}, {'abstract': 'Lending Club also disclosed that it intended to reserve some of the shares to be sold in the I.P.O. for investors who use the service to lend money directly to borrowers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/lending-club-picks-n-y-s-e-as-home-for-its-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'Lending Club also disclosed that it intended to reserve some of the shares to be sold in the I.P.O. for investors who use the service to lend money directly to borrowers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Lending Club finally begins life as a publicly traded company, the giant of the peer-to-peer lending industry will do so on the Big Board, the same exchange where many of the banks it has sought to displace now trade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/business/dbpix-lending-club/dbpix-lending-club-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/21/business/dbpix-lending-club/dbpix-lending-club-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 