witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/63387c5c-fe0b-564d-beb7-705bf8328954', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/63387c5c-fe0b-564d-beb7-705bf8328954'}, {'abstract': 'Relief agencies are finding it difficult to raise money to combat Ebola and are increasingly relying on large gifts from people like Mark Zuckerberg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/business/donations-for-ebola-relief-efforts-are-slow-to-take-off.html', 'snippet': 'Relief agencies are finding it difficult to raise money to combat Ebola and are increasingly relying on large gifts from people like Mark Zuckerberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mark Zuckerberg of Facebook and his wife, Priscilla Chan, donated $25 million last week to support the treatment of Ebola victims and their families, they gave the gift to the foundation that funnels private donations to the Centers for Disease Control, not one of the nonprofit groups that Americans typically shower with money during a humanitarian crisis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donations for Ebola Relief Are Slow to Gain Speed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Donations for Ebola Relief Are Slow to Gain Speed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Partners in Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '