': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a467da32-8b58-5f4f-88ab-cfd70b560a76', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a467da32-8b58-5f4f-88ab-cfd70b560a76'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Opera’s first performance of “The Death of Klinghoffer” was disrupted twice, but both protesters were ushered out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/arts/music/metropolitan-opera-forges-ahead-on-klinghoffer-in-spite-of-protests.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Opera’s first performance of “The Death of Klinghoffer” was disrupted twice, but both protesters were ushered out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Metropolitan Opera’s first performance of John Adams’s “The Death of Klinghoffer” on Monday night, men and women in evening attire walked through a maze of police barricades, while protesters shouted “Shame!” and “Terror is not art!” One demonstrator held aloft a white handkerchief splattered with red. Others, in wheelchairs set up for the occasion, lined Columbus Avenue. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Greet Metropolitan Opera’s Premiere of ‘Klinghoffer’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protests Greet Met’s Premiere of ‘Klinghoffer’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestine Liberation Organization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Death of Klinghoffer (Opera)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T17:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c549afa8-7b95-56dc-a872-08e2d9204e92', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c549afa8-7b95-56dc-a872-08e2d9204e92'}, {'abstract': 'Samuel Hynes’s new book, “The Unsubstantial Air: American Fliers in the First World War,” was inspired by his life of flying, most notably as an airman in World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/books/samuel-hynes-discusses-his-book-the-unsubstantial-air.html', 'snippet': 'Samuel Hynes’s new book, “The Unsubstantial Air: American Fliers in the First World War,” was inspired by his life of flying, most notably as an airman in World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRINCETON, N.J. — In his upstairs study, on a quiet side street here, Samuel Hynes has hung three black-and-white photographs that succinctly illustrate his life. On top is the poet W. H. Auden, wearing academic robes. On the bottom is an autographed photo of an aged Thomas Hardy. And in between, faded and a little out of focus, is a group picture of Marine Torpedo Bombing Squadron 232.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/jpsamhynes/jpsamhynes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/jpsamhynes/jpsamhynes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/jpsamhynes/jpsamhynes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/jpsamhynes/jpsamhynes-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/jpsamhynes/jpsamhynes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/jpsamhynes/jpsamhynes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/jpsamhynes/jpsamhynes-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Eye of a Pilot Serves a Writer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Eye of a Pilot Serves a Writer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hynes, Samuel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Unsubstantial Air: American Fliers in the First World War (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T17:07:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e5712dd-7313-54a7-bbbe-15df1acc9961', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e5712dd-7313-54a7-bbbe-15df1acc9961'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/walkabout-ebola-stokes-fears-among-travelers-picasso-museum-in-paris-reopens/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Home Two of three people diagnosed with Ebola in the United States flew on commercial flights shortly before falling ill. To put that in perspective, on an average day, about two million people fly with\xa0United States airlines. Still, travel agents say customers are asking whether it’s safe to fly. (USA Today)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/travel/Walkabout-picasso/Walkabout-picasso-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/travel/Walkabout-picasso/Walkabout-picasso-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/travel/Walkabout-picasso/Walkabout-picasso-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/travel/Walkabout-picasso/Walkabout-picasso-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/travel/Walkabout-picasso/Walkabout-picasso-thumbStandar