h Settlers Move Into East Jerusalem Neighborhood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: More Jewish Settlers Move Into East Jerusalem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T17:18:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2923ad5-819f-5299-811f-ca0f49a6a2ac', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2923ad5-819f-5299-811f-ca0f49a6a2ac'}, {'abstract': 'The unusual action indicates a heightened concern among regulators over the air bags, which are linked to at least two deaths in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/business/defect-in-takata-air-bags-prompts-urgent-warning-to-drivers.html', 'snippet': 'The unusual action indicates a heightened concern among regulators over the air bags, which are linked to at least two deaths in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal auto safety regulators on Monday warned the owners of about 4.7 million vehicles with defective air bags made by the Takata Corporation that they should “act immediately” to have them fixed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defect in Takata Air Bags Prompts Urgent Warning to Drivers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Takata Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T17:24:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f342657-b8c9-50e9-9bc6-c808a6219f9d', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f342657-b8c9-50e9-9bc6-c808a6219f9d'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Patrick Leahy, the Vermont Democrat who chairs the Judiciary Committee, called on Comcast to commit to never allow so-called fast lanes, or paid prioritization, on its network, even beyond the expiration of a current promise to avoid the practice through 2018.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/senator-calls-on-comcast-to-extend-net-neutrality-pledge/', 'snippet': 'Senator Patrick Leahy, the Vermont Democrat who chairs the Judiciary Committee, called on Comcast to commit to never allow so-called fast lanes, or paid prioritization, on its network, even beyond the expiration of a current promise to avoid the p...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chairman of the Senate committee that oversees mergers and antitrust issues sent a pointed letter to Comcast on Monday asking the company to strengthen its commitment to net neutrality by pledging never to create Internet fast lanes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/technology/20bits-leahy/20bits-leahy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/technology/20bits-leahy/20bits-leahy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/technology/20bits-leahy/20bits-leahy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/technology/20bits-leahy/20bits-leahy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1322, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/technology/20bits-leahy/20bits-leahy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/20/technology/20bits-leahy/20bits-leahy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/technology/20bits-leahy/20bits-leahy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Calls on Comcast to Extend Net Neutrality Pledge', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leahy, Patrick J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T17:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0504dc61-0a75-59e3-bb61-7e821bf7e04a', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0504dc61-0a75-59e3-bb61-7e821bf7e04a'}, {'abstract': 'Tarte tatin — not apple pie — is the single best thing you can make with fall’s most plentiful and alluring fruit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/dining/a-foolproof-tarte-tatin-recipe-from-gotham-bar-and-grill.html', 'snippet': 'Tarte tatin — not apple pie — is the single best thing you can make with fall’s most plentiful and alluring fruit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple pie is not easy. I have executed lovely crusts folded around inedible sour fillings, perfect fruit sandwiched between a pale bottom crust and a burned lattice top, and most other permutations of pie fail.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Easy as Pie', 'kicker': 'Recipe Lab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As American as Tarte Tatin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moskin, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paprocki, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paprocki, Ron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T17:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7f74b87-c98a-5c94-be43-691688ddb8a1', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7f74b87-c98a-5c94-be43-691688ddb8a1'}, {'abstract': 'An S.E.C. case against a high-frequency trading firm shows how difficult it is to draw the line between acceptable trading strategies and manipulation, Peter J. Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/why-high-frequency-trading-is-so-hard-to-regulate/', 'snippet': 'An S.E.C. case against a high-frequency trading firm shows how difficult it is to draw the line between acceptable trading strategies and manipulation, Peter J. Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stock manipulation is one of the great bugaboos among investors because it generates fear that the market is as rigged as a three-card monte game on a Bronx street corner. Since the publication of Michael Lewis’s book “Flash Boys” earlier this year, high-frequency traders have come under increased scrutiny for their use of sophisticated computer programs that can whipsaw prices by flooding the market with orders in milliseconds. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/business/dbpix-ebay/dbpix-ebay-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/21/business/dbpix-ebay/dbpix-ebay-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/business/dbpix-ebay/dbpix-ebay-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': No