ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa41e7e5-c925-56b7-bbc0-f30392b7161a', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa41e7e5-c925-56b7-bbc0-f30392b7161a'}, {'abstract': 'The new service, which is expected to start by June, will emphasize a curated selection of films intended for an art house audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/business/media/tribeca-enterprises-and-lionsgate-to-team-up-on-subscription-video.html', 'snippet': 'The new service, which is expected to start by June, will emphasize a curated selection of films intended for an art house audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Tribeca Enterprises and Lionsgate said on Monday that they would start an online video-on-demand service focused on “curated” prestige titles drawn from their libraries, along with a selection of foreign films.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tribeca Enterprises and Lionsgate to Team Up on Subscription Video', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tribeca and Lionsgate to Start On-Demand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribeca Enterprises', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lions Gate Entertainment Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tribeca Film Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Jane', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T17:59:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e493c515-8513-5df5-aca9-ab6a59650fd4', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e493c515-8513-5df5-aca9-ab6a59650fd4'}, {'abstract': 'Right now, only 350,000 or so American companies export their goods and services.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/growing-american-exports-one-small-business-at-a-time/', 'snippet': 'Right now, only 350,000 or so American companies export their goods and services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The International Trade Administration is like no other federal agency. Its theme for this year is “Dare to Be Great” — not the kind of rallying cry you expect from government administrators.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Growing American Exports, One Small Business at a Time', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Stefan M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weidenhamer, Deb', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auction Systems Auctioneers and Appraisers Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T18:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Weidenhamer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weidenhamer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5f0e092-cc53-5332-8277-ad2de8e3ea1b', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5f0e092-cc53-5332-8277-ad2de8e3ea1b'}, {'abstract': 'The Broken Arm has teamed up with the footwear label Adieu on a new design for its signature creeper style.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/adieu-the-broken-arm-type-28-creeper-shoe/', 'snippet': 'The Broken Arm has teamed up with the footwear label Adieu on a new design for its signature creeper style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like its Parisian neighbors Colette and L’Eclaireur, The Broken Arm boutique has quickly amassed a stylish cult following since opening last year. Its founders, Romain Joste, Guillaume Steinmetz and Anaïs Lafarge, operate under a simple philosophy: They only sell what they truly love. Joste, Steinmetz and Lafarge know a good matchup when they see one — they currently stock items like a Camper and Bernhard Willhelm-designed sandal and sneakers by Carven for No Name — and the trio has lately teamed up with the shoe label Adieu, also based in Paris, to produce Adieu’s first collaborative design. Founded by longtime friends Benjamin Caron and Isabel Guédon, previously a designer with Lanvin and Saint Laurent, Adieu is a favorite of the Broken Arm team. “Adieu reinvents each season while keeping the spirit and codes of the brand,” Steinmetz says. “Their work is uncompromising, raw and true to what they are intrinsically.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20adieu-bobb/20adieu-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {