ew fundraising strategy as it tries to augment its government financing with large donations from individuals and corporations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Smithsonian Institution said on Monday that it planned to raise $1.5 billion by 2017 in its first institution-wide fundraising campaign and had already raised more than $1 billion of that sum from private individuals, foundations, corporations and other donors. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smithsonian Details New Fundraising Approach', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubenstein, David M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group LP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Museum of American History', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T19:59:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fe4b3a6-bc8d-5d77-97fb-b2d52058a22d', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fe4b3a6-bc8d-5d77-97fb-b2d52058a22d'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Patrick J. Leahy, chairman of the Judiciary Committee, is asking Comcast not to “engage in paid prioritization” of Internet content after its proposed takeover of Time Warner Cable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/20/from-bits-senator-denounces-paid-prioritization-of-web-content/', 'snippet': 'Senator Patrick J. Leahy, chairman of the Judiciary Committee, is asking Comcast not to “engage in paid prioritization” of Internet content after its proposed takeover of Time Warner Cable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Federal Communications Commission reviews the antitrust implications of Comcast’s proposed takeover of Time Warner Cable, the Bits technology blog reports that the powerful chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee is asking Comcast to promise not to “engage in paid prioritization” of Internet content.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Bits: Senator Denounces ‘Paid Prioritization’ of Web Content', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T20:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73caa436-1980-598f-a226-3580c9db1561', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73caa436-1980-598f-a226-3580c9db1561'}, {'abstract': 'The allure of a free lunch is hard to resist, even for conservatives.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/republicans-against-toll-roads/', 'snippet': 'The allure of a free lunch is hard to resist, even for conservatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milton Friedman, the standard bearer for free-market economics, was so fond of the phrase “there is no such thing as a free lunch” that he used it as the title of a book of essays. Mr. Friedman is a hero to the right, but it would seem that the volume has not been well read by Republicans in Texas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Against Toll Roads', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tolls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Milton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T20:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aafa2165-fd32-5f6f-b62a-b1f0877d813a', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aafa2165-fd32-5f6f-b62a-b1f0877d813a'}, {'abstract': 'The author of the just-released “Brooks Headley’s Fancy Desserts” and part-time rocker offers up the secret to his Torta Caprese — and songs to listen to while preparing it.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/20/brooks-headley-fancy-desserts-recipe-playlist/', 'snippet': 'The author of the just-released “Brooks Headley’s Fancy Desserts” and part-time rocker offers up the secret to his Torta Caprese — and songs to listen to while preparing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a long time, Brooks Headley\xa0—\xa0the James Beard Award-winning executive pastry chef of Del Posto in New York, part-time veggie burger master and author of the just-released “Brooks Headley’s Fancy Desserts” ($30, W.W. Norton) — has led a double life. He started young, drumming in a succession of semi-obscure but revered underground bands down through the years, like Born Against, Skull Kontrol and Wrangler Brutes. Eventually he was also cooking at reputed restaurants, including Galileo in Washington, D.C., Los Angeles’s Campanile and Del Posto — the brightest star in Mario Batali and Joe Bastianich’s Italian-cuisine firmament — with an approach,\xa0not unlike his style of playing, that balanced precision and chaos. Headley kept these two sides of his life distinct, working full-time and slipping out of town on tour when he could. After Wrangler Brutes broke up in 2004, he focused primarily on cooking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20hartman-brooks/20hartman-brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20hartman-brooks/20hartman-brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20hartman-brooks/20hartman-brooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20hartman-brooks/20hartman-brooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1652, 'width': 1278, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20hartman-brooks/20hartman-brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20hartman-brooks/20hartman-brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/20/t-magazine/20hartman-brooks/20hartman-brooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooks Headley, Chef and Drummer, Shares a Recipe and a Playlist', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T20:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diego Hadis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diego', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hadis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5750858-441d-521a-86a8-7fe45c8d10c1', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5750858-441d-521a-86a8-7fe45c8d10c1'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Brown, the Republican Senate candidate in New Hampshire, is the latest in the Fixing Washington video series on First Draft, where he argues for more independents in Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/20/first-draft-video-scott-brown-on-fixing-washington/', 'snippet': 'Scott Brown, the Republican Senate candidate in New Hampshire, is the latest in the Fixing Washington video series on First Draft, where he argues for more independents in Congress.', 'lead_paragraph