ight television and read some mean Twitter messages in a YouTube video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ed Gillespie, the Republican Senate nominee in Virginia, copped a bit from late night television and read some mean Twitter messages in a YouTube video. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gillespie Reads Mean Tweets', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillespie, Ed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-20T20:36:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf65bd8d-12a7-5b59-aedd-402e6d2a805a', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf65bd8d-12a7-5b59-aedd-402e6d2a805a'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet’s fall season brought rich fare and was powerfully eventful, with numerous premieres, a potent farewell and a flood of role debuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballets-powerfully-eventful-fall-season.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet’s fall season brought rich fare and was powerfully eventful, with numerous premieres, a potent farewell and a flood of role debuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City Ballet’s fall season brought rich fare: world premieres by five choreographers; a New York premiere by a sixth; the historic farewell of the ballerina Wendy Whelan, after 30 years; and many revivals, which included 16 works by George Balanchine and a flood of role debuts bringing attention to dancers throughout the ranks. The fall season now seems like a fixture; it’s strange to remember that it began only in 2010, and that neither its 2010 nor 2011 editions amounted to much. Not everything in the 2014 season was good, but it was powerfully eventful.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/SEASON/SEASON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/SEASON/SEASON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/SEASON/SEASON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/SEASON/SEASON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/SEASON/SEASON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/SEASON/SEASON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/SEASON/SEASON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bountiful Season of Dizzying Challenges and New Peaks', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_k