n-in-what-officials-call-act-of-terror-dies.html', 'snippet': 'A warrant officer was killed and another soldier was injured in a car crash that the police said was the result of a Canadian man’s turn to radical Islam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — A hit-and-run car crash that killed one soldier and injured another this week was a terrorist attack, Canadian politicians, police and military commanders all suggested Tuesday, saying it had resulted from another Canadian’s turn to radical Islam. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hit-and-Run That Killed Canadian Soldier Is Called Terrorist Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hit-and-Run in Canada Is Called Terrorist Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hit-and-Run Drivers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouleau-Couture, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harper, Stephen J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T13:01:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9971364c-7918-5977-9fac-af0859bfc268', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9971364c-7918-5977-9fac-af0859bfc268'}, {'abstract': 'Why was Ron Paul staring at me?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/fly-the-derpy-skies/', 'snippet': 'Why was Ron Paul staring at me?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night Atif Mian and I flew up to Boston for a conference — and as I slid into my seat, who should I see staring at me but Ron Paul. It turned out that all of the seatback screens in the plane were showing Newsmax TV — who knew there was such a thing? Is it there to serve people who find Fox News too liberal? — and as best I could tell from the visual context (the sound was blessedly off), the elder Paul was lecturing us about monetary policy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fly the Derpy Skies', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T13:13:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c20ffe3-dc66-5b91-af94-4a25d0c1ff47', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c20ffe3-dc66-5b91-af94-4a25d0c1ff47'}, {'abstract': 'A veterinary medicine company, Ouro Fino Saúde Animal Participações, made its debut on Tuesday amid a weak economy and political uncertainty in Brazil.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/brazils-first-i-p-o-for-2014-to-start-trading/', 'snippet': 'A veterinary medicine company, Ouro Fino Saúde Animal Participações, made its debut on Tuesday amid a weak economy and political uncertainty in Brazil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil – Brazil’s first initial public offering of the year started trading on Tuesday as a veterinary medicine company, Ouro Fino Saúde Animal Participações, made its debut.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The 