ry of ‘High Times’', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 Decades of Inhaling Deeply', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'High Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chong, Tommy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T14:36:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/46a74a88-4d88-56da-b229-5a16bab46439', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46a74a88-4d88-56da-b229-5a16bab46439'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrities, designers and journalists took to social media to express their sadness over the death of the legendary designer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/fashion/mourning-oscar-de-la-rentas-passing-on-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'Celebrities, designers and journalists took to social media to express their sadness over the death of the legendary designer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday evening, Oscar de la Renta, a couturier whose career spanned more than a half-century, died at his home after an eight-year battle with cancer. Mr. de la Renta was widely known for outfitting Hollywood’s finest, including Sarah Jessica Parker, Taylor Swift and Jennifer Lawrence. He dressed four American first ladies and, most recently, designed the gown that Amal Alamuddin wore to wed George Clooney. As news of Mr. de la Renta’s passing spread, admiring celebrities, fellow designers and style writers took to Twitter to honor the man whom some considered fashion’s foremost gentleman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mourning Oscar de la Renta’s Passing on Twitter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Renta, Oscar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T14:48:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Fashion', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79985fd8-0827-57a0-8d8f-3b7115381b32', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79985fd8-0827-57a0-8d8f-3b7115381b32'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: An Ethiopian athlete set a marathon world record in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/1964-ethiopian-wins-2nd-olympic-marathon-in-tokyo/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: An Ethiopian athlete set a marathon world record in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Abebe Bikila, a member of Emperor Haile Selassie’s bodyguard, made Olympic history today when he won the marathon for the second Games in succession. Bikila’s victory, in the world’s best time for the marathon, was the climax of a final day of Olympic athletics in which many world records were shattered. In other track highlights today, the United States men’s relay teams set two world records; New Zealand’s Peter Snell completed his middle- distance double by strolling home the winner of the 1.500; and Russian Valery Brumel won the high-jumping title.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Oct. 22, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/blogs/22iht-oldoct22-bikila/22iht-oldoct22-bikila-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/22/blogs/22iht-oldoct22-bikila/22iht-oldoct22-bikila-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/blogs/22iht-oldoct22-bikila/22iht-oldoct22-bikila-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/blogs/22iht-oldoct22-bikila/22iht-oldoct22-bikila-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/blogs/22iht-oldoct22-bikila/22iht-oldoct22-bikila-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/22/blogs/22iht-oldoct22-bikila/22iht-oldoct22-bikila-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/blogs/22iht-oldoct22-bikila/22iht-oldoct22-bikila-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Ethiopian Wins 2nd Olympic Marathon in Tokyo', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2,