y Ballet principal, and Crazy Legs, the Bronx-born break dancer, presenting an award side by side. Yes to technical difficulties and no technical difficulties. Yes to free pizza for everyone after the show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bessie Awards Honor a Wide World of Dance', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T15:20:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbd5fa94-288f-5750-accf-03c5c4ae3874', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbd5fa94-288f-5750-accf-03c5c4ae3874'}, {'abstract': 'A healthy influx of young and college-educated people is important to a city, but percentage increase must be seen in context.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/upshot/where-the-graduates-are-going-and-where-they-already-are.html', 'snippet': 'A healthy influx of young and college-educated people is important to a city, but percentage increase must be seen in context.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Which cities are magnets for young college graduates?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/upshot/22UP-Cities/22UP-Cities-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/22/upshot/22UP-Cities/22UP-Cities-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargehe