e-team-examines-human-rights-watch-investigators.html', 'snippet': '“E-Team,” a documentary, follows the high-risk work of four globe-trotting investigators for the organization Human Rights Watch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bullet casings and shrapnel are probably not the most requested gifts by children whose parents travel for a living, but then most children don’t have parents like Anna Neistat and Ole Solvang. As emergency investigators for the international organization Human Rights Watch, they have raised a son whose keepsake preferences owe more to war zones than to vacation guides.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gallantry and Glamour in a War Zone', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gallantry and Glamour in a War Zone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'E-Team (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T18:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/504c2bd8-6f33-5711-9ada-16cc67248645', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/504c2bd8-6f33-5711-9ada-16cc67248645'}, {'abstract': 'The employer mandate was supposed to take effect at the beginning of this year.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/answering-the-hard-questions-on-the-a-c-a-does-the-employer-mandate-apply-to-your-business/', 'snippet': 'The employer mandate was supposed to take effect at the beginning of this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s post, another in our series attempting to answer lingering questions about the Affordable Care Act’s impact on small businesses, goes to one of the fundamental issues the law raises for employers: the responsibility to offer health insurance to workers or face a penalty. The employer mandate, as it’s known, applies to companies with at least 50 employees. Originally, it was supposed to take effect at the beginning of this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answering the Hard Questions on the A.C.A.: Does the Employer Mandate Apply to Your Business?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T18:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09efb977-17f4-54e7-9059-97890e9838cf', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09efb977-17f4-54e7-9059-97890e9838cf'}, {'abstract': 'A glimpse at what some of the guys