ri': 'nyt://article/0ee5eb6a-f2fb-54bd-8e64-793b3ce0be04'}, {'abstract': 'Vodka stars at this spot, where the menu includes more than 50 brands of the spirit, as well as a selection of small plates meant to complement a night of imbibing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/travel/restaurant-report-kachka-in-portland-ore-.html', 'snippet': 'Vodka stars at this spot, where the menu includes more than 50 brands of the spirit, as well as a selection of small plates meant to complement a night of imbibing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Kachka, a Russian restaurant that opened in Portland in April, there are no servers wearing Red Army garb, no silly dish names referencing Communist rule (KGBean dip, anyone?). The décor does skew kitschy — Khrushchev-era knickknacks in a homey-babushka setting — but the chef Bonnie Morales, a first-generation American of Russian parents (her maiden name is Frumkin), does an admirable job of enlivening a cuisine known for its stodginess by combining Slavic-inspired fare with a typically Portland emphasis on quality, locally sourced ingredients.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/travel/26BITES1/26BITES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/travel/26BITES1/26BITES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/travel/26BITES1/26BITES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/travel/26BITES1/26BITES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name'