and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T20:57:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eduardo Porter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eduardo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Porter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d57e8374-dc27-5253-b57b-7768d0f618dd', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d57e8374-dc27-5253-b57b-7768d0f618dd'}, {'abstract': 'In an exclusive video, the artist opens up his studio to discuss his collaboration with the record label, which celebrates its 15th anniversary this year.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/ghostly-international-15th-anniversary-charles-hinman/', 'snippet': 'In an exclusive video, the artist opens up his studio to discuss his collaboration with the record label, which celebrates its 15th anniversary this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since its founding in 1999, Ghostly International has grown beyond its roots as an electronic dance music label to encompass art and music distribution and an online shop. To celebrate its 15th anniversary, Ghostly is partnering with artists, designers and like-minded companies to release a run of limited-edition works. To kick off a year of collaborations, Ghostly International Editions, the visual-art arm of the brand, is issuing a small run of prints by the artist Charles Hinman, who for 42 years has been working from a studio space on the Bowery in downtown Manhattan. His 3-D canvases, collected by MoMA and exhibited at the Whitney and the Tel Aviv Museum of Art, explore the relationship between what Hinman calls “the real space of sculpture and the illusory space of painting.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/t-magazine/21hinman-yuan/21hinman-yuan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/21/t-magazine/21hinman-yuan/21hinman-yuan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/t-magazine/21hinman-yuan/21hinman-yuan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/t-magazine/21hinman-yuan/21hinman-yuan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/t-magazine/21hinman-yuan/21hinman-yuan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/21/t-magazine/21hinman-yuan/21hinman-yuan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/t-magazine/21hinman-yuan/21hinman-yuan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Charles Hinman Creates a Limited-Edition Print for Ghostly International', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hinman, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ghostly Inter