ically serious direction for exhibitions at the National Museum of the American Indian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Cornplanter left his mark. So did Big Sky, Handsome Lake and Soonohquaukau. Accompanied by 1,600 members of their tribes, the leaders of the Six Nations had assembled near Lake Canandaigua in upstate New York in 1794 to negotiate a treaty with the United States government. When the document was complete, each scratched a skewed X, certified with a red-wax seal. Below came the signature of George Washington. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/design/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/design/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/design/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/design/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/design/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/design/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/arts/design/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO/20141022NATIVE-slide-9KVO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Understanding Wasn’t Mutual ', 'kicker': 'Exhibition Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Understanding Wasn’t Mutual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothstein, Edward', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Museum of the American Indian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Treaties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T21:03:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e63922a-9aae-55ff-bd4f-f08bcbd27511', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e63922a-9aae-55ff-bd4f-f08bcbd27511'}, {'abstract': 'Marijuana is legal in some states and under some circumstances, and can now be munched and drunk as well as smoked. How does that change the way we talk about it with our kids?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/21/this-is-not-your-mothers-marijuana-talk-so-what-should-we-say/', 'snippet': 'Marijuana is legal in some states and under some circumstances, and can now be munched and drunk as well as smoked. How does that change the way we talk about it with our kids?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marijuana has changed. The laws around it are in flux; as of this writing, marijuana for medical use is legal in 23 states and the District of Columbia; two of those states (Colorado and Washington) have legalized recreational use as well. The stuff itself, once green, leafy and intended for smoking, has undergone a transformation that I’ve written about before: It may be a drug, but it looks like candy.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/us/motherlode-mj-bears/motherlode-mj-bears-jumbo.png', 'height': 297, 'width': 493, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/us/motherlode-mj-bears/motherlode-mj-bears-superJumbo.png', 'height': 297, 'width': 493, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/us/motherlode-mj-bears/motherlode-mj-bears-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/21/us/motherlode-mj-bears/motherlode-mj-bears-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/21/us/motherlode-mj-bears/motherlode-mj-bears-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is Not Your Mother’s Marijuana Talk. So What Should We Say?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': 