, 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/world/22hongkong-video/22hongkong-video-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Authorities and Students Meet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hong Kong Federation of Students', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T21:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/18ac07db-c949-580f-a0bd-e61875d374c4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/18ac07db-c949-580f-a0bd-e61875d374c4'}, {'abstract': 'Haroon Aswat, a Briton, is wanted in the United States on accusations that he conspired in 1999 to set up a terrorist training camp in Oregon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/world/europe/britain-extradites-terrorism-suspect-to-us.html', 'snippet': 'Haroon Aswat, a Briton, is wanted in the United States on accusations that he conspired in 1999 to set up a terrorist training camp in Oregon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — After nearly a decade, Britain has extradited to the United States a man alleged to have been a colleague of Mostafa Kamel Mostafa, known as Abu Hamza al-Masri, a London imam convicted of terrorism charges in New York in May, the police said Tuesday. The British say the man, Haroon Aswat, 40, is a paranoid schizophrenic and has been undergoing treatment in a high-security psychiatric hospital since 2008. A British citizen, Mr. Aswat is wanted in the United States, accused of conspiring with Mr. Mustafa to set up a terrorist training camp in Bly, Ore., in 1999. Last year, the European Court of Human Rights blocked his extradition, ruling that his detention in a potentially more hostile environment could further harm his mental and physical health. After American assurances, London’s High Court approved the extradition last month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Extradites Terrorism Suspect to U.S.', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Mentally Ill Terrorism Suspect, Long Sought by the U.S., Is Extradited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aswat, Haroon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T21:10:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14009399-468f-5694-be2d-d043d6123e68', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14009399-468f-5694-be2d-d043d6123e68'}, {'abstract': 'Abdullah Ibrahim, who just turned 80, performs in Carnegie Hall’s Ubuntu: Music and Arts of South Africa festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/arts/music/abdullah-ibrahim-at-the-schomburg-center.html', 'snippet': 'Abdullah Ibrahim, who just turned 80, performs in Carnegie Hall’s Ubuntu: Music and Arts of South Africa festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The South African pianist and composer Abdullah Ibrahim, who dealt out a broad sampler of range and power in a free two-hour performance at the Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture on Monday, seems to have found his originality the way a lot of artists do. He has let his work expose a kind of tension, a feeling of improbability or almost impossibility. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/arts/ABDULLAH/ABDULLAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/22/arts/ABDULLAH/ABDULLAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/arts/ABDULLAH/ABDULLAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/arts/ABDULLAH/ABDULLAH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/arts/ABDULLAH/ABDULLAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/22/arts/ABDULLAH/ABDULLAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/arts/ABDULLAH/ABDULLAH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Song Can Contain Multitudes', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Song Can Contain Multitudes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-21T21:17:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d2c9daf-2e68-5b1a-98eb-9385b74116dc', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d2c9daf-2e68-5b1a-98eb-9385b74116dc'}, {'abstract': 'There were fewer chanteuses onstage at this year’s New York Cabaret Convention than in the past, and a lot more male performers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/arts/music/male-performers-dominate-new-york-cabaret-convention.html', 'snippet': 'There were fewer chanteuses onstage at this year’s New York Cabaret Convention than in the past, and a lot more male performers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 25th New York Cabaret Convention began on Monday evening with a testosterone shot heard round Manhattan. For the first time, its opening-night concert, in Rose Hall at Jazz at Lincoln Center, was dominated by men. Along with the usual suave piano-bar veterans there was a healthy sprinkling of hard-charging young turks with one foot in rock ’n’ roll. Its host, Aaron Weinstein, the jazz violinist and raised-eyebrow wit who evokes a young Jack Benny, is only 29. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/a