on': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b0fd7ff-b43b-55f7-b303-bd2289fb4b82', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b0fd7ff-b43b-55f7-b303-bd2289fb4b82'}, {'abstract': 'Two leaders with a lot of influence who matter in very different ways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/opinion/thomas-friedman-putin-and-the-pope.html', 'snippet': 'Two leaders with a lot of influence who matter in very different ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading the papers these days I find that the two world leaders who stir the most passion in me are Pope Francis and Vladimir Putin, the president of Russia. One is everything you’d want in a leader, the other everything you wouldn’t want. One holds sway over 1.2 billion Roman Catholics, the other over nine time zones. One keeps surprising us with his capacity for empathy, the other by how much he has become a first-class jerk and thug. But neither can be ignored and both have an outsized influence on the world today.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType':