-9ed4-59d6-b793-7c54ac8bbf17'}, {'abstract': 'Nigeria and Senegal are free of the virus, and 43 people in Texas who had been monitored for 21 days have been cleared without any of them becoming sick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/opinion/some-good-news-on-the-ebola-front.html', 'snippet': 'Nigeria and Senegal are free of the virus, and 43 people in Texas who had been monitored for 21 days have been cleared without any of them becoming sick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans who are worried about the risk of an Ebola outbreak in this country can take heart from two recent successes. In Texas, 43 people who were being monitored because they had had direct or indirect contact with Thomas Eric Duncan, a Liberian who died of Ebola in a Dallas hospital, were found clear of the Ebola virus on Monday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Good News on the Ebola Front', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Good News on the Ebola Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Senegal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T00:49:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dd2252e-d90a-5a54-add7-4e523fe79ab6', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dd2252e-d90a-5a54-add7-4e523fe79ab6'}, {'abstract': 'HBO and CBS are moving toward à la carte services, a more pragmatic approach to selling content that should benefit consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/opinion/hbo-and-cbs-move-toward-selling-content-directly-to-consumers.html', 'snippet': 'HBO and CBS are moving toward à la carte services, a more pragmatic approach to selling content that should benefit consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Executives at media and cable companies have been resisting the idea of selling TV channels à la carte for years, saying it was not financially feasible. But that resistance is starting to give way to a more pragmatic approach that should benefit consumers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unraveling the Cable Bundle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unraveling the Cable Bundle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares