king out five as San Francisco became the first team to beat Kansas City this postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — It took nine games and a masterful pitching performance by Madison Bumgarner, but someone finally found a method for beating the Kansas City Royals this postseason. The Royals had rampaged their way through the early and middle rounds by winning their first eight games, and came into the World Series on a seemingly irrepressible tide of momentum.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/sports/SERIES1/SERIES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/22/sports/SERIES1/SERIES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/sports/SERIES1/SERIES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/sports/SERIES1/SERIES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/sports/SERIES1/SERIES1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/22/sports/SERIES1/SERIES1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/sports/SERIES1/SERIES1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants and Madison Bumgarner Upstage Royals', 'kicker': 'Giants 7, Royals 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bumgarner and Giants Upstage Royals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Royals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shields, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bumgarner, Madison', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T03:41:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39efd735-26cb-59fd-b847-e13afc65eb37', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39efd735-26cb-59fd-b847-e13afc65eb37'}, {'abstract': 'Margaret Braun, whose grandiose designs have graced a royal wedding and lit up a Brooklyn foodie festival, takes pupils on a culinary tour of Marche next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/t-magazine/margaret-braun-cakewalk-italy.html', 'snippet': 'Margaret Braun, whose grandiose designs have graced a royal wedding and lit up a Brooklyn foodie festival, takes pupils on a culinary tour of Marche next month.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What is inspiration? It’s not enough!” says the New York City-based sugar artist Margaret Braun. “I want to harness a flavor, or look, or sound and I want to share that with people.” Braun, who began as an aspiring artist toiling full-time in bakeries in the ’80s, soon combined uncommon colors and forms with confections, and became a self-made designer of works that fuse culinary arts and fine art. Her designs have included 2,000 individual desserts for a royal wedding in the Middle East, a mosaic-like treat for a Venetian masquerade ball and a hand-painted, 28-foot-tall wooden sculpture — that glowed in the dark — for Brooklyn’s Googamooga festival. These labor-intensive sweets, which often include pearl dust and gold leaf, are the ultimate in edible luxury. “Early on I learned how to do great work — and then let go,” Braun says about making beautiful things that have an inevitably short shelf life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/t-magazine/15braun-cohen/15braun-cohen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/15/t-magazine/15braun-cohen/15braun-cohen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/t-magazine/15braun-cohen/15braun-cohen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/t-magazine/15braun-cohen/15braun-cohen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/t-magazine/15braun-cohen/15braun-cohen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/15/t-magazine/15braun-cohen/15braun-cohen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/15/t-magazine/15braun-cohen/15braun-cohen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sugar Artist Leads a Cake Walk Through Central Italy', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TLiving', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e40de4be-393f-52a8-ac64-983a749cd1d3', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e40de4be-393f-52a8-ac64-983a749cd1d3'}, {'abstract': 'Volunteers were able to exercise harder when they listened to their favorite songs.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/how-music-can-boost-a-high-intensity-workout/', 'snippet': 'Volunteers were able to exercise harder when they listened to their favorite songs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intense, highly demanding exercise has many health benefits and one signal drawback. It can be physically unpleasant, which deters many people from beginning or sticking with an intense exercise program. An encouraging new study, however, suggests that listening to music makes strenuous workouts feel easier and may nudge people into pushing themselves harder than they had thought possible. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/science/28PHY