e than most surrounding towns and far more diverse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Chris and Serena Howerton had a baby last year, their 600-square-foot apartment in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, already shared with two cats, felt smaller than ever.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Affordability in Danbury, Conn., Just Over the Border', 'kicker': 'Living In', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Affordability Just Over the Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prevost, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Danbury (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T15:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae3b271c-34fb-5eb2-a895-47c957d1c35a', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae3b271c-34fb-5eb2-a895-47c957d1c35a'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French farmers disagreed with General de Gaulle’s threat to quit the E.E.C. in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/1964-french-farmers-assail-threat/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French farmers disagreed with General de Gaulle’s threat to quit the E.E.C. in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — France’s farm leadership today [Oct. 23] attacked President Charles de Gaulle’s threat to leave the European Economic Community if no agreement is reached on agricultural prices. Jean Deleau, vice-president of the national confederation of farming unions (FNSEA) indicated the general’s threat was not made to benefit the French farmer — as might appear — but for international political reason. The French farmers, he said, would rather wait until 1970 for a Common Market in farm goods than lose everything in a breakup now.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Oct. 23, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: French Farmers Assail Threat', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Gaulle, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T15:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cabbd897-55d8-5b96-bd98-84862ebbf10f', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cabbd897-55d8-5b96-bd98-84862ebbf10f'}, {'abstract': 'Arturo Bejar is trying to create empathy among teenage users to curb cyberbullying and harassment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/fashion/Facebook-Arturo-Bejar-Creating-Empathy-Among-Cyberbullying.html', 'snippet': 'Arturo Bejar is trying to create empathy among teenage users to curb cyberbullying and harassment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of Facebook’s 7,185 employees, Arturo Bejar may have the most difficult job.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi