he most important piece of software Apple produced. Mr. Forstall had long been one of Steve Jobs’s favored lieutenants, but in addition to presiding over a couple of prominent failures — including Apple’s Maps app — he was known for his combativeness within the company.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/business/23state-illo/23state-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/business/23state-illo/23state-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/business/23state-illo/23state-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/business/23state-illo/23state-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/business/23state-illo/23state-illo-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/business/23state-illo/23state-illo-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/business/23state-illo/23state-illo-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Strengthens Pull of Its Orbit With Each Device ', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple Strengthens Pull of Its Orbit With Each Device', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manjoo, Farhad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Timothy D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iOS (Operating System)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T16:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhad Manjoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manjoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39d9cb73-eee6-5a55-9ddf-c471d356518f', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39d9cb73-eee6-5a55-9ddf-c471d356518f'}, {'abstract': 'Maggie Gyllenhaal and Ewan McGregor are both making Broadway debuts in the revival of Tom Stoppard’s “The Real Thing.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/theater/ewan-mcgregor-and-maggie-gyllenhaal-in-the-real-thing.html', 'snippet': 'Maggie Gyllenhaal and Ewan McGregor are both making Broadway debuts in the revival of Tom Stoppard’s “The Real Thing.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For some of us, it is hard to imagine the modern theater without Tom Stoppard. His clever, imaginative and often metatheatrical works, starting with the ingenious “Rosencrantz and Guildenstern Are Dead” (1966), add intellectual heft to any theater season, and this fall, we are lucky enough to have a couple of options. In addition to the Off Broadway production of “Indian Ink” that opened last month, the Roundabout Theater Company is presenting a Broadway revival of Mr. Stoppard’s “The Real Thing.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26GUIDE2/26GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26GUIDE2/26GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26GUIDE2/26GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26GUIDE2/26GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26GUIDE2/26GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26GUIDE2/26GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26GUIDE2/26GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love, or Just Lust? Does It Matter? ', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater: Love, or Just Lust? Does It Matter?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGregor, Ewan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gyllenhaal, Maggie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Cynthia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stoppard, Tom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Josh (1969- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gold, Sam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Real Thing (Play)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T16:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/760e6257-9ff1-5ea1-8f2c-8e0a497be25b', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/760e6257-9ff1-5ea1-8f2c-8e0a497be25b'}, {'abstract': 'Neil Gaiman and Lorenzo Mattotti reinvent “Hansel and Gretel.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/books/hansel-gretel-by-neil-gaiman-and-lorenzo-mattotti.html', 'snippet': 'Neil Gaiman and Lorenzo Mattotti reinvent “Hansel and Gretel.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Written with a devastating spareness by Neil Gaiman and fearsomely illustrated in shades of black by Lorenzo Mattotti, the newest version of “Hansel and Gretel” astonishes from start to finish. It doesn’t hurt that the book itself is a gorgeous and carefully made object, with a black floral motif on its pages’ decorated borders, along with abundant red drop caps and tall, round gray page numbers. (Published by Toon Books, the New Yorker art director Françoise Mouly’s venture into richly illustrated books for children, it comes in two formats, with an oversize one that includes an afterword about the evolution of the tale.) All the well-chosen detail provides an ideal backdrop for what Gaiman and Mattotti have done with the Grimm Brothers’ familiar story of the two siblings who, after being abandoned by desperate parents, outwit their witchy captor. Their rendition brings a freshness and even a feeling of majesty to the little tale. Some great, roiling essence of the human condition — our fate of shuttling between the darkness and the light — seems to inhabit its pages.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/09/books/review/09RUSSO/09RUSSO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/09/books/review/09RUSSO/09RUSSO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/09/books/review/09RUSSO/09RUSSO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/09/books/review/09RUSSO/09RUSSO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/09/books/review/09RUSSO/09RUSSO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/09/books/review/09RUSSO/09RUSSO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/09/books/review/09RUSSO/09RUSSO-thumbLarge.j