}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T17:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6fe228f-d9fe-56c8-9d68-16f468712e00', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6fe228f-d9fe-56c8-9d68-16f468712e00'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Bush wrote a grateful message to her fans after completing 22 sold-out performances in London.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/kate-bush-thanks-fans-after-her-run-of-shows-concludes/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Bush wrote a grateful message to her fans after completing 22 sold-out performances in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that Kate Bush’s run of 22 ambitiously staged, rapturously received London concerts has come to an end, Ms. Bush has written a lavish thank-you note to her fans, and posted it on the web page where she announced the shows – her first since 1979 – in March.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kate Bush Thanks Fans After Her Run of Shows Concludes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Kate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T17:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edaf597a-7739-5829-af85-d6c7fe6ce374', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edaf597a-7739-5829-af85-d6c7fe6ce374'}, {'abstract': 'The richest Americans have almost completely recovered from the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/facts-figures-wealth-inequality-on-the-rise/', 'snippet': 'The richest Americans have almost completely recovered from the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A working paper released this month by two economists, Gabriel Zucman and Emmanuel Saez, finds that wealth inequality is growing alongside income inequality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: Wealth Inequality on the Rise', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saez, Emmanuel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zucman, Gabriel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T17:47:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ae8643a-73ca-5891-8207-642bb3cb1230', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ae8643a-73ca-5891-8207-642bb3cb1230'}, {'abstract': 'The Fed’s policies that drove down interest rates to historically low levels have actually exacerbated the inequality problem that Janet L. Yellen said concerned her, writes William D. Cohan in Street Scene.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/how-quantitative-easing-contributed-to-the-nations-inequality-problem/', 'snippet': 'The Fed’s policies that drove down interest rates to historically low levels have actually exacerbated the inequality problem that Janet L. Yellen said concerned her, writes William D. Cohan in Street Scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Janet L. Yellen, the chairwoman of the Federal Reserve, is regarded as a person of the highest integrity. And that is what’s so utterly confounding about the speech she gave in Boston last week about inequality. She did a wonderful job highlighting the growing disparity between rich and poor and how it is beginning to impinge upon what it means to be an American, but she ignored the fact that, in many ways, the Fed’s policies have compounded the problem. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/business/18fed-webpic1/18fed-webpic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/18/business/18fed-webpic1/18fed-webpic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/business/18fed-webpic1/18fed-webpic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/business/18fed-webpic1/18fed-webpic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1380, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/business/18fed-webpic1/18fed-webpic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/18/business/18fed-webpic1/18fed-webpic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/18/business/18fed-webpic1/18fed-webpic1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Quantitative Easing Contributed to the Nation’s Inequality Problem', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T17:56:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William D. Cohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9c94c4f-fe1b-5d26-b086-05b3bb96aeea', 'word_count': 1347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9c94c4f-fe1b-5d26-b086-05b3bb96aeea'}, {'abstract': 'Solange Monegro looks to Pharrell Williams for style inspiration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/fashion/style-in-corona-queens-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'Solange Monegro looks to Pharrell Williams for style inspiration.', 'lead_paragraph': '“People in Corona dress more for work, dressed down and not very fancy,” said Solange Monegro, who was spotted walking along 103rd Street in Corona, Queens. She was outfitted in a patterned Ralph Lauren bomber jacket layered over a plaid Uniqlo shirt, paired with roomy khakis and Nike sneakers. Ms. Monegro prefers men’s wear and draws inspiration from Pharrell Williams. “I do stand out a lot,” she said, “just because no one else really dresses this way around here.” This interview has been edited and condensed. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Runs in the Family', 'kicker': 'Intersection', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fashion Runs in the Family', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corona (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Pharrell', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T18:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Nikas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a1f1513-5815-5740-b8dc-faca0ad63eef', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a1f1513-5815-5740-b8dc-faca0ad63eef'}, {'abstract': 'When the firm Kaye Scholer moved its new Manhattan office this month, it did not take 95 percent of its tens of thousands of law books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/nyregion/so-little-paper-to-chase-in-a-law-firms-new-library.html', 'snippet': 'When the firm Kaye Scholer moved its new Manhattan office this month, it did not take 95 percent of its tens of thousands of law books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The law firm Kaye Scholer left a lot behind when it moved this month from 425 Park Avenue in Manhattan, where it had been since 1957, into new quarters at 250 West 55th Street.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/nyregion/BLOCKS1/BLOCKS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'x