d Death,” the Edgar Allan Poe story that begins: “The ‘Red Death’ had long devastated the country. No pestilence had ever been so fatal, or so hideous.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/arts/BOOKQUAMMEN/BOOKQUAMMEN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/arts/BOOKQUAMMEN/BOOKQUAMMEN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 904}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/arts/BOOKQUAMMEN/BOOKQUAMMEN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/arts/BOOKQUAMMEN/BOOKQUAMMEN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1704, 'width': 1131, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/arts/BOOKQUAMMEN/BOOKQUAMMEN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/arts/BOOKQUAMMEN/BOOKQUAMMEN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/arts/BOOKQUAMMEN/BOOKQUAMMEN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ebola Facts Are Scary Enough', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ebola Facts Are Scary Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quammen, Da