art operas, offered a concert of German lieder at Zankel Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leporello. Figaro. To many opera fans, those are the names synonymous with Luca Pisaroni, the 39-year-old Italian bass-baritone who has established a reputation as a first-rate singer of Mozart operas. Early next year he will return to the Metropolitan Opera as Leporello, Don Giovanni’s wily, seething servant. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Master of the Dramatic Turns Lyrical ', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Master of the Dramatic Turns Lyrical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pisaroni, Luca', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T19:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/beb155d3-12e9-5d15-9f32-f5c8c610bea3', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beb155d3-12e9-5d15-9f32-f5c8c610bea3'}, {'abstract': 'A Vice documentary series highlights the plight of African and Middle Eastern refugees headed for Italian shores —\xa0and what happens to them once (or if) they arrive.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/how-italy-became-the-refugees-gateway-to-europe/', 'snippet': 'A Vice documentary series highlights the plight of African and Middle Eastern refugees headed for Italian shores —\xa0and what happens to t