': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7847e41-e693-5399-8f95-f5eea2f4c545', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7847e41-e693-5399-8f95-f5eea2f4c545'}, {'abstract': 'In Wellington, Fla., the real estate market revolves around the equestrian community in the area, meaning you’ll pay more to live closer to the show grounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/your-money/a-place-to-hang-your-hat-and-bridles.html', 'snippet': 'In Wellington, Fla., the real estate market revolves around the equestrian community in the area, meaning you’ll pay more to live closer to the show grounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Depending on how committed their children are to the high-priced pursuit of show horses, the biggest expense for parents can be the equestrian property that goes with it. Because proximity to show venues is a paramount selling point, the most notable water feature of such expensive properties can be a horse trough. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WELLINGTON/23WELLINGTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WELLINGTON/23WELLINGTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WELLINGTON/23WELLINGTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image