9711-512a-8bee-a56602e731b7', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/820ef415-9711-512a-8bee-a56602e731b7'}, {'abstract': '“If You Lived Here You’d Be Home By Now,” inspired by a canon of thinkers and opening tomorrow at the boutique Tenoversix, features pieces that combine classical beauty with new modes of production.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/design-pop-up-los-angeles-tenoversix/', 'snippet': '“If You Lived Here You’d Be Home By Now,” inspired by a canon of thinkers and opening tomorrow at the boutique Tenoversix, features pieces that combine classical beauty with new modes of production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If every good grad-school conversation eventually comes around to the universal question of human existence — what’s the point? — then a theory-driven design pop-up opening tomorrow at the West Hollywood boutique Tenoversix\xa0offers the beginnings of an answer: that we’re all asking together. “My practice explores the interconnectivity of people, places, objects and events through the virtual and the subconscious,” says the design consultant Michelle Lane of Bread Studio, who went from a\xa0career as a fashion stylist to studying at the European Graduate School in Switzerland. “It’s nice to have objects that connect us to a shared materiality.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/t-magazine/22home-wu/22home-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/22/t-magazine/22home-wu/22home-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/22/t-magazine/22home-wu/22home-wu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJ