com/2014/10/23/your-money/can-watches-look-sharp-and-be-smart-.html', 'snippet': 'The rise of devices like the Apple Watch is creating a debate as to whether watches will remain a symbol of status and taste or shift toward high-tech tools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — For most of the last century, the wristwatch served one unambiguous purpose: to tell its wearer the time. The era of mobile phones and the rise of their smart offspring threatened that status quo — not to mention the watch industry itself. Many watchmakers reinvented themselves as purveyors of fashion, luxury and, in the most rarefied realms, art. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WATCH2/23WATCH2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WATCH2/23WATCH2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WATCH2/23WATCH2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WATCH2/23WATCH2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1333, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WATCH2/23WATCH2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/your-money/23WATCH2/23WATCH2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 