ine of autumnal kalamkari wall hangings, each made by hand in Pedana, India. The designs follow or are inspired by old Mughal patterns and are richly printed with vegetable dyes of burnt orange, antiqued red and dusty olive and gold.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23CURR_TEXTILES/23CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23CURR_TEXTILES/23CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23CURR_TEXTILES/23CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23CURR_TEXTILES/23CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1837, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23CURR_TEXTILES/23CURR_TEXTILES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23CURR_TEXTILES/23CURR_TEXTILES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23CURR_TEXTILES/23CURR_TEXTILES-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From India, Wall Hangings to Please a Mogul', 'kicker': 'Currents: Textiles', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_h