irs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Matthew (Interior Designer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T22:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fd206c5-dcfe-5479-ab00-c918aa4e4aa2', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fd206c5-dcfe-5479-ab00-c918aa4e4aa2'}, {'abstract': 'Over-the-knee boots for fall; a collection for GapKids from Kate Spade and Jack Spade; a denim collection from MiH Jeans for Net-a-Porter and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/fashion/over-the-knee-boots-gap-collaborates-with-jack-and-kate-spade-a-70s-inspired-denim-collection-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Over-the-knee boots for fall; a collection for GapKids from Kate Spade and Jack Spade; a denim collection from MiH Jeans for Net-a-Porter and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most coveted cool-weather footwear of the season are thigh-grazing over-the-knee boots. It’s an assertive and, let’s be honest, sexy style that’s an instant look-changer. You won’t wear the boots with pants (although a black pair can look chic over dark skinny jeans), but think of them with fall’s snuggle-worthy sweater dresses and with skirts of varying lengths. To turn it up, though, show a bit of skin.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/fashion/23BROWSE_COMBO/23BROWSE_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/fashion/23BROWSE_COMBO/23BROWSE_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/fashion/23BROWSE_COMBO/23BROWSE_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/fashion/23BROWSE_COMBO/23BROWSE_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/fashion/23BROWSE_COMBO/23BROWSE_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/fashion/23BROWSE_COMBO/23BROWSE_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/fashion/23BROWSE_COMBO/23BROWSE_COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Shopping News', 'kicker': 'Browsing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boots That Are a Step Ahead of Your Knee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gap Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Net-A-Porter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kate Spade & Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jeans (Apparel)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MiH Jeans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fortune Finds', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fortunato, Elizabeth', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fortunato, Kathryn', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T22:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica M. Blumenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36ec9fa-2c03-5565-bbd9-92c79b8fd57e', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e36ec9fa-2c03-5565-bbd9-92c79b8fd57e'}, {'abstract': 'Three English bands offer proof that guitar-driven rock is not extinct.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/cmj-2014-the-out-of-town-advantage-for-happyness-the-crookes-and-money/', 'snippet': 'Three English bands offer proof that guitar-driven rock is not extinct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The CMJ Music Marathon is an extremely rare New York City phenomenon: one that gives tourists an advantage. While Brooklyn bands are ubiquitous at the CMJ showcases, mileage traveled means a band has achieved escape velocity from its hometown; it’s one form of quality control. So most of the bands I saw on Tuesday, day one of CMJ, were out-of-towners, including a lucky run of three English bands: Happyness, the Crookes and Money, all of them proof that guitar-driven rock is not extinct—a bedrock tenet of CMJ. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CMJ 2014:  The Out-of-Town Advantage for Happyness, the Crookes and Money', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'CMJ Music Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guitars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CMJ Holdings Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Replacements, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T22:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a81dc456-21fb-594f-952c-e70e8251b5c5', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a81dc456-21fb-594f-952c-e70e8251b5c5'}, {'abstract': 'A black-tie benefit draws out celebrities like Sofia Vergara, Ryan Reynolds with Blake Lively and Kris Jenner on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/fashion/sofia-vergara-ryan-reynolds-with-blake-lively-and-kris-jenner-attend-the-angel-ball.html', 'snippet': 'A black-tie benefit draws out celebrities like Sofia Vergara, Ryan Reynolds with Blake Lively and Kris Jenner on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a Monday night, but no one at the Angel Ball was in a hurry. Dinner wouldn’t arrive until 10 p.m. and dancing would stretch until midnight at Cipriani on Wall Street. Angel Ball veterans knew the drill.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plenty of Diversions at the Angel Ball ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plenty of Diversions at the Angel Ball', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koblin, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Denise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T22:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Koblin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koblin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82026505-d15a-5f75-a765-dc1806266116', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82026505-d15a-5f75-a765-dc1806266116'}, {'abstract': 'Craig Dykers of the architecture firm Snohetta on his melting pot of projects, including designing Norway’s currency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/garden/an-interview-with-craig-dykers-of-snohetta.html', 'snippet': 'Craig Dykers of the architecture firm Snohetta on his melting pot of projects, including designing Norway’s currency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Craig Dykers, a principal, with Kjetil Thorsen, in the Norwegian and American architectural firm Snohetta, was born in Germany and has lived 33 of his 53 years abroad. His father, an Army corporal, and his mother, an English seamstress, met in London after World War II. Having earned his architecture degree at the University of Texas, Mr. Dykers received international acclaim after winning the $350 million commission for the Library of Alexandria in Egypt when he was only 28. Snohetta was founded in Oslo in 1989 and now encompasses landscape, interior and graphic design.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23QNA1-promo/23QNA1-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23QNA1-promo/23QNA1-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23QNA1-promo/23QNA1-promo-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23QNA1-promo/23QNA1-promo-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 1116, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23QNA1-promo/23QNA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23QNA1-promo/23QNA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/garden/23QNA1-promo/23QNA1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Norse Gods Now Have His Number', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Norse Gods Now Have His Number', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Linda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snohetta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dykers, Craig', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T22:42:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/8263ce26-0dd9-5a5f-82ef-a8f5da09149b', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8263ce26-0dd9-5a5f-82ef-a8f5da09149b'}, {'abstract': 'The curator and collector Sam Wagstaff had a seminal influence on photography’s migration to the realm of high art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/arts/design/sam-wagstaffs-passion-transformed-the-art-market.html', 'snippet': 'The curator and collector Sam Wagstaff had a seminal influence on photography’s migration to the realm of high art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not so long ago, photography was dismissed by the art world as nothing more than a utilitarian medium. In the mid-1970s, a photograph by Edward Weston, an early 20th-century master of optical precision, could be had for less than $200 (roughly $800 today). On Sept. 29, Weston’s “Nautilus Shell, 1927,” a print small enough to hold in one hand, was auctioned at Christie’s for $461,000, an apt barometer of photography’s migration to the realm of high art. Cindy Sherman is a reigning example: At its evening sale of postwar and contemporary art on Nov. 12, Christie’s hopes to sell 21 “Untitled Film Stills” in a single lot for an estimated $6 million to $9 million; images by Ms. Sherman, Andreas Gursky and Jeff Wall have already sold for several million dollars each. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26SUBWAGSTAFF1/26SUBWAGSTAFF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26SUBWAGSTAFF1/26SUBWAGSTAFF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26SUBWAGSTAFF1/26SUBWAGSTAFF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26SUBWAGSTAFF1/26SUBWAGSTAFF1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1264, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26SUBWAGSTAFF1/26SUBWAGSTAFF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26SUBWAGSTAFF1/26SUBWAGSTAFF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/26SUBWAGSTAFF1/26SUBWAGSTAFF1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man Who Loved Photographs ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man Who Loved Photographs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagstaff, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T22:43:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Gefter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gefter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02a4f1a7-e4e0-5ace-ac3c-d2424f85b7d5', 'word_count': 1590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02a4f1a7-e4e0-5ace-ac3c-d2424f85b7d5'}, {'abstract': 'The truth about my grandmother’s Puerto Rican childhood.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/22/the-other-side-of-the-living-sea/', 'snippet': 'The truth about my grandmother’s Puerto Rican childhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My grandmother was raised in Vega Baja, Puerto Rico. She said the name, Vega Baja, meaning the “low plains,” with such romance that it was clear she longed for the place. In her stories she described a big house, and a farm where the children could eat the fruit from the trees and learned to milk a cow. Every Sunday after church they went to the beach. She taught herself to swim because the other children always played in the deep water and she hated being left behind. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/opinion/1022PRIVATELIVES/1022PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/23/opinion/1022PRIVATELIVES/1022PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 603}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/opinion/1022PRIVATELIVES/1022PRIVATELIVES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/opinion/1022PRIVATELIVES/1022PRIVATELIVES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2038, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/opinion/1022PRIVATELIVES/1022PRIVATELIVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/opinion/1022PRIVATELIVES/1022PRIVATELIVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/opinion/1022PRIVATELIVES/1022PRIVATELIVES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Other Side of the Living Sea', 'kicker': 'Private Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Other Side of the Living Sea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Thomas (Virgin Islands)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-22T22:44:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiphanie Yanique', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiphanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yanique', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e56bdbd2-9d01-5312-961d-6979bec1c9db', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e56bdbd2-9d01-5312-961d-6979bec1c9db'}, {'abstract':