nt drought has put that lifestyle to the test.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/world/in-china-a-drought-tests-nomadic-herders-culture-of-survival.html', 'snippet': 'A tradition of herding has continued for centuries in western China, despite official efforts to force nomads to settle in villages. But a recent drought has put that lifestyle to the test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALTAY, China — It has been a bad year for the big-tailed sheep. The grass in the high mountain pastures here in northwest China has been sparse, and the sheep have not eaten well. They are scrawny. That means the Kazakh herders have suffered, too.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In China, a Drought Tests Nomadic Herders’ Culture of Survival ', 'kicker': 'Altay Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In China, a Drought Tests Nomadic Herders’ Culture of Survival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sheep', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nomadic People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Urumqi (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T00:23:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', 