'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed1f1a1d-4d49-5067-ba06-4b6848329723', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed1f1a1d-4d49-5067-ba06-4b6848329723'}, {'abstract': 'For its customized Leica X camera, the outfitter wraps the powerful point-and-shoot in its signature colors.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/moncler-leica-x-camera/', 'snippet': 'For its customized Leica X camera, the outfitter wraps the powerful point-and-shoot in its signature colors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the release of Moncler’s customized Leica X camera, which wraps the powerful point-and-shoot in the outfitter’s signature colors, the French art director and Interview Magazine editorial director Fabien Baron photographed the icebergs of Greenland, lit up “like monsters” against ink-black skies. Braving subzero temperatures and with nothing but frigid waters below, Baron used a series of strobes to give a cinematic heft to the massive structures, which can span several times the size of Manhattan and are prone to break off at any time. “It was a production,” he says of the multiboat setup that brought him dangerously close to the icebergs, “but it was worth it.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/t-magazine/02travel-look-moncler/02travel-look-moncler-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/t-magazine/02travel-look-moncler/02travel-look-moncler-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/t-magazine/02travel-look-moncler/02travel-look-moncler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy'