 NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bao, The (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T15:07:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f44c8f7-edda-51b8-ae82-d1d5bd49a94e', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f44c8f7-edda-51b8-ae82-d1d5bd49a94e'}, {'abstract': 'The Conceptual artist Hans Haacke continues to needle museums even as they snap up his work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/arts/design/hans-haacke-gets-establishment-nod-of-approval.html', 'snippet': 'The Conceptual artist Hans Haacke continues to needle museums even as they snap up his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANS HAACKE, a father of Conceptual art and one of its chief political firebrands, has often made works incorporating lists, visually unlovely but highly effective ways to show how the world works. If you were to borrow the technique to show the unusual position Mr. Haacke has occupied in the art world for more than 50 years, the list might look something like this:', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/arts/24HAACKE2/JPHAACKE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/arts/24HAACKE2/JPHAACKE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/arts/24HAACKE2/JPHAACKE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subTy