port for travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/world/europe/as-islamists-seek-to-fill-ranks-more-western-women-answer-their-call.html', 'snippet': 'Analysts estimate that 10 percent of recruits from the West are women, often influenced by social media networks that offer advice, tips and logistical support for travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The young Western Muslims trying to join radical Islamist groups in Syria and Iraq now include increasing numbers of young women who are seeking to fight or to become the wives of fighters. It is a new twist on a recruitment effort that has led several thousand men from Europe and beyond to flock to the battlefield. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In West, ISIS Finds Women Eager to Enlist ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In West, ISIS Finds Women Eager to Enlist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Nusra Front', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Katherine E', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T15:14:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f56c2731-0e04-516c-86be-fcdda50e1dc5', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f56c2731-0e04-516c-86be-fcdda50e1dc5'}, {'abstract': 'One reason that baseball teams are scoring less is that the strike zone has gotten larger in recent years, mostly around batters’ knees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/upshot/the-strike-zone-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'One reason that baseball teams are scoring less is that the strike zone has gotten larger in recent years, mostly around batters’ knees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pitch from Sergio Romo of the San Francisco Giants in the bottom of the ninth inning crossed just below Bryce Harper’s knee, and the umpire barked, “Strike,” to Harper’s obvious frustration. Had it been called a ball, Harper would have been in command of the at-bat, with three balls and no strikes. Instead, he was as close to a strikeout as to a walk.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/upshot/24UP-Strike/24UP-Strike-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/upshot/24UP-Strike/24UP-Strike-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/upshot/24UP-Strike/24UP-Strike-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/upshot/24UP-Strike/24UP-Strike-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbn