-d0170c18e57a'}, {'abstract': 'Once reluctant to accept the virtual world, institutions are now using interactivity, 3-D imaging and “augmented reality” in displays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/the-met-and-other-museums-adapt-to-the-digital-age.html', 'snippet': 'Once reluctant to accept the virtual world, institutions are now using interactivity, 3-D imaging and “augmented reality” in displays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the Metropolitan Museum of Art, a turning point came in 2011. Down went the signs imploring visitors to stow their cellphones. The Met revamped its website, tailoring it for viewing on smartphone screens. The museum was not only allowing visitors to use their mobile phones while browsing the artworks, but encouraging it.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museums Morph Digitally ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Museums Morph Digitally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohr, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Portrait Gallery (London)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Museum of American History', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T16:19:35+0000',