es/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/20141026-PICASSO-slide-9GV6/20141026-PICASSO-slide-9GV6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Side of Picasso', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roque, Jacqueline (1927-86)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T16:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/14a41491-56a3-5eec-9800-26471c324aab', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/14a41491-56a3-5eec-9800-26471c324aab'}, {'abstract': 'A lack of resiliency in the U.S. economy has been on display many times since the recession ended in mid-2009.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/will-the-rest-of-the-world-drag-down-the-u-s-economy/', 'snippet': 'A lack of resiliency in the U.S. economy has been on display many times since the recession ended in mid-2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When multiple economic calamities struck in the late 20th century – including the Asian financial crisis, the Russian debt default and the collapse of the hedge fund Long Term Capital Management – the United States economy did not falter. \xa0Growth remained strong. The stock market continued to boom and so did the job market. The rich kept getting richer, but the poor were also making money. The federal budget entered the black and surpluses were projected for years to come.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will the Rest of the World Drag Down the U.S. Economy?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T16:44:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Tritch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tritch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7871952a-83d1-59f7-920e-4c5e9b9cbb09', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7871952a-83d1-59f7-920e-4c5e9b9cbb09'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition in New York, will display works by Picasso that were inspired by Jacqueline Roque, with whom he lived from 1954 until his death in 1973.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/picasso-jacqueline-at-pace-gallery-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition in New York, will display works by Picasso that were inspired by Jacqueline Roque, with whom he lived from 1954 until his death in 1973.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We’ve seen so much about Picasso as a misogynist,” said Arne Glimcher, the founder of Pace Gallery in New York. “But someone who has so many women in his life doesn’t hate women. I think that’s ridiculous. Maybe he was not very good at maintaining relationships with women, but he seems to have found it with Jacqueline.”', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Picasso and His Last Muse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Picasso and His Last Muse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheets, Hilarie M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, 