fluential band Devo will have his first major solo exhibition at the Museum of Contemporary Art Denver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/mark-mothersbaugh-of-devo-to-exhibit-art-in-denver.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Mothersbaugh of the influential band Devo will have his first major solo exhibition at the Museum of Contemporary Art Denver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Mothersbaugh has had two very public careers. The first was as the frontman for Devo, the influential band that emerged in the 1970s and helped define the punk and alternative music scenes. And since the 1980s, he has also been a prolific composer of scores for movies and television shows, including “Pee-wee’s Playhouse,” “The Lego Movie” and many films by the director Wes Anderson.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Leading Devo to Solo Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Leading Devo to Solo Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Contemporary Art Denver (MCA Denver)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Devo (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mothersbaugh, Mark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lerner, Adam (Museum Executive)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T16:45:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ted Loos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Loos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12e26b5-5c07-543f-8066-18fcf078c3fd', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12e26b5-5c07-543f-8066-18fcf078c3fd'}, {'abstract': 'A groundbreaking conservation approach using projections of colored light aims to restore the paintings’ original hues for a new exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/a-return-for-rothkos-harvard-murals-.html', 'snippet': 'A groundbreaking conservation approach using projections of colored light aims to restore the paintings’ original hues for a new exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Rothko’s badly faded mural cycle painted for Harvard University in 1962 is getting a second life after decades in storage, through a groundbreaking conservation approach. Opening on Nov. 16 at the newly renovated Harvard Art Museums, “Mark Rothko’s Harvard Murals” will return the five monumental canvases to public view, enhanced by projections of colored light intended to restore the appearance of their original hues and the cohesiveness of the grouping. The exhibition also invites debate.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26HARVARD6/26HARVARD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26HARVARD6/26HARVARD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26HARVARD6/26HARVARD6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26HARVARD6/26HARVARD6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1635, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': '