and Space Museum in Manhattan displays artifacts from shipboard Equator-crossing ceremonies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You wouldn’t think that sailing over the Equator could cause so much drama or, for that matter, be a museum-worthy event. But the drama, or more precisely the pageant, of the centuries-old maritime ceremony of crossing the line is noteworthy enough that the Intrepid Sea, Air and Space Museum in Manhattan has collected hundreds of items documenting the ceremonies that were held aboard the ship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26CROSSING1/26CROSSING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 920, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26CROSSING1/26CROSSING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 920}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26CROSSING1/26CROSSING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26CROSSING1/26CROSSING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1336, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26CROSSING1/26CROSSING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspecial/26CROSSING1/26CROSSING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/arts/artsspeci