 private donors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/science/new-research-center-aims-to-develop-second-generation-of-surgical-robots.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers at the University of California, Berkeley, are establishing a center for medical robotics with funding from the National Science Foundation and two private donors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With funding from the National Science Foundation and two private donors, scientists at the University of California, Berkeley, will establish a research center intended to help develop medical robots that can perform low-level and repetitive surgical tasks, freeing doctors to concentrate on the most challenging and complex aspects of the operations they perform.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Research Center Aims to Develop Second Generation of Surgical Robots', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Science Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intuitive Surgical Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T19:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffe919e6-7a69-5f99-8d0a-eb6d780b6693', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffe919e6-7a69-5f99-8d0a-eb6d780b6693'}, {'abstract': 'Readers react to a gunman’s shooting of a soldier and entering Parliament before being killed himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/opinion/the-attack-on-canadas-parliament.html', 'snippet': 'Readers react to a gunman’s shooting of a soldier and entering Parliament before being killed himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Attack on Canada’s Parliament', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Attack on Canada’s Parliament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ottawa (Ontario)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T19:41:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f83409-3177-5b05-ac8f-acc12e9383c2', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f83409-3177-5b05-ac8f-acc12e9383c2'}, {'abstract': 'Buster Pointdexter, the alter ego of David Johansen, brought his lounge act to the Café Carlyle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/arts/music/buster-pointdexter-back-in-a-tux-coming-full-circle.html', 'snippet': 'Buster Pointdexter, the alter ego of David Johansen, brought his lounge act to the Café Carlyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Buster Poindexter, a.k.a. David Johansen, the original punk hipster lounge lizard, seems perfectly at home at the elegant Café Carlyle is a sure sign that the punk-rock insurgency that began four decades ago has completed its cycle. Everybody gets the joke, but the joke is still fresh. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source':