', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4b150e6-ea64-57b4-89d1-deafc419e17e'}, {'abstract': '“Paul Strand: Master of Modern Photography,” at the Philadelphia Museum of Art, reappraises Strand as a modernist turned humanist as well as a cinephile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/arts/paul-strands-lifetime-of-photography-at-philadelphia-museum.html', 'snippet': '“Paul Strand: Master of Modern Photography,” at the Philadelphia Museum of Art, reappraises Strand as a modernist turned humanist as well as a cinephile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — As a young man working in the orbit of Alfred Stieglitz, Paul Strand defined modernist photography. Later on, it defined him. Although Strand made films and books, and worked into the mid-1970s, his legacy has been shaped by his Cubist still lifes and rigorously geometric cityscapes of the 1910s, images like “Wall Street,” in which dark-coated workers, tagged by long shadows, look almost as abstract as the facade of the Morgan Trust building that looms over them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expatriate Humanist, Lens Up His Sleeve', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expatriate Humanist, Lens Up His Sleeve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strand, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-23T20:19:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported',