ard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/23/travel/23cirque/23cirque-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/23/travel/23cirque/23cirque-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Acrobatic at Club Med', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACROBATS AND ACROBATICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque du Soleil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Club Mediterranee SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dominican Republic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Punta Cana (Dominican Republic)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T00:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eff11a6-4e84-52a1-a8c5-ed3d1800e67a', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eff11a6-4e84-52a1-a8c5-ed3d1800e67a'}, {'abstract': 'A nationwide, door-to-door testing initiative has become a mobilizing force for better-quality education.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/23/in-india-revealing-the-children-left-behind/', 'snippet': 'A nationwide, door-to-door testing initiative has become a mobilizing force for better-quality education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Right now, all over rural India, this is happening: Two local volunteers with a few days’ training come into the village. They knock on randomly selected doors, asking to see all children ages 6 to 16 who live there. In the front yard of the house, they test the children one by one in reading and math. A crowd gathers: parents, neighbors, sometimes the whole village. Children jump up and down, shouting, “Test me! Test me!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In India, Revealing the Children Left Behind', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illiteracy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T00:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e56758-db99-5688-b339-cfd0f5f44b1e', 'word_count': 1788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e56758-db99-5688-b339-cfd0f5f44b1e'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge Thursday dismissed two lawsuits against the Internal Revenue Service related to the treatment of conservative groups seeking tax-exempt status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/us/lawsuits-against-irs-are-dismissed.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge Thursday dismissed two lawsuits against the Internal Revenue Service related to the treatment of conservative groups seeking tax-exempt status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge Thursday dismissed two lawsuits against the Internal Revenue Service related to the treatment of conservative groups seeking tax-exempt status, ruling that no remedy was necessary because the applications were approved. “The allegedly unconstitutional governmental conduct, which delayed the processing of the plaintiff’s tax-exempt application and brought about this litigation, is no longer impacting the plaintiff,” Judge Reggie B. Walton, of the United States District Court in the District of Columbia, wrote of the lead plaintiff in the case, True the Vote, a Tea Party-affiliated group. The I.R.S. has said it acted improperly when it held up tax-exempt applications from dozens of conservative-leaning groups before the 2012 election, using search terms like “Tea Party,” “Patriot” and “9/12.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawsuits Against I.R.S. Are Dismissed ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawsuits Against I.R.S. Are Dismissed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joachim, David S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walton, Reggie B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T00:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By David S. Joachim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Joachim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab41d02-9636-5a53-b871-696247078e09', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab41d02-9636-5a53-b871-696247078e09'}, {'abstract': 'Oligarchs hiding behind front groups — Citizens for Fluffy Pillows — are pulling the levers of the 2014 campaign. No wonder we feel revulsion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/opinion/the-disgust-election.html', 'snippet': 'Oligarchs hiding behind front groups — Citizens for Fluffy Pillows — are pulling the levers of the 2014 campaign. No wonder we feel revulsion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justice Anthony Kennedy doesn’t strike me as the kind of guy I’d want to share a beer and a brat with, or be stuck next to on a long flight. But I would like for the most influential swing voter on the Supreme Court to step away from his legal aerie, and wade through some of the muck that he and four fellow justices have given us with the 2014 campaign.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Disgust Election', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Disgust Election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Egan, Timothy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T00:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cc932ea-4936-54f4-8b47-f191454fa816', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cc932ea-4936-54f4-8b47-f191454fa816'}, {'abstract': 'Fall is peak season for roadkill. But we can cut the cost and the carnage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/opinion/our-highways-toll-on-wildlife.html', 'snippet': 'Fall is peak season for roadkill. But we can cut the cost and the carnage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOZEMAN, Mont. — FALL is the season of apples, frost, turning leaves and roadkill. A 2008 congressional study found that one in 20 reported motor vehicle collisions is animal-related, and the numbers peak in autumn. Annually, these incidents result in about 26,000 injuries and 200 human deaths.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/opinion/1024OPEDrinaldi/1024OPEDrinaldi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/opinion/1024OPEDrinaldi/1024OPEDrinaldi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/opinion/1024OPEDrinaldi/1024OPEDrinaldi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/opinion/1024OPEDrinaldi/1024OPEDrinaldi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1464, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/opinion/1024OPEDrinaldi/1024OPEDrinaldi-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/24/opinion/1024OPEDrinaldi/1024OPEDrinaldi-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/opinion/1024OPEDrinaldi/1024OPEDrinaldi-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'l