}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f41d0253-7791-5fda-a2cd-2ffe0545258d', 'word_count': 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f41d0253-7791-5fda-a2cd-2ffe0545258d'}, {'abstract': 'Flu season will bring a virus that spreads far faster than Ebola, and will kill thousands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/us/fallacies-are-spreading-as-readily-as-the-virus-has.html', 'snippet': 'Flu season will bring a virus that spreads far faster than Ebola, and will kill thousands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as American hospitals prepare for new cases of Ebola, they must brace for a more familiar invader. The flu season will arrive soon — although exactly when, scientists cannot say.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Ebola Spreads, So Have Several Fallacies', 'kicker': 'Matter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As an Outbreak Spreads, So Have Several Fallacies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T01:19:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dad44935-8c75-52c0-b27a-c833352a0504', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dad44935-8c75-52c0-b27a-c833352a0504'}, {'abstract': 'The well-known figure had been accused of harboring a fugitive monk from Chamdo in his own monastery in the Yushu area of Qinghai Province.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/world/asia/khenpo-kartse-tibetan-religious-leader-is-said-to-be-sentenced-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'The well-known figure had been accused of harboring a fugitive monk from Chamdo in his own monastery in the Yushu area of Qinghai Province.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A well-known Tibetan religious leader, Khenpo Kartse, has been sentenced by Chinese officials to two and a half years in prison, according to reports from International Campaign for Tibet, an advocacy group, and Radio Free Asia, which is financed by the United States government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Khenpo Kartse, Tibetan Religious Leader, Is Said to Be Sentenced in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Tibetan Abbot Is Sentenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karma Tsewang (Khenpo Kartse)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Campaign for Tibet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio Free Asia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T01:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb6b4832-4f8b-5e86-bf65-2abc7809156e', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb6b4832-4f8b-5e86-bf65-2abc7809156e'}, {'abstract': 'The Royals’ potent running attack is amplified by the speed of Terrance Gore, a recently acquired player who often pinch-runs for the team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/sports/baseball/world-series-2014-kansas-city-royals-terrance-gore-excels-as-a-pinch-runner.html', 'snippet': 'The Royals’ potent running attack is amplified by the speed of Terrance Gore, a recently acquired player who often pinch-runs for the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — Clusters of reporters pushed and nudged for elbow room in a packed Kansas City clubhouse Wednesday night in the aftermath of the Royals’ 7-2 win over the San Francisco Giants. The victory reinvigorated a fan base that had been shaken by the Royals’ loss in Game 1 of the World Series.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/sports/SILO-Y-RHODEN/SILO-Y-RHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/sports/SILO-Y-RHODEN/SILO-Y-RHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/sports/SILO-Y-RHODEN/SILO-Y-RHODEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/sports/SILO-Y-RHODEN/SILO-Y-RHODEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1284, 'width': 1990, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/sports/SILO-Y-RHODEN/SILO-Y-RHODEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/24/sports/SIL