 of Arkansas rested largely on whether Gov. Mario M. Cuomo of New York, who was considered a presumptive front-runner, decided to enter the race. Mr. Cuomo, of course, did not, and the rest is history.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Twist in the Drama of the Clintons and the Cuomos ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Twist in Drama of Clintons and Cuomos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Mario M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T01:42:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick and Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9d3c372-1e5d-51f5-aadd-6aab5b571f9c', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9d3c372-1e5d-51f5-aadd-6aab5b571f9c'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Dannel P. Malloy has found a rhythm in a rambunctious series of debates against his Republican challenger, Thomas C. Foley, that has otherwise eluded him on the campaign trail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/nyregion/in-connecticut-governors-race-malloy-finds-his-footing-in-the-heat-of-debates.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Dannel P. Malloy has found a rhythm in a rambunctious series of debates against his Republican challenger, Thomas C. Foley, that has otherwise eluded him on the campaign trail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most incumbent governors would blanch at such a sustained verbal clash. Over five near-weekly debates, Connecticut Gov. Dannel P. Malloy has fended off forceful questions about taxes and jobs from his Republican challenger, Thomas C. Foley, displaying a nimbleness and nerve that have boosted his prospects in this closely fought race.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/nyregion/24CTDEBATEcombo/24CTDEBATEcombo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/nyregion/24CTDEBATEcombo/24CTDEBATEcombo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/nyregion/24CTDEBATEcombo/24CTDEBATEcombo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/nyregion/24CTDEBATEcombo/24CTDEBATEcombo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 