article/2b7452d1-96ec-5550-aeef-e4ea6957537f'}, {'abstract': 'The successful launch of a spacecraft that will test flight paths and equipment brings China one step closer to its long-range goal of sending a probe to the moon that will return to Earth.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/chinas-latest-space-launch-is-next-step-in-lunar-ambitions/', 'snippet': 'The successful launch of a spacecraft that will test flight paths and equipment brings China one step closer to its long-range goal of sending a probe to the moon that will return to Earth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China took a step toward its plans to send an unmanned probe to the moon that will return to Earth by launching a spacecraft on Friday to test flight paths and equipment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Latest Space Launch Is Next Step in Lunar Ambitions', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T11:53:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e72f510a-2d14-5861-8ce6-f11d75bab371', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e72f510a-2d14-5861-8ce6-f11d75bab371'}, {'abstract': 'Test yourself. Which five companies would you identify?', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/who-are-fashio