orted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1e0f9af-7a36-5ded-a09a-29870aa52c8b', 'word_count': 2687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1e0f9af-7a36-5ded-a09a-29870aa52c8b'}, {'abstract': 'I came into the prison with anxiety and fear. What I didn’t expect was compassion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/magazine/the-man-on-death-row-who-changed-me.html', 'snippet': 'I came into the prison with anxiety and fear. What I didn’t expect was compassion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The visitation room was 100 feet square, with a few stools bolted to the floor and wire mesh running across the room. For family visits, inmates and visitors had to be on opposite sides of the mesh. Legal visits, on the other hand, were “contact visits” — the two of us would be on the same side of the room to permit more privacy. I began worrying about my lack of preparation. I had scheduled to meet with the client for one hour, but I wasn’t sure how I would fill even 15 minutes with what I knew. I sat down on a stool and waited until I heard the clanging of chains on the other side of the door.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '74', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/magazine/26lives/mag-26Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/magazine/26lives/mag-26Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/magazine/26lives/mag-26Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/magazine/26lives/mag-2