e, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eae647c9-522d-5b87-98e8-f08b225f46b4', 'word_count': 2155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eae647c9-522d-5b87-98e8-f08b225f46b4'}, {'abstract': 'Four reviewers share their memories of reading creepy books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/books/review/spooky-suggestions.html', 'snippet': 'Four reviewers share their memories of reading creepy books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Halloween upon us, we’ve rounded up recent releases in science fiction and fantasy, thrillers, horror and Nordic noir. I asked each of the four reviewers to describe a memorable scary reading experience. N. K. Jemisin cited Stephen King’s novella “The Mist,” about a Maine town terrorized by the precipitation that gives the book its title. She read it on a foggy night, in a “very creepy suburban town full of people who seemed nice but could have been into child sacrifice; hard to say. I never looked at a supermarket the same way after that story. Or a pharmacy. (Oh, my God, the pharmacy.)”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/books/review/1026-bks-Openbook/1026-bks-Openbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/books/review/1026-bks-Openbook/1026-bks-Openbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/books/review/1026-bks-Openbook/1026-bks-Openbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/books/review/1026-bks-O