o-brooklyn-feeling-ebola-anxiety.html', 'snippet': 'In the locations where Dr. Craig Spencer, who has the Ebola virus, traveled before his hospitalization, people expressed fear and uncertainty on Friday — with a dash of New York attitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than 24 hours after the first diagnosis of Ebola in New York City, worries about a public panic were already giving way to a desire to restore order as quickly as possible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials Soothe Fears, While Workers Sanitize Infected Doctor’s Path', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officials Soothe Fears, While Workers Sanitize Infected Doctor’s Path', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spencer, Craig Allen (1981- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bellevue Hospital Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T16:38:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0825f9a0-0747-5be4-bd0d-4d922f97399b', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0825f9a0-0747-5be4-bd0d-4d922f97399b'}, {'abstract': 'Musicians in nine subway stations were joined by Wi-Fi to a conductor in Bryant Park.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/signal-strength-connects-underground-ensemble-in-nine-subway-stations/', 'snippet': 'Musicians in nine subway stations were joined by Wi-Fi to a conductor in Bryant Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of us regard the introduction of Wi-Fi in the New York City subway system as an opportunity to catch up with email during those tedious commutes – at least, at the relatively few stops where connections are working. But artists think differently: Chris Shimojima, a filmmaker, quickly saw that Wi-Fi would allow subway buskers at different stations to be connected, and that there was a potential video project in the resulting interaction.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Signal Strength’ Connects Underground Ensemble in Nine Subway Stations', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subway Musicians Are Now Connected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhurbin, Lev', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T16:44:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f66c1b8d-2f70-5971-9c20-3436d11c5813', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f66c1b8d-2f70-5971-9c20-3436d11c5813'}, {'abstract': 'The Mail & Express Building, built in 1892, was not the tallest, biggest or first skyscraper, but it was certainly the lightest, the most refined.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/realestate/an-early-new-york-city-skyscraper-remembered.html', 'snippet': 'The Mail & Express Building, built in 1892, was not the tallest, biggest or first skyscraper, but it was certainly the lightest, the most refined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the history of the skyscraper, the Mail & Express Building, built in 1892 at Broadway and Fulton Street, gets short shrift. It was not the tallest or the biggest or the first, but it was certainly the lightest, the most refined — which didn’t save it when demolition came in 1920. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/realestate/26SCAPES/26SCAPES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/realestate/26SCAPES/26SCAPES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/realestate/26SCAPES/26SCAPES-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/realestate/26SCAPES/26SCAPES-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1584, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/realestate/26SCAPES/26SCAPES-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/26/realestate/26SCAPES/26SCAPES-thu