the police violated the rights of protesters and should re-examine their practices, standards and training.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/us/amnesty-internation-report-faults-the-police-in-ferguson-mo.html', 'snippet': 'The human rights group said the police violated the rights of protesters and should re-examine their practices, standards and training.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police in Ferguson, Mo., violated the rights of protesters during demonstrations after the killing of 18-year-old Michael Brown in August, according to a report issued by Amnesty International on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amnesty International Report Faults the Police in Ferguson, Mo.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rights Group Faults Police in Ferguson, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T20:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/146e8ea2-d528-545d-9e21-b789f4901529', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/146e8ea2-d528-545d-9e21-b789f4901529'}, {'abstract': 'Analysts say the far-flung plots and attacks are a change in the nature of the group and its threat to the West.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/world/middleeast/string-of-attacks-in-west-raise-new-fears-over-isis-influence.html', 'snippet': 'Analysts say the far-flung plots and attacks are a change in the nature of the group and its threat to the West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The British police arrest four men accused of plotting a bombing on the scale of the Mumbai hotel attack six years ago. The Australian authorities arrest a ring of 12 accused of plotting daring murders, including a public beheading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attacks in West Raise New Fears Over ISIS’ Influence', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baghdadi, Abu Bakr al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T20:13:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a1f180a-c955-5f73-9a5e-67c4bf156276', 'word_count': 1338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a1f180a-c955-5f73-9a5e-67c4bf156276'}, {'abstract': 'A new ad from Senator Mitch McConnell in the Kentucky Senate race is getting some attention for its choice of featured women voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/24/not-all-young-kentucky-women-for-mcconnell-are-from-kentucky/', 'snippet': 'A new ad from Senator Mitch McConnell in the Kentucky Senate race is getting some attention for its choice of featured women voters.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In the tug-of-war for women’s votes in Kentucky, Senator Mitch McConnell has released a new ad starring four “young Kentucky women’’ criticizing his Democratic opponent, Alison Lundergan Grimes. But one of the women appears to be registered to vote in Pennsylvania, not Kentucky.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not All ‘Young Kentucky Women’ for McConnell Are From Kentucky', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimes, Alison Lundergan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T20:14:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3478cb6e-73bf-52c3-a560-287478da7e37', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3478cb6e-73bf-52c3-a560-287478da7e37'}, {'abstract': '“Lights Out,” a song from the band’s self-titled debut album, premieres here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/haerts-lights-out/', 'snippet': '“Lights Out,” a song from the band’s self-titled debut album, premieres here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With only a four-song EP and one buzzed-about single (“Wings”) to its curious name, the Brooklyn-based band Haerts managed to land choice slots at festivals like South by Southwest and Bonnaroo earlier this year. Now, the band is preparing for the release of its self-titled debut LP on Columbia next week. Recorded with Jean-Philip Grobler — known as St. Lucia — and Patrik Berger, a Swedish producer who has also worked with Robyn, Icona Pop and Lana Del Rey, it’s a breezy pop album with an\xa0intelligent edge. The drum machines and cosmic synths that are standard for today’s indie pop are all accounted for, but what really sets the band’s sound apart is the German-born front woman Nini Fabi’s powerful voice — which might bring Stevie Nicks’s to mind — along with earworm melodies and richly layered lyrics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24haerts-ledonne/24haerts-ledonne-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24haerts-ledonne/24haerts-ledonne-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24haerts-ledonne/24haerts-ledonne-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24haerts-ledonne/24haerts-ledonne-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24haerts-ledonne/24haerts-ledonne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24haerts-ledonne/24haerts-ledonne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24haerts-ledonne/24haerts-ledonne-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Track by the Indie-Pop Quartet Haerts, Inspired by Bad Weather', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T20:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Ledonne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ledonne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55da2b83-e560-57bb-9c3f-1bcbf8ad5f46', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55da2b83-e560-57bb-9c3f-1bcbf8ad5f46'}, {'abstract': 'Readers vented frustration in reaction to an editorial, “The Democratic Panic: Alison Lundergan Grimes, Kay Hagan and Other Candidates Avoid Obama.”', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/readers-respond-on-the-democratic-panic/', 'snippet': 'Readers vented frustration in reaction to an editorial, “The Democratic Panic: Alison Lundergan Grimes, Kay Hagan and Other Candidates Avoid Obama.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks out from Election Day 2014, some Democrats running for re-election to the United States Senate in heavily Republican states are running away from President Obama’s record.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url