 '2014-10-24T21:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ad1df6a-b3a3-5c9c-8e41-7712f2edab1d', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ad1df6a-b3a3-5c9c-8e41-7712f2edab1d'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic, under the direction of Alan Gilbert, performed Bruckner’s towering Symphony No. 8 and Bartok’s Piano Concerto No. 3.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/arts/music/alan-gilbert-conducts-the-new-york-philharmonic.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic, under the direction of Alan Gilbert, performed Bruckner’s towering Symphony No. 8 and Bartok’s Piano Concerto No. 3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruckner is difficult. Not just for players, who have to marshal enormous stamina in symphonies that last well over an hour, or for conductors, tasked with making sense of the vast architecture of these works with their succession of foaming crescendos and mystical lulls, sweeping plateaus and glittering climaxes. Bruckner’s music can also be daunting to the listener, as I was reminded during Thursday’s performance of his Symphony No. 8 by the New York Philharmonic under the direction of Alan Gilbert at Avery Fisher Hall. It was a performance that offered many thrills and sonic marvels, but also left me feeling adrift and disengaged.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bruckner Symphony and a Bartok Piano Concerto: A Study in Contrasts', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bruckner Symphony and a Bartok Piano Concerto: A Study in Contrasts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avery Fisher Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronfman, Yefim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T21:03:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d1dede9-994f-5450-8917-d699015da785', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d1dede9-994f-5450-8917-d699015da785'}, {'abstract': 'Rafal Blechacz’s recital on Thursday night at Zankel Hall included familiar pieces like Beethoven’s “Pathétique” Sonata and Chopin’s “Minute” Waltz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/arts/music/the-pianist-rafal-blechacz-at-zankel-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Rafal Blechacz’s recital on Thursday night at Zankel Hall included familiar pieces like Beethoven’s “Pathétique” Sonata and Chopin’s “Minute” Waltz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The thoughtful and elegant young Polish pianist Rafal Blechacz was doing very well — an international career, a recording contract with Deutsche Grammophon — even before he was named the seventh recipient of the 2014 Gilmore Artist Award in January. This grant of $300,000 is bestowed upon an unsuspecting pianist every four years by the Gilmore Foundation in Michigan, determined by jury members who attend candidates’ concerts secretly. Along with the heightened recognition, the award brings raised expectations.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/RAFAL/RAFAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/RAFAL/RAFAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/RAFAL/RAFAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/RAFAL/RAFAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1148, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/RAFAL/RAFAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/RAFAL/RAFAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/arts/RAFAL/RAFAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Take That, Elevated Expectations!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Take That, Elevated Expectations!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blechacz, Rafal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T21:07:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d447a7e9-ea7a-5045-a4ad-cf55864f0460', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d447a7e9-ea7a-5045-a4ad-cf55864f0460'}, {'abstract': 'A robust election result for the Working Families Party is threatened by the Women’s Equality Party, which is part of a branding effort on the part of Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to appeal to female voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/nyregion/a-gap-within-a-gender-in-new-york-politics.html', 'snippet': 'A robust election result for the Working Families Party is threatened by the Women’s Equality Party, which is part of a branding effort on the part of Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to appeal to female voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, Gloria Steinem, still feminism’s leading oracle, sent an email to 200,000 New Yorkers urging them to vote for Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and other candidates seeking election on the Working Families Party line. Her note pointed to the organization’s work on paid sick leave (she mentioned it twice), on raising wages for the underclass, on fighting for tax increases on the wealthy and for expanded rights for domestic workers. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26BIG/26BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26BIG/26BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 268}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26BIG/26BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 457, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26BIG/26BIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 913, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_