3 states because of concerns that they can impale drivers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/business/trinity-industries-halts-shipments-of-highway-guardrails.html', 'snippet': 'The move comes after regulators ordered more crash testing of the barriers, which have been banned in 13 states because of concerns that they can impale drivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trinity Industries, facing mounting criticism that its guardrails can impale drivers in crashes, said on Friday that it would stop selling the product, which 13 states have now banned, until further testing could be completed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Producer of Highway Guardrails to Halt Sales', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Producer of Highway Guardrails to Halt Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kessler, Aaron M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity Industries Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Highway Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T21:15:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory and Aaron M. Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddadcf0d-ca41-5c03-924c-8ce3c2380813', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddadcf0d-ca41-5c03-924c-8ce3c2380813'}, {'abstract': 'Two vital efforts to tamp down unfounded fears of Ebola contagion.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/why-americans-should-fear-fear-of-ebola-more-than-the-virus/', 'snippet': 'Two vital efforts to tamp down unfounded fears of Ebola contagion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As New York City grapples with tracing the contacts of Craig Spencer, a young physician infected with the Ebola virus, It’s worth drawing attention to two worthy efforts to tamp down unreasoned\xa0fears — President Obama’s White House embrace of Nina Pham, the Dallas nurse who contracted Ebola while treating a dying patient, and David Ropeik’s fine piece on the perils posed by Ebola fears, published by the Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/us/25pham-obama-copy/25pham-obama-copy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/25/us/25pham-obama-copy/25pham-obama-copy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/us/25pham-obama-copy/25pham-obama-copy-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/us/25pham-obama-copy/25pham-obama-copy-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1048, 'width': 1575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/us/25pham-obama-copy/25pham-obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': 