, {'abstract': 'Titled “Prospect.3: Notes for Now,” the event’s third iteration opens to the public Oct. 25.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/prospect-3-new-orleans/', 'snippet': 'Titled “Prospect.3: Notes for Now,” the event’s third iteration opens to the public Oct. 25.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though it only launched in 2008, Prospect New Orleans — the city’s ambitious attempt at an internationally competitive art biennial — has seen more than its share of\xa0trials and tribulations. Board blunders and cash-flow hiccups delayed the edition planned for 2010 and marred its reception. But at\xa0Prospect.3, the event’s\xa0third iteration, which opens on Saturday, Oct. 25 and runs through Jan. 25, 2015, things are looking up. The event has found a dynamic executive director and effective fund-raiser in Brooke Anderson. And the city has eagerly opened up its venues and streets — as well as rallied its local social contingent, including T contributing editor Sara Ruffin Costello, who has lured art-inclined friends from New York, Los Angeles and Europe to support the endeavor at tonight’s sold-out opening benefit party, titled Miss Vesta’s Swamp Galaxy Gala.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24art-baumgardner-1/24art-baumgardner-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24art-baumgardner-1/24art-baumgardner-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/t-magazine/24art-baumgardner-1/24art-baumgardner-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',