tion_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e834acc-22bf-5ab0-963f-beef9f27c940', 'word_count': 1483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e834acc-22bf-5ab0-963f-beef9f27c940'}, {'abstract': 'Recently, Nest has been delving deeper into integrating its products with other smart devices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/24/nest-buys-revolv-maker-of-smart-appliance-manager/', 'snippet': 'Recently, Nest has been delving deeper into integrating its products with other smart devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine an unoccupied house with a bunch of machines sitting around talking to one another. Saturday morning cartoons? The opening of a dystopic thriller? No, it’s the idea behind a recent acquisition by Nest, the Google-owned maker of Internet-connected appliances like a thermostat and a fire alarm. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nest Buys Revolv, Maker of Smart Appliance Manager', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thermostats', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nest Labs Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolv', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-24T23:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Conor Dougherty', 'person': [{'firstname'