ue': 'Freundel, Barry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rabbis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T00:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77ccfbad-67b9-5398-a86e-c8e453599ee3', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77ccfbad-67b9-5398-a86e-c8e453599ee3'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s “Education” television ad appears to be a response to criticism from his opponent, Rob Astorino, of his support for the Common Core standards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/nyregion/cuomo-with-a-daughters-help-tweaks-his-education-image.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s “Education” television ad appears to be a response to criticism from his opponent, Rob Astorino, of his support for the Common Core standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rob Astorino, the Westchester County executive and Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s Republican opponent, has sought to elevate the issue of education in the campaign, in particular the Common Core, a set of academic standards that has been adopted by more than 40 states. In New York City, the rollout has been criticized as rocky. Many parents saw their children’s test scores fall sharply under assessments aligned with the new standards and were angered by the changes. Mr. Astorino has tried to tap into this frustration, tying Mr. Cuomo, a Democrat, to the Common Core rhetorically and starting a ballot line called Stop Common Core. Mr. Cuomo’s ad, “Education,” appears to be a response to that messaging.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo, With a Daughter’s Help, Tweaks His Education Image', 'kicker': 'The Ad Campaign', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo, With a Daughter’s Help, Tweaks His Education Image', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astorino, Robert P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AKPD Message and Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Michaela Kennedy (1997- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T00:16:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66085c0b-294e-5f3d-bd92-0a0cbeb96cea', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66085c0b-294e-5f3d-bd92-0a0cbeb96cea'}, {'abstract': 'Bellevue Hospital Center has long been on the front line of global health crises. But rising to the cha