'uri': 'nyt://article/244de231-ec58-576d-9ea9-b58b522e8ff3'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo offered soothing words to worried New Yorkers about the city’s first Ebola case. Less than 19 hours later, Mr. Cuomo struck a starkly different tone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/nyregion/after-calling-for-calm-cuomo-joins-christie-in-ordering-some-quarantines.html', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo offered soothing words to worried New Yorkers about the city’s first Ebola case. Less than 19 hours later, Mr. Cuomo struck a starkly different tone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday night, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo sat beside Mayor Bill de Blasio at Bellevue Hospital Center as they offered soothing words to worried New Yorkers: New York City’s first case of Ebola, they said, was no reason for panic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo, Shifting His Policy on Outbreak, Opens Up Public Rift With de Blasio ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo, Shifting His Policy on Outbreak, Opens Up Public Rift With de Blasio', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bellevue Hospital Center', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spencer, Craig Allen (1981- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T00:58:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan and Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1536aef-fbfc-5176-aa58-d0a972a0edfc', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1536aef-fbfc-5176-aa58-d0a972a0edfc'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Curtis M. Scaparrotti, the top American military leader in South Korea, says he believes the North is capable of making a nuclear weapon small enough to fit atop a ballistic missile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/world/asia/us-commander-sees-key-nuclear-step-by-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Curtis M. Scaparrotti, the top American military leader in South Korea, says he believes the North is capable of making a nuclear weapon small enough to fit atop a ballistic missile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The top American military commander in South Korea said on Friday that he believed North Korea had most likely completed its yearslong quest to shrink a nuclear weapon to a size that could fit atop a ballistic missile. His assessment, if correct, could change American calculations about the vulnerability of the United States and its allies, and the North’s ability to sell nuclear weapons to others. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Commander Sees Key Nuclear Step by North Korea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Commander Sees Key Nuclear Step by North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name'