tary school in the Bronx on Friday, hitting and killing an 8-year-old girl and injuring five other people, the authorities said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Car Kills a Girl Outside a Bronx School', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Car Kills a Girl Outside a Bronx School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T03:53:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e2ec364-df3f-5cdb-869a-2a1552c60e47', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e2ec364-df3f-5cdb-869a-2a1552c60e47'}, {'abstract': 'Syria’s director general of antiquities and museums will be the recipient of a new prize that recognizes important efforts to preserve cultural heritage.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/syrian-official-honored-for-work-protecting-antiquities/', 'snippet': 'Syria’s director general of antiquities and museums will be the recipient of a new prize that recognizes important efforts to preserve cultural heritage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maamoun Abdulkarim, Syria’s director general of antiquities and museums, has been awarded a new prize established to reward the protection of endangered cultural heritage sites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Official Honored for Work Protecting Antiquities', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rutelli, Francesco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Monuments Fund', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T04:01:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c854a5d9-68f7-5a3b-b664-8889e69aec26', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c854a5d9-68f7-5a3b-b664-8889e69aec26'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (HBO Signature) THE CONJURING (2013) Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga play Ed and Lorraine Warren, the real-life paranormal investigators who declared an infamous Dutch colonial-style house on Long Island haunted, leading to the many “Amityville” movies. Their target this time is a Rhode Island farmhouse, where the blissful dreams of Carolyn and Roger Perron (Lili Tayor and Ron Livingston, above, with Mr. Wilson, right) and their five daughters become a moaning, creaking nightmare when they find themselves playing cat-and-mouse with an evil force. The director, James Wan, “smartly keeps enough distance from the Warrens that you can see that these true believers are also hovering at the edge of dangerous fanaticism,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “That gives the movie a shiver of political currency, even if a greater, more sustaining pleasure of this particular haunted-house fantasy is how it works as a metaphor for moviegoing itself. When the Perrons first settle into their house, they’re facing the future with bright, anxious smiles that aren’t much different from those of the horror-film faithful who are waiting nervously, hopefully, to be jolted by the next great shocker. It’s here.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ca6940a-a5c6-5e05-8a45-d56824328d1e', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ca6940a-a5c6-5e05-8a45-d56824328d1e'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, October 25, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/pageoneplus/quotations-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, October 25, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A voluntary Ebola quarantine is not enough. This is too serious a public health situation.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotations of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotations of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T05:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/40557822-9d7c-558f-b23f-bb70018aedbe', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40557822-9d7c-558f-b23f-bb70018aedbe'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Saturday, October 25, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/pageoneplus/corrections-october-25-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Saturday, October 25, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 25, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T05:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db38fab0-705d-55fa-94a3-f7ffd45d6ade', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db38fab0-705d-55fa-94a3-f7ffd45d6ade'}, {'abstract': 'Morgan Dixon, who left the hospital on Saturday to continue her quarantine at home, is described as a private person who helps others from behind the scenes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/nyregion/new-york-ebola-patients-fiance-shares-his-altruism-.html', 'snippet': 'Morgan Dixon, who left the hospital on Saturday to continue her quarantine at home, is described as a private person who helps others from behind the scenes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morgan Dixon always had a plan, and it never involved staying in Cincinnati. Even in high school, she thought far beyond her hometown, writing officials in developing countries as part of the school’s Amnesty International club and urging them to stop violating human rights. “You have the world to explore!” her parents wrote next to her picture in her 2002 yearbook. “Enjoy Life!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ebola Patient’s Fiancée Shares His Passion for Helping Those in Need, Friends Say ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ebola Patient’s Fiancée Shares His Passion for Helping Those in Need, Friends Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spencer, Craig Allen (1981- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dixon, Morgan (1984- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T09:20:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Barker and Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f6dd1ba-1c79-50ad-8aff-f917f7af3933', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f6dd1ba-1c79-50ad-8aff-f917f7af3933'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Cardinals discuss the meaning of marriage and family at the Ecumenical Council.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/1964-council-reviewing-catholic-theology-on-marriage/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Cardinals discuss the meaning of marriage and family at the Ecumenical Council.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — Cardinal Ruffini noted in this session of the Ecumenical Council that the part of the schema on the church and the modern world that deals with family and marriages states: “… That, if in particular cases, married couples have sufficiently serious reasons to limit the number of their children, they must still manifest to each other their tender love, but the text fails to explain how this love can be expressed, because Catholic teaching has always maintained that in these circumstances the physical end of marriage is unlawful.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Council Reviewing Catholic Theology on Marriage', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Popes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T10:25:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2112d2e6-d6d8-573b-bfdd-98564906cf58', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2112d2e6-d6d8-573b-bfdd-98564906cf58'}, {'abstract': 'Gremlins don’t like music?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/friday-night-gone/', 'snippet': 'Gremlins don’t like music?', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, this is weird. I posted Friday Night Music last night, or at least thought I did, and it’s gone — no post, not even a draft. I may try to reconstruct it later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Gone', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T11:18:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42ca2f34-fc58-5b72-8bc2-ee4996958c4d', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42ca2f34-fc58-5b72-8bc2-ee4996958c4d'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t believe the haters.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/25/notes-on-easy-money-and-inequality/', 'snippet': 'Don’t believe the haters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve received some angry mail over this William Cohan piece attacking Janet Yellen for supposedly feeding inequality through quantitative easing; Cohan and my correspondents take this inequality-easy money story as an established fact, and accuse anyone who supports the Fed’s policy while also decrying inequality as a hypocrite if not a lackey of Wall Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes on Easy Money and Inequality', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T12:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 't