g and shaking, summoned the courage to confront him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Mullah Who Raped Girl in His Mosque Receives 20-Year Prison Sentence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan Mullah Who Raped Girl in His Mosque Receives 20-Year Prison Sentence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amin, Mohammad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Women for Afghan Women', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T17:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5929b7a-e690-5a3d-b3b8-375ad82d81a1', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5929b7a-e690-5a3d-b3b8-375ad82d81a1'}, {'abstract': 'Caryl M. Stern travels a lot as president of the United States Fund for Unicef, and on Sundays she cooks meals for her family to enjoy in her absence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/nyregion/caryl-m-stern-talks-cooking-and-baking-as-catharsis.html', 'snippet': 'Caryl M. Stern travels a lot as president of the United States Fund for Unicef, and on Sundays she cooks meals for her family to enjoy in her absence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As president of the United States Fund for Unicef, or Unicef USA, Caryl M. Stern travels the globe at a frenetic fund-raising pace, most recently to combat Ebola in Africa and to assist Syrian refugees. Halloween month, when the children’s poverty organization sends cardboard trick-or-treat boxes to schools, is typically the busiest. This fall, Ms. Stern is also promoting her memoir, “I Believe in Zero: Learning From the World’s Children.” She and her husband, Donald LaRosa, live in Bayside, Queens, with their youngest son, James LaRosa, a high school student. Their middle son, Lee, is a college sophomore. Brian, their eldest, and his wife, Cara, have two children, making Ms. Stern a grandmother at 57. And then there is Chip, the 11-year-old chow-shepherd mix.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE4/26ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE4/26ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE4/26ROUTINE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE4/26ROUTINE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE4/26ROUTINE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType':