ions', 'value': 'Newark Liberty International Airport (NJ)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T17:27:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis and Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/503b6ca1-d1f0-59b4-9d64-6624508ef00d', 'word_count': 1421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/503b6ca1-d1f0-59b4-9d64-6624508ef00d'}, {'abstract': 'A&A Bake & Doubles Shop in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, offers typical Trinidadian food, including doubles, a traditional breakfast of chickpeas stuffed inside fried bread.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/nyregion/a-caribbean-outpost-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'A&A Bake & Doubles Shop in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, offers typical Trinidadian food, including doubles, a traditional breakfast of chickpeas stuffed inside fried bread.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day of the week except Sunday, a line begins to form in the early morning outside a narrow storefront on Nostrand Avenue in Brooklyn’s Bedford-Stuyvesant, often before the sun rises and the shop opens. Customers wait in their cars or line up on the sidewalk as the spicy-sweet smell of fried doubles drifts out the door.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Double Dose of Trinidad', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Double Dose of Trinidad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flock, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'A&A Bake & Doubles Shop (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T17:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Flock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b69ce55f-9f90-5da8-8bc2-4d90afce5fc8', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b69ce55f-9f90-5da8-8bc2-4d90afce5fc8'}, {'abstract': 'When Jaylen Ray Fryberg pulled out a handgun in the school cafeteria on Friday, according to witnesses, he did not randomly target fellow students, nor authority figures, but friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/us/contrasting-portraits-emerge-of-jaylen-ray-fryberg-shooter-at-washington-school.html', 'snippet': 'When Jaylen Ray Fryberg pulled out a handgun in the school cafeteria on Friday, according to witnesses, he did not randomly target fellow students, nor authority figures, but friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARYSVILLE, Wash. — If the bullet-scarred American psyche has an archetype for a school gunman, it looks very little like Jaylen Ray Fryberg. He was not a loner or a known misanthrope — far from it. He was a football player with a million-dollar smile, popular enough to be elected homecoming prince of his freshman class at Marysville-Pilchuck High School.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/us/WASHINGTON/WASHINGTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/26/us/WASHINGTON/WASHINGTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/us/WASHINGTON/WASHINGTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/us/WASHINGTON/WASHINGTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1439, 'width': 1944, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/us/WASHINGTON/WASHINGTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/26/us/WASHINGTON/WASHINGTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/us/WASHINGTON/WASHINGTON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tangled Portrait of a Student Emerges in Washington Shooting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tangled Portrait of a Student Emerges in Washington Shooting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dewan, Shaila K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fryberg, Jaylen Ray', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marysville (Wash)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tulalip Indian Reservation (Wash)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marysville-Pilchuck High School (Marysville, Wash)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T17:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson and Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fca84ec3-4201-5765-a1a4-a8a14d3bbe6d', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fca84ec3-4201-5765-a1a4-a8a14d3bbe6d'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of apologizing, N.B.A. owners should promise not to make season-ticket holders buy into meaningless preseason games that lack star players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/sports/basketball/with-meaningless-nba-tickets-apology-is-a-tough-sell.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of apologizing, N.B.A. owners should promise not to make season-ticket holders buy into meaningless preseason games that lack star players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the grandstanding audacity of a politician in prime time, the Phoenix Suns’ owner, Robert Sarver, strolled to the public-address microphone at US Airways Center late in a recent one-sided game against what amounted to the San Antonio Spurs’ junior varsity and told the remains of a generously announced crowd of 13,552: “This is not the game you paid your hard-earned money to watch. I apologize for it.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Meaningless Tickets, Apology Is a Tough Sell ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Meaningless Tickets, Apology Is a Tough Sell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phoenix Suns', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarver, Robert (1961- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-25T17:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f767214-2432-5c2f-8120-c28bdd199f09', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f767214-2432-5c2f-8120-c28bdd199f09'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs of Broad Channel, an island in Jamaica Bay in Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/nyregion/broad-channel-the-island-in-the-city.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs of Broad Channel, an island in Jamaica Bay in Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many New Yorkers, Broad Channel is a blur of a neighborhood they pass, by car or A train, from mainland Queens on the way to Rockaway Beach. That was the case for the photographer Maureen Drennan, who had been shooting pictures of surfers in the Rockaways in 2010 when she got off the A train in Broad Channel one day and started walking.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bouncing Back ', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bouncing Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major':