9e86f2-4f84-5364-bbd5-dd2459352871', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/099e86f2-4f84-5364-bbd5-dd2459352871'}, {'abstract': 'On Monday of my third week back at work after our son was born, I came home and found my husband sipping a beer with a frown, a sauce-stained dish in front of him, and no dinner for me.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/dont-expect-dinner/', 'snippet': 'On Monday of my third week back at work after our son was born, I came home and found my husband sipping a beer with a frown, a sauce-stained dish in front of him, and no dinner for me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Out of the corner of my eye, I saw my cell phone light up from where it was nestled in the open front pocket of my bag. I debated checking it. My students were working in small groups and probably wouldn’t notice. And I did have a 6-month-old at home, I rationalized. But I resisted. I had already scolded a number of freshmen for texting, even though it was only the third week of the semester. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/us/motherlode-plate/motherlode-plate-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/24/us/motherlode-plate/motherlode-plate-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/us/motherlode-plate/motherlode-plate-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1022, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/us/motherlode-plate/motherlode-plate-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1022, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/us/motherlode-plate/motherlode-plate-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/24/us/motherlode-plate/motherlode-plate-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/24/us/motherlode-plate/motherlode-plate-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Don’t Expect Dinner.’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T18:03:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzanne Cope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86d52390-a874-5627-8f3f-4efb77848541', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86d52390-a874-5627-8f3f-4efb77848541'}, {'abstract': 'With more faith in metrics than he is usually given credit for and an ability to delegate, Sabean, in his job since 1996, helped San Francisco reinvent itself as baseball evolved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/sports/baseball/world-series-2014-gm-brian-sabean-is-giants-implacable-leader.html', 'snippet': 'With more faith in metrics than he is usually given credit for and an ability to delegate, Sabean, in his job since 1996, helped San Francisco reinvent itself as baseball evolved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Brian Sabean lives across the street from AT&T Park, where he works as the general manager of the San Francisco Giants. He has had the job since 1996, before any of his contemporaries had theirs. It is hard to get away.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/kepner1-see-note/kepner1-see-note-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/kepner1-see-note/kepner1-see-note-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/kepner1-see-note/kepner1-see-note-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/kepner1-see-note/kepner1-see-note-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/kepner1-see-note/kepner1-see-note-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/kepner1-see-note/kepner1-see-note-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/kepner1