-oct-27.html', 'snippet': 'Tax-exempt fixed-income issues scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday. There will also be auctions of two-year notes on Tuesday, two-year floating-rate notes and five-year notes on Wednesday and seven-year notes on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions for the Week of Oct. 27', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T21:37:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f2db477-86f0-5931-a406-d8dfce11785c', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f2db477-86f0-5931-a406-d8dfce11785c'}, {'abstract': 'TLC has canceled production of “Here Comes Honey Boo Boo,” a reality series centered on Alana Thompson, 9, and her family in rural Georgia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/arts/television/tlc-says-goodbye-to-honey-boo-boo.html', 'snippet': 'TLC has canceled production of “Here Comes Honey Boo Boo,” a reality series centered on Alana Thompson, 9, and her family in rural Georgia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TLC has canceled production of “Here Comes Honey Boo Boo,” a reality series centered on the beauty pageant contestant Alana Thompson, 9, and her family in rural Georgia. The announcement came after TMZ reported that the family matriarch, June Shannon (below, with her daughter), was dating Mark McDaniel, a registered sex offender who was released from prison in March after serving 10 years for aggravated child molestation. TLC did not respond to a request for comment but said in a statement that it had “ended all activities around the series, effective immediately.” Ms. Shannon responded in a video posted on her daughter Alana’s Facebook fan page, calling the rumors about her relationship with Mr. McDaniel “totally untrue.” “I would not ever, ever, ever put my kids in danger,” Ms. Shannon said. The program is a spinoff of TLC’s “Toddlers & Tiaras,” where Alana, nicknamed Honey Boo Boo, first gained attention as a 6-year-old pageant contestant. That show stirred controversy for her precontest drink, a mixture of Red Bull and Mountain Dew, which she called “go-go juice.” “Here Comes Honey Boo Boo” had its debut in August 2012 to immediate success and produced multiple holiday specials.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/ARTS3/ARTS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/ARTS3/ARTS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 503}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/ARTS3/ARTS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 859, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/ARTS3/ARTS3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1718, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/ARTS3/ARTS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/ARTS3/ARTS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/ARTS3/ARTS3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TLC Says Goodbye to ‘Honey Boo Boo’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TLC Says Goodbye to ‘Honey Boo Boo’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Alana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TLC (TV Network)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Here Comes Honey Boo Boo (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T21:43:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b59135f-9eeb-502b-a227-778b177fed0e', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b59135f-9eeb-502b-a227-778b177fed0e'}, {'abstract': 'José Cohen and Lorenzo Hagerman have won the 2014 Margaret Mead Filmmaker Award for “H20 MX.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/movies/h20-mx-wins-margaret-mead-filmmaker-award.html', 'snippet': 'José Cohen and Lorenzo Hagerman have won the 2014 Margaret Mead Filmmaker Award for “H20 MX.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'José Cohen and Lorenzo Hagerman have won the 2014 Margaret Mead Filmmaker Award for “H20 MX”, above, a documentary about the economic, political and geographical difficulties that stand between Mexico City’s 22 million residents and a safe, reliable water supply. The award, presented on Saturday evening at the Margaret Mead Film Festival at the American Museum of Natural History, was established in 2010. The prize is named for Mead, the anthropologist, author and social critic, who was curator emeritus in the museum’s anthropology department at her death, in 1978.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/26MEAD/26MEAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/26MEAD/26MEAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/26MEAD/26MEAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/26MEAD/26MEAD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/26MEAD/26MEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/26MEAD/26MEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/26MEAD/26MEAD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘H20 MX’ Wins Margaret Mead Filmmaker Award', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Margaret Mead Filmmaker Award', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kozinn, Allan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Jose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagerman, Lorenzo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mead, Margaret', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T21:49:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ee1e35e-ae7a-51e6-8ebd-f6f83ea03ab6', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ee1e35e-ae7a-51e6-8ebd-f6f83ea03ab6'}, {'abstract': 'The paper published its first issue on Oct. 29, 1764, a one-page edition of what then was called The Connecticut Courant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/business/media/for-the-hartford-courant-250-years-in-print.html', 'snippet': 'The paper published its first issue on Oct. 29, 1764, a one-page edition of what then was called The Connecticut Courant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a time when many newspapers are just trying to survive, it is hard to think of them lasting another century.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/business/courant/courant-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/business/courant/courant-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/business/courant/courant-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/business/courant/courant-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/business/courant/courant-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/27/business/courant/courant-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/business/courant/courant-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For The Hartford Courant, 250 Years in Print', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hartford Newspaper Celebrating 250 Years ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hartford Courant', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haughney, Christine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartford (Conn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Connecticut Historical Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T21:50:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93bc1f2d-39ea-51fd-bb6f-6da64fd44d26', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93bc1f2d-39ea-51fd-bb6f-6da64fd44d26'}, {'abstract': 'Musicians like Davell Crawford and Antony Hegarty joined in a memorial service in Harlem for the singer Jimmy Scott, who died in July at 88.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/arts/music/jimmy-scott-honored-at-abyssinian-baptist-church-in-harlem.html', 'snippet': 'Musicians like Davell Crawford and Antony Hegarty joined in a memorial service in Harlem for the singer Jimmy Scott, who died in July at 88.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jimmy Scott, who died in June at 88, had a voice out of time: ripe and cutting, nestled between male and female registers, utterly unmistakable in tone as well as timbre. His influence on other singers has been profound, especially taking into account the many years he lurked in obscurity. And the breadth of that influence — its great range of possibilities, not all of them emulation — was a striking feature of his memorial service on Saturday afternoon, at the Abyssinian Baptist Church in Harlem.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'r