-a0eb6aa33d6e'}, {'abstract': 'The return of Stanley Newman.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/what-you-are/', 'snippet': 'The return of Stanley Newman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Links Alert! As many of you have noticed, the box that contains the links to the puzzle and the syndicated Wordplay posts is not working. I am removing it from posts until it is fixed, so until then, please download your copy of the puzzle from the main puzzle page. Thank you for your patience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Are', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T22:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5308c60f-1ad8-5a4c-bb97-fcf8032edbb5', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5308c60f-1ad8-5a4c-bb97-fcf8032edbb5'}, {'abstract': 'The annual CMJ Music Marathon showcase had the flavor of earlier days, with touches of updated psychedelia, but also some new pop product.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/arts/music/newcomers-and-comebacks-.html', 'snippet': 'The annual CMJ Music Marathon showcase had the flavor of earlier days, with touches of updated psychedelia, but also some new pop product.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Slowdive, the British band that performed on Saturday night at Terminal 5, held pride of place at this year’s CMJ Music Marathon, the annual showcase that brought more than 1,300 bands to Manhattan and Brooklyn clubs from Tuesday through Saturday (with some stragglers continuing into Sunday afternoon). For Slowdive, the festival’s biggest club was sold out, the audience was reverent, and the performance was imposing, giving the band’s magisterial songs a weight and resonance that was never captured in the studio. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newcomers and Comebacks ', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Newcomers and Comebacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'CMJ Music Marathon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T22:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6287627f-5bb6-5194-bba3-f357ffbed8a8', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6287627f-5bb6-5194-bba3-f357ffbed8a8'}, {'abstract': 'Another New York Times crossword puzzle contest is in the books, and we take a look at the puzzle suite that Patrick Blindauer put together … as well as spill the beans on the answer.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/26/wrapping-up-the-2014-crossword-contest/', 'snippet': 'Another New York Times crossword puzzle contest is in the books, and we take a look at the puzzle suite that Patrick Blindauer put together … as well as spill the beans on the answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Across Lite Solvers Alert! Did you solve the Saturday, Oct. 25 puzzle using Across Lite? The answers were locked away until the contest closed, but if you’d like to unlock them now, the code is 1356.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrapping Up the 2014 Crossword Contest', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-26T22:05:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94f6ebbe-1a6c-5fad-9873-2994acb4a8f2', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94f6ebbe-1a6c-5fad-9873-2994acb4a8f2'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater continued its fall season with works like “Sinfonietta,” “Raymonda Divertissements” and “Seven Sonatas.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/arts/dance/ballet-theater-offers-sinfonietta-and-seven-sonatas.html', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater continued its fall season with works like “Sinfonietta,” “Raymonda Divertissements” and “Seven Sonatas.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a few lucky men at American Ballet Theater on Friday night, the sound of trumpets and the sight of a large bare stage were a gift: an invitation to cover space. At the start of “Sinfonietta,” a 1978 work by Jiri Kylian performed at the David H. Koch Theater, seven men reveled in jetés that sent them soaring from one side of the stage to the other. If the stage was a field, they were its horses. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/BALLET/BALLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/arts/BALLE