s', '_id': 'nyt://article/40293b4b-5103-5ab0-9b8f-511f0cc7e0bd', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40293b4b-5103-5ab0-9b8f-511f0cc7e0bd'}, {'abstract': 'In a country that has long been ill at ease with its hard-living son, Thomas’s granddaughter is trying to refocus public attention on the poet’s work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/world/europe/a-toast-to-dylan-thomas-on-his-100th-birthday.html', 'snippet': 'In a country that has long been ill at ease with its hard-living son, Thomas’s granddaughter is trying to refocus public attention on the poet’s work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAUGHARNE, Wales — Down the footpath from his writing shed, along the curve of the water and up the hill, you see what the poet Dylan Thomas once saw: tall birds on the “heron priested shore,” a “sea wet church the size of a snail” atop the ridge, the castle ruin to your left still “brown as owls.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Wales, a Toast to Dylan Thomas on His 100th Birthday', 'kicker': 'Laugharne Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Toast to Dylan Thomas on His 100th Birthday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Dylan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Laugharne (Wales)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Laugharne (Wales)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T00:23:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/18c84867-0a64-5f85-97ae-41b83188ddc2', 'word_count': 1160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18c84867-0a64-5f85-97ae-41b83188ddc2'}, {'abstract': 'A report by the PEN American Center cited police interference with journalists, including holding reporters in areas that denied them access to the protests, and accusations of threats and assaults.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/business/media/-us-inquiry-sought-in-police-treatment-of-press-at-ferguson-protests-.html', 'snippet': 'A report by the PEN American Center cited police interference with journalists, including holding reporters in areas that denied them access to the protests, and accusations of threats and assaults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Compiling 52 accusations of violations of the freedom of the press during the protests in Ferguson, Mo., after the killing of Michael Brown, the PEN American Center will announce on Monday that it is calling on the Justice Department to investigate the local police forces’ treatment of the news media.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' U.S. Inquiry Sought in Police Treatment of Press at Ferguson Protests ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' U.S. Inquiry Sought in Police Treatment of Press at Ferguson Protests ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Noam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PEN American Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T00:25:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e10ff19a-736f-5ebf-8de0-618dad34a6d0', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e10ff19a-736f-5ebf-8de0-618dad34a6d0'}, {'abstract': 'A percolating class of teams is trying to break up the dominance of the Spurs and the Thunder in the Western Conference, where there is a reasonable chance that teams will need 50 wins just to make it to the playoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/sports/basketball/good-nba-teams-jostle-to-join-the-best-in-the-west.html', 'snippet': 'A percolating class of teams is trying to break up the dominance of the Spurs and the Thunder in the Western Conference, where there is a reasonable chance that teams will need 50 wins just to make it to the playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once again, the N.B.A.’s Western Conference is so deep that there is a reasonable chance it will take 50 wins just to make the playoffs. In the Eastern Conference, only the Cavaliers and the Bulls are expected to win as many as 50. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/NBAWEST/NBAWEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/NBAWEST/NBAWEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 670}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/sports/NBAWEST/NBAWEST-jumb