1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ef2b61f-5ebd-52fa-92cc-0d376526e5ff', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ef2b61f-5ebd-52fa-92cc-0d376526e5ff'}, {'abstract': 'When New York State settled a seven-year-long lawsuit, it started to move in a better direction with this core but neglected constitutional right to provide lawyers for the indigent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/opinion/a-rare-victory-for-public-defense.html', 'snippet': 'When New York State settled a seven-year-long lawsuit, it started to move in a better direction with this core but neglected constitutional right to provide lawyers for the indigent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Sixth Amendment guarantees a lawyer for all criminal defendants, whether or not they can afford one. But that promise is often broken as states continue to cut spending on indigent defense, leaving the poorest people without proper legal assistance. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rare Victory for Public Defense', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rare Victory for Public Defense', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders and Court-Appointed Lawyers (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sixth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Schulte Roth & Zabel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value'