n-the-georgia-race-has-become-a-dead-heat.html', 'snippet': 'Michelle Nunn has caught up to David Perdue in polling, and her gains can be attributed to changes in the racial composition of likely voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most startling developments in the fight for the Senate this year is that Michelle Nunn, the Democratic candidate in Georgia, has closed the gap with the Republican David Perdue. Her gains came after it was revealed that Mr. Perdue, a business executive, said in a deposition in 2005 that he was proud of his record of outsourcing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Reason the Georgia Race Has Become a Dead Heat', 'kicker': 'Midterm Calculus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perdue, David A Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nunn, Michelle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T12:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd6d97cd-1c1c-5787-8db7-6dbd85b59f8a', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd6d97cd-1c1c-5787-8db7-6dbd85b59f8a'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Paul LePage has opened a big lead in his bid 