 packaging as well — embracing what brain scientists call the smorgasbord effect, offering shoppers a variety of tastes in one purchase. And the strategy is spreading throughout the grocery store.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Chocolate Halloween Candy in the Trick-or-Treat Bag', 'kicker': "What's in It?", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trick-or-Treat Bag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Halloween', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Candy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hershey Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mars Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T14:59:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e30dfd5-4a63-51d4-b9ba-9a18d9827823', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e30dfd5-4a63-51d4-b9ba-9a18d9827823'}, {'abstract': 'My mother rarely travels without my father, but when she went away for a week this month, our family dynamic was thrown out of whack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/fashion/when-dads-other-half-is-away.html', 'snippet': 'My mother rarely travels without my father, but when she went away for a week this month, our family dynamic was thrown out of whack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like most adult children of long-term marriages, it is nearly impossible for me to imagine one of my parents without the other. In my case, it is not just because my mother and father are two years’ shy of having been married for six decades, but also because I live with my folks, and rarely see them apart from morning till night. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 539, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 539, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Dad’s Other Half Is Away', 'kicker': 'Reverse Parenting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Dad&#8217;s Other Half Is Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T15:04:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Conlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Conlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d692d86f-df8a-5a2c-bb33-5eae68eae7c1', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d692d86f-df8a-5a2c-bb33-5eae68eae7c1'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: German emperors wait for their crowns in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/1889-new-crowns-for-german-emperors/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: German emperors wait for their crowns in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Emperor and Empress of Germany have just been measured for their new autumn crowns, and the maker has promised to have them ready by the time their Majesties return from Constantinople. The Emperor’s new crown is of very much the same shape as his grandfather’s crown, but the latter was far too large for the present Emperor, who, with a discretion that President Harrison might have exhibited, said that he would not make himself ridiculous by wearing a crown too big for him, merely because it belonged to his grandfather. The Empress’s crown is a sweet thing in gold, and the first Sunday that she goes to church with it on her head she will make the Berlin ladies mad with envy.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Oct. 28, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/blogs/28iht-oldoct28-kaiser/28iht-oldoct28-kaiser-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 481, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'captio