s” and runs through March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of Arts and Design, in Columbus Circle, is presenting a look at the city of Baltimore as it has been captured for the silver screen by five directors who represent a broad range of sensibilities. The series, “It Came From Baltimore: 40 Years of Cinema From the Charm City,” opens on Nov. 21 with “Pink Flamingos,” John Waters’s 1972 study in depravity (characters compete for the title “filthiest person alive”), and ends on March 5, with a screening of “Putty Hill,” a 2010 film by Matthew Porterfield about a group of friends reflecting on the death of a young man.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum of Art and Design Series Focuses on Baltimore in Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Arts and Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T18:43:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a9feac8-8116-5a03-a011-b90e86d82a28', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a9feac8-8116-5a03-a011-b90e86d82a28'}, {'abstract': 'Reuven Rivlin, Israel’s new president, visited the site of an infamous 1956 massacre, with the goal of healing Jewish-Arab relations and urging tolerance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/world/middleeast/working-to-heal-in-israeli-town-with-a-deep-arab-wound.html', 'snippet': 'Reuven Rivlin, Israel’s new president, visited the site of an infamous 1956 massacre, with the goal of healing Jewish-Arab relations and urging tolerance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAFR QASSEM, Israel — When Reuven Rivlin, Israel’s recently elected president, visited this predominantly Arab town northeast of Tel Aviv on Sunday, there were no Israeli flags lining the streets. There were only black flags, marking the 58th anniversary of a painful chapter in Israel’s history, the Kafr Qassem massacre.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Working to Heal, in Israeli Town With a Deep Arab Wound', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivlin, Reuven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T18:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33b68cb9-3790-5ffd-bf28-8c5e6802294e', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33b68cb9-3790-5ffd-bf28-8c5e6802294e'}, {'abstract': 'Bright colors appear on the wings of male fruit flies when held against a dark background, a characteristic that female fruit flies use to decide whom to mate with, researchers say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/science/fruit-flies-pass-mating-test-with-flying-colors.html', 'snippet': 'Bright colors appear on the wings of male fruit flies when held against a dark background, a characteristic that female fruit flies use to decide whom to mate with, researchers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bright colors appear on the wings of male fruit flies when held against a dark background, a characteristic that female fruit flies use to decide whom to mate with, researchers from Lund University say. The colors on the wings, barely a millionth of a millimeter thick, are caused by thin-film interference, the kind of light refraction that causes rainbows to appear on the surface of an oil streak, says the study, which was published in Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/science/28SUBFLOA/28SUBFLOA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/28/science/28SUBFLOA/28SUBFLOA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/science/28SUBFLOA/28SUBFLOA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/science/28SUBFLOA/28SUBFLOA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1288, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/science/28SUBFLOA/28SUBFLOA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/28/science/28SUBFLOA/28SUBFLOA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images