g uniformity to a messy patchwork of responses by states.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Moves to End Patchwork of Policies on Returning Ebola Workers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rules for Health Care Workers Returning From West Africa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T18:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed9b0d3-b3c7-56f8-88b4-de6dc9867243', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed9b0d3-b3c7-56f8-88b4-de6dc9867243'}, {'abstract': 'Rail heads made by Trinity Industries, meant to reduce damage in a collision, are suspected of having a defect and have been banned by 13 states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/business/virginia-plans-to-remove-suspect-guardrail-parts.html', 'snippet': 'Rail heads made by Trinity Industries, meant to reduce damage in a collision, are suspected of having a defect and have been banned by 13 states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adding to pressure on the guardrail manufacturer Trinity Industries, Virginia said on Monday that it planned to remove the company’s products after it failed to meet a state deadline to supply documentation for new crash testing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia to Remove Suspect Guardrails', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia to Remove Suspect