/27/1914-allies-advance-in-west-africa/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The war rages on in Africa in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — While the Allies have been fighting strenuously in France and Belgium, the German possessions in West Africa have also been the scene of some keen struggles. On August 25 a British force in carrying out a reconnaissance from Yola, Nigeria, crossed the Anglo- German frontier and, after meeting with some resistance, occupied Tepe. In this action several casualties occurred, and the enemy is known to have lost one German officer killed.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Oct. 28, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/blogs/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/28/blogs/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/blogs/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/blogs/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/blogs/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica/28iht-oldoct28-WestAfrica-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/