rogram turns 15 next year. To celebrate, he has compiled a new double album, a song from which premieres here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/27/beats-in-space-party-night/', 'snippet': 'D.J. Tim Sweeney’s cult-favorite program turns 15 next year. To celebrate, he has compiled a new double album, a song from which premieres here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since September 2000, the underground dance music show Beats in Space — hosted by Tim Sweeney, who was a college freshman when he began the project — has aired every Tuesday night from the campus of New York University’s WNYU station. And more or less since then, it has been a vital component of underground dance culture. DFA acts like the Rapture and James Murphy served as early D.J. guests; icons like DJ Harvey, Todd Terje and Juan Atkins have manned the decks over the years. Next month, Beats in Space will celebrate its 15th birthday a bit early with a series of parties (in locations including Brooklyn, London and Berlin) as well as a two-disc set compiling both exclusive dance tracks and some classics that have been staples of the show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/t-magazine/27beta-hartman/27beta-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/t-magazine/27beta-hartman/27beta-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 719}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/t-magazine/27beta-hartman/27beta-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 855, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/t-magazine/27beta-hartman/27beta-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 