r of the T contributor’s life and work, a brief look back at some of his appearances in the Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What I really like about photography is that there’s this degree of detachment, where you’re mediating a person rather than actually being with them,” said the photographer and T contributor David Armstrong ahead of his “Mad About the Boy” exhibition at Half Gallery in 2010. “It’s a heightened kind of being with them: You want to know them but you also want to get a good picture of them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering the Photographer David Armstrong', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Armstrong, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-27T22:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c44dc88e-ca47-5cc1-91ab-878f80535295', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c44dc88e-ca47-5cc1-91ab-878f80535295'}, {'abstract': 'D. A. Pennebaker and Chris Hegedus, whose documentaries have captured moments in history and counterculture, are seeking a home for their film archive and related materials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/movies/d-a-pennebaker-and-chris-hegeduss-counterculture-archive.html', 'snippet': 'D. A. Pennebaker and Chris Hegedus, whose documentaries have captured moments in history and counterculture, are seeking a home for their film archive and related materials.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Johnny’s in the basement, mixing up the medicine,” and a young Bob Dylan, lean of body and scruffy of hair, flips cue cards along to his lyrics as the poet Allen Ginsberg stands off to the side, chatting. This landmark video, for “Subterranean Homesick Blues,” opened the 1967 documentary “Dont Look Back,” which became a rock doc classic and also earned the man behind the camera, D. A. Pennebaker, a place in film history. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/arts/jppennebaker/jppennebaker-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/28/arts/jppennebaker/jppennebaker-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/arts/jppennebaker/jppennebaker-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/arts/jppennebaker/jppennebaker-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/arts/jppennebaker/jppennebaker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/28/arts/jppennebaker/jppennebaker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/arts/jppennebaker/jppennebaker-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanted: Home for a Prized