.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/sports/baseball/ratings-for-the-world-series-remain-on-the-low-side.html', 'snippet': 'Game 4 on Saturday had an average of 10.7 million viewers, and Game 5 on Sunday had an average of 12.6 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The audience for the World Series on Fox remained stubbornly modest over the weekend. Game 4 on Saturday had an average of 10.7 million viewers, and Game 5 on Sunday had 12.6 million. Last year, for the comparable games between Boston and St. Louis — which were played on Sunday and Monday nights — the viewership was 16 million for Game 4 and 14.5 million for Game 5.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ratings for the World Series Remain on the Low Side', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Series Garners Low Ratings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Royals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T03:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd4f783c-10e5-5f1d-b894-2a040947a2ac', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd4f783c-10e5-5f1d-b894-2a040947a2ac'}, {'ab