014-10-28T04:58:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b3f2292-9873-5615-9c88-53de33da8ade', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b3f2292-9873-5615-9c88-53de33da8ade'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (MoreMax) NON-STOP (2014) An air marshal (Liam Neeson), consumed by heartache and a complicated past, tries to outwit a villain on a flight from New York to London who has vowed to kill a passenger every 20 minutes unless $150 million is transferred to a bank account. In this thriller directed by Jaume Collet-Serra, Julianne Moore, Corey Stoll, Michelle Dockery, Scoot McNairy, Lupita Nyong’o, Linus Roache and Shea Whigham add to the suspense in their roles as prospective heroes or villains. And while the movie doesn’t always make sense, that’s “incidental to the pleasures of a slow-season Liam Neeson release as diverting as this one,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “A lot has been written about Mr. Neeson’s surprising resurrection as an older action hero, which has sometimes been more rewarding theoretically than cinematically. Mr. Collet-Serra, however, makes good on that promise with a sure genre hand and real feeling for what Mr. Neeson brings to the screen at this stage of his career, including beauty etched by time and a still-imposing body that moves with the heaviness and grandeur of an old warrior raising his sword one last time. When Mr. Neeson runs through the aisles, he can sometimes seem too big for this vehicle, even if he turns out to be exactly right.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9e670ef-6448-5299-ace1-5e1938123c68', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9e670ef-6448-5299-ace1-5e1938123c68'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, October 28, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, October 28, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Solomon would be on his knees after a week here. Every day there’s a new dilemma we haven’t considered.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T05:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b3b5ea2-dc27-5888-8ec5-394713f54de6', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b3b5ea2-dc27-5888-8ec5-394713f54de6'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Tuesday, October 28, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/pageoneplus/corrections-october-28-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Tuesday, October 28, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 28, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T05:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f6ad8d4-49bf-55e0-81a8-c9f3bce1739c', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f6ad8d4-49bf-55e0-81a8-c9f3bce1739c'}, {'abstract': 'Ultranationalist cyberactivists have menaced the village of Sarufutsu over a memorial to Korean laborers who died building an airfield there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/29/world/asia/japanese-village-grappling-with-wartime-sins-comes-under-attack.html', 'snippet': 'Ultranationalist cyberactivists have menaced the village of Sarufutsu over a memorial to Korean laborers who died building an airfield there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SARUFUTSU, Japan — More than a half-century has passed since the postmaster in this seaside hamlet on the frigid, northern tip of Japan pulled aside a young man and shared a secret. Somewhere in the village, the old man confided, was a lost graveyard hiding Korean bones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/world/asia/29japan-01/29japan-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/29/world/asia/29japan-01/29japan-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag