history of appealing to voters as self-styled feisty populists. The midterms are no different. (They’re worse!)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/magazine/the-bumpkinification-of-the-midterm-elections.html', 'snippet': 'From Andrew Jackson to Joni Ernst, American politicians have a long history of appealing to voters as self-styled feisty populists. The midterms are no different. (They’re worse!)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joni Ernst, the Iowa state senator and Iraq War veteran, was standing in a barn in a purple flannel shirt and an unzipped vest. Beside her, various swine burrowed in the hog lot; two small pigs spooned; there was copious squealing. When Ernst, who grew up on a farm castrating hogs, opened her mouth to speak, she drew the inevitable connection between her upbringing and her current role as a Republican candidate for the United States Senate. “When I get to Washington, I’ll know how to cut pork,” Ernst said, smiling. Title cards reinforced her credentials. (“Joni Ernst: Mother. Soldier. Conservative.”) “I’m Joni Ernst, and I approve this message because Washington is full of big spenders. Let’s make ‘em squeal.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/magazine/02leibovich1/02leibovich1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 502, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/magazine/02leibovich1/02leibovich1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 502}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/magazine/02leibovich1/02leibovich1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/magazine/02leibovich1/02leibovich1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 989, 'width': 1181, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/magazine/02leibovich1/02leibovich1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/magazine/02leibovich1/02leibovich1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/magazine/02leibovich1/02leibovich1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bumpkinification of the Midterm Elections', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If Pigs Could Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovich, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ernst, Joni', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrow, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McFadden, Mike', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T08:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Leibovich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leibovich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61cf6c3a-2908-5520-b43b-ab238225fd09', 'word_count': 1802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61cf6c3a-2908-5520-b43b-ab238225fd09'}, {'abstract': 'Tomas van Houtryve took the idea of foreign drone strikes and instead targeted similar domestic situations, putting them under surveillance using his drone in public spaces.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/bringing-the-drone-war-to-american-skies/', 'snippet': 'Tomas van Houtryve took the idea of foreign drone strikes and instead targeted similar domestic situations, putting them under surveillance using his drone in public spaces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomas van Houtryve was reading about the thousands of combatant and civilian deaths from United States military drone strikes when he wondered what the aftermath of these bombings looked like. But when he searched — hoping to find a latter-day equivalent of Nick Ut’s 9-year-old napalm victim — he found little. Instead, he saw photos from the drone manufacturers, showing off their products soaring in clear blue skies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing the Drone War to American Skies', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burrows, Larry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ut, Nick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Investigative Journalism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty Images', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Harper's Magazine", 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rena Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silverman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad58ee1a-999e-55d8-aa2f-89c33f692c58', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad58ee1a-999e-55d8-aa2f-89c33f692c58'}, {'abstract': 'How do you decide what news sources to trust?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/how-do-you-get-your-news/', 'snippet': 'How do you decide what news sources to trust?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Previous generations tended to get their news from network news anchors or the hometown newspaper. Then came cable and the Internet, and the news business still continues to evolve. More and more consumers — especially young people — are now getting their news from Facebook and other social media sites. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/26/business/media/Algorithms-Illustration2-LN/Algorithms-Illustration2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None