rk Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/opinion/nyto-headline/nyto-headline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/27/opinion/nyto-headline/nyto-headline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 595}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/opinion/nyto-headline/nyto-headline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1015, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/opinion/nyto-headline/nyto-headline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1965, 'width': 1982, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/opinion/nyto-headline/nyto-headline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/27/opinion/nyto-headline/nyto-headline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/27/opinion/nyto-headline/nyto-headline-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens to the News When Ebola Reaches New York', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spencer, Craig Allen (1981- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T10:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38a7c067-4859-5405-aee3-1d01347ccbe1', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38a7c067-4859-5405-aee3-1d01347ccbe1'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A radio play sows panic in Charleston in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/1939-radio-play-terrifies-hundreds/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A radio play sows panic in Charleston in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — Several hundred radio listeners in the Charleston region rushed terror-stricken from their homes last night after listening to a fictional radio play in which were described experiments with an ‘‘anti-aircraft defense ray.’’ The play was interrupted seven times for announcements reminding listeners that it was fictional, but the narration of how ‘‘this ray has destroyed all matter, even the earth’s supply of air’’ started the rumor that a near-by dam had been blown up. The play was called ‘‘Salute to Orson Welles,’’ whose radio drama on a Martian invasion of the earth caused widespread panic a year ago.\xa0 — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Oct. 29, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Radio Play Terrifies Hundreds', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welles, Orson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T10:50:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65ed0156-094d-506c-8dcd-c55b55dc89dd', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65ed0156-094d-506c-8dcd-c55b55dc89dd'}, {'abstract': 'Gaming offers a wonderful variety of experience to a diverse audience. It’s no longer just a boys’ club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/29/opinion/anita-sarkeesian-on-video-games-great-future.html', 'snippet': 'Gaming offers a wonderful variety of experience to a diverse audience. It’s no longer just a boys’ club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — I remember, when I was a kid, desperately trying to persuade my mom and dad to buy me a Game Boy. They were very reluctant. The conventional wisdom of the early ’90s said that video games would rot kids’ brains, and as immigrants who came to North America from Iraq to provide a better life for me and my sister, my parents bought into that myth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Game Over for ‘Gamers’', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Game Over for the 'Gamers'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkeesian, Anita', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wii (Video Game System)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T10:52:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Sarkeesian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sarkeesian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cea019ca-5fe1-5c0f-9c7b-1d6950b46533', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cea019ca-5fe1-5c0f-9c7b-1d6950b46533'}, {'abstract': 'The British bank, which generates most of its profit in Asia, said it planned to look for an additional $400 million in cost reductions in 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/standard-chartered-profit-falls-in-third-quarter/', 'snippet': 'The British bank, which generates most of its profit in Asia, said it planned to look for an additional $400 million in cost reductions in 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The British bank Standard Chartered, which generates most of its profit in Asia, said on Tuesday that pretax profit declined 16 percent in the third quarter on higher charges for bad loans and other credit risks as weaker commodity markets affected some clients.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/business/dbpix-standard-chartered/dbpix-standard-chartered-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/29/business/dbpix-standard-chartered/dbpix-standard-chartered-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/business/dbpix-standard-chartered/dbpix-standard-chartered-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/business/dbpix-standard-chartered/dbpix-standard-chartered-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/business/dbpix-standard-chartered/dbpix-standard-chartered-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/29/business/dbpix-standard-chartered/dbpix-standard-chartered-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/business/dbpix-standard-chartered/dbpix-standard-chartered-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Standard Chartered Profit Falls 16%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fa