SG move forward with the split, it would be the latest in a wave of breakups that have swept through corporate America in recent years. MSG’s breakup would also come after the sale of the Los Angeles Clippers professional basketball team to Steven A. Ballmer, formerly Microsoft’s chief executive, for a blockbuster $2 billion price that spurred discussions about what other sports franchises are now worth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Madison Square Garden Co. Weighs Split', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T11:47:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2e689f9-c0b5-51b1-a4c0-72e56d49ad0a', 'word_count': 2379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2e689f9-c0b5-51b1-a4c0-72e56d49ad0a'}, {'abstract': 'I try to avoid simply harping on my own pet peeves when citing phrases as overused or tired. But I can’t deny that I find this expression particularly irksome: “channeling one’s inner something-or-other.”', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/phrases-we-love-too-much-6/', 'snippet': 'I try to avoid simply harping on my own pet peeves when citing phrases as overused or tired. But I can’t deny that I find this expression particularly irksome: “channeling one’s inner something-or-other.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I try to avoid simply harping on my own pet peeves when citing phrases as overused or tired. But I can’t deny that I find this expression particularly irksome: “channeling one’s inner something-or-other.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'he