'abstract': 'Literary figures give readers a literal entree into their novels.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/authors-auction-off-novelistic-naming-rights/', 'snippet': 'Literary figures give readers a literal entree into their novels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ian McEwan is offering “the genuine opportunity of an afterlife.” The same promise is coming from the authors Margaret Atwood, Julian Barnes, Ken Follett, Hanif Kureishi, Will Self, Alan Hollinghurst and Zadie Smith. It’s not a new literary religion but an auction, to be held on Nov. 20 for the charity Freedom from Torture, during which 17 authors will sell the right to name characters in their upcoming novels.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/arts/arts2/arts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/29/arts/arts2/arts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 795}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/arts/arts2/arts2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 773, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/arts/arts2/arts2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1545, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/29/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/29/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'ca