, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krause, Stefan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schenck, Marcus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T19:24:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing and Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7494edf9-eb21-5ebf-b01a-63e863183a51', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7494edf9-eb21-5ebf-b01a-63e863183a51'}, {'abstract': 'For a new book and app, Steven Sebring created unique composite images of the supermodel using 100 cameras arranged in a circle around her.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/28/steven-sebring-coco-rocha-book/', 'snippet': 'For a new book and app, Steven Sebring created unique composite images of the supermodel using 100 cameras arranged in a circle around her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1880s, the photographer Eadweard Muybridge captured human and animal figures in motion, producing images the likes of which the world had never seen before. A generation of artists, including Duchamp, Bacon and Picasso, were inspired by what those grainy black-and-white photos revealed. Now, the photographer and filmmaker Steven Sebring has focused on the human form in a dynamic new dimension, creating his own revolution. In a new book, “Study of Pose,” which includes an introduction by Jean Paul Gaultier, Sebring has shot the chameleonic supermodel Coco Rocha, known as the “Queen of Pose,” in 1,000 different positions. Sebring captured each of Rocha’s postures — from the sultry stance of a rock star to the pointed pirouette of a prima ballerina — using a setup he calls the Rig, which consists of 100 cameras arranged in a circle that allows for a 360-degree view of each moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Photographer Reinvents the Pose With Coco Rocha', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaultier, Jean Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rocha, Coco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebring, Steven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-28T19:25:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Royal Young', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Royal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Young', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8c021fa-72fd-5a27-a8c1-c776d445d5bb', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8c021fa-72fd-5a27-a8c1-c776d445d5bb'}, {'abstract': 'Plagued by complaints about jet activity, the Santa Monica Municipal Airport is facing a vote next week on whether residents or the city should control its future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/29/realestate/at-santa-monica-airport-the-noise-off-the-runway-is-getting-louder.html', 'snippet': 'Plagued by complaints about jet activity, the Santa Monica Municipal Airport is facing a vote next week on whether residents or the city should control its future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTA MONICA, Calif. — Residential neighborhoods encircle the municipal airport here on three sides. And 