dtrack-johann-johannsson/', 'snippet': 'Creating a soundtrack for the biopic “The Theory of Everything” represented a departure for the Icelandic musician Johann Johannsson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When discussing his soundtrack for James Marsh’s upcoming biopic about the physicist Stephen Hawking, “The Theory of Everything,” the Icelandic musician and composer Johann Johannsson can’t help but tend toward scientific metaphors. He describes the lush, strings-driven orchestration in evidence throughout the work as “shimmery and sparkling — like the stars in the sky, almost.” And as for the four-note piano ostinato figure that anchors the score: “It’s like the DNA of the film that mutates and evolves,” he says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28symonds-johann/28symonds-johann-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28symonds-johann/28symonds-johann-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28symonds-johann/28symonds-johann-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28symonds-johann/28symonds-johann-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28symonds-johann/28symonds-johann-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/