 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50a020ac-351c-5fda-b618-d5b0c22c43e7'}, {'abstract': 'New studies show that the effects of marijuana on young people may be greater than we thought.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/education/edlife/this-is-your-brain-on-drugs-marijuana-adults-teens.html', 'snippet': 'New studies show that the effects of marijuana on young people may be greater than we thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The gray matter of the nucleus accumbens, the walnut-shaped pleasure center of the brain, was glowing like a flame, showing a notable increase in density. “It could mean that there’s some sort of drug learning taking place,” speculated Jodi Gilman, at her computer screen at the Massachusetts General Hospital-Harvard Center for Addiction Medicine. Was the brain adapting to marijuana exposure, rewiring the reward system to demand the drug?', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SCIENCE_COMBO/02SCIENCE_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SCIENCE_COMBO/02SCIENCE_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 587}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SCIENCE_COMBO/02SCIENCE_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1001, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SCIENCE_COMBO/02SCIENCE_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 1091, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag