1', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/231861f5-9af2-5a3c-845b-695e9a1b5541'}, {'abstract': 'The World Health Organization’s assistant director general said there had been a decline in burials in the West African nation and no increases in confirmed cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/world/africa/ebola-liberia-who.html', 'snippet': 'The World Health Organization’s assistant director general said there had been a decline in burials in the West African nation and no increases in confirmed cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — Three months after declaring West Africa’s Ebola epidemic a global emergency, the World Health Organization said Wednesday that new infections in Liberia, one of the worst affected countries, appeared to be declining. But the organization also warned against complacency in international efforts to fight the disease.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/world/30ebola/30ebola-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/world/30ebola/30ebola-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/world/30ebola/30ebola-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/world/30ebola/30ebola-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/world/30ebola/30ebola-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail'