b46', 'word_count': 17, 'uri': 'nyt://article/253f8cd2-f661-54c5-ad66-e2ab4bd87b46'}, {'abstract': 'The tastemaker behind the Miami retail emporium the Webster has outfitted a poolside space at the St. Regis Bal Harbour in true South Beach style.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/29/webster-cabana-st-regis-bal-harbour/', 'snippet': 'The tastemaker behind the Miami retail emporium the Webster has outfitted a poolside space at the St. Regis Bal Harbour in true South Beach style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miami boutique the Webster has become the shop heard round the world thanks to collaborations with brands ranging from Target to Berluti and the eye-catching personal style of its C.E.O. and co-founder,\xa0Laure Heriard Dubreuil. Now, just in time for resort-getaway season, Dubreuil has lent her creative and curatorial talents to The St. Regis Bal Harbour, where she has outfitted a poolside cabana in true South Beach style. Featuring marble floors, antique mirrors and floral-print furniture by Paul Frankl, the 600-square-foot space — which can be rented by hotel guests and nonguests for private lounging or intimate gatherings — is, as Dubreuil puts it, “confidential and tropical, an Americana visual from the ’40s and ’50s.” Amenities include butler service, air-conditioning, a flat-screen TV, Hampton sunscreen and plush robes and slippers. Note to Art Basel-goers: book now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28hartman-webster/28hartman-webster-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28hartman-webster/28hartman-webster-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/28/t-magazine/28hartman-w