d-we-put-baseball-on-speed/', 'snippet': 'The seemingly pointless, time-killing rituals of the game are a buffer against the frenetic pace of everyday life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the World Series rolls around, as it has again this year, there are statistics (wins, losses, E.R.A.s, strikeouts, errors) — and there are statistics (Nielsen viewer ratings, advertising revenue). It is this second type that has caused some discussion this year about the state of the game of baseball and its appeal to its many millions of fans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should We Put Baseball on Speed?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-29T21:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark C. Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9b05e18-dfe9-5838-9763-5269ec3a70b6', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9b05e18-dfe9-5838-9763-5269ec3a70b6'}, {'abstract': 'Last October, some New Yorkers were brave enough to wear their costumes to work. We asked how people reacted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/fashion/halloween-costumes-on-the-job.html', 'snippet': 'Last October, some New Yorkers were brave enough to wear their costumes to work. We asked how people reacted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some people never grow out of the habit of wearing a costume on Halloween, even if it means going to work dressed as Little Red Riding Hood. Last October, these four New Yorkers did just that, and recently recalled the experience. These interviews have been edited and condensed.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'