: 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b832e3e9-5538-5f35-bb01-2e2da1108863'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Nobel Physics Prize goes to researchers working on the maser-laser light beam in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/29/1964-nobel-physics-prize-goes-to-3/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Nobel Physics Prize goes to researchers working on the maser-laser light beam in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles Hard Townes today, age 99, talks about how he invented the laser, for which he won a Nobel Prize for physics in 1964. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Nobel Physics Prize Goes to 3', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laser (Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-29T21:25:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23066b2a-a895-53f3-8292-b81f8ca10002', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23066b2a-a895-53f3-8292-b81f8ca10002'}, {'abstract': 'The actor and advocate discusses his forthcoming movie, “Shelter.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/29/paul-bettany-shelter-coalition-for-the-homeless/', 'snippet': 'The actor and advocate discusses his forthcoming movie, “Shelter.”', 'lead_paragraph': "When the actor Paul Bettany set out to write and direct his first feature film, the upcoming “Shelter,” inspiration came from an unlikely source: a homeless couple who lived outside his apartment building. After Hurricane Sandy hit, Bettany never saw them again. “I’m not a religious man, but I grew up a Catholic, and my father always used to say to me, ‘There but for the grace of God go I,'” Bettany says. He was keen to explore the disparity between that sense of empathy and what he sees as today’s dismissive view of homelessness. “Now there’s this sort of slightly aggressive response,” he says. “This idea that you must have done something to bring yourself this low, and you’re responsible for it.” In their research for “Shelter,” Bettany and his wife, Jennifer Connelly, who stars in the film, became involved with the organization Coalition for the Homeless; tomorrow they will be honored at its annual ArtWalk\xa0gala, hosted by Dolce & Gabbana, at which works from such artists as Cindy Sherman, Chuck Close and Louise Bourgeois will be auctioned off. (Pre-bids can also be submitted online at Paddle8.)", 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Bettany on Directing His First Film and His Mission to Help the Homeless', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Q. and A.: Man and Mission', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettany, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connelly, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coalition for the Homeless', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-29T21:26:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/088d6a9c-b04c-518d-ac7b-989e81be5b04', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/088d6a9c-b04c-518d-ac7b-989e81be5b04'}, {'abstract': 'Colin Kaepernick, Nick Foles and Ronnie Hillman are among the recommended fantasy football players in Week 9.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/sports/football/fantasy-football-week-9-matchup-breakdown.html', 'snippet': 'Colin Kaepernick, Nick Foles and Ronnie Hillman are among the recommended fantasy football players in Week 9.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those of us who championed Steelers quarterback Ben Roethlisberger in Weeks 5 and 6 when he was set up for fantasy football success against two friendly secondaries only to post two duds, it was difficult to stomach his mind-boggling performance in Week 8. He totaled 522 passing yards and six touchdowns for 56 standard fantasy points. This was done, no less, against the Colts, who were the second toughest defense for opposing quarterbacks to face entering the game.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/sports/30fantasy1/30fantasy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/sports/30fantasy1/30fantasy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/sports/30fantasy1/30fantasy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ra