be scared: Simple, pleasing terror returns in Alien: Isolation, The Evil Within and P. T.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because video games are so good at making players feel powerful, they also excel at conveying powerlessness. Rendering a player weak, instead of strong, creates vulnerability and often fear. Yet it’s been a while since big-budget games really zeroed in on making the skin crawl. So it’s welcome that horror has made a comeback this year with two major games — Alien: Isolation and The Evil Within — that want you to feel hopelessly overmatched against a malevolent force. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/arts/HORRORGAMES-SUB/HORRORGAMES-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/arts/HORRORGAMES-SUB/HORRORGAMES-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/arts/HORRORGAMES-SUB/HORRORGAMES-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 545, 'width': 978, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/arts/HORRORGAMES-SUB/HORRORGAMES-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 545, 'width': 978, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/arts/HORRORGAMES-SUB/HORRORGAMES-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/30/arts/HORRORGAMES-SUB/HORRORGAMES-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'ca