ucational Testing Service said it had reliable information that tests had been compromised for thousands of South Korean and Chinese students applying to American colleges and universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/world/asia/sat-cheating-inquiry-delays-scores-for-south-korea-and-china.html', 'snippet': 'The Educational Testing Service said it had reliable information that tests had been compromised for thousands of South Korean and Chinese students applying to American colleges and universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to cheating allegations, the company that administers the SAT tests around the world is withholding scores, at least temporarily, for thousands of Chinese and South Korean students just days before the early application deadlines for most American colleges and universities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SAT Cheating Inquiry Delays Scores for South Korea and China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SAT Cheating Inquiry Delays South Korea and China Scores', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SAT (College Admission Test)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Board', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Educational Testing Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-29T23:52:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1494ce0c-ec64-5116-a7e1-519c450bd136', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1494ce0c-ec64-5116-a7e1-519c450bd136'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a lesson on voting rights in a Supreme Court decision that 32 years ago allowed undocumented children a free public education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/opinion/a-supreme-court-misstep-on-voting-rights.html', 'snippet': 'There’s a lesson on voting rights in a Supreme Court decision that 32 years ago allowed undocumented children a free public education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two articles about young people in search of an education caught my attention last week. Both appeared in The Times on the same day. One celebrated the improbable journey of a young man “from a Rwandan dump to the halls of Harvard.” Justus Uwayesu, photographed in front of the iconic John Harvard statue in Harvard Yard, didn’t run as the other children did when a American charity worker approached them more than a decade ago as they scavenged for food. “I want to go to school,” the boy told his American rescuer. This fall, he enrolled as a freshman at Harvard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circu