.com/2014/10/30/us/federal-rule-would-cut-funding-to-some-career-training-programs.html', 'snippet': 'Career-training programs with more than 800,000 students may be threatened under a new federal rule measuring whether graduates earn enough to pay off student loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Career-training programs with more than 800,000 students face a threat to their survival under a new federal rule measuring whether graduates earn enough to pay off student loans, the latest move by the Obama administration against for-profit schools.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Rule Would Cut Funding to Some Career-Training Programs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T04:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b341edba-4321-5e4b-9b5e-0ca1cad12e46', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b341edba-4321-5e4b-9b5e-0ca1cad12e46'}, {'abstract': '“FLEXN” at the Park Avenue Armory, featuring 18 dancers from Brooklyn, will be directed by Peter Sellars.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/peter-sellars-to-direct-dance-event-at-park-avenue-armory/', 'snippet': '“FLEXN” at the Park Avenue Armory, featuring 18 dancers from Brooklyn, will be directed by Peter Sellars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Sellars has directed operas and theater, collaborated with Toni Morrison and staged St. Matthew’s Passion with the Berlin Philharmonic. Now, he will turn his attention to Flex, a Brooklyn-born form of street dance, in a commission from the Park Avenue Armory. “FLEXN,” created with Reggie “Regg Roc” Gray, a pioneer of Flex, will feature 18 dancers from Brooklyn performing on a 70-foot runway in the Wade Thompson Drill Hall and will run March 25-April 4. Images by the photographer Richard Ross will be featured, and live music will be offered by DJ Epic. The choreography, which meshes elements of breaking, mime and profile-angled movement called “tutting,” will be created collaboratively by the dancers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Sellars to Direct Dance Event at Park Avenue Armory', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sellars, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T04:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4699552-e430-54ef-a3bc-59f2ded17b3d', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4699552-e430-54ef-a3bc-59f2ded17b3d'}, {'abstract': 'The latest version of the Flipboard tablet magazine offers a staff-selected “front page” of stories and a wide range of extremely specialized topics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/technology/personaltech/the-latest-flipboard-serves-up-the-news-and-some-surprises.html', 'snippet': 'The latest version of the Flipboard tablet magazine offers a staff-selected “front page” of stories and a wide range of extremely specialized topics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FEW months after Apple began selling the iPad in 2010, Mike McCue, a former employee at Microsoft, and Evan Doll, formerly with Apple, unveiled the first truly great app for the new tablet computer. The app was called Flipboard, and in many ways it was a harbinger of the great mobile-app-fueled frenzy that would soon overrun much of the web, especially news sites.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/business/GADGET-1/GADGET-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1154, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/business/GADGET-1/GADGET-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1154}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/business/GADGET-1/GADGET-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 533, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/business/GADGET-1/GADGET-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1065, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/business/GADGET-1/GADGET-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/30/business/GADGET-1/GADGET-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/business/GADGET-1/GADGET-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height':