n_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fafa642-4bfc-56e6-a3c0-8bc43636437e', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fafa642-4bfc-56e6-a3c0-8bc43636437e'}, {'abstract': 'Whittier, who in 1969 became the first black player on the Texas football team, has filed a proposed federal class-action lawsuit, saying that the N.C.A.A. failed to warn players of the risks that head trauma presented.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/sports/ncaafootball/former-texas-player-julius-whittier-files-suit-against-ncaa.html', 'snippet': 'Whittier, who in 1969 became the first black player on the Texas football team, has filed a proposed federal class-action lawsuit, saying that the N.C.A.A. failed to warn players of the risks that head trauma presented.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julius Whittier, who in 1969 became the first black player on the Texas football team, has filed a proposed federal class-action lawsuit, saying that the N.C.A.A. failed to warn players of the risks that head trauma presented. The suit seeks relief for all N.C.A.A. football players from 1960 to 2014 who did not play in the N.F.L. and have been found to have “a latent brain injury or disease.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Texas Player Julius Whittier Files Suit Against N.C.A.A.', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | College Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia Star Still Barred', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tracy, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whittier, Julius', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T05:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/33d5dd18-947a-5678-9122-e356ef30fe8c', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33d5dd18-947a-5678-9122-e356ef30fe8c'}, {'abstract': 'Arlington High School in Riverside, Calif., is 0-8 this season and has seen a sharp decline in participation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/sports/football/a-program-crumbles-one-season-after-a-players-death.html', 'snippet': 'Arlington High School in Riverside, Calif., is 0-8 this season and has seen a sharp decline in participation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIVERSIDE, Calif. — The hallmarks of a football season that had long since unraveled were plain to see. There was a young offensive lineman getting in the face of the quarterback, who had blamed a teammate for another play gone awry. There was a receiver yelling at a referee and slamming his helmet against the bench, indiscretions that led to his benching and a promise from the coach that the player would “see God” at practice on Monday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Program Crumbles, One Season After a Player’s Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Program Crumbles, One Season After a Player’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interscholastic Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T05:52:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af73244d-bf28-5b61-8f7d-f4ae044757f7', 'word_count': 1373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af73244d-bf28-5b61-8f7d-f4ae044757f7'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s first Moreland Commission, which investigated electric companies’ failures in the 2012 storm, omitted mention of his administration’s shortcomings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/nyregion/cuomos-role-in-hurricane-sandy-inquiry-foretold-fate-of-his-ethics-panel.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s first Moreland Commission, which investigated electric companies’ failures in the 2012 storm, omitted mention of his administration’s shortcomings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo has faced intense scrutiny in recent months, including an investigation by federal prosecutors, over his management of a commission that he created to root out corruption in New York politics, but prevented from examining his administration’s conduct and then prematurely shut down.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/nyregion/MORELAND-web1/MORELAND-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/nyregion/MORELAND-web1/MORELAND-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 576}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '