 universities, most of them free and enrolling throngs of students. An essay in Education Life excerpts one of them.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/a-history-of-moocs-open-online-courses/', 'snippet': 'Two new books look at the phenomenon of MOOCs, online courses from prestigious universities, most of them free and enrolling throngs of students. An essay in Education Life excerpts one of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When massive open online courses first made headlines in 2011, they were trumpeted for their potential to reduce costs and expand access to higher learning, especially elite education. So how’s that going so far?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A History of MOOCs, Open Online Courses', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haber, Jonathan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selingo, Jeffrey J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T13:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Karr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d718f072-b39c-5c5e-b62e-93f96aa8a449', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d718f072-b39c-5c5e-b62e-93f96aa8a449'}, {'abstract': 'Mayday PAC, a group that supports political spending limits, is spending millions of dollars to beat Representative Fred Upton, a Michigan Republican.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/30/in-michigan-spending-big-money-to-stop-big-money/', 'snippet': 'Mayday PAC, a group that supports political spending limits, is spending millions of dollars to beat Representative Fred Upton, a Michigan Republican.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mayday PAC started up this year, the group, co-founded by the Harvard professor Lawrence Lessig, had a big plan to focus public attention on big money in politics: spend millions of dollars to show that political spending limits can be a winning campaign issue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/us/politics/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/us/politics/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/us/politics/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/us/politics/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/us/politics/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/30/us/politics/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton/30firstdraft-Fred-Upton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im