fa83d-94d3-57f0-9432-d6b707e1a2a3', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/191fa83d-94d3-57f0-9432-d6b707e1a2a3'}, {'abstract': 'The Educational Testing Service, which administers the test worldwide, is withholding the scores of those who took it on Oct. 11 while the company investigates the allegations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/world/asia/china-south-korea-students-fallout-suspected-sat-cheating.html', 'snippet': 'The Educational Testing Service, which administers the test worldwide, is withholding the scores of those who took it on Oct. 11 while the company investigates the allegations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The announcement by administrators of the SAT college entrance test that scores are being withheld for students from China and South Korea who took the exam earlier this month has infuriated many and raised anxiety about what for a number of them is a high-stakes college application process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese and South Korean Students Face Fallout From Suspicions of SAT Cheating', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SAT (College Admission Test)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T14:33:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong and Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/831663b8-a22c-5435-b8b0-0c0cf5c7b892', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/831663b8-a22c-5435-b8b0-0c0cf5c7b892'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Republic of Vietnam gets a new premier in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/1964-saigons-mayor-now-premier/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Republic of Vietnam gets a new premier in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAIGON — The mayor of Saigon, 60-year- old Tran Van Huong, was named premier today to succeed Maj. Gen. Nguyen Khanh. Gen. Khanh and his cabinet resigned earlier this week following the appointment of a new chief of state, Phan Khac Suu. ‘‘I’m not sure whether I should be congratulated or offered condolences,’’ Mr. Huong said when he was told the news. ‘‘But this is a critical period in Vietnamese history and I have accepted this sacrifice for my nation as a matter of conscience.’’\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Oct. 31, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Saigon’s Mayor Now Premier', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T14:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75a28cfa-a1b3-52b3-aff8-3c01df445a1d', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75a28cfa-a1b3-52b3-aff8-3c01df445a1d'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Duane Michals talks about his art and the new retrospective of his work at the Carnegie Museum of Art in Pittsburgh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/arts/design/duane-michals-prepares-for-his-retrospective.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Duane Michals talks about his art and the new retrospective of his work at the Carnegie Museum of Art in Pittsburgh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'McKEESPORT, Pa. — It’s a bright September morning in this Pittsburgh suburb, but Duane Michals ought to be blue. He’s on a visit to the house where he was born 82 years ago, the son of a millworker father. But the mills have closed, whole blocks are returning to nature, and Mr. Michals has just discovered that his home has collapsed into a tangle of lumber and weeds.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documents of a Contrarian ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Documents of a Contrarian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michals, Duane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Museum of Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T14:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Blake Gopnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Blake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gopnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2291e049-9f1c-5359-8c8c-3eb0317bab26', 'word_count': 1626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2291e049-9f1c-5359-8c8c-3eb0317bab26'}, {'abstract': 'In the mind of a teenager who self-injures, cutting helps regulate emotions, and strategies that might help most teens can backfire.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/why-teenagers-cut-and-how-to-help/', 'snippet': 'In the mind of a teenager who self-injures, cutting helps regulate emotions, and strategies that might help most teens can backfire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I noticed Sarah’s arms as soon as I met her. It is hard not to, as 15 years of self-injury have rendered them more scar than skin. Sarah isn’t my student, but I’ve taught plenty of kids like her, and she offered to talk to me about why she has cut herself for a decade and a half, and how the adults in her life could have helped her manage the pain that prompted her to self-injure. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/us/motherlode-cutting/motherlode-cutting-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/us/motherlode-cutting/motherlode-cutting-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/us/motherlode-cutting/motherlode-cutting-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/us/motherlode-cutting/motherlode-cutting-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit'