, 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m grateful to Father John O’Malley of Georgetown University and the Society of Jesus for taking the time to respond to my column this week on the doctrinal perils that (I argued) may soon face the Roman Catholic Church under Pope Francis. His comments deserve a much longer response than I’m going to offer here, but I imagine I’ll be\xa0continuing this discussion with various people across different forums in the weeks and months ahead, so some points can be saved for later. For now, I just want to address Father O’Malley’s comments on how Catholics\xa0who desire to be faithful to the church should think about what seems like a possible alteration in longstanding church teaching:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Church, Not a Party', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protestant Churches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jesus Christ', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Society of Jesus', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T15:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d2ea17-be36-5e23-ac58-53b187252b12', 'word_count': 1421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d2ea17-be36-5e23-ac58-53b187252b12'}, {'abstract': 'On a trip to the Seine-et-Marne region, where Brie has been produced since the seventh century, the author goes on an indulgent cheese tasting tour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/travel/a-brie-binge-east-of-paris-.html', 'snippet': 'On a trip to the Seine-et-Marne region, where Brie has been produced since the seventh century, the author goes on an indulgent cheese tasting tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two summers ago, in a village outside Coulommiers, an old market town an hour east of Paris, an old love affair of mine came back to life. On my way to a borrowed house for a few weeks, my partner, Bruno, and I had stopped at a farm for eggs, cream and produce — including a Coulommiers cheese in a round wooden box. I lifted the lid and poked it; it yielded easily to the touch. When we ended a barbecue under the walnut tree in the garden that night, this locally made raw-milk beauty — runny and pleasantly tangy with a suave, complex taste of mossy wells and toasted hazelnuts — shot me back through time to a snowy Saturday in Connecticut when I was 11.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/travel/02-pursuits-promo/02-pursuits-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/travel/02-pursuits-promo/02-pursuits-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/travel/02-pursuits-promo/02-pursuits-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '