 were able to do music every day, which felt really good.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/t-magazine/30symonds-erving/30symonds-erving-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/30/t-magazine/30symonds-erving/30symonds-erving-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/t-magazine/30symonds-erving/30symonds-erving-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/t-magazine/30symonds-erving/30symonds-erving-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/t-magazine/30symonds-erving/30symonds-erving-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/30/t-magazine/30symonds-erving/30symonds-erving-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/30/t-magazine/30symonds-erving/30symonds-erving-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Menswear Designer Siki Im’s New Band', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erving, Julius', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T18:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aly Comingore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Comingore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e620d3f-1dcc-555f-9701-d3d31bf4c9a6', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e620d3f-1dcc-555f-9701-d3d31bf4c9a6'}, {'abstract': 'Doctors make mistakes, but they don’t like to talk about them, writes Susan Gubar, who suffered from medical mistakes made during surgery to remove ovarian cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/30/living-with-cancer-not-talking-about-medical-mistakes/', 'snippet': 'Doctors make mistakes, but they don’t like to talk about them, writes Susan Gubar, who suffered from medical mistakes made during surgery to remove ovarian cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite my best efforts, I remain bewildered about the surgical mishap I suffered in 2008. It was a debulking operation — the removal of all organs affected by a cancer that originated in my ovaries. The procedure was undertaken by the proper specialist, a gynecologic oncologist, but as I recounted in my memoir, the surgery did not go well for me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/health/well_women/well_women-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/23/health/well_women/well_women-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/health/well_women/well_women-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 780, 'su