: 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e01c5cc4-94ff-5e77-9677-31cd25361f17'}, {'abstract': 'Smoke and wood are part of Claudio Parmiggiani’s work, which is on display in a show at Bortolami Gallery in Chelsea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/arts/design/claudio-parmiggiani-at-bortolami-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'Smoke and wood are part of Claudio Parmiggiani’s work, which is on display in a show at Bortolami Gallery in Chelsea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most interesting works in this show come from Claudio Parmiggiani’s “Delocazione,” or “de-location,” series, inspired originally by the dust silhouettes left by objects leaning against a wall. For over 40 years, Mr. Parmiggiani has been creating his own versions of this effect, filling rooms with smoke from burning tires and capturing the outlines of objects with soot and smoke.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6/31CLAUDIOGALLERY6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Claudio Parmiggiani at Bortolami Gallery', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parmiggiani, Claudio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T20:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/94147673-c7fd-51b2-bf6b-f5c91fe972ee', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94147673-c7fd-51b2-bf6b-f5c91fe972ee'}, {'abstract': 'Asian contemporary art and Mother Nature shine in Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/nyregion/asian-art-celebration-heads-to-queens-for-grand-finale-.html', 'snippet': 'Asian contemporary art and Mother Nature shine in Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exhibitions of works by art-world stars like the Korean-American multimedia pioneer Nam June Paik and the mercurial Chinese artist Ai Weiwei have claimed their share of attention this season. Slightly out of the spotlight, the 12th-annual Asian Contemporary Art Week has showcased a group of relatively lesser-known Asian artists (though Paik made a cameo) for over a week, with a series of shows, screenings, lectures and events. The series closes on Saturday evening by celebrating the opening of three new exhibitions at the Queens Museum. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian Art Celebration Heads to Queens for Grand Finale ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asian Art Celebration Heads to Queens for Grand Finale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queens Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T20:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dc00a2c-795e-5bdf-bb0e-58e28642f9bf', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dc00a2c-795e-5bdf-bb0e-58e28642f9bf'}, {'abstract': 'The acerbic Café Deutschland paintings of Jörg Immendorff are on view in bulk in New York for the first time since 1982.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/arts/design/jrg-immendorff-caf-deutschland.html', 'snippet': 'The acerbic Café Deutschland paintings of Jörg Immendorff are on view in bulk in New York for the first time since 1982.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The acerbic Café Deutschland paintings of Jörg Immendorff are back in New York in bulk for the first time since this German Neo-Expressionist’s American debut at the Sonnabend Gallery in 1982. This show of 15 examples confirms that their fusion of painterliness and politics retains much of its original vehemence.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JORGGALLERY4/31JORGGALLERY4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JORGGALLERY4/31JORGGALLERY4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JORGGALLERY4/31JORGGALLERY4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JORGGALLERY4/31JORGGALLERY4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1546, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JORGGALLERY4/31JORGGALLERY4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JORGGALLERY4/31JORGGALLERY4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JORGGALLERY4/31JORGGALLERY4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jörg Immendorff: ‘Café Deutschland’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Werner, Michael, Gallery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Immendorff, Jorg', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2