': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb9318f5-9994-5d17-bd59-51f18a200511', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb9318f5-9994-5d17-bd59-51f18a200511'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition at the Library of Congress recounts American Ballet Theater’s 75-year history, but omits some of the company’s weaknesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/arts/dance/american-ballet-theater-the-museum-exhibition.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition at the Library of Congress recounts American Ballet Theater’s 75-year history, but omits some of the company’s weaknesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In January, American Ballet Theater, now giving a two-week season at the David H. Koch Theater, reaches its 75th anniversary. This summer, the company donated its archive to the Library of Congress. In turn, the library is celebrating both the company’s anniversary and its gift with a small exhibition, “American Ballet Theater: Touring the Globe for 75 Years.” The exhibition, drawing on other archives as well as that of Ballet Theater, occupies one smallish room alone. Nothing fascinates more than a small, plain poster (no image, just words) for the company’s January 1940 debut season.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BALLET1/31BALLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BALLET1/31BALLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BALLET1/31BALLET1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 797, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BALLET1/31BALLET1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1594, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BALLET1/31BALLET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BALLET1/31BALLET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BALLET1/31BALLET1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A History Built on Stars ', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A History Built on Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Library of Congress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T21:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f321bcf-dddb-59ce-8af2-937138c4de68', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f321bcf-dddb-59ce-8af2-937138c4de68'}, {'abstract': '“Bitter Honey,” a documentary by the U.C.L.A. anthropologist Robert Lemelson, examines an island that remains mired in ancient patriarchy and domestic violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/movies/bitter-honey-looks-at-multiple-spouses-in-bali.html', 'snippet': '“Bitter Honey,” a documentary by the U.C.L.A. anthropologist Robert Lemelson, examines an island that remains mired in ancient patriarchy and domestic violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is nothing remotely salacious about “Bitter Honey,” an agonizing documentary examination of polygamy in Bali, Indonesia, from the U.C.L.A. anthropologist Robert Lemelson. There is only vivid evidence of a society that, despite limp efforts at discouraging domestic abuse, remains mired in ancient patriarchy, sanctioning polygamy and, implicitly, often attendant violence. (A “honey,” we learn, is an old regional expression for a second wife.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BITTERHONEY/BITTERHONEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BITTERHONEY/BITTERHONEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BITTERHONEY/BITTERHONEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BITTERHONEY/BITTERHONEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31BITTERHONEY/BITTERHON