yline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a209c31b-d6d2-56b3-be87-faf842225379', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a209c31b-d6d2-56b3-be87-faf842225379'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Dreary Coast,” an immersive theatrical work from Jeff Stark, Hades, king of the underworld, sits enthroned on the banks of the Gowanus Canal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/theater/the-dreary-coast-on-the-banks-of-the-gowanus-canal.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Dreary Coast,” an immersive theatrical work from Jeff Stark, Hades, king of the underworld, sits enthroned on the banks of the Gowanus Canal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How wrong Jean-Paul Sartre was. Hell isn’t other people.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A River to Hell, Reeking but Rhapsodic', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A River to Hell, Reeking but Rhapsodic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stark, Jeff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gowanus Canal (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swoon (1978- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gowanus (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Dreary Coast (Play)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T21:38:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/af4d78ec-11ed-5bfb-a49f-cc8b5c1ceb25', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af4d78ec-11ed-5bfb-a49f-cc8b5c1ceb25'}, {'abstract': '“Jane Wilson at 90: East Village/East End” celebrates a painter at home in two worlds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/arts/design/jane-wilson-at-90-east-village-east-end.html', 'snippet': '“Jane Wilson at 90: East Village/East End” celebrates a painter at home in two worlds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The painter Jane Wilson has been making intensely atmospheric views of the East Village and the East End of Long Island since the days when both were affordable artists’ enclaves. “Jane Wilson at 90” gives us the best of Ms. Wilson’s two worlds, finding her equally enraptured by Tompkins Square Park and the bays and beaches of Water Mill. It also shows her as a painter of many affiliations, a New York School artist who is also an honorary member of some much older regional art tribes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2/JANEWILSON-GALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2/JANEWILSON-GALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2/JANEWILSON-GALLERY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2/JANEWILSON-GALLERY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1508, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/arts/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2/31JANEWILSONGALLERY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jane Wilson at 90’: ‘East Village/East End’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'WILSON, JANE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T21:40:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/feead6ae-0207-58fa-99ba-0a1087c7e651', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feead6ae-0207-58fa-99ba-0a1087c7e651'}, {'abstract': 'Fox’s three-man booth had plenty of voices, but sometimes struggled to say the right thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/sports/baseball/world-series-is-over-but-fox-crew-still-has-a-ways-to-go-.html', 'snippet': 'Fox’s three-man booth had plenty of voices, but sometimes struggled to say the right thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Fox Sports executives refused to add a third voice to the World Series broadcast booth. But after Tim McCarver’s departure last year, Fox replaced him with Harold Reynolds, the former Seattle Mariner best known for his studio work, and Tom Verducci, a baseball writer at Sports Illustrated. The result has been predictable: too many voices saying too much, a sin of three-man booths.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox’s Chatty Booth Makes Few Good Points to Speak of During World Series', 'kicker': 'TV Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fox’s Chatty Booth Makes Few Good Points to Speak of', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buck, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andrews, Erin (1978- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Royals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Harold (1960- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T21:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aeff2dd-78c4-5081-b009-7644614f0f67', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aeff2dd-78c4-5081-b009-7644614f0f67'}, {'abstract': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton spoke at Georgetown University on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/30/first-draft-focus-hillary-visits-hoya-country/', 'snippet': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton spoke at Georgetown University on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Draft Focus: Hillary Visits Hoya Country', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgetown University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-30T21:42:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jabin Botsford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jabin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botsford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed14e79b-7b28-5b61-8e4c-a9a284e8e48b', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed14e79b-7b28-5b61-8e4c-a9a284e8e48b'}, {'abstract': 'The notion of making peace with the past and getting on with one’s life drives the drama in “Angels and Ministers of Grace,” on stage at New Jersey Repertory Company in Long Branch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/nyregion/a-review-of-angels-and-ministers-of-grace-in-long-branch.html', 'snippet': 'The notion of making peace with the past and getting on with one’s life drives the drama in “Angels and Ministers of Grace,” on stage at New Jersey Repertory Company in Long Branch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The words for the title of Elaine Smith’s new play, “Angels and Ministers of Grace,” are taken from Shakespeare. Hamlet speaks them when he first sees his father’s ghost.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/sub02ARTSNJ1/sub02ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/sub02ARTSNJ1/sub02ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/sub02ARTSNJ1/sub02ARTSNJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/sub02ARTSNJ1/sub02ARTSNJ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1487, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/sub02ARTSNJ1/sub02ARTSNJ1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/sub02ARTSNJ1/sub02ARTSNJ1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/sub02ARTSNJ1/sub02ARTSNJ1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Past That Persists Through Quirks and Crises ', 'kicker': 'Theater Review | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Past That Persists Through Quirks and Crises', 'name': None, 'seo'