', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc890fa2-9d56-59ef-8ff0-8739530f54b3', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc890fa2-9d56-59ef-8ff0-8739530f54b3'}, {'abstract': 'His grievances sound like those from the days of the U.S.S.R.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/opinion/blaming-the-west-for-things-gone-wrong-mr-putin-sings-an-old-tune.html', 'snippet': 'His grievances sound like those from the days of the U.S.S.R.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOCHI, Russia — Vladimir Putin’s annual appearance before the Valdai “discussion club,” a gathering of international analysts and journalists who follow Russia, is his chance to sound off on a global stage. Last week, with sanctions and dropping oil prices choking Russia’s economy and stoking Mr. Putin’s anger, the predictable target was his bête noire, America.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blaming the West for Things Gone Wrong, Mr. Putin Sings an Old Tune', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blaming the West for Things Gone Wrong, Mr. Putin Sings an Old Tune', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T01:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge Schmemann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 