5-f94d3f5d6158'}, {'abstract': 'The gainful employment provision sets a rule based on the percentage of a program graduate’s income that can be used for loan payments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/us/new-federal-standard-for-aid-to-for-profit-colleges-draws-criticism.html', 'snippet': 'The gainful employment provision sets a rule based on the percentage of a program graduate’s income that can be used for loan payments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a new bid to shut down career-training programs that leave students with low earnings and high debt, the Obama administration drew cries of foul Thursday, with for-profit schools saying the government overreached, and those schools’ harshest critics saying it did not go far enough.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Federal Standard for Aid to For-Profit Colleges Draws Criticism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Federal Standard for Aid to For-Profit Colleges Draws Criticism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T02:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05baa192-a70d-51ff-8116-3d5c211df211', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05baa192-a70d-51ff-8116-3d5c211df211'}, {'abstract': 'In a swing through Democratic territory, the president cited evidence that his policies have worked and sought to dramatize the stakes on Election D