y 20th century provided meals as well as emotional support to those in need. “Every single class I bring treats,” she said. “It’s a reminder that we aren’t just clinicians. We cater to the whole human being.”', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SUBCANDY/02SUBCANDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SUBCANDY/02SUBCANDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SUBCANDY/02SUBCANDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SUBCANDY/02SUBCANDY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1540, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SUBCANDY/02SUBCANDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SUBCANDY/02SUBCANDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/02SUBCANDY/02SUBCANDY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Connecting Online, Via Snail Mail', 'kicker': 'Blackboard | Social (Net)work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Connecting Online, Via Snail Mail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pappano, Laura', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simmons College', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leeman, Dana Grossman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T10:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Pappano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pappano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/749bb179-f48e-5221-8a83-da32b6a742cd', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/749bb179-f48e-5221-8a83-da32b6a742cd'}, {'abstract': 'José Antonio Bowen takes risks and makes headlines. But he bets on the human factor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/education/edlife/a-conversation-with-gouchers-new-president.html', 'snippet': 'José Antonio Bowen takes risks and makes headlines. But he bets on the human factor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'José Antonio Bowen, the new president of Goucher College in Baltimore, made headlines this fall with the announcement that the college would accept two-minute videos from applicants as an alternative to high school transcripts. But Dr. Bowen, a jazz musician who has played with Stan Getz, Dave Brubeck and Bobby McFerrin, has been shaking up college instruction for years, in workshops across the country, preaching the lessons of his book, “Teaching Naked: How Moving Technology Out of Your College Classroom Will Improve Student Learning.” His ideas about higher education in the Internet age are far-reaching, and could be threatening to some faculty members. But he makes a strong case that colleges will become obsolete if they cling to old habits, when so much of the learning dispensed on campus is available online.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/1102-QA/1102-QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/1102-QA/1102-QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/1102-QA/1102-QA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/1102-QA/1102-QA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/1102-QA/1102-QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/1102-QA/1102-QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/education/edlife/1102-QA/1102-QA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With Goucher’s New President', 'kicker': 'Talking Head | José Antonio Bowen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reclaiming the Classroo