snippet': 'Deserted by their enigmatic father, three brothers struggle to find themselves in Daniel Kehlmann’s tragicomedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing nearly certain about a novel whose title is merely a letter of the alphabet is that any review will probably contain what grammarians call “modals,” words that imply possibility: “This enigmatic title may refer to . . . ” or “Given the author’s many winks at the reader, such a title might. . . . ” ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-Salvatore/1102-bks-Salvatore-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-Salvatore/1102-bks-Salvatore-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 537}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-Salvatore/1102-bks-Salvatore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-Salvatore/1102-bks-Salvatore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1834, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-Salvatore/1102-bks-Salvatore-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-Salvatore/1102-bks-Salvatore-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-Salvatore/1102-bks-Salvatore-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daniel Kehlmann’s ‘F’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scam Artists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kehlmann, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Janeway, Carol Brown', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T16:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Salvatore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Salvatore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec7302ff-b8bd-546e-9af7-3688bccd37f1', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec7302ff-b8bd-546e-9af7-3688bccd37f1'}, {'abstract': 'The stories in “Wallflowers,” Eliza Robertson’s debut collection, portray people surviving loss and heartbreak in a world full of uncanny moments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/books/review/eliza-robertsons-wallflowers.html', 'snippet': 'The stories in “Wallflowers,” Eliza Robertson’s debut collection, portray people surviving loss and heartbreak in a world full of uncanny moments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading “Wallflowers,” Eliza Robertson’s debut story collection, is like taking a solo swim across a chilly lake. You become mesmerized by details — the silken texture of the water, the cool air on your arms as they rise and fall, the rhythm of your breath, the dark scrub of trees on the distant shore — without ever forgetting the mysteries and potential dangers that lurk beneath. In this captivating book, people drown in gray water, shacks burn on stony beaches, planes crash into rivers, hummingbirds are trapped and tethered to wrists, neighborhoods flood. Grief and loss cast long shadows over these stories, which sometimes bring us to the threshold of disaster and sometimes explore its aftermath.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eliza Robertson’s ‘Wallflowers’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disaster Areas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robertson, Eliza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T16:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Serber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Serber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d005172-68da-568b-af0d-c2d89f05ec5d', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d005172-68da-568b-af0d-c2d89f05ec5d'}, {'abstract': 'New books by Julie Schumacher, Cathie Pelletier, Stuart Rojstaczer and Jonathan Coe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/books/review/julie-schumachers-dear-committee-members-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'New books by Julie Schumacher, Cathie Pelletier, Stuart Rojstaczer and Jonathan Coe.', 'lead_paragraph': ' DEAR COMMITTEE MEMBERS  By Julie Schumacher  Doubleday, $22.95.  ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/books/review/1102-bks-SHORT/1102-bks-SHORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, '