 on presidential terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/01/world/asia/un-panel-faults-sri-lanka-over-presidential-powers.html', 'snippet': 'A human rights report criticized a constitutional change that allows the president to appoint or dismiss judges, and repealed the limit on presidential terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLOMBO, Sri Lanka — A United Nations human rights panel urged Sri Lanka on Friday to repeal a constitutional amendment that critics say gives the country’s president too much power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Panel Faults Sri Lanka Over Presidential Powers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sri Lanka: U.N. Panel Seeks Checks on Leader’s Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajapaksa, Mahinda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T18:40:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dharisha Bastians', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dharisha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bastians', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3240e31e-c67a-5c87-b071-0b7a2077731a', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3240e31e-c67a-5c87-b071-0b7a2077731a'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department found a pattern of excessive force in the Albuquerque Police Department, after a string of shootings in which 23 people