s', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cebaa8c-a258-5b19-becf-2723d6af9373', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cebaa8c-a258-5b19-becf-2723d6af9373'}, {'abstract': 'The new problem, which could cause too much pressure in an airbag’s casing, is different from the defect that prompted the recall of about 14 million vehicles in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/01/business/nissan-recalls-1800-suvs-over-another-defect-in-takata-made-airbags.html', 'snippet': 'The new problem, which could cause too much pressure in an airbag’s casing, is different from the defect that prompted the recall of about 14 million vehicles in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 14 million older vehicles have been recalled in recent years because airbags made by the Takata Corporation can explode in a crash, shooting pieces of metal into the cabin. But a different Takata defect that can have the same effect is emerging in newer vehicles.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Defect in Airbags Affects Some Infinitis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Defect in Airbags Affects Some Infinitis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Takata Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infiniti Division of Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T18:59:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d19c3b0-f1cb-52c8-a828-96cc7ede51bd', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d19c3b0-f1cb-52c8-a828-96cc7ede51bd'}, {'abstract': 'Maine will vote on a ballot measure to restrict bear hunting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/10/31/races-to-watch-save-the-bears/', 'snippet': 'Maine will vote on a ballot measure to restrict bear hunting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of The Times’ interactive presentation on the races and ballot measures to watch across all 50 states, we here on First Draft will be highlighting some of our favorites from now until Election Day. Up next is vote in Maine that would restrict bear hunting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Races to Watch: Save the Bears', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bears', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Humane Society of the United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec8164b6-ef90-5c5d-87b2-b8ca8157c041', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec8164b6-ef90-5c5d-87b2-b8ca8157c041'}, {'abstract': 'A “split the baby” proposal would regulate “wholesale” Internet transactions similar to utilities, and lightly regulate “retail” transactions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/01/technology/fcc-considering-hybrid-regulatory-approach-to-net-neutrality.html', 'snippet': 'A “split the baby” proposal would regulate “wholesale” Internet transactions similar to utilities, and lightly regulate “retail” transactions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The chairman and staff of the Federal Communications Commission are moving toward a proposal that for the first time would give the agency regulatory authority over how Internet traffic flows between content providers and the companies that provide Internet service to consumers, according to people close to the discussions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. Considering Hybrid Regulatory Approach to Net Neutrality', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.C.C. Is Said to Consider Hybrid Rules for Internet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyatt, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Thomas E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:09:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt: