 shoes, hats and bourbon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Daitz’s Num Pang Cambodian-style sandwich shops in Manhattan are classified in culinary circles as “fast casual,” which he defines as offering fresh, inventive and inexpensive food conceived and prepared with rigorous attention to ingredients and flavors. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comfort Me With Sneakers', 'kicker': 'What I Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comfort Me With Sneakers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daitz, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Num Pang Sandwich Shop (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Shaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fb3d32e-bbf0-5c7e-aaf3-f30d7937e4db', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fb3d32e-bbf0-5c7e-aaf3-f30d7937e4db'}, {'abstract': 'Nine of today’s hottest food talents — Grant Achatz, Brooks Headley and Andrew Carmellini included — share their favorite places to eat pre-flight.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/david-chang-rene-redzepi-and-more-chefs-on-where-to-eat-on-the-fly/', 'snippet': 'Nine of today’s hottest food talents — Grant Achatz, Brooks Headley and Andrew Carmellini included — share their favorite places to eat pre-flight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the winter travel issue of T, Jacob Z. Gross runs the numbers on one of food’s fastest-improving venues: airport restaurants. The preflight eateries have seen a dramatic uptick in both business and quality in recent years thanks to an increase in air traffic and exciting new entries from chefs like the U.K.’s Heston Blumenthal and Spain’s Carles Gaig. But where do the chefs themselves grab a bite when flying? To find out, we asked nine of the top talents in the field who don’t have airport joints — yet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/t-magazine/31airport-oloizia-2/31airport-oloizia-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/t-magazine/31airport-oloizia-2/31airport-oloizia-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/t-magazine/31airport-oloizia-2/31airport-oloizia-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/t-magazine/31airport-oloizia-2/31airport-oloizia-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/t-magazine/31airport-oloizia-2/31airport-oloizia-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/31/t-magazine/31airport-oloizia-2/31airport-oloizia-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'cap