4/11/01/sports/football/fantasy-football-introducing-weekly-matchup-analysis-charts.html', 'snippet': 'These charts indicate how difficult a fantasy matchup a player will have depending on how many standard fantasy points the opposing defense has allowed to his position.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are excited to share our fantasy football matchup analysis charts with you for the quarterback, running back and wide receiver (WR1 and WR2) positions. They are a way to visualize matchup data as well as to see how well a player has done in recent weeks or for the entire season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: Introducing Weekly Matchup Analysis Charts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Sablich and Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0879b3d2-2966-593e-88b6-53862b357937', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0879b3d2-2966-593e-88b6-53862b357937'}, {'abstract': 'A full-floor, four-bedroom aerie near the pinnacle of One57 was the sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/realestate/56-million-for-prime-new-york-city-views.html', 'snippet': 'A full-floor, four-bedroom aerie near the pinnacle of One57 was the sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A full-floor aerie near the pinnacle of One57, the Extell Development Company’s 90-story Midtown tower with glass curtain walls that capture 360-degree views of the city and beyond — the Catskills and the Atlantic are part of the scenery on a clear day — sold for $56,079,298.25 and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/realestate/02TICKET/02TICKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/realestate/02TICKET/02TICKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 896}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/realestate/02TICKET/02TICKET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/realestate/02TICKET/02TICKET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1371, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/realestate/02TICKET/02TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/realestate/02TICKET/02TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/realestate/02TICKET/02TICKET-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '$56 Million for Prime New York City Views', 'kicker': 'Big Ticket', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prime Views Everywhere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Extell Development Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods and Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e544bd3f-6d5c-5656-839d-d9db12ad8c47', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e544bd3f-6d5c-5656-839d-d9db12ad8c47'}, {'abstract': 'None of the Democratic candidates have mentioned that the budget is in far better shape largely because taxes went up on the rich, and because health care costs are falling.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/a-deficit-of-reality-on-the-democratic-campaign-trail/', 'snippet': 'None of the Democratic candidates have mentioned that the budget is in far better shape largely because taxes went up on the rich, and because health care costs are falling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s clearly too much to expect that Democratic candidates would tell voters that a smaller deficit is the last thing the economy needs right now. Not even Senator Elizabeth Warren campaigns that way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deficit of Reality on the Democratic Campaign Trail', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46b99bf1-db9b-5791-99fe-4d1b1efb00d7', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46b99bf1-db9b-5791-99fe-4d1b1efb00d7'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The American hospital of Paris reserves beds for the war wounded in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/1939-hospital-designated-auxiliary/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The American hospital of Paris reserves beds for the war wounded in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In accordance with plans formulated last April and fully approved by the French authorities, the American Hospital of Paris is now on a war basis and officially designated as an auxiliary hospital for war wounded. Forty beds in the hospital, however, will continue to be reserved for American civilian patients, officials of the institution said yesterday. In addition to the Hospital at Neuilly, there has also been equipped another auxiliary base hospital at Etretat, of which Dr. Laurence Fuller will be the chief of medical staff and Harold F. Johnson the manager, it was announced. The American Hospital at Neuilly was in normal times a 150-bed hospital. Converted for the purpose of receiving war wounded, it will now have 200 beds, which can readily be increased to 300 or 400 should the necessity arise.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Nov. 1, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multim