d is playing video games again. Well, sort of. Kevin Spacey won’t say whether the politician he portrays on Netflix’s “House of Cards” will still find a way to get his first-person shooter fix now that Underwood has ascended to the presidency. “I cannot be the spoiler in chief,” he said when asked about some of that political drama’s finer points.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02VIDEOACTING2/02VIDEOACTING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02VIDEOACTING2/02VIDEOACTING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02VIDEOACTING2/02VIDEOACTING2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02VIDEOACTING2/02VIDEOACTING2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1183, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02VIDEOACTING2/02VIDEOACTING2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02VIDEOACTING2/02VIDEOACTING2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02VIDEOACTING2/02VIDEOACTING2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Casting the Single-Player Movie Star ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Casting the Single-Player Movie Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suellentrop, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Call of Duty: Advanced Warfare (Video Game)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spacey, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'House of Cards (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Video Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Suellentrop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suellentrop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b7ed68c-41eb-5780-8f2f-1b14ebc53f73', 'word_count': 1507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b7ed68c-41eb-5780-8f2f-1b14ebc53f73'}, {'abstract': 'Shamel Pitts, a New York-born Juilliard graduate, talks about what it’s like to live in Tel Aviv as part of the Batsheva Dance Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/arts/dance/shamel-pitts-on-a-dancers-life-in-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Shamel Pitts, a New York-born Juilliard graduate, talks about what it’s like to live in Tel Aviv as part of the Batsheva Dance Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether onstage or on the streets of Tel Aviv, Shamel Pitts commands attention. When performing with the Batsheva Dance Company, Israel’s premier contemporary dance troupe, he projects magnetic focus and pounces with ferocious abandon. When strolling down Rothschild Boulevard in the center of town, often with oversize glasses, flowing graphic shirts, nudged-off-center hats and a cool stride, he makes you turn and think, “There goes a personality.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 862}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1427, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning Heads in Tel Aviv', 'kicker': 'Snapshot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turning Heads in Tel Aviv', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitts, Shamel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Batsheva Dance Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T19:59:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'As told to Brian Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3628f4bf-c86f-51c2-9bcc-fb58fbd4b901', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3628f4bf-c86f-51c2-9bcc-fb58fbd4b901'}, {'abstract': 'A stay at a nice hotel can give us a brief opportunity to escape our regular lives, to be someone else and to return home refreshed. So, we hope, can a magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/great-escapism/', 'snippet': 'A stay at a nice hotel can give us a brief opportunity to escape our regular lives, to be someone else and to return home refreshed. So, we hope, can a magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this travel issue, we could have offered you specific suggestions of places to visit, meals to eat, sights not to miss. Instead, we decided to focus on the pleasures of various kinds of travel and the meanings of different destinations. The hope is that you will be transported by these ideas and images, whether or not you plan on making any of the journeys our writers undertook — going, for instance, from London to Venice aboard the luxurious Orient Express. A pair of mystery author friends realize that the train’s original luxury, speed, has been replaced by the more contemporary luxury of time. (It takes two days to cover what would be a two-hour flight.) Those days are spent in close quarters with strangers, liveried staff and the authors’ own imaginations. More energetically, our critic at large Jody Rosen heads to Bhutan, a country where the royal family’s passion for bicycling might just rival Buddhism as the path to nirvana. Perhaps it’s no surprise that the place that engendered the concept of Gross National Happiness should also endorse a more scenic, wind-in-your-face form of getting from A to B. Closer to home — or at least to the home of the photographer Bruce Weber — a shack on the beach provides the fantasylike backdrop to a fashion shoot that evokes the freedom and beauty of youth, as captured by the teenagers Jean Campbell, a new model, and Brooklyn Beckham, child of David and Victoria. The pictures conjure a sense of the carefree idealism in those long summer days between childhood and adulthood, which — however far away those things might seem — we ought not to lose if we can help it. It is some aspect of that feeling we seek to capture in any vacation by the sea.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/t-magazine/02travel-edletter/02travel-edletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/t-magazine/02travel-edletter/02travel-edletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 732}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/t-magazine/02travel-edletter/02travel-edletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 840, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/t-magazine/02travel-edletter/02travel-edletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/t-mag