ansion plans announced this week, that is merely the beginning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brewster Kahle is a librarian by training and temperament. In the mid-1990s, when many saw the nascent World Wide Web as a place to sell things, he saw it as data that cried out to be preserved and cataloged. Later, he widened his scope to include material — film, books, music — that was not native to the web but could be digitally gathered there.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-internetarchive/31bits-internetarchive-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-internetarchive/31bits-internetarchive-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-internetarchive/31bits-internetarchive-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-internetarchive/31bits-internetarchive-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 864, 'width': 1199, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-internetarchive/31bits-internetarchive-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-internetarchive/31bits-internetarchive-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-internetarchive/31bits-internetarchive-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Internet Archive, Trying to Encompass All Creation', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Internet Archive Aims to Preserve All of Creation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahle, Brewster', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internet Archive', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T20:01:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7c6be79-ee32-5d9b-9392-fc0e25b2afbd', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7c6be79-ee32-5d9b-9392-fc0e25b2afbd'}, {'abstract': '“House of DVF,” making its premiere Sunday night, follows Diane von Furstenberg and her team as they search for a brand ambassador.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/arts/television/a-designer-is-dressed-to-cull.html', 'snippet': '“House of DVF,” making its premiere Sunday night, follows Diane von Furstenberg and her team as they search for a brand ambassador.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diane von Furstenberg, the designer of the timeless wrap dress, now celebrating its 40th anniversary, understands the value of connecting with the younger generation. But she does worry about its behavior. “House of DVF,” the newest reality addition to the E! roster, making its premiere Sunday night, follows Ms. von Furstenberg and her team as they search for a brand ambassador: preferably someone who has polished manners and a voice that doesn’t grate, and who won’t pilfer the merchandise when left alone in the accessories department. Good luck with that.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE2/02GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 812, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE2/02GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 812}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE2/02GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE2/02GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1515, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE2/02GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE2/02GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE2/02GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Designer Is Dressed to Cull', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Designer Is Dressed to Cull', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T20:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/888f1372-52d4-5056-9ae2-4e619bba23bc', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/888f1372-52d4-5056-9ae2-4e619bba23bc'}, {'abstract': 'Albert G. Horvath, the Smithsonian Institution’s current senior finance official, will serve as secretary until David J. Skorton can take up his permanent role in July.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/smithsonian-names-a-temporary-leader/', 'snippet': 'Albert G. Horvath, the Smithsonian Institution’s current senior finance official, will serve as secretary until David J. Skorton can take up his permanent role in July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Smithsonian Institution has appointed Albert G. Horvath, its current senior finance official, as its acting leader for the first half of next year, until the incoming secretary, David J. Skorton, can take up his position in July.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smithsonian Names a Temporary Leader', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smithsonian Names Interim Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skorton, David J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T20:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c39215b-d1bc-5a70-9f8f-a9607e83787f', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c39215b-d1bc-5a70-9f8f-a9607e83787f'}, {'abstract': 'Stevie Wonder comes to Madison Square Garden a day before Usher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/arts/music/an-rb-master-and-maybe-an-heir.html', 'snippet': 'Stevie Wonder comes to Madison Square Garden a day before Usher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At this point, a recording of Stevie Wonder tapping a table while humming would be cause for celebration, but word is he’s working on a pair of proper new releases. In the meantime, he’s embarking on a short tour that arrives Thursday at Madison Square Garden, where he’ll perform a show devoted to his album “Songs in the Key of Life.” That’s one of the signature documents of 1970s soul music, and one of the most ambitious albums in pop history, one that helped cement Mr. Wonder’s larger-than-life standing. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE7/02GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE7/02GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE7/02GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE7/02GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'wi