rofessor fights a zombie attack with the help of tangent vectors and parametric curve derivatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is it about professors and zombies?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Academic Zombies Attack! (Again)', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T20:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72b6072e-65e9-54c5-b269-2cda4d8c664f', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72b6072e-65e9-54c5-b269-2cda4d8c664f'}, {'abstract': 'In the premiere of “Actual Size,” Sally Silvers uses Hitchcock’s “North by Northwest” as the structural grid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/arts/dance/taking-directions-from-hitchcock.html', 'snippet': 'In the premiere of “Actual Size,” Sally Silvers uses Hitchcock’s “North by Northwest” as the structural grid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sally Silvers and Alfred Hitchcock? Stranger pairings have happened, and it’s more fitting than not: Both the choreographer and the film director have their whimsical, devious ways. In the premiere of “Actual Size,” Ms. Silvers uses Hitchcock’s “North by Northwest” as the structural grid for a work that brings together an extraordinary cast of six, including the former Merce Cunningham dancers Melissa Toogood and Dylan Crossman. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/arts/02GUIDE8/02GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subT