 left, whose shared focus on explicitly familial and sexual\xa0relationships may be crowding out Christian ideas, and Christian models of community and religious life, that the modern world is going to need, perhaps desperately, if current trends in social life persist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Synod and the Single Catholic', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abstinence (Sexual)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celibacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinenberg, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scandinavia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T20:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4b20d69-9749-54c0-a016-95a611c5ba93', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4b20d69-9749-54c0-a016-95a611c5ba93'}, {'abstract': 'Rukmini Callimachi, a Times reporter, answers readers’ questions about the 23 Western hostages who were held by the Islamic State in in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/01/world/middleeast/q-and-a-on-isis-hostages-held-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Rukmini Callimachi, a Times reporter, answers readers’ questions about the 23 Western hostages who were held by the Islamic State in in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times published a detailed account earlier this week of the horror 23 Western hostages faced when they were held by the Islamic State, also known as ISIS or ISIL, in an underground network of prisons in Syria. Invited to ask questions of the reporter, Rukmini Callimachi, in the comments of the article, readers addressed a variety of topics, including countries’ policies toward paying ransoms, the Islamic State’s finances and how to help the remaining hostages. Ms. Callimachi responded to a selection of the questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/world/JP-HOSTAGES9/JP-HOSTAGES9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/25/world/JP-HOSTAGES9/JP-HOSTAGES9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/world/JP-HOSTAGES9/JP-HOSTAGES9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/world/JP-HOSTAGES9/JP-HOSTAGES9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/25/world/JP-HOSTAGES9/JP-HOSTAGES9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/25/world/JP-