_id': 'nyt://article/8666d16c-6aab-5ca6-ab84-7fe7dc563ed8', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8666d16c-6aab-5ca6-ab84-7fe7dc563ed8'}, {'abstract': 'On Sundays, Amy Ryan, an actress known for her dramatic roles, gets in touch with her playful side in Brooklyn Heights, where she lives with her husband and daughter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/02/nyregion/amy-ryan-a-break-from-the-drama.html', 'snippet': 'On Sundays, Amy Ryan, an actress known for her dramatic roles, gets in touch with her playful side in Brooklyn Heights, where she lives with her husband and daughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amy Ryan is known for her dramatic roles, most recently as the supportive ex-wife of a washed-up actor in the movie “Birdman.” “My mother always said, ‘Your career surprised me, because you were a funny kid,’ ” she said. She described herself as “still pretty goofy,” akin to Holly Flax, the character she played on the NBC sitcom “The Office.” But Ms. Ryan, 46, continues to flex her dramatic muscles while shooting two movies in New York, one opposite Tom Hanks, the other with Gabriel Byrne. On Sundays she gets in touch with her playful side in Brooklyn Heights, where she lives with her husband, Eric Slovin, 47, a comedy writer and a producer on the television series “Broad City,” and their 5-year-old daughter.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Away From ‘The Office,’ and the Drama ', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Away From ‘The Office,’ and the Drama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Heights (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Amy (1968- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T20:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro',