 captivated the international cricketing community during the early 2000s with his lightning-fast bowling: an intimidating dart-like delivery that could dismiss batsmen almost before they saw the ball coming. But controversy marred his career, and Mr. Lawson, a Jamaican cricketer who played for the West Indies, gradually faded from the sport’s spotlight, leaving his admirers to wonder as to his whereabouts.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02UPDATE/02UPDATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02UPDATE/02UPDATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 719}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02UPDATE/02UPDATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 855, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02UPDATE/02UPDATE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1839, 'width': 1534, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02UPDATE/02UPDATE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02UPDATE/02UPDATE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02UPDATE/02UPDATE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Brooklyn Cricketer, Extra Innings ', 'kicker': 'Update', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Brooklyn Cricketer, Extra Innings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vadukul, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawson, Jermaine (1982- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T22:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Vadukul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vadukul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d051980-d5b5-5128-b3d6-c23724f4aaec', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d051980-d5b5-5128-b3d6-c23724f4aaec'}, {'abstract': 'Power 105’s Powerhouse concert on Thursday in Brooklyn presented a lineup of rising talent, and bigger stars like Chris Brown, Trey Songz, Young Jeezy and T.I.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/01/arts/music/bobby-shmurda-young-jeezy-and-ti-at-powerhouse.html', 'snippet': 'Power 105’s Powerhouse concert on Thursday in Brooklyn presented a lineup of rising talent, and bigger stars like Chris Brown, Trey Songz, Young Jeezy and T.I.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hot Boy,” by Bobby Shmurda, is currently the No. 8 song in the country, according to Billboard. Let’s stop for a moment and think about how remarkable that is. “Hot Boy” (that’s the clean version of the title, anyhow) — began life early this year as a little-watched video in which Bobby Shmurda and his friends — “grimy shooters dressed in G-Star” — ran rowdy on the streets of Brooklyn. It’s bare-bones hip-hop, full of charismatic menace, street anxiety and just the faintest dash of Caribbean flair.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '10 Minutes, and They’re Gone ', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '10 Minutes, and They’re Gone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '105.1-FM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bobby Shmurda (1994- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young Jeezy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'TI (1980- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T22:41:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dde9ab0-c7ec-5b16-b955-5a99eb777c89', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dde9ab0-c7ec-5b16-b955-5a99eb777c89'}, {'abstract': 'The yellow-rumped warbler (Setophaga coronata) overwinters farther north than any other North American wood warbler, and is very hardy.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/meet-the-butter-butt-one-tough-bird/', 'snippet': 'The yellow-rumped warbler (Setophaga coronata) overwinters farther north than any other North American wood warbler, and is very hardy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Weighing only a few ounces, warblers are not known for their winter hardiness, but the yellow-rumped, or myrtle, warbler is one tough bird. As warblers go, this species is just a little larger, a little heavier and a little bulkier than its kin. They can be downright abundant in the late fall landscape, darting through the thinning tree branches, or even shaking off the season’s first snowflakes. The yellow-rumped warbler (Setophaga coronata) overwinters farther north than any other North American wood warbler, and is very hardy. Butter butts, as birders call them because of the bright yellow patch above their tails, are just beginning to show up in our local woodlands as their passerine brethren abandon the cold Northeast for the warmth of Central and South America. The birds are official New Yorkers throughout the winter months.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02NATURE_SUB/02NATURE_SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02NATURE_SUB/02NATURE_SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02NATURE_SUB/02NATURE_SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02NATURE_SUB/02NATURE_SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02NATURE_SUB/02NATURE_SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/02/nyregion/02NATURE_SUB/02NATURE_SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnai