n, who were credited as executive producers of the film, and Open Road, which was to distribute it, had no direct responsibility for it. Ms. Jones, a film crew member, was killed by a freight train that unexpectedly caught her and others on a set across the tracks in Georgia. The film’s director, Randall Miller, and others remain defendants in the suit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gregg Allman Dropped From Wrongful-Death Suit', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gregg Allman Dropped From Wrongful-Death Suit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allman, Gregg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Sarah Elizabeth (1986-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Open Road Films', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehman, Michael', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-10-31T22:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a5d0afc-5d71-5e74-85f3-adc7eb36a737', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a5d0afc-5d71-5e74-85f3-adc7eb36a737'}, {'abstract': 'The proposal comes after the commission has noticed an increase in the number of 911 system outages in recent months.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/10/31/f-c-c-weighs-backup-system-for-911/', 'snippet': 'The proposal comes after the commission has noticed an increase in the number of 911 system outages in recent months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Federal Communications Commission is considering whether it should adopt specific requirements for backup batteries to residential phone systems to make sure that consumers can call 911 during a power outage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-911/31bits-911-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-911/31bits-911-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-911/31bits-911-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-911/31bits-911-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-911/31bits-911-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-911/31bits-911-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/10/31/business/31bits-911/31bits-911-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. Weighs Backup System for 911', 'kicker